9-29T18:17:00-07:00","id":978752,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: X/////O (-2)<br /> [Pattern Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken]<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 4<br /> </div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative +6 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441025\" target=\"_blank\">12</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:46:34-07:00","id":978983,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> You blink your eyes, trying to clear away the haze surrounding your mind, but you struggle to remember anything that happened after going through the portal. You don't know why, but you feel <i>exhausted</i> and emotionally taxed like you haven't felt since the aftermath of Hakim's death.<br /> <br /> When you try to look around you, you realize that you are wearing Hakim's cloak; you don't remember putting that on. You are a formless shadow, lying on the ground beside Phoenix. When you look up, you stare into the face of a creature out of your worst nightmares.<br /> <br /> One memory is crystal clear: In your arrogance, your hubris, <i>you</i> summoned this creature. It infected your magic, tainting your very soul. There is still some of it within you, threatening to ruin your next spell. The shame of this realization rocks you to your core.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You groan in pain. Why are you in <i>so much </i>pain? What happened?<br /> <br /> You blink your eyes and try to dispel your pounding headache. You realize that your memories of what happened after going through the portal are hazy at best. Glimpses of a long hallway, and a sea of stars, flash through your mind's eye. You hear the faintest echo of a woman crying, but don't remember why.<br /> <br /> When you look up, you see a large humanoid creature of darkness. It sparks another memory: Moonstone, foolishly allowing something into the world, and you trying to fend it off at great personal risk.<br /> <br /> You blink again as you realize that you're lying on something. Looking down, you see a long, round staff. Its surface is covered with intricate geometric runic carvings. It feels slightly warm to the touch.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If you choose to use it, the staff can be used as a weapon with the following stats: +1L damage, -1 initiative, Strength 2, Size 4. Special: +1 Defense bonus against opponents who are unarmed or wield weapons of Size 1; two-handed (+1 Strength required if wielding with one hand).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>The Abyssal Entity</b><br /> Looking directly at the creature is difficult. Anywhere that it touches the creature's skin, sunlight splits and collides together again, creating impossible pockets or bubbles of prismatic visions in the air around it. Some of the light seems to <i>sizzle</i>, creating pockets of shadow on the wall and street.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal creature raises its arms into the air and emits a terrible, inhuman roar. The light around it grows darker. You all feel a pulse of energy on your Periphery, and anyone standing near the creature feels a supernatural wave of fear crash into you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The creature will activate its Emotional Aura Numen using 1 WP: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441216\" target=\"_blank\">Emotional Aura (17)</a> = <b>8</b> successes. Everyone is currently standing within a 5-yard circle of this thing, so on your turn, roll Resolve + Composure + Gnosis; if you get less than 8 successes, take -2 on all actions as long as the aura remains (I'll tell you when it's over) or as long as you remain within the aura.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mathias</b><br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Shit! It's a Gulmoth!&quot;</span> Mathias exclaims. He holds up his crystal wand and makes a stabbing motion towards the creature. You all feel another burst of energy on your Periphery as he casts a spell on the creature. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I can make it hurt more if someone else hits it,&quot;</span> he explains. Mathias stands in front of the creature, trying to goad it into attacking him before hurting anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mathias will cast <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441226\" target=\"_blank\">Grave Misfortune</a>: Gnosis (3) + Fate (4) + Order Tool (1) - Potency (-2) - Emotional Aura (2) = 4d10: <b>1</b> success. He has 2 free Reach; spending 3 on instant casting, sensory range, and advanced duration (1 scene). The spell succeeds with Potency 5, to help overcome some of the creature's Withstand.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441227\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox</a> (containing, 1st roll this scene): 2d10 = <b>0</b> successes.<br /> <br /> Moonstone may make an Intelligence + Occult roll to see if he remembers anything about Gulmoth.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Initiative:</b><br /> Gulmoth (20) -- Emotional Aura<br /> Ragnar (17) -- Exceptional Luck<br /> Mathias (16) -- Grave Misfortune<br /> Phoenix (13) -- Kinetic Blow<br /> Moonstone (12) -- Telepathy<br /> Binder (12) -- Mind over Matter<br /> Lynx (12) -- Waiting<br /> <br /> For this fight, I'd like to try a posting convention that might help speed things up, given the number of people in combat. You can take your action for the round whenever you have time, but I will resolve actions in order of initiative. If someone ahead of you in initiative order does something that would make you want to change your action, you can edit your post to include a different action up until you're up in order. If this doesn't work well or causes issues, we can try something different for the future. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-02-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:28:42-07:00","id":979041,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: LBBBBBO (-2)<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Fear Aura -2]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Resolve 3 + Composure 4 + Gnosis 1 - 2 (Wounds) = 6 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441242\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Binder is first confused at the approach of the strangers, then relieved and worried when Pheonix reappears, then terrified as the huge <i>thing</i> rips its way into reality.<br /> <br /> He'd been scared when he summoned the demon, but the demon was <i>true</i>. It was <i>right</i>. This thing, this &quot;gulmoth&quot; is wrong in a way he can't explain. A wrongness he feels deep in his being.<br /> <br /> Binder steps back, on the edge of flight. <i>This is too much... I-I can't-</i>. Weakly, almost unconciously, he waves his knife in a pattern at his side.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Mind over Matter (Mind 2)<br /> Reach: 2 Free; Spending for instant speed and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Yantras: Knife (reflexive)<br /> Factors: Potency 3, Duration Scene<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 + 1 (Yantra) - 2 (wounds) - 2 (fear) = 1 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441244\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>It's no use...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:56:20-07:00","id":979124,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><b>RAGNAR</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: Exceptional Luck<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Emotional Aura (-2 all rolls while within 5 yards of Gulmoth)<br /> Health: BOOOOOOO I WP: 1/4 I Mana: 8/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ragnar freezes for a moment as the creature roars. He feels his body start to seize up with fear.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Resolve 2 + Composure 2 + Gnosis 1= 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441253\" target=\"_blank\">4 successs</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He manages to work through the fear, but he's shaken.<br /> <br /> He hears Mathias' words, but he can't even begin to think of attacking that <i>thing. </i>His eyes fall on the young, tanned man standing with the staff who came through the portal. Legs feeling like jelly, and his chest throbbing as if he had been tackled by a linebacker, he rushes to the other man's side and places a hand on his shoulder. With all his might, he wills the threads of Fate to coalesce around him. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Don't panic, I'm helping.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar casts his Exceptional Luck Praxis on Phoenix, and boosts it to Potency 2. He takes a -2 to his role to boost Duration to 2 rounds. Gnosis 1 + Fate 2 + Willpower 3 + Concentration 2 - Potency 2 - Emotional Aura 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441257\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. He spends his free Reach to make it Instant Casting, and gives Phoenix a +1 to a Brawl role, and also gives him the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> Ragnar now has 0 Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sensing the spell has succeeded, he manages a tight smile. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Now take that staff and <i>hit </i>the sonofabitch&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:27:25-07:00","id":979144,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Abyssal Backlash (+6 Paradox), [Fear Aura -2]<br /> Health: LLB</b>OOO<b> | Willpower: 1/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair, Hakim died like a week ago, so it's not a huge surprise to feel that exhausting wave of <i>i can't do this </i>washing over him again as he fades into consciousness.<br /> <br /> What <i>is </i>a surprise is the fact that he doesn't have a body right now. He's just ink. <i>Wh- how...?</i><br /> <br /> <i>His cloak. Right. Still keeping me safe.</i><br /> <br /> Phoenix is here. He opens his Mind Sight to confirm that the Obrimos is alive and conscious. Oh, and there are other minds here too. Is Binder here? Did Binder make it into the portal? What happened in there, exactly?<br /> <br /> He turns his awareness upward. Oh, look, it's the nightmare beast that he brought into the waking world.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Activating Mind/Space Sight.<br /> <br /> Resolve 4 + Composure 4 + Gnosis 1 - Divergent 2, 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441249\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes,</a> nope.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There isn't the context to put all the pieces together. But he remembers the mocking laughter he's heard since the train stopped, the stinging black hail, the feeling of soul corruption and magic gone horribly wrong. And especially what he saw in his mirror when the Paradox went off, all his worst moments, fragments of shattered Time. There was a certain intelligence behind it all. And this creature had a kind of intelligence, in its way.<br /> <br /> He's transfixed on the burning light and shadow around the entity. Someone says &quot;Gulmoth.&quot; He knows that word. <i>Gulmoth.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intelligence 1 + Occult 4 - Fear 2, 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441250\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A physical being from the Abyss. See also: Acamoth. Relevant Arcanum: Spirit(?). Moonstone is fairly sure that he's <i>fought </i>a Gulmoth by his masters' sides before, although it's difficult to keep the whole awful bestiary straight right now.<br /> <br /> And this one is his. His Gulmoth, his Paradox. He needs revelation, some kind of closure. He needs to face the thing before this whole nightmare warhellride spirals completely out of control.<br /> <br /> Still an inky shadow on the ground, one of the many anonymous twisted shadows in this particular street, he reaches out across the gap between them with his Mind.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Moonstone is going to briefly attempt to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hxC3ILPiz98\" target=\"_blank\">make direct mental contact with the Gulmoth,</a> and whatever that entails. Running and screaming and treating it like a random encounter isn't going to solve anything, he needs to take some sort of ownership and face his terror and get some answers, despite the risks and the unknowns. Hoping this fulfills my Vice of Naive.<br /> <br /> The effect I'm looking for is like Mind 2 &quot;Telepathy,&quot; where we can both read surface thoughts and potentially send coherent messages. 1 Reach spent on Instant cast, 1 Reach spent on sensory range. Paradox is 7 dice, going to contain it: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441556\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a><br /> Wisdom 7: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441560\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes.</a> Does this count as &quot;fully containing a Paradox&quot; for purposes of resolving the Abyssal Backlash?<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Mind 2 + Concentration 2 + Willpower 3, 8 dice. Base Potency is 2, raising that to Potency 4 is -4 dice. And another -2 from the fear aura. 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441260\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's a link. Moonstone feels like he's touching a corpse, and it just moved. His thoughts spill across the void:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><i>(don'tgocrazydon'tgocrazydon'tgocrazy)</i></span><br /> <b><u>You.</u> I've seen you.</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(don't go crazy - this can't be happening - am i really doing this?)</i></span><br /> <b>Are you the same one that has been following me all day? Laughing at me?</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(where did this thing come from - please aion don't let other people die because of me)</i></span><br /> <b>Did you show me those things in the mirror before?</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>(i'm scared that you're going to erase the whole world and stick me in a pocket where today is the only day that exists and you kill me one billion times (1,000,000x) and i'm responsible for ruining the whole world and everyone knows-)</i></span><br /> <b>Do you have a name?</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><i>(i'm so thirsty - should've brought water - not the time)</i></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:30:54-07:00","id":979236,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Heightened Senses (Life 2; Potency 1, 1 week duration: +1 to Perception rolls); Body Control (Life 2; Potency 2, 1 week duration);<br /> Willpower: 2/5. Mana: 7/10</b><br /> <b>Conditions/Tilts: Inspired</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441298\" target=\"_blank\">Resistance roll versus Gulmoth's Emotional Aura \u2192 4 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Stille...v\u00e6r stille... ((Quiet...be quiet...))</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx feels the eyes upon him - the eyes of the predator, the chill of being hunted - only ... <i>wrong.</i> Cruel. He stands frozen in place as his senses catch up to him, the eldritch creature's scream rippling through his mind...<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Focus... </span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\">For faen!<i> What can I do!? I don't know how to fight, but... but...</i></span><br /> <br /> His vision image tightens as he sees the young man wounded on the ground, watching as Ragnar helps the man up. He glances at the... <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Gulmoth, Mathias called it.</span></i> .. and with a growl in his throat, he rushes over to the both of them. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar! And... guy who's hurt! Hello! Really not the time to... to talk. I don't think we should stand next to this thing.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx will wait and see if either of them will follow him out of the ominous aura.</b></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:48:27-07:00","id":979273,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> Forces | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> Kinetic Blow [Potency 2, Scene-long]<br /> <b>Health:</b> LLLL<b>B</b>BB | <b>WP:</b> 3/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Steadfast (Resolves at end of post) | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pain. Lots and lots of pain. Where the hell did it come from?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441319\" target=\"_blank\">Resolve 3 + Composure 2 + Gnosis 1 - 3 Woundsl = 3 dice \u2192 2 successes</a> <b>NEWP!</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That roar, that...thing, the Gulmoth. That horrifying freak that should not exist. It almost killed me. It was about to kill me. I have to run, get away. Don't think, just run.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Moves just outside the radius, then stops, so it's just the move part of the action, it's not a double move.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wait a minute...Why was I ru-? I swirl around. Oh, you've gotta be kidding me! Son of a bitch. You're gonna pay for that. Eyeing the staff, I smirk at the idea that just popped into my head. First thing's first, gotta don some armor before a battle.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Forces armor again</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just when I was about to cast my spell, this random dude comes up to me.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Don't panic, I'm helping.&quot;</span> he says as I instinctively jolted. Was that magic I just felt? Another mage. I don't know why, but I feel like I was going to meet other mages. Maybe he's one of 'em. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Now hit the sonofabitch.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;One step ahead of you,&quot;</span> I chuckle, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Just distract it for a bit, I've got an idea.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><s>Phoenix is going to cast Kinetic Blow (Forces 2, p.143) but he's using two Yantras (Concentration and Dedicated Tool to reduce the Paradox dice) so it'll take a turn to prepare, then a turn to cast, then attacks by the third turn.</s><br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Considering the Duration of Exceptional Luck, Phoenix'll cast Kinetic Blow right now.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Kinetic Blow (Forces 2, p.143 Corebook)</u></b><br /> <b>Reach:</b> 1 free; 3 used for instant casting, switching PSF, and Advanced Duration<br /> <b>Paradox:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441788\" target=\"_blank\">Overreach 2 - 2 Dedicated Tool = Chance die \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <b>Containment:</b> None.<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Dedicated Tool to reduce Paradox<br /> <b>Factors:</b> PSF Potency to 2<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441789\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Forces 2 + 3 WP - 3 Wounds = 3 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Dammit. Would've liked to have saved Steadfast just in case, but I'll need to resolve it now. Phoenix's Brawl attacks do 2L now.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-02-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T04:26:13-07:00","id":980189,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> You feel your magic surge through your veins and muscles, and you feel ready to inflict some hurt. Time to put those martial arts skills to the test on this foul creature. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your unarmed attacks currently count as +2L weapons. The bonus damage adds after a successful hit and will stack with Grave Misfortune.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You've heard of these creatures, and your knowledge is true. They are like twisted reflections of spirits, prone to the same strengths - and weaknesses. This one is Manifested, drawing on Resonance in the area to make itself present in a powerful way here in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> You stare into this creature's mind and attempt to make contact. It makes sense to you that the only way to defeat such a creature is to first understand it, so you try to understand the patterns and thoughts passing through its mind. <br /> <br /> The problem, you instantly realize, is that there <i>is</i> no pattern to this creature's mind that you can understand. You do see shattered fragments of images, emotions, and impulses. You see an otherworldly place of shadows and foul things you can't even put a name to. You do see it watching you from across the Abyss, waiting for a chance to take advantage of you. You form a name to describe its presence: Alux, the anti-light, the very physical impossibility of the destruction of light and creation of shadow. <br /> <br /> And then there's this Gulmoth's own emotions and urges: It wants to devour you, all mages, all worlds, until nothing but the Abyss exists. It craves mana and magic, and will target mages to exploit their weakness -- just as it used you to arrive here. The torrent of information threatens to overwhelm you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Roll Resolve + Composure, including -2 to the roll because of your Divergent condition. If you fail, you gain the Insane Tilt, which gives you +1 to combat rolls but makes you last in Initiative order and impacts your judgment.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Your feeble attempt at casting your spell in these conditions feeds into your fear. How could anything stop such a creature? You are keenly aware of your na\u00efvet\u00e9 when it comes to magic and the supernatural. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You wait on the edge of this creature's aura, trying to distance yourself far enough from it to think clearly. The others hear you but invest themselves in the fight, risking their lives to stop this creature.<br /> <br /> You feel pulses of energy all around you as the other mages cast spells, trying to draw on their Supernal connections to bring an end to this monster. You feel a primal desire in you to join them, but there's real fear there, too. <br /> <br /> One thing you do notice while you stand and watch with uncertainty: This creature reminds you of the spirits you saw earlier, in a twisted way. Somehow, this thing seems to be otherworldly in a way those spirits were. What that means and how you can use that knowledge, you have very little idea. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Gulmoth</b><br /> The Abyssal entity scans the room and sets its focus on Mathias, perceiving the strongest threat to come from him. It lifts its arms and points its talons at Mathias. Black bolts of energy explode from its arms, striking towards the mage in a barrage.<br /> <br /> Strangely, Mathias smirks and...takes a step to the side. He spins his body and somehow, impossibly, he simply moves where the blasts do not hit him. The Gulmoth, Alux, roars with fury. But as it does, you feel the unnatural aura of fear temporarily subside, as its energy was transferred to its attack. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alux uses its turn to Blast Mathias, who activates his Fate Armor (adds 4 to Defense and applies to firearm attacks such as this Blast).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441898\" target=\"_blank\">Blast</a>: 5d10 = <b>0</b> successes.<br /> <br /> Emotional Aura ends, as he uses another Numen.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mathias</b><br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Hurry, we must try to stop it now while its defenses are weaker!&quot;</span> Mathias yells. He spins the crystal rod in his hand and makes another slashing motion towards the Gulmoth. He yells with desperation, and you all feel another powerful pulse of energy on your Periphery. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Mathias will improvise a Fate spell to try and make it so that the creature is caught entirely off guard, losing its Defense for a number of attacks equal to Potency during the spell's duration. PSF is Potency, and I think this needs to be an Unraveling spell (Fate 4).<br /> <br /> <b>The Perfect Strike</b><br /> Yantra: Path Tool +1<br /> Reach: 1 free; 2 spent on instant casting and sensory range (so I can hit the damn thing)<br /> Factors: Potency 5, Duration 2 rounds<br /> <br /> Paradox: 2 (overreaching) + 1 (successive rolls in scene) = 3d10. Will attempt to contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441899\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox (3)</a> = <b>1</b> success, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441900\" target=\"_blank\">Wisdom</a> = 0 successes. Of course. <br /> <br /> Spell roll: Gnosis (3) + Fate (4) + Yantra (1) + WP (3) - Factors (4) = 7d10: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441901\" target=\"_blank\">The Perfect Strike</a>: <b>4</b> successes. The next 2 attacks against Alux over the next two rounds ignore his Defense. Mathias gains the Abyssal Nimbus condition as he fails to fully contain the Paradox.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Initiative</b><br /> Alux (20) -- Blast<br /> --&gt; Ragnar (17) -- Draw attention<br /> Mathias (16) -- The Perfect Strike<br /> Phoenix (13)<br /> Moonstone (12)<br /> Binder (12) -- Mind over Matter<br /> Lynx (12) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Updated initiative 10-02-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:31:23-07:00","id":980216,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><b>RAGNAR</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 8/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5<br /> </div> <br /> Suddenly, the sense of dread vanishes. Ragnar watches in shocked awe as Mathias dodges the gulmoth's attacks with the grace of a ballet dancer. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Ah man, he needs to teach me that.</i></span><br /> <br /> Then Phoenix's words spring to his mind, and Ragnar starts running. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Distract it. I think I can do that. </span></i>He starts running, trying to position himself so that the gulmoth is between him and Phoenix. He pulls his silver knife out if his backpack, and points it right at the gulmoth. Without the creature's aura affecting him, he raises his voice and shouts, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Hey, you bargain brand dementor! I'm over here!&quot;</span> <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200bThis might be the stupidest thing I've ever done. </span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar roles Presence and Expression to try and distract Alux. Presence 2 + Expression 3 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441907\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:01:32-07:00","id":980241,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: LBBBBBO (-0)<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Mind Over Matter Pot 3]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> The unnatural fear lessens, but Binder is still shaken by his incompetence in the face of such a foe.<br /> <br /> <i>The only way I can help is to get through this...</i><br /> <br /> As he begins casting, Binder realizes that the others might benefit from his spell as well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I feel kind of stupid doing basically the same thing again, but here we are.<br /> <br /> Casting Mind over Matter (Mind 2)<br /> Reach: 2 Free; spending for instant speed, advanced duration, sensory range, and advanced scale.<br /> Containing Paradox: 2 - 2 (dedicated tool) vs Wisdom 7 = 0 vs 7 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441915\" target=\"_blank\">0</a> vs <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441916\" target=\"_blank\">2</a> <br /> <br /> Yantras: Knife (reflexive, dedicated)<br /> Factors: Potency 3, Druation Scene, Scale 5 Subjects (Binder, Pheonix, Moonstone, Ragnar, Lynx)<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 - 2 (wounds) = 2 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441917\" target=\"_blank\">1 success!!!</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Binder feels the spell settle over him like a shroud, blunting the worst of his pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:23:11-07:00","id":980352,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> The Gulmoth turns to look at you -- that is to say, the upper half of its torso twists to position its face towards you, but the rest of its shadowy form remains facing the rest of the group. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Be careful, son,&quot;</span> Mathias warns you, eyes flickering towards you as he slashes his crystal wand towards the Gulmoth and casts his spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your spell will succeed and take effect, but not until your turn in initiative. So it will help you this round, but not Phoenix until next round.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Initiative</b><br /> Alux (20) -- Blast<br /> Ragnar (17) -- Draw attention to himself<br /> Mathias (16) -- The Perfect Strike<br /> Phoenix (13) -- Attack<br /> Moonstone (12) -- Glory Days<br /> Binder (12) -- Mind over Matter<br /> Lynx (12) -- Knit </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-03-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:53:35-07:00","id":980364,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Active Spells: Telepathy<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active)<br /> Health: LLB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 1/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <i>Alux.</i><br /> <br /> Well, this experience is burning itself into the ol' long-term memory.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Resist Insanity, 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441944\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> on the very last die, barely made it. Also cancelling Telepathy.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He tries to tug himself away from the mental link, but it's painfully hard, like when your muscles lock up on a power line. Think of something else: something, anything to fill the empty void. Memories of camaraderie with the Knights of Alhambra, learning to fight under Ghost Dog, dreaming of being useful to the masters as a warrior if he couldn't be a sorcerer...<br /> <br /> <i>Focus! That's you! Not a mess- not a wreck- not crazy- not corrupted! You're better than this! You've fought monsters, you can fight them again!</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting the Merit-gaining spell we talked about in the OOC thread. Mind 2 Ruling, primary factor Potency. I gain [Potency] Merit dots in a single Merit, and can use them for [Potency] actions during the spell's Duration. Merits have to be things the subject might plausibly have had experience with. +1 Reach to let me spend Potency on a second Merit.<br /> <br /> 1 Reach for Instant, +1 for Scene duration, +1 to access 2 Merits. Containing any Paradox. 2 Paradox dice, +1 for risking Paradox this scene, 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441955\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2, Willpower 3, +Potency -2, 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441959\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> and I'm at 0 Willpower.<br /> <br /> So this is Potency 3 and lasts for up to a scene. I can make 3 rolls that benefit from my new Merits in that time. I'm taking Quick Draw (Weaponry) 1 and Fighting Style: Light Weapons 2. This will let me pick up/draw a weapon reflexively, and sacrifice points of Defense 1:1 for bonus dice on an attack roll if I haven't used Defense yet that turn.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A human shape rises up out of the bubbling shadows, congealing into a young-looking Vietnamese dude with gloved hands and a messenger bag and a ballcap and a leather jacket over what appears to be an ink-black hoodie. He grabs the runic staff on the way up, tests the balance, turns it over in his right hand, and he's in the ready position by the time he solidifies. He's aware of the other Minds in this Space at this Time, but he's focused on the weapon and the enemy. Feels right.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Shadow Flesh ends, Moonstone is solid again. Reflexively picking up the staff and wielding it as a one-handed weapon. I have Initiative 11 and Defense 9 next turn, or Defense 10 if Alux counts as &quot;unarmed or wielding weapons of Size 1.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-02-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:41:49-07:00","id":980385,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Heightened Senses (Life 2; Potency 1, 1 week duration: +1 to Perception rolls) (Ends this post); Body Control (Life 2; Potency 2, 1 week duration) (Ends this post);<br /> Willpower: 1/5. Mana: 7/10</b><br /> <b>Conditions/Tilts: Inspired</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah... the fear is gone! Good!</span></i><br /> <br /> As fear fades, Lynx glances at the spectacle and his would-be allies, before his focus returns to Ragnar and the other man. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Okay, first things first. I need to take care of that man's wounds.</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx sees it in his mind, the Primal Wild surging through the man's flesh, sealing the wounds, leaving him whole... yet as he brings it to reality, he feels the lingering chill in his soul, already burdened with the Wild.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">No, not like that. Too dangerous... Is it my other spells? Yeah, that feels right.</span></i><br /> <br /> He lets go of the spells that surround his soul, brushing them away into non-existence. His breath returns to normal, and his senses are blunted, much to his frustration. He clenches his fists as he clutches his necklace with his left hand; with his right, he weaves the Wild into the man's body.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I call the wild! O' Great Bear,</span>&quot; Lynx says instinctively as the spell shapes, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I ask of you: please! Heal him!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> The Wild surges through him, his shadow momentarily turning into a bear: large, bristling, enveloping the area momentarily with a display of endurance, and full of fury, primal anger directed towards the twisted and malevolent entity.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar and... and guy! I've got your backs, but be careful!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx cancels his Body Control and Heightened Senses spells. This reduces Ragnar and Lynx's Initiative by 2. <br /> <br /> He then attempts to cast Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; on Phoenix as an instant action through Sensory range, Reaching to heal Lethal damage, and gains 2 successes, healing Phoenix for 3 Lethal Damage.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Phoenix<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice)<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot;: Life (3) + Gnosis (1) + Willpower (3)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 1 Free Reach: 1 spent on Instant Cast. 2 Extra Reaches for Sensory Range (1 reach) and for Knit to heal 1 Lethal per Potency rather than 2 Bashing (1 reach).<br /> <br /> <b>Base Paradox Dice pool:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Paradox modifiers:</b> -2 from Dedicated Tool.<br /> <b>Final Paradox Dice pool:</b> 0. <br /> If Paradox is obtained, Lynx will release it. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441967\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Paradox \u2192 0 successes.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/441968\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; \u2192 2 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:20:52-07:00","id":980487,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> Forces | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> Kinetic Blow [Potency 2, Scene-long]<br /> <b>Health:</b> L<b>B</b>BBOOO | <b>WP:</b> 2/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> Payback time, bitch. I charge straight towards the &quot;bargain brand dementor&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Closes in on Alux and makes a Brawl attack<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442021\" target=\"_blank\">Strength 3 + Brawl 4 + 3 WP + 1 Exceptional Luck - 3 Wounds = 8 dice \u2192 <b>5 successes MOTHAFUCKA!!!</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/390C1meyxRU?t=1m16s\" target=\"_blank\"><b>FALCON PAAAUNCH!!!</b></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I open with fist straight to the gut, utilize the head's downward momentum to guide the jaw right into a rising knee, then thrust the foot right into its wide open chest. Normally, a combo like that would leave someone on the ground and not being able to speak properly for at least a week. However, nothing about this situation was normal. With my spell, that attack would mince a normal human into Ragu pasta sauce. This thing? Haven't a clue, but it certainly seems like I hurt the fucker something fierce.<br /> <br /> And there goes quite a bit of blood as I pant from the exhaustion. Or there would be, if my wounds didn't suddenly seal up. Wait...why are my wounds sealing up?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perception to notice Lynx healing Phoenix<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442033\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Composure 2 = 5 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Looks like you did a thankless job, Lynx</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Y'know what? Doesn't matter. I need to focus on dealing with this thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-02-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:39:04-07:00","id":980766,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> Your attack is an example of perfection.<br /> <br /> You know from the moment you throw your first punch that you have the <i>perfect </i>angle of attack. The creature has swiveled away to face the young man drawing attention to himself, looking away from you for the first time since you came out of the portal, at precisely the moment you moved forward. Your arm moves with supernatural speed and force, colliding with the creature's physical form with a force that could kill a normal man with a single blow. Somehow, the creature shifts at the worst possible time, twisting its form in such a way that you land your blows <i>exactly</i> where you wanted to. The Gulmoth screams, letting out another angry roar that makes the air tremble and causes flashes of light to explode around it.<br /> <br /> But this creature is not a normal man -- there's nothing normal about it at all. You see a large crack extending across its torso, and tendrils of dark energy seem to be leaking out from its surface. But It doesn't seem very fazed; in fact, you watch as the shadows swirl around the creature's body and the large crack already begins to reform. You have the sense that this thing has natural resistance to physical harm.<br /> <br /> Although you don't know where it comes from, you feel two separate pulses of energy on your Periphery. Your wounds start to knit themselves back together, causing instant relief of the pain you were feeling from your most grievous wounds that adrenaline was holding at bay. You also feel a sense of peace in your mind that gives you clarity through the remaining pain. You feel as if you're uninjured, even though you know you still are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think the bonus from Exceptional Luck will wear off this turn, but there is one more use of Grave Misfortune and The Perfect Strike active on the Gulmoth, so the next successful attack by any character will ignore Defense and apply an extra 2 damage. You also temporarily ignore wound penalties due to Binder's spell.<br /> <br /> You also gain a beneficial Condition of your choice (e.g., Steadfast, Inspired) for the exceptional success on your Brawl roll. Go ahead and pick one, and then put it in your header on your next post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You very narrowly manage to rip yourself away from the mental connection, clearing your mind as best as possible. Now that it's easier for you to focus, you spring into action and return to your human form. The staff feels warm to the touch.<br /> <br /> Through your Active Sight, you see spells springing into shape around you. Many of the spells include Arcana that you don't know, but you know enough about Supernal magic to make some logical guesses. The young, bear-like man casts something that knits Phoenix's wounds back together. Binder casts a Mind spell that settles on all of you, and it provides a blanket over your physical distress that suggests it will block pain reception.<br /> <br /> Phoenix strikes the creature <i>hard</i>, with a force that could kill a man. But you remember from your lessons with Hakim and his cabal that Gulmoth, like spirits, are resistant to physical damage when they take on a physical form in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can see the spells being cast, but don't forget that any rolls unrelated to using/perceiving magic (including Weaponry) are at -2.<br /> <br /> You get +1 Defense against this creature using the staff. However, why is your Defense 9? I see you have a base Defense of 6, so that would make it 7 with the staff. Are you using some kind of Mage Armor?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You watch with a surge of pleasure as your spell takes hold, wrapping up around the athletic man and knitting his wounds back together. The largest lacerations and open cuts simply vanish as his skin reforms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alux</b><br /> The Gulmoth spins around, staring at each of you with a look of calculated fury. It settles its gaze on Ragnar and raises its arms, shrieking with an alien voice that sends chills up your spine. Each of you feels a powerful pulse of energy on your Periphery.<br /> <br /> Thick, inky-black spears of energy explode out, thicker than you have previously seen. They <i>shred</i> into Ragnar's body, inflicting massive damage. Large gashes create sprays of blood, which falls on each of you nearby. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;<i>Noooo!</i>&quot;</span> Mathias screams in horror. Ragnar looks to be on the cusp of passing out; you're not sure how he's still standing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alux spends 6 Essence and a WP to use its Blast Numen on Ragnar, making it a +3L firearm attack. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442176\" target=\"_blank\">Blast (14) + WP (3)</a> = <b>4</b> successes, resulting in <b>7 lethal damage</b>. You are welcome to activate Fate Armor and/or Dodge, but per our rolling convention, unfortunately all of the successes came at the start of the roll, so even Dodging won't change the damage you take. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Fortunately you benefit from Binder's spell, so you temporarily ignore wound penalties.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mathias</b><br /> The older mage grits his teeth and looks to Phoenix and Moonstone. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;We need to take this thing out, now! If we hit it hard enough, it will either discorporate or flee,&quot;</span> he quickly explains. He waves his crystal wand and yells, creating another powerful burst of energy on your Periphery.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mathias will attempt to cast another Fate spell to help, using his Praxis Superlative Luck.<br /> <br /> <b>Superlative Luck </b>(p. 137)<br /> Yantra: Path tool<br /> Reach: 2 free; spending 2 on instant casting and sensory range<br /> Scale: 2 subjects<br /> Potency: 2<br /> Duration: 5 rounds<br /> <br /> No Paradox roll. Spellcasting: Gnosis (3) + Fate (4) + Yantra (1) + WP (3) - Factors (4) = 7d10: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442187\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a> (bummer, no exceptional success). Phoenix and Moonstone each gain 2 uses of rote quality rolls on mundane actions in the next 5 rounds. Specify in advance which rolls you want to apply the rote quality to.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to get the syntax correct on Orokos, unfortunately. So roll normally, look at the results, and roll a second time (also giving URL link here) for any number of dice that come up as 7 or lower on the original roll, then add the successes together. If someone else gets the syntax to work so it's simpler, let me know!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Initiative</b><br /> Alux (20) -- Blast<br /> Mathias (16) -- Superlative Luck<br /> --&gt; Ragnar (15)<br /> Phoenix (13)<br /> Binder (12)<br /> Moonstone (11)<br /> Lynx (10) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:10:24-07:00","id":980857,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: LLLLOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 8/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5</div> <div align=\"left\">Ragnar's not sure how it happened. One second, he watches as the muscular young man unleashes a devastating flurry of blows on the gulmoth. His eyes flicker over to the form of a fine-featured Vietnamese man rising from a patch of shadow he has ignored up until that very moment. Then he's suddenly, painfully aware of his heart pounding in his chest from adrenaline and exertion as Lynx dismisses his spell. Then the gulmoth turns back to face him with a blood-curdling shriek, and the bottom of his stomach seems to fall out. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Ah, shit.</span> </i>The thing raises its arms, and tendrils of blackness shoot at him like striking snakes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar attempts to Dodge the incoming attack. He reflexively invokes Fate Mage Armor, spending a point of Mana to do so. (Defense 4 x 2) + (Fate Mage Armor 2 x 2) -&gt; 12 dice = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442243\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. So I think that leaves 1 success from the roll, and the +3L from the Essence makes that 4. So 4 Lethal in total. Still stings, but not as bad as it was. Let me know if I'm wrong on that.<br /> <br /> Ragnar now has Fate Mage Armor active for the rest of the scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the spare few moments he has before the tendrils reach him, he reaches for something deep inside of himself, beyond even the now-depleted strength of his own will, and weaves the threads of Fate around himself, allowing them to pull him away from the tendrils as they will.<br /> <br /> He spins away from one, stops just short of moving into the path of another, and then jukes his torso away from the other. Unfortunately, that seems to be the extent of what Fate can do for him, as the remainder slice and stab him. He gasps and cries out at the pain of it, but he seems to be okay for the time being. If not for Fate, the damage would have been much worse.<br /> <br /> He looks at the gulmoth with a new sense of caution, but he can't help but offer another insult. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Touchy bastard, ain't cha,&quot; </span>he growls at it. All the same, he retreats back towards the others, never taking his eyes of the thing. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Last time I do that,&quot; </span>he says to Mathias.</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-03-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:25:43-07:00","id":981124,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> Forces | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> Kinetic Blow [Potency 2, Scene-long]<br /> <b>Health:</b> L<b>B</b>BBOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Steadfast | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Taking Steadfast from the previous exceptional success</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;We need to take this thing out, now!&quot;</span> one of the mages shouts. Don't need to tell me twice. Let's see if I can break its legs.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Targeted attack to the leg, using Focused Attack (from Martial Arts Merit) to reduce the penalty to -1.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442318\" target=\"_blank\">Strength 3 + Brawl 4 + 3 WP - 1 Targeted Attack (Leg) w/ Rote quality = 9 dice \u2192 5 successes</a><br /> <br /> When Alux gets back to the Abyss, he's gonna be saying &quot;I used to be a powerful Abyssal like you, but then I took a mage's perfectly-placed foot to the knee.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I land right in the thing's outstretched knee with a kick that would cleave a human's leg in half. Then I follow it up with an uppercut straight to the jaw to sit him down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-03-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:58:52-07:00","id":981226,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> You pull Fate around you like a shield, and dance your way through part of the attacks. It's not as graceful or as successful as Mathias was, but you can tell that it made a powerful difference. Mathias practically sighs in relief, and offers a quick smile to you. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Just be smart and try not to egg it on too much, ok?&quot;</span> he suggests. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Your fists explode into the Gulmoth with extraordinary precision and force. Once again, you feel like you could take on the world; the creature tries to squirm away but accidentally moves into your follow-up blows. <br /> <br /> This time, the strike causes the crack in the Guomoth's body to burst open. Light touching its skin is absorbed into the wound, creating a dark halo of energy around the creature. It growls again, but this time its tone sounds...a touch concerned?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You deal a total of 9 more damage due to Grave Misfortune and Kinetic Blow, both of which wear off now. You also use up the last benefit of The Perfect Strike, so Alux gets its Defense back (6) on other attacks. You still get one more rote action roll over the next few rolls of desired. Attaching in the knees does not appear to have any observable effect with that roll. <br /> <br /> Gain another beneficial condition for the exceptional success. Can't be Steadfast though, you already have it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Initiative</b><br /> Alux (20) -- Blast<br /> Mathias (16) -- Superlative Luck<br /> Ragnar (15) -- Dodge<br /> Phoenix (13) -- Brawl attack<br /> --&gt; Binder (12)<br /> Moonstone (11)<br /> Lynx (10) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-03-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:47:37-07:00","id":981245,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: LLBBBBB (-0)<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Mind Over Matter Pot 3]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> Binder watches in awe as Pheonix lands blow after blow on the monster, but not entirely sure who is specifically responsible. <i>He's landing the hits, but the older man did something... Either way, it suddenly seems like we can win this!</i><br /> <br /> He confidently raises his knife and slashes out an attack on the monster's mind.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Casting Psychic Assault (Mind 3)<br /> Reach: 1 Free; spending for instant speed, sensory range, and casting over spell control.<br /> Containing Paradox: 2 + 1 (prior risk) - 2 (dedicated tool) vs Wisdom 7 = 1 vs 7 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442413\" target=\"_blank\">2</a> vs <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442415\" target=\"_blank\">2</a> <br /> <br /> Wow. Just wow.<br /> <br /> Yantras: Knife (reflexive, dedicated)<br /> Factors: Potency 3<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 = 4 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442418\" target=\"_blank\">1 success!</a> <br /> <br /> I get the spell off, at least!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T22:46:43-07:00","id":981282,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Spells: None<br /> Mage Armor: Time 2 | Conditions: Divergent (Active)<br /> Health: LLB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> Moonstone hears and feels the magic firing around him, Supernal symbols shining like fireworks. A Fate working to briefly create heroes settles onto him and Phoenix. A dull gleam of Fated unimportance and weakness surrounds Alux- Supernal magic is so hesitant around the Gulmoth, like a floating leaf protected from the depths by surface tension alone- and shuts out the futures where it blocked his blows effectively, vanishing as soon as the hex serves its narrative purpose. A crack in the hungry darkness grows wider. Binder forms a knife of his Mind and twists it in the wound. The corrupt anti-symbols that make up the Gulmoth groan and sputter.<br /> <br /> This particular moment belongs to him. He closes his third eye and retreats from Pandemonium to the Fallen World alone. Everything he needs to see is right ahead of him. The second Phoenix weaves away after his god-killing uppercut, Moonstone grips his weapon in his right hand and shouts a well-known Adamantine Arrow <i>kiai</i>: <i><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Arrows, point the way!&quot;</span></b></i><br /> <br /> Then he drops his guard, runs ahead, crouches like a coiled spring, and lunges up and drives the staff deep, deep, <i>deep</i> into the crack in Alux.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First: reflexively ending Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Second: sacrificing my entire Defense 10 this turn for +10 dice on my attack, as per Fighting Style: Light Weapons 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD 63</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thrust (\u2022\u2022): Your character knows when to defend himself,<br /> and when to move in for the kill. At any time, you can<br /> sacrifice points of Defense one-for-one to add to attack pools.<br /> This cannot happen if you\u2019ve already used Defense in the<br /> same turn. If you use this maneuver, you may not sacrifice<br /> your full Defense for any other reason. For example, you<br /> cannot use Thrust with an all-out attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third: attack roll. Strength 3 + Weaponry 4 + Thrust 10 - Defense 6, 11 dice with rote quality from Mathias and 9-again for Profession Skill: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442330\" target=\"_blank\">10 successes.</a> And the staff has +1 damage. Hopefully that tags it with some Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Fourth: I'd like to apply this Condition to myself, if possible. If not, I'll take Inspired with the same focus of boasting about his prowess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fabled</b><br /> Your character has performed an impressive feat in battle, and it makes for a great story. When your character speaks of their action to a receptive audience, you may resolve this Condition. This grants +5 to one Social roll and restores a point of Willpower. </div> </div> </div>Fifth: when the next turn starts, Moonstone regains full Defense (10) and reflexively reactivates Mind and Space Sight.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:24:42-07:00","id":981505,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> You reach out with your blade and assault the Gulmoth's &quot;mind,&quot; if that's what you can call it. The creature roars as your spell digs painfully deep into its consciousness, but in the act of casting your spell, the Lie weighs heavily on your body. You manage to contain the pressure of the Abyss threatening to leak out again, but in doing so feel another sharp spike of pain.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You need to make the Stamina roll on the same turn. It's a moot point in terms of the fight (see below), but go ahead and roll now.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You grip the staff tightly in your hands as you leap through the air at the Gulmoth. At your shout, Mathias' head snaps towards you with a startled expression, but your focus is all about Alux.<br /> <br /> Your blow strikes true, finding its mark at the heart of the Gulmoth. Alux <i>screams</i> in pain. Before your attack, it had clearly begun to grow hesitant, but the creature must have sorely underestimated your group. Alux's body <i>explodes </i>outward in a shower of sparks and a boom like thunder. The force of the explosion knocks you off your feet, and the staff clatters to the ground beside you. When you blink and look up, you see dark clouds in a sphere before you, which quickly dissipates like fog under a hot sun.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll allow the Condition, sure. Gaining a WP on resolution of a beneficial Condition is a little atypical from what I see in the core book, but you can get it from Inspired, and it's not game breaking by any means. Unless this is from a specific book or Mage 2E reference I haven't seen?<br /> <br /> One question for anyone here...I thought you couldn't apply both 9-again and Rote Action permutations to the same dice pool? Based on the description of how dice tricks apply to Paradox rolls for presence of Sleepers, I thought it went 10-again (standard) --&gt; 9-again --&gt; 8-again --&gt; Rote action.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> Mathias leans against the wall with a ragged sigh of relief. For a moment, he says nothing. His gaze lingers on Moonstone, but he turns to the rest of you with a broad smile. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Well done, all of you,&quot;</span> he says warmly. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Well done.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We're out of initiative now. Combat is over. You all gain 1 Beat for your success at confronting and defeating a powerful enemy, and learning more about yourselves and each other in the process.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-04-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:11:53-07:00","id":981596,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LLBB</b>BBB (-0)<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Mind Over Matter Pot 3] [Unconcious]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Stamina 2 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442530\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Marlin responds to Mathias by unceremoniously toppling over onto the pavement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 10-04-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:34:10-07:00","id":981612,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Spells: None<br /> Mage Armor: Time 2 | Conditions: Divergent (Active)<br /> Health: LLB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I checked the dice rules on 214 and I think you're right and I was mistaken about rote and 9-again. Rote action specifies that &quot;you may only re-roll each die once,&quot; which would preclude getting 9-again on any new dice that came up. And several other effects build in the 9-again to 8-again to rote action way. If you removed the successes I got from 9-again on that roll, I would have 8 successes instead of 10 if it matters. I'll avoid that in the future!<br /> <br /> I built Fabled from the custom Condition guidelines on 289. It's basically Inspired except it gives a dice bonus instead of exceptional success on 3 successes.<br /> <br /> Also, canceling my Glory Days spell now that we're out of battle. The Merits disappear back into the fog of happy memory.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He's been knocked on his ass and disarmed by the Gulmoth's ontological collapse. Adrenalin fades within about five seconds, all of his elation jarred loose by the breathtaking <i>thud</i> of the impact and the end of battle and glory. At least his bag is safe.<br /> <br /> Moonstone wants to jump back to his feet, dust himself off, laugh and shout and smile and hug Phoenix tight and not let go (<span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;we did it! i knew we could!&quot;</span>), and help Binder back up (<span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;i'm so glad you're okay!&quot;</span>), and thank his new friends and ask all their names and take a bow and make a wonderful first impression. Any second now, he'll get up and make it happen and everything will be great.<br /> <br /> He doesn't. Thanks, BPD. He lays on his back on the cold, uncomfortable pavement and looks up at the dark clouds fading away in Mage Sight. The older Fate mage looks at him and says something Moonstone pays no attention to. He turns over and draws his mirror out of his bag, not significantly more cracked than before, holds it up above him and gazes into it. He's looking into his own future. It's like haruspicy with the fading ephemeral entrails of the Gulmoth.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#008080\">Will I encounter Alux again within the next month?<br /> <br /> Will learning that I summoned Alux (through my own stupidity, worthlessness, naivete, total lack of wisdom or merit, etc etc) make the other mages around me right now hate me?</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Don't cast spells under the influence, kids. Casting my Praxis, Divination. Gnosis 1, Time 2, Path Tool 1, and I'd like to use a +1 Environment yantra for casting a spell about Alux at the site of a victory over that entity. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for detailed responses. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442545\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>, let's make that a dramatic failure as long as Moonstone is crashing hard. Don't draw on the Abyss for Environment yantras, either!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:22:39-07:00","id":981723,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> L<b>B</b>BBOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Inspired | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ending the armor and spell.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Looks like Moonstone dealt the final blow. Appropriate, considering he summoned the damn thing in the first place. I sigh as I shed the armor and spell. He's on the concrete with that stupid little mirror of his. I think now's a good time for them words. At first, I was gonna deliver a fist to his face, but since he cleaned up the mess he made, I'm feeling generous. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hey buddy?&quot;</span> I smile sarcastically as I pull away the mirror, then I give him a good smack.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix slaps Moonstone. No damage, but I resolve Steadfast to guarantee success. It's more of a role-playing thing, anyways.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Don't ever do that again,&quot;</span> I demand, wiping away the smile for a dead serious look in his eyes.<br /> <br /> Now with that outta the way, I stand up and face the others. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I don't recall us introducing ourselves. My name's Phoenix, the man down there's Moonstone,&quot;</span> I point, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Thank you very much for helping us.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:21:24-07:00","id":981928,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: LLLLOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: (7-1)/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar walks over to the fallen man and kneels down beside him. He has no idea what's wrong with him. He seemed a little roughed up, but did he faint from nerves or injuries. His brows furrow as he considers the question before him, and whether he has the tools for the job. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Fate and Time won't do it. I need Life. </i></span>He has only touched Life once, when he opened himself to it it through his Sight. He reaches out for it again, using the same logic he did when he had used previously. Just as all things are bound to each other by the threads of fate, tugging on each other and altering the trajectory of their probabilities... all living things are connected to each other through trophic interactions, exchanging energy and chemicals through the endless cycle of life and regeneration. <br /> <br /> He places his hand on the man's chest. And he opens himself to magic, and turns his attention to Life, an art as fickle and mutable as Fate. He begins lightly drawing the flat of his knife over the man's body, tracing the path of his veins and arteries to and from his heart. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar attempts to cast Analyze Life (Life 1). He has one free Reach, and uses it to reduce casting time to Instant. He uses his knife as a Path Tool yantra. He pays one Mana for a common Arcana spell. <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Life 1+ Path Tool 1 = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442662\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it doesn't seem to work, and the spell eludes him. Ragnar shakes his head in frustration. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Lynx, wanna take a look at him for me? I tried myself, but I lost the spell.&quot; </span>He looks at the others: the younger man, Phoenix; and the Vietnamese man, Moonstone. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I'm Ragnar. The big guy over there is Lynx, and this guy here is Mathias.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:13:34-07:00","id":981995,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> Whatever nightmarish thing (or nothing) Moonstone sees while gazing slack-jawed into the future in his magic mirror, his reverie (and Mage Sight) breaks when Phoenix pulls the mirror away from his face.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hey buddy?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He shakes his head and confusedly meets Phoenix's smile, half sitting up, still distracted. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Huh? Oh! I'm so-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Hard surprise <i>smack</i> to the face<i>. </i>Deadly serious look. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Don't ever do that again.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone doesn't respond, just puts his hand on his stinging cheek and stares at Phoenix, deer-in-headlights style. He keeps forgetting that his delusions aren't the same as reality. He wasn't a comrade-in-arms to him just now; he almost got Phoenix and the others <i>killed </i>thanks to his utter incompetence...not that he remembers what actually triggered the Abyssal intrusion beyond the portal, only that it was unequivocally his own fault. He's been nothing but a burden. As always, he had it coming. It's like Hakim never left!<br /> <br /> That's the second Divination question answered, at least. Vivid fantasies well up in his mind about revenge and abandonment and violence, as is his mind's usual response to perceived betrayal on a low day, but they're just thoughts, just passing clouds. Remember the meditation. Close your eyes and count them and let them pass you by. Thoughts don't have to come true, even if you're a mage. He puts his mirror down and mumbles: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;uh- sorry. glad you made it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He rises to his feet while Phoenix makes introductions, dusts himself off, picks up the staff again and rests on it. He's real quiet, but waves a little at Ragnar. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Well-met by daylight, proud Ragnar. You three were a godsend.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He points the staff at Phoenix and wearily explains: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Nameless.&quot;</span> Points to the unconscious Mr. Marlin Matheson. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Nameless.&quot;</span> Points his own thumb at himself. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Arrow.&quot;</span> Gestures out at Ragnar, Lynx and Mathias. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Did you also get caught in the Highstorm?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rolling Int 1 + Politics 3 (Chicago Consilium) in advance of the conversation. Does &quot;Fate mage named Mathias&quot; remind Moonstone of any trivia or rumors? 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442698\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-05-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:03:46-07:00","id":982004,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5. Mana: 7/10</b><br /> <b>Conditions/Tilts: Inspired</b></div> <br /> The dust settles. Metaphorically, at least. Lynx walks over to the man who collapsed - joined by Ragnar - and he watches his friend's Life magic simply not... work.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Lynx, wanna take a look at him for me? I tried myself, but I lost the spell.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He opens his senses to the Wild to assess the man, and lays his own hand on the man's heaving chest.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">O' great bear</span>,&quot; he repeats, though quieter than before, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I ask of you once more, please, heal him.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, his shadow becomes the bear, but this time without the brutal anger, or the instinctive hatred towards that Eldritch horrir. It is, like Lynx, calmer, more protective as the Wild permeates through Lynx's soul, and then pours into the man's flesh. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I think he'll be fine,</span>&quot; he tells Ragnar as he shifts into a sitting position. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'll take care of him. You're better at the talking to people stuff than I am. Are you awake?</span>&quot; He adds as he watches the man stir. When he hears the slap, he instinctively looks up to see the conversation unfold.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>He attempts to cast Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; on Binder as an instant action, delivering it through touch. He gains 1 success, healing Binder for 6 Bashing damage (though effectively only 3)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Binder<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice)<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot;: Life (3) + Gnosis (1)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 1 Free Reach: 1 spent on Instant Cast. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/442700\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; \u2192 1 success.</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:34:50-07:00","id":982172,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: LLLLOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 6/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar studies his injuries for a moment. They're painful and deep, but nothing life threatening. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Did you also get caught in the Highstorm?&quot; </span>Ragnar shakes his head. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Lynx and I and... another mage. We were in a class when the storm made the power go out. I saw some sort of portal out the window, and we decided to investigate. I used Time to see what would come of it, and I had a vision of Mathias here. After we went...&quot; </span>he looks into the middle distance, once more trying to remember what happened. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot; ... wherever it is that we went, Mathias was waiting for us. Then he led us to you three.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He looks at the others. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200b&quot;So can anybody tell me what the hell that thing was? And why did you call Phoenix 'Nameless'?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:39:39-07:00","id":982233,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LLBB</b>OOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Mind Over Matter Pot 3]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> <br /> Binder groans as he slowly comes to, and staggers to his feet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;So can anybody tell me what the hell that thing was? And why did you call Phoenix 'Nameless'?&quot;</span> Asks one of the strangers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;It wasn't the only one that came through, either. There was a smaller one a little while ago, but I was the only one on this side of the portal.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:38:41-07:00","id":982406,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;We were in a class when the storm made the power go out. I saw some sort of portal out the window, and we decided to investigate. I used Time to see what would come of it, and I had a vision of Mathias here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Likewise. Well- we were on a train. Phoenix and I went into the door as well, and I expected,&quot; </span><i>don't say Marlin, </i><span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;our companion to follow. But apparently he had his own trouble.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone heads over to Lynx and Marlin, and lays his hand on the big friendly Norwegian bear's shoulder. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you. Lynx, right? Moonstone. Um- I'm hurt, but not from battle. Would you mind taking a look at my Pattern? I'd be very grateful if you could heal the rest of us, but please don't exert yourself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He helps Marlin steady himself on his feet, laughs and breathes a sigh of relief. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Aion be praised, you're alright. I don't remember what happened in the portal, but I'm sure I was worried sick about you the whole time. Did my hair not work?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar speaks: <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;So can anybody tell me what the hell that thing was? And why did you call Phoenix 'Nameless'?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Marlin replies: <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;It wasn't the only one that came through, either. There was a smaller one a little while ago, but I was the only one on this side of the portal.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone blinks. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Wait, a smaller one? Did it escape? Do you have Sympathy to it? You should, if you were able to work magic on it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He responds to Ragnar over his shoulder. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Nameless? It's nothing insulting. He's just not with an Order yet. Are you two?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There's a harder question, too. He squeezes his fists from nervous tension, and fantasizes about donning the Cloak and melting into shadows again. Just thinking about it already hurts, after what he saw in the mirror. <i>Close your eyes, get through it.</i> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That was Alux. It's like...the Abyssal symbol of anti-light. I learned its name. Or named it, maybe. It's a Gulmoth, a kind of Abyssal spirit that can take physical form. It was watching me all day.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He steps away from Marlin and wraps his arms tight around himself, eyes still closed, speaking faster. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I don't remember what happened beyond the door, but I <i>know </i>I let it out. It manifested because of what I did. It <i>used </i>my soul to descend into the Fallen World. Alux- all these Gulmoth prey on weak,&quot;</span> <i>stupid, naive, unworthy, etc etc</i> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;mages like me who can't control their magic, and now it's looking for more magic and mages and Mana to defile and consume. It almost killed Phoenix and Ragnar! We hurt it for now, probably sent it into hibernation, but it's in our world now, it's just going to come back in a few weeks.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Deep breath, long sigh. He looks at Ragnar and half-smiles. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It's not my place to tell you all the Mysteries. You should ask your master.&quot;</span> He gestures to Mathias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T20:21:32-07:00","id":982530,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> You feebly attempt to cast another spell, thirsting for the knowledge about what the future holds for you in regards to Alux. But your spell fails, and if that wasn't enough, Phoenix's blunt words and actions magnify your feelings of guilt and shame.<br /> <br /> Now that the dust has settled and you have the luxury of time, you take a closer look at Mathias and draw on your existing knowledge of mage society. When you do, you realize that you actually might remember hearing about Mathias from Hakim. If you're remembering clearly, he's a popular and well-respected member of the Silver Ladder; not a Master yet, but definitely an Adept. You don't remember much about him except that he was in a cabal of five mages, one from each Pentacle Order.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for the dramatic failure. You gain the Guilty condition, which will stack with your Divergent condition for relevant social rolls that use Resolve or Composure.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Your spell fails you, but you feel like if you had more time you could make more sense of the Life Arcanum. You feel a rush of eager excitement at the possibility of learning more, of growing your magical abilities. It's a fleeting urge, but a strong one, strong enough to catch you off guard.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">FYI, this &quot;urge&quot; isn't a Condition or anything, just for roleplay flavor...Magic is really invigorating and something to Obsess over.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> With a slow, steady breath, you find inner peace and channel it into Binder. As before, instantly upon your spell taking hold, you see the man's bruises fade and ultimately vanish. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <b>*NEW SCENE*</b></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> While you have been talking, Mathias has stood quietly, leaning against the wall. He looks around at each of you and studies you, following the conversation intently but silently. You can tell, however, that his eyes linger the most on Moonstone; as the conversation continues, he begins to narrow his eyes and crosses his arms. He clenches his jaw when Moonstone calls himself an Arrow, and his eyes widen suddenly at the mention of another small Gulmoth that was here. But when Moonstone admits to summoning a Gulmoth and <i>naming</i> it that, for the first time since meeting him, you see red-hot anger on Mathias' face.<br /> <br /> For an older man, Mathias moves deceptively fast. He grabs Moonstone by the collar and slams him against the wall where the Highstorm portal had appeared not long ago. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You <i>fool!&quot;</i></span> he growls. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Do you have any idea what damage you have caused, what you have risked? It took <i>six</i> of us to defeat it, and several of you could have died in the process. And I don't need Fate to know the odds of that thing coming back -- it's a certainty,&quot;</span> Mathias spat. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;With luck, it can be found when it is still weak, but what if it runs loose in a shopping mall or a subway?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Anyone interested can roll Wits + Empathy to get a read on Mathias right now.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mathias lets Moonstone go roughly and takes a step back with a deep breath, very obviously trying to keep his anger in check. He looks over his shoulder and sees that a few people are starting to wander down the street again. He sighs heavily and says, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;We need some privacy so we can discuss this further, and other things.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Just as he says that, you all feel another pulse on your Periphery: a whiff of chalk powder, a ringing bell, or perhaps an odd feeling of being watched. Mathias nods and begins to walk past Moonstone. It's then that you all notice that there is suddenly somewhere to even <i>go</i> past Moonstone; where the wall had previously just ended, now there is a small alley several yards long that leads to an ornate iron door. Mathias walks and waves you to follow. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Please, trust me, this is a friend,&quot;</span> he asks wearily.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/43/44/6b/43446be11e8002cd34dc484c2016cb49.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm going to post the next part assuming you all follow. Feel free to say or do anything before you go, and if you wouldn't follow, let me know and we can edit this as needed.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.idesignarch.com/wp-content/uploads/Palm-Royale-Mansion_3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Mathias touches the door, and it opens quietly on its own. As you step through the door, you find yourself in the foyer of what appears to be a mansion. Double stairwells on either side of the foyer lead up to another level, passing a crystal chandelier hanging from the ceiling. You hear two people talking from a nearby room, a man and a woman's voice. Shortly after entering, the door closes behind you and a strikingly handsome man in his mid to late 30s walks into the entryway. He has a glass of liquor, probably Scotch neat, in his left hand, and he's wearing a custom-tailored suit with matching handkerchief and necktie.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/8b/b4/e8/8bb4e8cf3a228be0e7e08151e56174f4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The man smiles and nods his head in greeting to Mathias, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Ah, there you are, Mathias,&quot;</span> he says as he offers the older mage a firm handshake. He flashes another smile at the rest of you. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Welcome to my humble abode. A pleasure to meet you all. My name is Valentine.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As Valentine introduces himself, you hear the click of boots and turn to see a young, slim woman with a fire-red mowhawk, colorful tattoo sleeves, and a fishnet shirt. She stops in the foyer with a grin and rests her hands on her hips nonchalantly. A loud pop echoes in the room as she blows a bubble in her chewing gum.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/c1/a5/a1/c1a5a1d5fa2c5da0a0fa1f5900b2df10.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Name's Boomer,&quot;</span> she says simply. Boomer gives an obvious look-over of Lynx, and her smile widens. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Nice shirt,&quot;</span> she comments. She doesn't say anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-05-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T02:00:25-07:00","id":982604,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> L<b>B</b>BBOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Inspired | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Previous Scene</b><br /> (Just before Mathias leads everyone to the mansion)</div> <br /> <br /> Seems Moonstone is really engaged with this Ragnar fellow, so I leave him to it with the explanations and simply give a <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Thank you for backing us up there, we really needed it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I was about to ask Ragnar about if he was the one who healed me, but then I notice Binder being healed by another mage, Lynx, was his name. After asking if Binder was doing okay, I went over to Lynx. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;That was some pretty good healing, were you the one who did that for me earlier?&quot;</span> I ask Lynx, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Just trying to find who I need to thank for that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Suddenly, I hear a body thud on brick right behind me, and I pivot straight towards it. Looks like that Mathias guy is a lot harsher about the incident than I was. Looks like those Gulmoths are a bigger deal than I thought.<br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Current Scene</b></div> <br /> Mathias &quot;opens&quot; up an alley way that leads straight to a mansion, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Please, trust me, this is a friend,&quot;</span> he requests. He did save our asses, so I can pay his friend a visit, I guess.<br /> <br /> Upon entering, I take in mansion's interior, getting a handle on my new surroundings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Welcome to my humble abode. A pleasure to meet you all. My name is Valentine.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Nice place ya got,&quot;</span> I respond, still taking it in.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Does Inspired end? I mean, fight's done and all. Also, would I get a beat for resolving Steadfast for the slap? That's mainly why I resolved it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-06-2016, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T02:56:09-07:00","id":982612,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: Life (starts and ends in scene)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> Lynx takes a deep breath as he gets up on his feet. He grins as the scene unfolds, when the man known as Phoenix approaces.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">That was some pretty good healing, were you the one who did that for me earlier? Just trying to find who I need to thank for that.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah, thanks,</span>&quot; Lynx laughs as he rubs his beard. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I wasn't sure if I could heal it at all, to be honest, but hey! I could!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Though that chill... I need to ask Mathias. Is it that...Abyss thing?</i><br /> <br /> Then he's addressed by the one known as Moonstone. &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">Thank you. Lynx, right? Moonstone. Um- I'm hurt, but not from battle. Would you mind taking a look at my Pattern? I'd be very grateful if you could heal the rest of us, but please don't exert yourself.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> With a nod, Lynx sinks into the Senses of the Wild, looking at Moonstone. His ... <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Pattern?</span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\"> Faen<i>, too many questions!</i></span> - wounds look... wrong, somehow. Even the thought of summoning the Wild into his body makes him bristle. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't think I can. Your wounds are... I don't know. Corrupted? Wrong? And... I could heal the others, only if I try to go beyond the bruises, there's this... this... cold that tries to consume me. Though...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Lynx activates Life Senses to assess everybody's wounds.</span></b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When his eyes fall on Ragnar, he grits his teeth. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Excuse me.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar, you're hurt,</span>&quot; Lynx says soothingly as he walks around his friend. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I can't leave you like that.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He grabs his pendant instinctively as he lays his hand on Ragnar. In his mind, the Wild mends him completely, and he murmurs, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">O'great bear, I ask of you, heal him.</span>&quot; As the chill creeps up on him, he grits his teeth and feels his body surge, pushing it away far more aggressively than before - he feels energy - <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Mana!</span></i> - lash out from his soul. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah...thank you, great bear,</span>&quot; Lynx whispers to himself as his spell is successfully invoked, free of the chill. He gives Ragnar a proper bear hug before he steps back, grinning. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">That was brave of you. Stupid too, but brave.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx ends his Life Senses.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Then he attempts to cast Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; on Ragnar as an instant action through Touch, Reaching to heal Lethal damage, and gains 2 successes. He heals Ragnar for 4 Lethal damage.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Ragnar.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice)<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot;: Life (3) + Gnosis (1) + Willpower (3) - Potency (2)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 1 Free Reach: 1 on Instant Cast. 2 Extra Reaches for Sensory Range (1 reach) and for Knit to heal 1 Lethal per Potency rather than 2 Bashing (1 reach).<br /> <br /> <b>Base Paradox dice:</b> 3 - 2 from Reach, 1 from Second Paradox roll. <br /> <b>Paradox modifiers:</b> -2 from Dedicated Tool, -1 from Mana expenditure. <br /> <b>Final Paradox dice:</b> 0. <br /> If Paradox is obtained, Lynx will release it. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443078\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Paradox \u2192 0 successes.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443080\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Life 3 &quot;Knit&quot; \u2192 2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>((OOC: It says Phoenix, not Ragnar - I copy-pasted the previous description and forgot to change the name. My bad. :&lt; ))</b></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---NEW SCENE---<br /> <br /> Lynx doesn't look too surprised when Mathias goes off on Moonstone, having seen Phoenix do the same already, yet he assesses the man all the same. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx tries to assess Mathias, and gets 1 success.</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443081\" target=\"_blank\">Empathy Roll \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008000\">We need some privacy so we can discuss this further, and other things. Please, trust me, this is a friend.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx doesn't hesitate in the slightest, following him into the exquisite foyer. His ears twitch at the sound of the conversation, while he looks around with giddiness. Then...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\">&quot;Welcome to my humble abode. A pleasure to meet you all. My name is Valentine.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx turns to the man, and tilts his head. &quot;...Wow. Handsome.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF1493\">Name's Boomer,</span>&quot; Lynx turns to the woman, who smiles at her. &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF1493\">Nice shirt</span>.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Awesome hair,</span>&quot; he replies with a widening grin. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">All of you's wicked. I'm Lynx,</span>&quot; he adds, nodding to Valentine as well. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Thanks for welcoming us.</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:50:22-07:00","id":982791,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 6/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5<br /> </div> <b>Previous Scene</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Nameless? It's nothing insulting. He's just not with an Order yet. Are you two?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This is all moving way faster than Ragnar can really process. He trades a confused look with Lynx and spreads his hands. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Look- Moonstone, right?- Before today, I didn't even know there were other mages. So I guess Lynx and I are both Nameless.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He watches appreciatively as Lynx heals Binder. Impressive. Life definitely seems to be his forte. Then he feels Life course through himself as Lnyx heals his own wounds. He was on to something with the connectivity of living things, he knows that, but Lynx's magic seems so vital and raw. Yes, living things are connected, but they have an agency of their own. He'll have to keep that in mind when he attempts Life magic again- and in the meantime, perhaps he can pick Lynx's brain about it. <br /> <br /> He briefly stiffens with surprise as Lynx embraces him, but returns it, because honestly? He could use one. <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#800000\">That was brave of you. Stupid too, but brave.</span><span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar smiles sheepishly. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Eh, I think it was mostly stupid, but thank you.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <b>New Scene</b><br /> <br /> Ragnar's eyes narrow when he hears the exchange between Moonstone and Mathias. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 2 + Empathy 0 = 1 die -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443145\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He seethes slightly at the realization that Moonstone was the cause of their problems. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well, next time we fight him, we know who to use as bait.&quot; </span>His tone is mostly light, but there's an edge to it as he gives Moonstone an accusatory look. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;Please, trust me, this is a friend.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well, no point standing around where every normie in Chicago can hear us.&quot; </span>He follows after Mathias. Through the door, he gapes at the opulence. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Okay, quick question: where the hell in Chicago is this place, or is this your own private pocket dimension?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He looks around in naked awe, until a guy who looks like Gerard Butler's more handsome, upscale cousin walks in. <span style=\"color:#808080\">&quot;Welcome to my humble abode. A pleasure to meet you all. My name is Valentine.&quot; </span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Ohhhh myyyy. </i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;...Wow. Handsome,&quot; </span>he hears Lynx murmur beside him. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Tell me about it,&quot; </span>he mutters in agreement, but then blinks and looks at Lynx with realization. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Huh. </i></span><br /> <br /> Suddenly, an impulsive thought wanders through his mind. What are the odds that the first other mage he meets is also attracted to men? Is there some greater force at work, that brought them together for more reason than one? He once more studies the stream of Time. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Is there any future for me and Lynx? Are there any people or choices I could make that would prevent that from coming to pass? </span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar casts Divination (Time 1) as an improvised Spell. He has two free Reach, one of which he spends for specific answers, and the other he spends for Instant Casting. <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Time 2= 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443146\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. This is just not my day.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The spell fails to take form. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Well, maybe I need to just work this one out on my own. For now. </span></i>His eyes wander over Valentine's form for a moment. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Can't lie, I wouldn't mind getting a piece of that. </i></span><br /> <br /> His stomach gets a weird little wobble when he notices the looks that Lynx and Boomer give each other. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200bEnter the competition. What kind of codename is &quot;Boomer,&quot; anyways? </span></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:34:47-07:00","id":982855,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LLBB</b>OOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Mind Over Matter Pot 3]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Aion be praised, you're alright. I don't remember what happened in the portal, but I'm sure I was worried sick about you the whole time. Did my hair not work?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Marlin smiles wryly. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;It turned out to be a little more complicated than advertised, and then I was interrupted.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Wait, a smaller one? Did it escape? Do you have Sympathy to it? You should, if you were able to work magic on it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Yeah, messed me up and got away. And I guess I'm not sure about the sympathy... I didn't interact with it for that long.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Binder watches the healing magic with interest. He's slightly surprised by it; his magic is so much more ephemeral that affecting something in such an explicitly physical way is a little fascinating.<br /> <br /> <br /> *NEW SCENE*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 2 + Empathy 1 = 3 -&gt; 2 successes </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Binder's face darkens at Mathias's treatment of Moonstone. While everyone is filing into the magic alley, he approaches the young man. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Hey, look, I don't know much about magic, but I do know that mistakes happen. And I can tell you're the kind of person willing to work to fix your mistakes. That,&quot;</span> he gestures generally toward Mathias, <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;was uncalled for.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Once inside, he can't help but smile and shake his head at the way Boomer, Lynx, and Ragnar are looking at each other. Ah, youth! What a mess! Not to mention the sheer incongruity of Boomer's outfit against this backdrop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:00:01-07:00","id":982912,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: None<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Fabled, Guilty<br /> Health: LLB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a wet <i>thud</i> as Mathias slams Moonstone against the bricks, and a wheeze of air being forced out of his lungs. He struggles to catch his breath as the th\u00e9arch denounces him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You <i>fool!&quot;</i></span> Mathias growls. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Do you have any idea what damage you have caused, what you have risked? It took <i>six</i> of us to defeat it, and several of you could have died in the process. And I don't need Fate to know the odds of that thing coming back -- it's a certainty,&quot;</span> Mathias spat. <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;With luck, it can be found when it is still weak, but what if it runs loose in a shopping mall or a subway?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I- I don't remember what happened! I wasn't thinking straight!&quot;</span> he blurts out, his heart pounding fast, sweating under his ballcap. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I wasn't trying to hurt anyone, I swear on my name!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He fantasizes about Hakim walking up behind him, pulling Mathias away, beating him to a pulp, and holding Moonstone tight. Or at least one of the other mages telling Mathias to lay off. But no one comes. So he falls back on a response he's developed from dealing with angry men, and quietly pleads the familiar words: <i><span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;i'm sorry for making you hit me, i promise i won't tell anyone, please just let me go?&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> Being femme, the burden is on him to understand the angry men who hit him, and while Mathias has him against the wall he sculpts that instinct into an Imago. <i>Who are you?</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Mind 1 &quot;Know Nature&quot; on Mathias at touch range. 2 free reach on instant casting and learning his Aspirations and Obsessions, +1 reach to learn his Resolve rating, +1 reach to learn his Composure rating. 2 paradox dice, +2 for risking paradox already this scene. Going to contain. 4 Paradox: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443182\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. 7 Wisdom: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443183\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Seriously? 1 bashing damage for me, and a Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> Now then. Gnosis 1, Mind 2, +2 for Concentration, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443184\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He barely holds the Imago together through the pain and confusion, but he can't prove Mathias right. So he holds it, and the answers appear.<br /> <br /> When Mathias lets him go, he slumps to the ground, breathing hard. Ragnar shoots him an accusatory look: <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;Well, next time we fight him, we know who to use as bait.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There's an edge in his voice. Moonstone gives him a wide-eyed stare of confusion in return, but can't find any words.<br /> <br /> Mathias moves on to more important matters. <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;We need some privacy so we can discuss this further, and other things.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone feels that sensation in his Periphery of being centered at an auspicious moment in Time and Space. The Hour of Babel. He looks over his shoulder, and now he is slumped next to an alley that wasn't there before. It's magic!<br /> <br /> He pushes himself to his feet while the others chatter and file into the alleyway. Marlin stops to talk with him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Hey, look, I don't know much about magic, but I do know that mistakes happen. And I can tell you're the kind of person willing to work to fix your mistakes. That,&quot;</span> he gestures generally toward Mathias, <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;was uncalled for.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone doesn't say anything back, but he wraps his arms around the man and hugs him. Then steps back, squeezes his shoulder, nods and smiles. He picks up the rune-carved staff, takes one more look at the alley, and follows the others through the gate. But before stepping through, he reaches under his jacket and fastens the death's-head-moth clasp on the Cloak of Night. Just in case.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 Mana from the Cloak to activate its Wards and Signs effect. 7 dice, -2 for +1 Potency: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443313\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Spending another Mana to try again. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443314\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Moonstone has <b>Withstand 5 </b>against all spells with him as a subject for the rest of the scene, including spells like Divination that are normally not Withstood. The Cloak now contains 8/10 Mana.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He takes a look around the opulent foyer and frowns. Valentine's tailored suit and formal greeting are met with rolled eyes and obvious distaste. His ears are still burning from the embarrassment of getting hit by this guy's cabalmate, but he curtsies briefly and politely. <span style=\"color:#008080\"><i>&quot;</i></span><span style=\"color:#008080\"><i>Enchant\u00e9.&quot;</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-07-2016, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T02:52:11-07:00","id":983836,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, inspired should probably end. You can gain the Steadfast beat before the scene changes, so you can still gain a Beat in this scene for resolving a condition if relevant.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> There's something about the sudden intensity in Mathias' tone, and his lack of anger in other situations today, that suggests to you that the source of his emotional distress is personal. Mathias seems to be projecting or reacting to something, and you can see from the way he tries to suppress his anger that he knows his reaction is probably unwarranted. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Of course,&quot;</span> Valentine replies warmly. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Any friend of Mathias' is a friend of mine.&quot;</span> The well-dressed man walks briskly to the door after you all enter and peers out into the alley before closing it. He rests a hand on the door, and after a moment you catch another scent of chalk powder and hear a quiet bell ring on your Periphery. Valentine exhales quietly and his shoulders relax more than they had a moment ago. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Mathias is one of the first mages you've met who appears truly wise and experienced, and he seems to share your temperament and magical expertise; it's only natural that you would gravitate towards seeing things from his perspective.<br /> <br /> If Valentine hears your comment about his appearance, he doesn't seem to react or respond. He does try to answer your question, though. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Distance and location are a construct of an unenlightened mind.&quot;</span> He holds up his index finger on each hand, shoulder width apart, then moves them together until they touch. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Those who have Awakened can learn how the relationship between two objects, people, or locations is mutable. Distance is an expression of sympathy, of <i>connection</i>, between two things. I suppose the most accurate answer is that this place is in a 'private pocket dimension' currently separated from the world, but it can be connected anywhere as needed.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Your spell fizzles, leaving you wondering what your future holds. After even your brief exposure to Supernal truth, the lack of future knowledge is incredibly disappointing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> You've generally been good at reading people, and you do do this time as Mathias publicly rebukes Moonstone. Mathias seems to recognize that he is being very harsh, and for a moment you wonder if he is responding to some kind of personal guilt or memory here. He didn't need to impress upon you all how dangerous the Gulmoth could be; you experienced it for yourself. It suggests that there is more under the surface here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> The spell forms instinctively, but it brings up that now-familiar chill in your soul that you associate with pushing your magic beyond reasonable limits. You press it down with your will, but still find yourself briefly double over in pain. No one seems to notice that, especially after being shoved against the wall, but Mathias frowns as your spell triggers his Sight.<br /> <br /> A flood of information flashes through your mind as your spell unfolds, not in the form of memories or thoughts, but gut feelings and instinctive knowledge about this man's character. Although his current actions don't reflect it, you sense that at his core, Mathias is a warm and generous man. He has a strong sense of pride, but he tries to compensate by mentoring and caring for others. He thirsts for knowledge about Highstorms and how to predict them, and he is desperate to learn more about how to rid this world from the influence of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> At your plea, Mathias pulls away, and a look of guilt flashes across his face -- something you never saw from Hakim.<br /> <br /> Inside the mansion, Valentine chuckles and studies you curiously. You feel a pulse of magic on your Periphery, and suddenly Valentine blinks and frowns. He swirls his Scotch and takes a sip. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;If I may ask, where did you find that staff?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Boomer is looking at you and tapping a finger on her chin. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I feel like I've seen you before,&quot;</span> she says. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Do I know you from somewhere?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You gain Abyssal Backlash at +1 on your next Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Virtue: Generosity<br /> Vice: Pride<br /> Resolve 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Obsessions: Learn how to predict timing and severity of Highstorms; study how to better defeat or protect against Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Find and train a Legacy mentor (long-term); study about tribal weather rituals; introduce a newly Awakened mage to the local Consilium<br /> <br /> You can roll Int + Politics again to see if you've heard of this cabal, and Boomer specifically. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> After you've had a chance to introduce yourselves, Valentine leads you all into a sitting room and offers you a drink of your choice. He takes a seat in a large leather lounge chair and nurses his Scotch, turning to watch Mathias, who takes a seat in another chair beside him. Boomer stands against the wall, crossing her arms.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Valentine and Boomer are my colleagues and companions,&quot;</span> Mathias explains. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;We are members of a cabal, a group of allied mages, that we call the Shields of Dawn. We created our group to root out and defeat darkness in our lives and world, in whatever way we could. Each of us comes from a different Path and Order, because we thought it made sense to learn from each other from different perspectives and strengths.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias pauses. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I suppose there is a lot to help explain. I'll try to keep it brief...Please feel free to interrupt with questions. I'm sure you have many.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine grins and shakes his head as he takes another sip. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I would've brewed a pot of coffee if I had known Mathias was preparing a lecture,&quot;</span> he jokes. Boomer barks a laugh and slides down into a cross-legged seating position, but she smiles at Mathias and nods at him.<br /> <br /> The older mage explains what he describes as the most basics of Supernal magic: the Arcana, the Paths, and the legends of the Fall, which created the Lie and invited the Abyss into the world. He then explains about mage society, including the Pentacle Orders and their purposes, and how they form cabals for personal reasons and convene in cities around the world in Consilia. Mathias explains that he is an Acanthus of the Silver Ladder; Valentine, a Mastigos and Guardian of the Veil; and Boomer is an Obrimos of the Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> Boomer speaks up as the information settles in. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;So. What do you want to know?&quot;</span> she asks. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;There's been a lot going on here in Chicago lately. We could fill you in on some things that have happened very recently,&quot;</span> she offers.<br /> <br /> Valentine chimes in, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;There's also the matter of the Highstorms, and the objects they provide.&quot;</span> He looks at Moonstone, but he makes a point of glancing towards Ragnar and Lynx.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T06:54:06-07:00","id":983895,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 6/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar sits, absorbing all of the information that has been dumped on him. He looks at each of them in turn. Two Acanthi, three Mastagoi, two Obrimoi, and one Thyrsus. One for the Ladder, one for the Guardians, one for the Arrows. Four Nameless, one calling himself an Arrow.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;So what's the situation here in Chicago? How do the Orders relate to each to each other? Why did each of you join your Order?&quot; </span>He looks at Moonstone, and feels a little apologetic. He was angry about getting sliced up by Alux, but Moonstone said it was an accident. Now it makes sense: Moonstone must have cast a spell and reached way beyond his abilities. Maybe he had thought he could contain it, maybe he hadn't understood the danger. And Ragnar can't confirm, but Moonstone seems to be a little... disturbed. And not just because he accidentally summoned an Abyssal abomination. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;When you introduced yourself to us, you called yourself an Arrow. How did you know about them if you were newly Awakened?&quot; </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-08-2016, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:14:59-07:00","id":983907,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> L<b>B</b>BBOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> I chuckle as everybody seems to be checking each other out. Might as well get on the action myself. Moonstone? Bit of a weenie, folded against the old man. Binder? Too old. Ragnar? Eh, nothing noteworthy at the moment. Lynx? Ooooh man, I so wanna wrestle that bear, but I'm probably gonna have to get in line first. Mathias? Way too old. Valentine? Looks a little too prissy for my tastes. Boomer? Stands out like a sore thumb and gives absolutely no fucks about it. Now <i>that</i> is my type.<br /> <br /> But enough of that, on to more important matters. They give a prep talk on the wizarding world like the other mages from before, but they give a lot more detail. So each Path is connected to a different Supernal Realm, I guess that's why Moonstone's and Binder's magic felt so different to mine when I observed them. At first, I thought they were drawing completely different types of magic from different worlds. Guess I was half-right. I'll have to put an experience behind the names of these Paths, so I cross a palm over my eyes to observe the stuff of these Realms.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Praxis<br /> <br /> <b><u>Supernal Vision (Prime 1, Corebook p, 166)</u></b><br /> <b>Reach:</b> 2 free; 2 used for instant casting and advanced scale<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Dedicated Tool for +1<br /> <b>Factors:</b> PSF Potency 2, Scale 5 subjects<br /> <br /> Targetting Mathias, Valentine, Boomer, Ragnar, and Lynx and asking for Path and Gnosis<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443695\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Prime 2 + 1 Tool = 4 dice \u2192 3 successes</a><br /> <br /> That makes it an exceptional success, so I'll have Phoenix regain a Mana (so I could heal the lethal damage with pattern restoration).</div></div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Interesting. Acanthus reminds me of Grimm's fairy tales, Mastigoes has that whole breaking the flawed chains I felt earlier, and Thyrsus feels of pure breath, blood, and bone. Only four of the five, though. Moros I believe is the one that's absent. Wonder what it's like.<br /> <br /> With all the basics done, Boomer chimes in with <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;So. What do you want to know? </span><span style=\"color:deeppink\">There's been a lot going on here in Chicago lately. We could fill you in on some things that have happened very recently,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do you guys know about a mage named Anubis?&quot;</span> I respond. Hopefully I can get some answers so my trip to the metropolis wasn't a complete waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:27:33-07:00","id":984008,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Those are excellent questions that need longer answers,&quot;</span> Mathias replies, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;but I'll try to do my best. <br /> <br /> &quot;I joined the Silver Ladder because I wanted to be a part of something that helped make the world and mage society better. I realized that if I could dedicate my life to helping others Awaken, and help new mages find their way, that it would give me a sense of fulfillment and meaning,&quot;</span> Mathias shares. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Our Order tries to expose Sleepers to kernels of Supernal truth. The theory is that it helps nudge them towards seeing the truth and Awakening.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I actually think we've seen you before, Binder,&quot;</span> Valentine chimes in. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Mathias came and dropped off some books at your store that had some rituals and theory about Supernal magic.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias chuckles. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Yes, that's right. Valentine insisted on coming because he wanted to make sure I didn't expose anything too serious or let anything into the wrong hands.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine shrugs. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The Guardians are tasked with keeping magic secret and safe, and ensuring that it is used appropriately. Anyone can make a mistake and overreach, potentially releasing a Paradox or even allowing an Abyss to enter into this world. Anyone.&quot;</span> His eyes focus on Mathias for a moment. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The Silver Ladder have been guilty of this often, but they are usually well-intentioned and I trust you, Mathias. The Guardians make sure people use magic responsibly, for the safety of all. And they work to find and stop any who might intentionally cause Paradox to further the Lie or their own means.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer sits up straighter and chimes in. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I actually joined the Arrow because I was told I couldn't,&quot;</span> she smirks. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I came up with my Shadow Name shortly after I Awakened and I was...a bit of an ass, honestly. My mentor at the time said it would be a terrible fit, but something about the challenge made it seem fun.&quot;</span> Her smirk becomes softer, almost nostalgic. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;When I tried to join, I was really stubborn. I wanted to prove that I had the perseverance and courage, the strength. But what I actually learned was discipline. The Arrows have an incredibly important calling, to safeguard not just our societies but our truths. By mastering ourselves, we master the Supernal, because they're so intricately linked.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Boomer</b><br /> You will your Imago into place, drawing on Prime to unlock the Truth of each mage here. You feel and visibly see the connection each has to the Supernal, and put a personal experience to each of the verbal descriptions you've heard from the mages here. The Shields of Dawn seem equally skilled in their raw mastery of magic, all quite stronger than the other new mages whom you met today. <br /> <br /> As you cast your spell using your tattoos, Boomer leans forward and looks at you curiously. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Whoa, did you just use your tattoos to power your magic? That's wicked,&quot;</span> she grins.<br /> <br /> At your question, Mathias frowns and shakes his head slowly, then looks to Valentine, who also shakes his head. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;No, I haven't heard of anyone by that name. But plenty of people have their secrets, and some might use another name or identity for safety reasons. Why do you ask?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Paths all match as described above. Mathias, Valentine and Boomer are all currently Gnosis 3. Everyone else is Gnosis 1.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:53:57-07:00","id":984019,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: None [Wards and Signs, Potency 5, scene]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Fabled, Guilty, Abyssal Backlash (+1)<br /> Health: LL</b><b>BB</b>OO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Valentine seems to have been stymied by Moonstone's ward. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;If I may ask, where did you find that staff?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone turns it over in his hands. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;On the ground in a dark alley. It's probably filthy. </span><i><span style=\"color:#008080\">Tch.&quot;</span> </i>He glances up at Valentine. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It's from the Highstorm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer studies him.<span style=\"color:deeppink\"> &quot;I feel like I've seen you before,&quot;</span> she says. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Do I know you from somewhere?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He gives her a little professional smile. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Seen, but not heard. I'm Moonstone, Hakim's Sleepwalker. I used to serve the Knights of Alhambra. I was hoping you would say something, Boomer.&quot;</span> <i>Because I'm super vain.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intelligence+Politics (Consilium), 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443743\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> That should be at -1 from wound penalties, but it would still succeed. I assume Moonstone's bashing damage recovers over the next while.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He knows <i>of </i>the Shields of Dawn, but he's never been their guest like this. Much as he wants to process his grief by getting blackout drunk, this doesn't seem like the right time. He just requests a mixed drink from Valentine to be polite.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I would've brewed a pot of coffee if I had known Mathias was preparing a lecture,&quot; </span>Valentine jokes. Moonstone fake-laughs, also to be polite. That's the closest he comes to acknowledging or making eye contact with Mathias for the next hour or so. He just sits in a big comfy armchair, closes his eyes and lets his aches and pains recede. He doesn't add anything during the explanation of The Truth About The World, just sits quietly and enjoys the experience of watching other people learn. He doesn't have a cat to pet, so he runs his fingers along the warm rune-carved staff instead. It feels good.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Well, he does say one thing. After Mathias explains the nature of the Fallen World, Moonstone (eyes still closed) speaks up in a quiet voice. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Here's a brain-teaser for you: the Supernal World is the source of the Fallen World. All true things originate in the Supernal. But the Supernal can only act by manifesting in the Fallen; for example, by the Awakening. The Fallen World contains good and virtuous things, but it also contains evil and impure things. Does that make the Supernal World complicit in evil?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's a riddle Hakim taught him years ago, in circulation among the Diamond Orders for centuries. Sort of a koan, although it derives from a Neo-Confucian philosophical problem rather than Zen. There is no right answer, but debate and reconsideration of the question is meant to increase Gnosis and cultivate Wisdom.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He's calmer and in less pain by the time Boomer chimes in, but he's still worn down to the bone. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;There's been a lot going on here in Chicago lately. We could fill you in on some things that have happened very recently,&quot; </span>she offers.<br /> <br /> He's still quiet when he answers her, but direct. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I heard Cielo and her sisters made a play for the Hierarchy. What does that mean for us?&quot;<br /> <br /> ---</span><br /> <br /> Question from Phoenix:<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do you guys know about a mage named Anubis?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Thinking out loud:<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;How many mages named Anubis do you think there are in the United States alone? It has to be up there with like, <i>Loki. </i>Or <i>Shadow. </i>Actually- how do you know a mage, Phoenix? Were you part of this world too?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Question from Ragnar: <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;When you introduced yourself to us, you called yourself an Arrow. How did you know about them if you were newly Awakened?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone smiles with nostalgia, the bittersweet variety. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;My soul is precious to the Oracles. Because of them, I could see and remember magic since the day I was born. People thought I was crazy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Completely deadpan pause, uncomfortable silence. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That's a joke, you can laugh.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There are other people like me. Walking in our Sleep. Many of us are drawn to the Orders, if we discover them. Some of us Awaken, but we're very useful regardless. Someone has to chalk the summoning circle, translate the grimoire from Classical Chinese, boil the eye of newt, deal with the cops. It's worth it to be around true magic. You can't go back to a normal life once you've seen it. I know many other Sleepwalkers in Chicago who feel the same, but everyone's experience is different.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm older than I look. I've served mages...probably since before Ragnar knew how to read. My master was Hakim, a Thunderbolt Guardian of the Adamantine Arrow. <span style=\"font-size:11px\">He,</span> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">um,</span> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">seems to have been</span> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">killed in the Deathstorm.</span>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Rapid change of topic before that settles in. Valentine said earlier, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;There's also the matter of the Highstorms, and the objects they provide.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone lifts the staff. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm familiar, but you may want to edify the others. Hakim had a shadow-cloak from a Highstorm, but this weapon is new to me. I don't remember anything that happened in the other world. How does one learn to...activate it? What's the approach? Is there a spell, or does it have to be Scrutinized with Prime? Is it cursed? Did it <i>exist</i> somewhere in the Fallen World before it appeared in the alley, or did it just spontaneously pop into being?&quot;<br /> <br /> ---</span><br /> <br /> He's been listening carefully when Valentine talks about the Guardians and Paradox. He's heard it before in broad strokes, but it makes more sense after today. He leans in and speaks carefully to him:<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;Listen, Warlock to Warlock...I have some questions about the Deathstorm. Burning questions. Don't apologize, just be frank. Do we know how many mages died? And...when that many people die, all at once, all from the same thing...does Sympathy arise from that spontaneously? Or did all of them die alone? I feel this need, the idea is in my mind, but I only knew Sympathy academically until now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Trying to advance my Obsession here, if possible.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-08-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:58:41-07:00","id":984050,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lynx has settled on the floor, leaning on a wall, in the mood of a flat surface to rest upon. He closes his eyes and keeps his ears on the conversation. He draws it all in.<br /> <br /> Orders. Paths. Arcana. Cabals.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">So tired...</span></i><br /> <br /> Hakim. Anubis. Cielo. Arrows. Exposing people to magic. Protecting mundane folks - <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Sleepers, was it?</span></i> - Building discipline. Sympathy. Highstorms. Deathstorm.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah...</span>&quot; Lynx sighs as he opens his eyes and looks up. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Mathias, and Valentine, and Boomer...what do you think of the other Orders? I guess you wanted to give us an objective overview, but... what do you think when you meet a Libertine? Or a Mysterium member? What about another Mastigos? Or...or a Thyrsus?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh! Right, you mentioned Highstorms and objects!</span>&quot; His voice perks up as he reaches for his pocket. There, he pulls out the round pebble. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">After we woke up, I had this in my pocket...whatever it is. With Mathias finding us and all the chaos around that... that Gulmoth thing, I forgot about it until now.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He holds it up to the light, studying it for the very first time. He then glances at everybody expectantly, though something else washes over him - not a chill, more like... ... He rubs his beard quietly, and when he speaks his voice is softer.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;I don't suppose you also have a Thyrsus nearby? Only I can't relate to anyone of you in that... well. <i>That</i> way, I guess? All about the Time and Mind and Prime and... Here I feel more like a ... dog. Or bear, or...any animal, really.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He glances down at the floor for a moment, looking vulnerable and weak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-09-2016, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:10:01-07:00","id":984107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OOC: This scene will last long enough that your bashing rounds will all heal. Go ahead and mark them as healed as of now. </div> </div> </div><b>Moonstone</b><br /> Boomer's face falls at the mention of Hakim. She has a look of recognition on her face as you describe yourself, though, and a look of surprise blends in with sadness. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I thought your name sounded familiar...Despite what the th\u00e9archs say about Sleepwalkers being closer to Awakening than Sleepers, I can't help but be surprised when I hear of one Awakening. Hakim was a skilled willworker and respected colleague. I know he had...complicated relationships with his cabal recently, but he was a member of my Order. His death is a great loss.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine has a different reaction; he now gives you a measuring look with furrowed eyebrows. He says nothing, however. <br /> <br /> Mathias interjects to provide more context. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;As I was explaining earlier, the Hierarch is the highest ranking official in Mage society among a local Consilium. In a very unorthodox move, Cielo garnered enough political leverage to convince the previous Atlas, a Mystagogue Obrimos and then Hierarch, to step down in favor of her.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer nods and continues, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I'm not sure what impact it will have yet. Consilium politics aren't exactly my strength,&quot;</span> she smirks. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;But I do know that it has drawn a lot of attention to the Adamantine Arrow. And Cielo and her cabal, Medianoche, have personally led raids on half a dozen cabals engaging in unsavory practices...things like summoning Abyssal entities,&quot;</span> she scowls. <br /> <br /> Turning to Moonstone specifically, she says, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Just to be blunt, but you need to know that you're not technically an Arrow, even though you have served Hakim. You still need to pass the formal initiation tasks. Everyone does. I'm sorry.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> After Boomer answers more of your questions, Valentine speaks up. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Well, if you ignore the possibility of the curse, you can experiment with it by trial and error. But it is indeed safer to Scrutinize with Prime, or an Unveiling Prime spell. But the latter tends to be difficult to work consistently because of the nature of the objects; the spells sometimes just...fail,&quot;</span> he shrugs. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The items do seem to come from another dimension. Mystagogues believe that they come from another dimension from a time before the Fall, but most have no memory of their time in the Highstorms, or perhaps a few fleeting images at best. <br /> <br /> &quot;What I do know, though, is that whoever finds them seems to have some kind of sympathetic connection to the item. Which is why I'm confused.&quot;</span> Without looking, Valentine points over to Lynx's pocket, just before he pulls the pebble out and reveals it. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;That young man has a sympathetic link to that item. Ragnar has a link to another one on his person.&quot;</span> The corner of his lips twitch into a hint of a smile. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;But that staff has a sympathetic link to Phoenix. It's not really my business -- Cielo has made it clear that artifact recovery and claims should be at the discretion of the mages involved, preferably by Duel Arcane if not by verbal agreement -- but I find it interesting. <br /> <br /> &quot;As for the Deathstorm, Cielo announced that there were 32 deaths. Including a few Masters.&quot;</span> He pauses to let that sink in. Boomer and Mathias shift uncomfortably. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I...actually believe that what you suggest could be possible. And there is some rumor that that might be true, that the deaths are somehow all related. But the Council is still investigating the deaths, and even outside of them, many are...uncomfortable discussing the Deathstorm.&quot;</span> From his tone, you can tell that he is one of them. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I will still award the Arcane Beat because you're doing everything you can at this moment to learn more.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> The Shields of Dawn look relieved for a chance to change the subject. Mathias is the first to reply. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;It's a great question, but a pretty broad one that's hard to answer quickly or exhaustively. In short, I think the three of us have a little more positive opinions of the other Orders, because our cabal was built on collaboration across Paths and Orders. Obviously, there are stereotypes and tensions between the groups, and it's different in every Consilium around the world. I think you'll find that the Mystagogues are still upset about their Hierarch being pressured to step down, and the Free Council have been struggling with some of their humanitarian efforts downtown due to lingering fears about the Deathstorm. The Silver Ladder and Guardians have been at odds with each other a bit more, but some of us still get along just fine,&quot;</span> he grins at Valentine. <br /> <br /> As soon as you ask about a Thyrsus mage, the three experienced mages all stop talking or moving. There is a long, awkward silence, and Mathias looks overcome with grief. Valentine leans towards him and tries to whisper to him, but Mathias shakes his head and briskly walks from the room, with Valentine right behind him. <br /> <br /> Boomer is quiet, and she looks choked up. She coughs to clear her throat. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;We...We lost two of our cabal members in the Deathstorm. Our Thyrsus and Moros mages. I'm sorry.&quot;</span> She seems at a loss for words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:05:27-07:00","id":984175,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: None [Wards and Signs, Potency 5, scene]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Fabled, Guilty, Abyssal Backlash (+1)<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I thought your name sounded familiar...Despite what the th\u00e9archs say about Sleepwalkers being closer to Awakening than Sleepers, I can't help but be surprised when I hear of one Awakening. Hakim was a skilled willworker and respected colleague. I know he had...complicated relationships with his cabal recently, but he was a member of my Order. His death is a great loss.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Believe me, no one is more surprised than me. We gave up hope years ago.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone nods along with the rest of Boomer's words.<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;Thank you. And his cabal...Wisdom is relative, and that is all I will say on that for now. I want to break the news to the Knights personally, if they'll meet me. I would be grateful if you would mention me to them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The news about the political shakeup makes him pensive. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I respect Cielo's decisiveness. I know I'm speaking above my station, but I think this is a mistake. The third precept of the Adamant Way: <i>'Service is Mastery.'</i> An Arrow should not sit in the Hierarch's seat. There are different ways of being a strong leader.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Just to be blunt, but you need to know that you're not technically an Arrow, even though you have served Hakim. You still need to pass the formal initiation tasks. Everyone does. I'm sorry.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That stings. But he just doesn't have the energy to argue, and it's not Boomer's decision anyway. He bows his head. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;No, I understand. I'll prove my worth along with everyone else.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As for the magic items, a bit of intrigue.<span style=\"color:gray\"> &quot;But that staff has a sympathetic link to Phoenix. It's not really my business -- Cielo has made it clear that artifact recovery and claims should be at the discretion of the mages involved, preferably by Duel Arcane if not by verbal agreement -- but I find it interesting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Oof. That's disappointing. Moonstone looks over at Phoenix, keeping the staff jealously close.<span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Well- I thought I wielded it well. Let's start by learning what it does, and decide on the details later.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Duel Arcane. There's an idea. He's been a spectator, even served as a courier to deliver a challenge or two- Hakim was a somewhat infamous duelist- but to compete himself? He never imagined. Hell of a way to avenge an insult. <i>Hmm.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I...actually believe that what you suggest could be possible. And there is some rumor that that might be true, that the deaths are somehow all related. But the Council is still investigating the deaths, and even outside of them, many are...uncomfortable discussing the Deathstorm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Talking about the Deathstorm with someone who <i>knows</i>, rather than just turning it over and over in his own head, fills him with purpose. It's a rush. He's obsessed, but he's getting somewhere with it. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It hurts me, too. But it's not going anywhere. I Awakened to Pandemonium when I couldn't hide anymore. I'm not going to turn away now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Muttered: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Let's hold off on the magic pebble for right now, Lynx.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Tension. Death. Mathias is overcome, Valentine leaves with him. Moonstone is...stressed the hell out. <i>Am I supposed to feel sympathy for you? You think you're like me because you've known death too?</i> He was able to keep the water of his mental pond still over the last hour, but now it's freezing and boiling and churning, and he can't keep his mind straight. He hadn't really thought about <i>other </i>people being victimized by the Deathstorm, left behind as survivors. Even if it is the logical next step from his Obsession.<br /> <br /> He doesn't say a word to Boomer, he just locks up and pulls his cap down over his eyes and digs in his messenger bag for his mirror, and gazes into the cracked reflection. It's half honest spellcasting and half nervous tension, obviously doing <i>anything </i>to keep his mind occupied.<br /> <br /> Two questions: <i>The next time I fight the Duel Arcane, will I win? </i>And also: <i>Will I comfort Mathias in his grief?</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Praxis, Time 1 Divination. 1 reach on instant casting. Yes/no/irrelevant answers. Gnosis 1, Time 2, path tool +1, concentration +2, 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443835\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Except I misused the Concentration yantra, so this is actually a failure. I'll make it a dramatic failure and take an Arcane Beat, because Moonstone (like Phoenix) is falling apart and just keeps striking out with Divination today.<br /> <br /> Also, I restored 1 Mana from hitting my Obsession.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-09-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:19:30-07:00","id":984230,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 6/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 2/5</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ragnar continues to listen to the conversation, interjecting where he sees fit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;I joined the Silver Ladder because I wanted to be a part of something that helped make the world and mage society better.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I understand that,&quot; </span>says Ragnar. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200b&quot;Looking at all those people, knowing they can never understand what I can see, what I can do...&quot; </span>He thinks back to the first few days after Awakened, and was coming to grips with the fact that he was virtually alone in a crowded world. The thought threatens to bring up memories from even further back, memories of college and frightened self-discovery and <i>home</i>, and Ragnar pushes them aside. He looks Mathias in the eye. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;All of the Orders sound like they have valid methods and noble goals. But I hate the notion of allowing people to be ignorant when I can teach them. I taught Lynx how to use his Mage Sight, and what's the Lie but a form of ignorance that pervades the whole universe? I respect whatever decision you guys make,&quot; </span>he says to his fellow Nameless, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;but me? I think I favor the Silver Ladder.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\">&quot;The Guardians make sure people use magic responsibly, for the safety of all. And they work to find and stop any who might intentionally cause Paradox to further the Lie or their own means.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I've risked Paradox before,&quot; </span>he says. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I didn't understand what I was doing at the time, but today I've seen what Paradox can bring about. You're right, we Mages need to work our wills within our limits.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is going to make a Perception role to see if he can get any meaning from Valentine looking at Mathias when he mentioned Paradox and Abyssals. Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443867\" target=\"_blank\">sheesh, I just cannot catch a break</a>. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> When Phoenix casts his spell, Ragnar also leans forward. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Whoa. Are your tattoos your dedicated tools, then?&quot; </span>He produces his silver knife and holds it for everybody to see. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;This was lying on the ground next to me when my Awakening ended.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Moonstone sits there and listens, until he speaks up and throws his riddle into the mix. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well, isn't that the question of evil all over again? Except where theists have to answer it without proof of a higher power, and atheists have to answer it without allowing for a higher power, we Awakened know for a fact that the Supernal is real.&quot; </span>He tilts his head a little and stares at a spot on the floor as he considers the crux of the question. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;The notion that the Supernal is &quot;complicit&quot; in evil assumes that it's sentient, and not some sort of impersonal force. If it </span><i>is</i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"> sentient, then mustn't the Supernal permit evil to exist so that good may, too? One is the absence of the other. Everything in the world can only be truly understood, even defined, in the presence of its opposite.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The discussion of the Deathstorm deeply disturbs Ragnar. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200b&quot;During today's Highstorm, we,&quot; </span>he gestures to himself and Lynx, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;noticed that the hail had some sort of magical quality to it. I didn't know it then and I can't confirm it, but I think the hail may have been tainted with the Abyss. Did anybody notice similar phenomena during the Deathstorm?&quot; </span><i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">32. My god. Assuming there were a hundred mages in Chicago at the time, that's a one-in-three mortality rate. </span></i>If work on unraveling the mystery of the Deathstorm hasn't already begun, he's going to make sure it does when he's more fully integrated into Chicago's Awakened society.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Valentine's words throw him off. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>No point lying about it. </i></span>He produces the black-bladed knife from his pocket. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;It looks like obsidian, but it's probably not. I was meaning to try and study it when things quieted down. I figured a life-and-death situation wasn't the best time to wave a strange artifact in people's faces and ask if they knew what it was.&quot; </span>It's not really a lie; he really was going to try and figure it out on his own, and then bring it to somebody else if he got stumped.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Lynx's question brings a sudden stand-still to the conversation. Mathias becomes suddenly very upset, and walks off, and Valentine tries to comfort him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF1493\">&quot;We...We lost two of our cabal members in the Deathstorm. Our Thyrsus and Moros mages. I'm sorry.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar looks at Boomer, and he no longer sees a romantic rival. He just sees a woman- a fellow mage- suffering from deep emotional pain. He suddenly feels like an ass- for the second time in a couple hours, after figuratively biting Moonstone's head off.<br /> <br /> He looks over at Lynx and touches his forearm in consolation. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Don't beat yourself up over it. How could you have possibly known?&quot; </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-09-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:22:29-07:00","id":984381,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Whoa, did you just use your tattoos to power your magic? That's wicked,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Whoa. Are your tattoos your dedicated tools, then?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Oh! Um...yeah,&quot;</span> I jolt a bit at the sudden words, then I gaze at my palms, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Uh, they burned in during my Awakening.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I flashback to that moment. My death, the tattoos, my dead comrades.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;How many mages named Anubis do you think there are in the United States alone? It has to be up there with like, <i>Loki. </i>Or <i>Shadow. </i>Actually- how do you know a mage, Phoenix? Were you part of this world too?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Uhhh, kind of...&quot;</span> I trail off.<br /> <br /> Another flashback. Mom and dad. They loved each other so much. But they could never agree. <i>Magic was good! Magic was bad! Magic was bad, bad, bad!!! Good magic didn't exist. Good magic had to leave...</i><br /> <br /> <i>Answer the damn question, fuckwit!</i> Wait, was that me, or-?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I was born with my eyes open to magic. I poked my nose here and there.&quot;</span> Certainly the truth, just not the whole truth.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;My soul is precious to the Oracles. Because of them, I could see and remember magic since the day I was born. People thought I was crazy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Magic is real! Oh yeah? Prove it! You're so stupid. Do you believe in Santa and the Easter Bunny, too? I can see it. What's it look like? Your mom?</i> Punchs, kicks, bloody noses, black eyes, but none on me. <i>You're suspended. But they-? Doesn't matter. Just stop pretending you can see magic and they'll stop picking on you.</i><br /> <br /> <i>What...?</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That's a joke, you can laugh.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Doesn't seem all that funny to me...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Everyone tries to solve Moonstone's riddle, but they seem to miss the point.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;It's irrelevant,&quot;</span> I answer, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;The whole thing is based on an appeal to emotion. You want to believe that the Supernal is good by default...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Magic is good! I've seen it heal, bring people together, even create miracles.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;..So when someone suggests the Supernal might not be, you wanna prove them wrong...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>No, it isn't! Magic drives people crazy. It kills the people you care about, it maims everything you have, and leaves you a wreck without hands to pick up the pieces! Even if you try to use it for good, there's always a price! Always!!!</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;...But you can't, because the Supernal isn't good. Never was...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Good magic isn't real. So good magic had to leave. For you.<br /> <br /> It's always for you, isn't it?</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;...However, the same can be said for the Supernal being evil...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>You were born of magic.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;...It's only in how one wields it.&quot;</span> I end my little rant.<br /> <br /> <i>The dragon is but a mirror.</i><br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;But that staff has a sympathetic link to Phoenix. It's not really my business -- Cielo has made it clear that artifact recovery and claims should be at the discretion of the mages involved, preferably by Duel Arcane if not by verbal agreement -- but I find it interesting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Well- I thought I wielded it well. Let's start by learning what it does, and decide on the details later.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Wait, if it has a sympathetic link to me,&quot;</span> putting two and two together from my earlier pep talk, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Then can't it be used to target me or something? I mean, that's how one's birth name works, doesn't it? I think it might be best if I keep it. Not saying you'd do anything bad with it, just...I'd feel more secure.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Considering his track record with the Abyss, I don't want him having something connected to me if it's at all contagious. That, and it's generally unhealthy for me anyways I realize as I put a hand on one of the few remaining wounds.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;We...We lost two of our cabal members in the Deathstorm. Our Thyrsus and Moros mages. I'm sorry.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Flashback to my dead comrades. <i>I died too, but why am I still alive? I wanna rest with them! <b>WHY!!!?</b> I failed them. I betrayed them, I was supposed to fight it, but I didn't. Dad didn't want this. You betrayed him, too. You made your mother leave, your father weep, and you killed your friends. You promised them you'd succeed, instead you died and turned yourself into a monster.<br /> <br /> <b>HOW DARE YOU!!!</b></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix is trying his damnedest to keep his grief from showing<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/443911\" target=\"_blank\">Composure 2 - 1 Untrained Subterfuge = 1 die \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Make that a dramatic failure. He's breaking down.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I can't help but let it out a little in the form of a sudden gasp and biting my fist. I stood up, I had to leave. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I just...gotta be alone now,&quot;</span> I state as I quickly walk off to some other room. I let it all out there, screaming and punching the walls. Couldn't help myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:21:32-07:00","id":984830,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Boomer glances down the hallway to where you can all hear Mathias and Valentine quietly talking to each other, but the words are muted. She changes the subject in response to your questions, looking grateful for a chance to do so. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Moonstone, look...About the Arrows. Perhaps this is an opportunity. As a Sleepwalker, you fell in with an Order because of Hakim's influence. But as an Awakened mage, you have finally uncovered your <i>true</i> self. I think that truth may help guide you towards a greater mission, and while it's possible the Adamantine Arrow will still be the best organization to help you along with that...it might not be.&quot;</span> Her words seem genuine, but you've come to expect that of many Arrows; the Knights of Alhambra, at least, seemed very open about many things -- during conversations you were privy to, anyway.<br /> <br /> As you disengage from the others and withdraw into the comfort of your mirror, you attempt to dip your mind into the stream of Time. But the mirror shows nothing but a cracked reflection of your face, and dark clouds swirling around you. Your failure at learning the truth <i>again</i> is maddening.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for the dramatic failure. As a result, I'm giving you a custom condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Irritable.</b> Like a lion lashing its tail and looking ready to pounce, your character is feeling on edge and thinking about lashing out. Small things that you might normally ignore or brush away have a tendency to get under your skin. Take -2 to Composure rolls.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution:</u> This Condition is resolved when your character's anger causes you to do something that you might later regret about yourself or someone else, such as saying or doing something that might cause harm to a significant relationship (e.g., spreading a negative rumor, breaking something you or someone else owns).<br /> <br /> <u>Beat:</u> N/A.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You don't glean anything meaningful from the interaction between Valentine and Mathias before they leave. It seems like something anyone in this cabal might say about the Abyss. Valentine was most likely just trying to remind everyone of the risk of hubris for overreaching when casting spells.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll go with the suggestion for engaging in the Supernal riddle/philosophizing, as it's a neat idea. Take an Arcane Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Boomer gives a small smile and nods at you as you reveal the obsidian knife in your pocket. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Wow, three items from your first Highstorm. Granted, most of the things people pull out of those portals aren't true artifacts in the strictest sense. Some are kind of like artifacts but much weaker, but they can still be handy as spellcasting tools.&quot;</span> She looks around at the three objects and offers, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;If you'll allow me, I can try to learn their function. It would take more effort to determine if they're cursed, and like Valentine said, it's an inexact science. But learning what they do may help you decide what to do with them. We didn't bring this up yet, but the Mysterium collects and catalogues these things. No one can force you to turn them in, but anyone who lets the Mysterium borrow the item for a time can receive some knowledge or a small favor; if you give it to them outright, you can get a bigger favor. Lots of mages use them as bargaining tools, even if they're not Mystagogues.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer waits for permission, and then arranges the items in a small semi-circle in front of her. She holds her hands out with palms facing up and closes her eyes. You each sense a spell on your Periphery, and she tilts her head as if listening to something you can't perceive. After a moment, she opens her eyes and smiles.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;These each work like artifacts, but with fairly weak spell effects. This knife,&quot;</span> she gives the blade carefully to Ragnar, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;can be used to shape shadows. It seems like you need to draw the blade tip along some flat surface and 'draw' what you want to happen, and they'll animate. A Moros mage could also use it as a tool for casting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Next, she turns to the small pebble and hands it to Lynx. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;This is attuned to the Primal Wild, young Thyrsus, so you can use it as a basic Yantra -- a tool -- to fuel your casting. It also can mimic a Life Knowing spell that reveals living things nearby by speaking to it and setting it on the ground.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Finally, she holds the staff in both hands and gently returns it to Moonstone. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;This staff is attuned to the Aether. It seems well-crafted, perhaps a little better than a normal staff as far as a weapon goes. But it also can allow the user to pierce active deceptions -- hear lies as they are spoken, or see through illusions -- by planting it on the ground with your hands.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She adds, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Honestly, the items are weak enough that the spell effects probably won't be that useful or reliable, but they are convenient at the least.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Here are the stats/descriptions of the items, now revealed to you via a Prime Unveiling spell:<br /> <br /> <b>Knife of Shadow (Artifact 1)</b><br /> This small ritual knife has a hilt of steel and a blade of obsidian. Retrieved from a Highstorm by Ragnar. Contains the spell Shadow Sculpting (Death 1).<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 1<br /> Effective Arcana: 1<br /> Mana: 2/2<br /> Path Tool for Moros mages<br /> Effect: Mold and shape existing shadows in the area of effect into any likeness of your choice. Activated by holding the knife and tracing the blade tip on a solid surface (e.g., wall, floor) to \u201cdraw\u201d the desired effect (requires an instant action). 2 dice before spell factors. (Shadow Sculpting, 1 reach spent on instant casting.)<br /> <br /> The knife can be used as a weapon with the same stats as a normal knife: +0L damage, -1 initiative, Strength 1, Size 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Living Stone (Artifact 1)</b><br /> This is a small, round pebble that fits into the palm of your hand. It feels slightly warm to the touch. Retrieved from a Highstorm by Lynx. Contains the spell Web of Life (Life 1).<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 1<br /> Effective Arcana: 1<br /> Mana: 2/2<br /> Path Tool for Thyrsus mages<br /> Effect: Detect the presence of any living things nearby, which can be specified by a category (e.g., \u201chumans\u201d, \u201cinsects\u201d). Activated by speaking the desired target to the stone and setting it on the ground. 2 dice before spell factors. (Web of Life, 1 reach spent on instant casting.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Staff of Truth (Artifact 1)</b><br /> This long staff appears to be made of a pliable wood that is deceptively resilient. The surface of the staff is covered in intricate geometric runic carvings and feels slightly warm to the touch. Retrieved from a Highstorm by Phoenix. Contains the spell Pierce Deception (Prime 1).<br /> <br /> The staff can be used as a weapon with the following stats: +1L damage, -1 initiative, Strength 2, Size 4. Special: +1 Defense bonus against opponents who are unarmed or wield weapons of Size 1; two-handed (+1 Strength required if wielding with one hand).<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 1<br /> Effective Arcana: 1<br /> Mana: 2/2<br /> Path Tool for Obrimos mages<br /> Effect: Reveals \u201cactive\u201d untruths that you can perceive (e.g., see through illusions, recognize fraud or lies). Activated by holding the staff with both hands and planting one end on the ground. 2 dice before spell factors. (Pierce Deception, 1 reach spent on instant casting.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At the mention of the hail, Boomer nods slowly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It's different with each storm, but many of the Highstorms we see have very odd weather patterns. And some of them carry that quality you're talking about...Something that reminds you of the Abyss. It tends to send spirits scattering, but some of the darker ones -- hate or violence spirits, or shadow spirits -- seem attracted to it. At least, that's how...that's how Orca, our Thyrsus friend, described it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Your grief washes over you, threatening to drown you with sorrow. It's too much. You stand up abruptly and leave the room. You head down a hallway in the same direction as Mathias and Valentine, and find yourself in an empty sitting room. There are large bookshelves covering the wall, with hundreds and hundreds of texts that have old, worn binding. There are two more large, leather arm chairs and a padded footstool beside a small glass table with a vase of irises and lilies. You feel anger boiling inside of you along with the grief, and it kind of makes you want to just smash everything.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for the discussion on philosophy. You, too, gain the Irritable Condition described above, as well a a normal Beat for the dramatic failure on a mundane roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You hear Valentine and Mathias' voices drift into the room from an adjacent hallway. You can't quite make out all of the words, but you catch a few.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;...not your fault, Mathias.&quot;</span> Valentine's voice sounds sad. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;You warned...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Umbra at least should have...&quot;</span> Mathias sounds bitter, and his words are broken by long pauses. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;<i>Why? </i>I told...storm coming...How did...?</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can roll Wits + Composure for a perception roll to see if you hear more. Everyone in the other room can attempt as well, but at a -2 penalty due to the distance.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:55:58-07:00","id":984923,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: None [Wards and Signs, Potency 5, scene]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Fabled, Guilty, Abyssal Backlash (+1), Irritable<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 0/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Moonstone smiles at Ragnar and Phoenix's replies. Feels good to be the mentor for once. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;There's no right answer, but approaching it helps. You think on it more as you develop Gnosis. It's like a pearl forming around a grain of sand.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That being said- I've been considering it for years, and I feel like Phoenix right now. Maybe it helps to have a head start on magic.&quot; </span>Playfully smug, preening, examining his nails.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Moonstone, look...About the Arrows. Perhaps this is an opportunity. As a Sleepwalker, you fell in with an Order because of Hakim's influence. But as an Awakened mage, you have finally uncovered your <i>true</i> self. I think that truth may help guide you towards a greater mission, and while it's possible the Adamantine Arrow will still be the best organization to help you along with that...it might not be.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer is honest and frank, and it goes a long way toward making her words more palatable. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Why do the Awakened always say <i>true self?</i> Who was I until now? I thought I was free from the Lie.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's rhetorical, the kind of thing Sleepwalkers debate after their duties. But he listens carefully.<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;I'll remember that. Thank you for your candor.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He willingly passes the staff over with the others, lost in his reflection. Part of his awareness catches what Boomer says: (a tool for the Aether, of course it would be useless to him, but being able to see what's true and false would be very helpful...) He can always return to this memory if he wants more details.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Highstorm and the Abyssal taint, he chimes in: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;The hailstones burned out my Mana until Phoenix weather-warded me. And his ward disappeared when he passed through the portal. Physical contact with the black ice did it, not some ethereal curse- I could avoid it by hiding under an awning. But I was also resonant with Paradox at the time, no one else lost Mana. I'm fairly sure that sparked the reaction. I'm not a scientist, but maybe the source of the Abyssal taint was within the storm clouds themselves, where the hailstones formed. In the Fallen World, clouds are just cold air and water stuck together, but they also represent a Supernal symbol of storms and bad omens. Maybe the symbol of storms, itself, has been tainted in Chicago. The Chicago symbol for storms is clearly unique, I can promise you they don't have Highstorms in Los Angeles. What if the Highstorms (if they are a Supernal phenomenon) have caused Paradox recently and are resonant with the Abyss, as I was?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Man, you just set me up for a layup with that Condition. I've been waiting to do this since Mathias went off on Moonstone, now it makes much more sense.<br /> <br /> Perception-2: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444291\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Phoenix leaves. He can't stand it either. Moonstone hears voices and things breaking. <i>Good.</i><br /> <br /> For all the power of his magic, he sees nothing in the mirror. It just reflects his own ideas back at him, until they congeal. Much like Ragnar's dating divination, he's going to have to make his own answer to the questions.<br /> <br /> He gets up suddenly and says <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm going to check on Phoenix.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Still gripping his mirror tight, he leaves in the direction that the Obrimos warrior went, and hums a little tune. When he gets to the sitting room with the library and the fine accoutrements, he picks up a book at random off the shelf. There's an incredibly sharp contrast between the austere intellectualism of the sitting room, and the openly emotional rage and regret of the man inside it. Two minds in one place. It's inspirational.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting &quot;One Mind, Two Thoughts.&quot; 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for advanced duration, +1 reach to perform 2 instant actions at once. +1 paradox for Abyssal Backlash, 2 dice, going to contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444301\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a> Resolving Abyssal Backlash for 1 Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2, path tool 1, environment 1. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444302\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He's holding the book in one hand, opened to a random page, and his precious mirror in the other. The book is an old botany journal: this page happens to poetically describe how leaves sprout from branches. Moonstone visualizes a tree and lets the Pattern of his Mind bloom outwards, one trunk splitting into two branches, with the leaves of his thoughts scattered between them. One of the branches is assigned to deal with his grief and indignation and fury, and it rocks in a harsh Deathstorm wind. The other branch is assigned to focus on the task at hand with grace and poise, and it remains still in a light breeze. The leaves are across two branches, but it's all one tree.<br /> <br /> Moonstone looks down at his mirror and realizes that the person looking back is someone else, a different fork of his consciousness. One smiles serenely, the other wails and shouts, but they're together.<br /> <br /> Serene Moonstone puts the book away and looks up at Phoenix, steering well clear of his fists if necessary. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It's okay. I feel it too. I also lost someone I love. Sometimes when I'm around strong emotions, I can't stand it. I feel it too much, and I have to do something or I'll go crazy. I think we're a lot alike. Maybe.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Without offering anything else, he slips past Phoenix and into the hallway where Mathias and Valentine are arguing. He clears his throat for attention.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Mathias.&quot;</span> It's the first thing he's said to him since they came to the sanctum.<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;I can see that you're in pain. I think I understand now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He puts his mirror away in his bag, and takes off his ballcap too. He touches his hand to his cloak. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You think because I'm soft, you can hurt me, and expect me to tend your wounds after. But you don't get to hurt me because you're in pain. No one does! Never again!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He keeps talking, even if he's interrupted: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;If my master were alive, you would pay in <i>blood </i>for laying a finger on me. Since he has passed, I will rectify his name and honor instead.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And then there's a rush of Pandemonium as his Nimbus flares in the Fallen World, and Space warps in the hallway, and Moonstone is alive with magic and talking backwards and growing ten feet taller and smaller and upside-down with every word: <span style=\"color:#008080\"><i><b>&quot;I, Moonstone, Apprentice of Mind, Apprentice of Space, Apprentice of Time, Nameless and sworn to the Iron Gauntlet of Pandemonium, challenge you, Mathias, to the Duel Arcane. <u>Here.</u> <u>Now.</u> <u>Immediately.</u>&quot;</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In which Moonstone responds to grief in an unhealthy way. Just to make it completely clear that he's 100% serious, Moonstone spends 1 Mana from his Cloak (now at 7/10) to flare his Immediate Nimbus (page 89). It's visible even in the Fallen World. Not intending to apply his Nimbus Tilt, but here's the roll for Nimbus Strength just in case: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444310\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> <br /> I want to use knowledge of the Code Duello to incite Mathias to respond to the challenge in the same format Moonstone used, listing his Arcana ratings (Adept of Fate, etc). Manipulation 2, Politics 3 (Chicago Consilium): <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444312\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Resolving Irritable, I don't believe I get an Arcane Beat because I already did this scene. I would like to count this for my Bold Virtue. Moonstone was wronged by Mathias and he cowered before, but now he's standing up for himself and demanding justice, even against unlikely odds and very much against proper etiquette. And really, challenging someone to the Duel Arcane in their own Sanctum is pretty bold.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-10-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:54:48-07:00","id":985012,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">Here's a brain-teaser for you: the Supernal World is the source of the Fallen World. All true things originate in the Supernal. But the Supernal can only act by manifesting in the Fallen; for example, by the Awakening. The Fallen World contains good and virtuous things, but it also contains evil and impure things. Does that make the Supernal World complicit in evil?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">How...</span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\">naive.<i> If evil didn't originate from the Supernal, then it wouldn't be complicit; if it did, it's part of the world as a necessity, isn't it? Besides which, what </i>is<i> 'Evil'?</i></span><br /> <br /> Lynx holds his tongue, however. His eagerness and inexperience doesn't lead him to raise his voice much, not with the force of Moonstone and Phoenix and Ragnar dominating the conversation, at least from the side of the Nameless. He glances at Binder, pondering what the silent man must be thinking.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Primal Wild, huh...</span>&quot; Lynx mutters as he retrieves his pebble from Boomer and pockets it. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">A Yantra's neat, at least.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He paces around the room a little, keeping his senses peeled while he keeps to his own thoughts. He looks over at Ragnar during the man's declaration of Order preference.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I respect whatever decision you guys make, but me? I think I favor the Silver Ladder.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'll have to think about it. I don't think I have an inclination right now, one way or the other.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">So much at once. I'm lost. And... </span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Faen da<i>, why do I feel so misplaced?</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I'm going to check on Phoenix.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> They go from 5 to 4. Lynx looks at Boomer, at Ragnar, at Binder. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm not good at expressing myself. I have so many questions, but I don't know where to start.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Then he bristles, his nose turning to the door, a distortion of footsteps in his ears at first. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Did anyone else feel that? That's what you called Periphery, right? Only, there's something...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't like that...Nimbus, is it?</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I know I'm more of an... animal compared to you lot,</span>&quot; Lynx says as he closes his eyes, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">And that, as a Thyrsus, I'm inclined to go with my gut, but does it mean anything that I sometimes have a gut instinct to something that hasn't quite yet...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\"><i><b>I, Moonstone, Apprentice of Mind...</b></i></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Aaaand there it is.</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx doesn't think twice. He hurries down the hallway, dread washing over him momentarily. <i>Moonstone scares me.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">...<i><b>Apprentice of Space, Apprentice of Time, Nameless and sworn to the Iron Gauntlet of Pandemonium, challenge you, Mathias...</b></i></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Faen da...</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">...<i><b>to the Duel Arcane. <u>Here.</u> <u>Now.</u> <u>Immediately.</u></b></i></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He arrives only ten feet from Moonstone, staring at the warped world that unfolds around him. The dread raises the hairs on his arms as he takes a step back. <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Do I... Do I interfere? Only, it's Moonstone... </span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-10-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:03:26-07:00","id":985055,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 6/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;There's no right answer, but approaching it helps. You think on it more as you develop Gnosis. It's like a pearl forming around a grain of sand.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar smiles a little at Moonstone. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Okay, rocky start, but first impressions aren't permanent. </span></i>The conversation is edifying, and Ragnar almost feels like his understanding of magic has increased a little bit from the conversation. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well I guess that's the question, isn't it? Is the Supernal a conscious entity, or is it simply a neutral force that we can manipulate to good or bad ends?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He hands the black knife over to Boomer.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0099\">&quot;No one can force you to turn them in, but anyone who lets the Mysterium borrow the item for a time can receive some knowledge or a small favor; if you give it to them outright, you can get a bigger favor. Lots of mages use them as bargaining tools, even if they're not Mystagogues.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;It belongs in a museum, huh?&quot; </span>Ragnar smirks, and watches as she casts her spell. He assumes, based on his new knowledge of magic, that she is using a spell from the Prime Arcana to analyze the items.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF1493\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:deeppink\">This knife</span> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">can be used to shape shadows. It seems like you need to draw the blade tip along some flat surface and 'draw' what you want to happen, and they'll animate. A Moros mage could also use it as a tool for casting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar examines the knife with a mixture of caution and curiosity, like someone looking at a spider or snake. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Death Arcana, I take it? I don't think I have any talent for it, but this might be useful in a pinch. I might let the Mysterium have a look at it one of these days so they can catalogue it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF1493\">&quot;It's different with each storm, but many of the Highstorms we see have very odd weather patterns. And some of them carry that quality you're talking about...Something that reminds you of the Abyss. It tends to send spirits scattering, but some of the darker ones -- hate or violence spirits, or shadow spirits -- seem attracted to it. At least, that's how...that's how Orca, our Thyrsus friend, described it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;The hailstones burned out my Mana until Phoenix weather-warded me. And his ward disappeared when he passed through the portal. Physical contact with the black ice did it, not some ethereal curse- I could avoid it by hiding under an awning. But I was also resonant with Paradox at the time, no one else lost Mana. I'm fairly sure that sparked the reaction. I'm not a scientist, but maybe the source of the Abyssal taint was within the storm clouds themselves, where the hailstones formed. In the Fallen World, clouds are just cold air and water stuck together, but they also represent a Supernal symbol of storms and bad omens. Maybe the symbol of storms, itself, has been tainted in Chicago. The Chicago symbol for storms is clearly unique, I can promise you they don't have Highstorms in Los Angeles. What if the Highstorms (if they are a Supernal phenomenon) have caused Paradox recently and are resonant with the Abyss, as I was?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar sits forward, suddenly eager, just as he does whenever he thinks there's a potential breakthrough on a topic, or when somebody puts forward an intriguing hypothesis. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well, between the lightning and wind, storms would probably fall under Forces. So I guess we could have some Obrimoi and other mages skilled with Fate and Prime take a look the next time there's a Highstorm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> First Phoenix leaves, then Moonstone. He's now left with just Binder, Lynx, and Boomer. He looks around and tries to dispel the tension. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Um, anybody got cards?&quot; </span>He looks around at the others, sees that none of them seem receptive, and sighs.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Look. Boomer. I know this might not be the best time for this, but I think I want Mathias to take me on as an apprentice. So far, he's the only other Acanthus I've met, and he's a member of the Silver Ladder. And I think I want to join them. So...&quot; </span>he stands from where he was sitting, and walks out into the hallway-<br /> <br /> - Where he's greeted by a very irate Moonstone shouting at Mathias. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You think because I'm soft, you can hurt me, and expect me to tend your wounds after. But you don't get to hurt me because you're in pain. No one does! Never again! </span><span style=\"color:#008080\">If my master were alive, you would pay in <i>blood </i>for laying a finger on me. Since he has passed, I will rectify his name and honor instead.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Then the fabric of space goes wonky, like the effects of a funhouse mirror made real, centered around Moonstone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><i><b>&quot;I, Moonstone, Apprentice of Mind, Apprentice of Space, Apprentice of Time, Nameless and sworn to the Iron Gauntlet of Pandemonium, challenge you, Mathias, to the Duel Arcane. <u>Here.</u> <u>Now.</u><u>Immediately.</u>&quot;</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Oh Merlin's beard, you have got to be fucking kidding me.</span></b></i><br /> <br /> Ragnar immediately rushes forward, and places himself directly between Moonstone and Mathias. He immediately allows his Nimbus to flare in challenge to Moonstone's: the floor around him becomes covered in a century's worth of dust in a moment, the walls stain with mildew and age, the wood begins to rot.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone, please! Think about this for a second. Yes, Mathias may have acted inappropriately, but given what happened today and what he's been through, I'm sure it wasn't intentional. Are you really going to throw away the only source of information and help that the rest of us have?! Please, stand down. Or if you're not willing to, then allow me, Ragnar, Apprentice of Fate, Apprentice of Time, Initiate of Life, Initiate of Space, Nameless and sworn to the Lunargent Thorn of Arcadia, to duel you, Moonstone, in his stead, in this time and place.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm going to attempt Social Maneuvering on Moonstone to try and persuade him to abandon the duel, or fight Ragnar instead. Moonstone's Resolve and Composure are both at 4, so that's four doors. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 2 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444345\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-10-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:03:36-07:00","id":985093,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would venture 5 doors, because backing down would involve acting against his Virtue, Bold!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A challenger! Moonstone trembles with rage, raises his mirror at the resplendent Ragnar and says: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Does my dignity offend you? Where were you when he struck me and screamed in my face? Laughing. But my grievance is with your master, proud Ragnar, not you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Mind 2 &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; on Ragnar. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for sensory, 1 reach for scene duration, 1 reach for a complex command. Paradox is 4 dice, -2 from using my dedicated tool, -1 for spending 1 Mana from the Cloak (now at 6/10). 1 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444350\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2. -2 to raise Potency to 3. +3 from spending a Willpower (which I presumably regain from Bold.) 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444351\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Moonstone instills the command &quot;Step aside, be still, and remain silent.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Imago forms. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Your student is loyal. Accept my challenge and I will break the enchantment.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:15:59-07:00","id":985114,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Active Sight:</b> Prime (Peripheral after 1 turn) | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 0/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I take my anger out on the more durable items in the room. Hope I don't damage anything too awfully bad. I mostly end up punching a wall anyway. A few minutes of that and I'm leaning on it, my head pressing down on my crossed arms. I can't help but catch a few words from Valentine and Mathias, but I don't wanna eavesdrop, so I ignore it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It's okay. I feel it too. I also lost someone I love. Sometimes when I'm around strong emotions, I can't stand it. I feel it too much, and I have to do something or I'll go crazy. I think we're a lot alike. Maybe,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> How long was he there? Y'know what? I don't care, they could probably hear me yelling anyways. He doesn't do a very good job at comforting me, but at least he's trying. Gotta give him credit for that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Thanks,&quot;</span> I reply simply, not turning to look at him.<br /> <br /> He leaves and then says something to Valentine or Mathias, don't know which, don't really care. But then I sense his signature magic, and that does get my attention.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><i><b>&quot;I, Moonstone, Apprentice of Mind, Apprentice of Space, Apprentice of Time, Nameless and sworn to the Iron Gauntlet of Pandemonium, challenge you, Mathias, to the Duel Arcane. <u>Here.</u> <u>Now.</u><u>Immediately.</u>&quot;</b></i></span><br /> <br /> Okay, this is...interesting. On one hand, it's pathetic. Mathias gave you a dose of what you needed. But then, this'll give me a chance to see what a Duel Arcane looks like, so I swivel around my back to the door frame, watching it all unfold.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone, please! Think about this for a second. Yes, Mathias may have acted inappropriately, but given what happened today and what he's been through, I'm sure it wasn't intentional. Are you really going to throw away the only source of information and help that the rest of us have?! Please, stand down. Or if you're not willing to, then allow me, Ragnar, Apprentice of Fate, Apprentice of Time, Initiate of Life, Nameless and sworn to the Lunargent Thorn of Arcadia, to duel you, Moonstone, in his stead, in this time and place.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Enter Ragnar, the plot thickens.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Does my dignity offend you? Where were you when he struck me and screamed in my face? Laughing.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He didn't laugh Moonstone. No one did.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;But my grievance is with your master, proud Ragnar, not you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Wait a minute, he's casting something. I open my senses to what, and...<br /> <br /> No. This will not stand. I can forgive a genuine mistake, but that is a deliberate act.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Improvised casting<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dispel Magic (Prime 1, Corebook 166)</u></b><br /> <b>Reach:</b> 2 free; 4 used for instant casting, sensory range, and Lasting effect<br /> <b>Paradox:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444362\" target=\"_blank\">Overreach 2 - 2 DT = Chance die \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <b>Containment:</b> None.<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> DT for Paradox penalty<br /> <b>Factors:</b> PSF Potency 3 (-2)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444365\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Prime 2 + 3 WP - 2 Factors = 4 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After I destroy the spell, I rush the caster to put him in a lock.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Grappling Moonstone. <s>Would this count as an ambush? I mean, sure Phoenix isn't hidden, but it would still be a surprise to Moonstone, right?</s><br /> <br /> Just to settle things easier, I'll simply have Phoenix make the grapple an All-Out Attack.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444366\" target=\"_blank\">Strength 3 + Brawl 4 + 2 AOA - 7 Defense = 2 dice (ignoring last 5) \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:03:56-07:00","id":985168,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaaand there goes the Mind spell<span style=\"color:#008080\">, </span>easily torn from his grasp by Phoenix's magic. Unexpected complication. Moonstone grits his teeth and quotes poetry:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Though I die and die again,<br /> though I die one hundred deaths,<br /> Long after my bones have turned to dust,<br /> whether I have a soul or not:<br /> My one red heart, forever loyal to my Lord,<br /> will never fade away.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And Phoenix goes in for the body check! Moonstone slows down Time at the sight of physical danger, giving him a precious moment to turn away.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 Mana from the Cloak (now at 6/10) to activate Time Armor reflexively.<br /> <br /> Clearly I'm biased, but I think Defense applies here. Moonstone talked to Phoenix 10 seconds ago, he's totally aware that he's present and just broke his spell, and it's clearly a tense situation so he'd be on guard. Moonstone has Defense 7, or 9 with Mage Armor, so Phoenix would either fail or roll a chance die for the grapple, depending on how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> handles it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T22:04:05-07:00","id":985267,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Boomer nods at your observations. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;There are a number of mages who have researched the Highstorms, including Mathias, and they've made some similar points. But their research suggests this is all deeper than any one mage or event; they believe that the Highstorms reflect the war between the Exarchs and the mages of the time before the Fall. The portals go back, they believe, to times and places of significance in the war for Ascension.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> While you listen, you make out Mathias' voice distinctly from the other room. Although it's faint, he made a strong negative impression, so your mind focuses on his speech with speed and clarity. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Umbra at least should have known better,&quot;</span> you hear him say sadly. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;<i>Why?</i> I told her that a storm was coming. How did I know? The spells have never seemed to work for that purpose, but if it did, it meant a storm of terrible proportions. I should have convinced her...&quot;</span> His voice drifts into obscurity once more. <br /> <br /> You feel emboldened by your Mind spell, which allows you to focus on two distinct actions at the same time. You draw upon your inner magic and flex your will, causing your Nimbus to flare as you challenge him to the Duel Arcane. Mathias hears your challenge issued like a thrown gauntlet, but he shakes his head. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I apologize for striking you earlier,&quot;</span> he begins to say. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Valentine is right, perhaps I--&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His words cut off abruptly as you cast your Mind spell and attempt to coerce Ragnar into obeying your command. Although Phoenix quickly intervenes and counters your spell as you cast it, your intentions are clear. Phoenix lunges at you, but with Time on your side, you just barely manage to slow down time around you enough to sidestep his grapple. Mathias looks at you with shock and anger.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can gain WP back per Bold Virtue, yes. There's more at stake here and it fits much better in this situation than earlier. <br /> <br /> Although your spell was quickly dispelled, you attempted to use magic to coerce another person against their well. Make a roll for an Act of Hubris at the Understanding level (3 dice).<br /> <br /> You can apply Defense here because you're angry and in a combative mood. Because you used Time Armor, you have Defense 9, reducing Phoenix's attack to a chance roll that fails.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Boomer grins at you. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Honestly, I think Mathias would be glad to hear that. He's been thinking of taking a pupil lately, and I think it would be good for him. He is a good man and a fair mentor,&quot;</span> she shares. <br /> <br /> Commotion in the distance, followed by spells on your Periphery, cause Boomer to stand and roll her eyes. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;For fuck's sake, this drama is really getting old fast.&quot;</span> She and Lynx follow shortly after you get up to check on Moonstone and Phoenix.<br /> <br /> Moonstone's spell settles on you, and before you know what you're doing, your mouth snaps shut and you start to move out of the way. But then Phoenix reaches out and casts away the spell, and the fog surrounding your mind burns away.<br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You see the magic around Ragnar burst apart as you rip through it with Prime instinctively. But when you try to grab Moonstone, he somehow spins out of the way with supernatural speed, evading your grasp.<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;ENOUGH!&quot;</span> Mathias yells over the commotion. Boomer crosses her arms and frowns at Moonstone, while Valentine shrugs and smiles knowingly. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;It was wrong of me to hit you, and I let my anger interfere with my judgment,&quot;</span> Mathias admits. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;But you <i>must</i> learn control and discipline, over your magic and your emotions. You have witnessed magic all your life, Moonstone, but if you do not learn restraint, your experience will lead you down the path of hubris and ruin,&quot;</span> he warns. His tone hardens. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;If you so demand it, very well. I, Mathias, <i>Adept</i> of Fate, Disciple of Time, Apprentice of Forces, th\u00e9arch of the Silver Ladder and sworn to the Lunargent Thorn of Arcadia, accept your challenge to the Duel Arcane.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer throws up her hands in protest with a muttered <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;<i>Fuck</i> this noise,&quot;</span> and Valentine merely shakes his head. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I will second for Mathias,&quot;</span> he chimes in quickly.<br /> <br /> Boomer sighs. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I'll second for Moonstone. Just so it's fair. I'm not going to stand up for your <i>honor</i> or anything,&quot;</span> she explains to him, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;but I promise to make sure the rules are followed.&quot;</span> She turns to Mathias with a questioning look. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;You're serious, aren't you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias nods. His eyes never leave Moonstone's face. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;We must set the terms. If I win, I want you to complete a private lesson, once with me and once with Valentine, to impress upon you the importance of discipline. I also want you to apologize to Ragnar for attempting to coerce him with magic. What are your stakes?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:03:40-07:00","id":985300,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: One Mind Two Thoughts (Potency 1, scene) [Wards and Signs, Potency 5, scene]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Fabled, Guilty<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> At the lowest point, he feels like himself again. Clarity. The image refocuses, the pond grows still.<i> I challenged a much more powerful, friendly mage to the Duel Arcane. I hurt Ragnar. I made Phoenix very, very upset. I disappointed Boomer.</i><br /> <br /> <i>I've really fucked up, haven't I?</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Divergent returns to its Passive state as Moonstone gets full Willpower back. Rolling for Act of Hubris, 3 dice +1 for acting in defense of his Virtue: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444455\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes,</a> or 1 success if Virtue doesn't apply. +1 Arcane Beat for risking Wisdom loss.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He closes his eyes and takes a deep breath for just a second.<br /> <br /> Serene Moonstone thinks: <i>Yes. I have really fucked up.</i><br /> <br /> Grieving Moonstone thinks: <i>I wish you were here. Is this what you want?</i><br /> <br /> Serene Moonstone thinks: <i>I wasn't thinking clearly. But I can't back down now.</i><br /> <br /> Grieving Moonstone thinks: <i>I can't do this without you. If you were with me, it would be okay.</i><br /> <br /> Serene Moonstone thinks: <i>Am I the villain?</i><br /> <br /> Grieving Moonstone thinks: <i>I have to believe this is what you would want me to do. You're all I have.</i><br /> <br /> The second passes. He opens his eyes. A quick word to Boomer: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As for Mathias, he meets his gaze and speaks clearly. He can't bear to look at Ragnar or Phoenix or anyone else, and he needs to focus, anyway. Center. Relax. Flow.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So here's what Moonstone is trying to do here. Explicitly invoking Mathias' Vice of Pride, which he learned from his Know Nature spell earlier, he wants to propose stakes that Mathias will find insulting. He should be <i>infuriated </i>that this scrawny little Abyss-tempting Mind-controlling gender-nonconforming Sleepwalker is saying this to his face, in his own Sanctum, in front of his own cabal, at a time like this. Based on everyone's reactions so far, it shouldn't be that difficult, haha.<br /> <br /> The reason that he's doing this is to <b>goad or trick Mathias into attacking rather than defending on his turn for as long as possible.</b> He's trying to mundanely play on his Vice to influence his behavior during the Duel. And he'll use One Mind, Two Thoughts to give himself a better chance of it. He's going to do a Teamwork action with himself, having one train of thought (Mental) develop a plan and choose the best possible approach while the other train (Social) does the talking and presents the stakes. I hope this is okay, this is the reason I cast the spell!<br /> <br /> First train of thought, supporting action with Wits+Politics (Consilium), 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444459\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Second train of thought, primary action. Manipulation 2, Subterfuge 2, teamwork +2, and I'll resolve Fabled for +5. 11 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444461\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Resolving Fabled gives me 1 Beat and 1 Willpower, so I'm at 8/8 again. I'd like to apply the following Condition to myself, a variant of Steadfast:<br /> <br /> <b>Determined</b><br /> You're at your best in a battle of wills. When you're in a contested action and your opponent rolled more successes than you, you may resolve this Condition to instead treat the action as if you rolled 1 more success than your opponent. This does not count as an exceptional success, even if you would roll 5 or more successes.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>This Condition is resolved as described above.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Your words are water, and you know nothing about my life, Witch. But your stakes are agreeable, and I accept them. I propose the following terms, in accordance with the Code Duello: both duelists will enter the squared circle with no active spells affecting them. There will be no outside interference, mundane or magical, to affect the outcome of the duel. The outcome of the duel will be publicly announced by the defeated party at the next gathering of the Consilium- in a few days, I believe. These terms will be enforced by our seconds. Is this acceptable?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Assuming that it is, he proceeds. He's controlling his breathing, putting his mirror away, trying to calm down. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Now. My stakes. If I win, I want you to explain the significance of victory in the Duel Arcane to the mages gathered here, in order to further their magical education. I want you to get on your knees in front of me, formally thank me for saving your and the others' lives from the Gulmoth, request my forgiveness for striking, insulting, and disrespecting me after I put my life on the line for your sake, and kiss my hand before rising to your feet. I want all consequences for this Duel to fall on myself, rather than the other Nameless mages- as you can see, they are not with me. And when you announce my victory before the Consilium, I want you to acknowledge that the Thunderbolt Guardian Hakim is your better as a mage and a man, and apologize for dishonoring his memory by assaulting his favored student, and...and dear companion.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His voice quavers a little at the end there, but he catches himself. He's trying to focus on Serious Arcane Duelist mode, but it's hard not to slip into natural language. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I am not your student, Mathias. I am not your servant, or your disciple, or your friend. I am your equal. I will teach you discipline. I will show you the fear I feel when a white man twice my size shoves my queer brown ass against a brick wall in a dark alley and insults me for the crime of saving his life, and the people I saved watch and do nothing. I will show you the power of my magic. Defeating and humiliating you in front of your own cabal will give me special pleasure.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Deep breath. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;This is my gift to you. This is how I display my Wisdom. Are these terms agreeable to you?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T02:39:21-07:00","id":985326,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 1/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> Moonstone dodges just before I grab him. Mage Armor, I suspect. I turn heel to face him and start casting a spell to give me an ed-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;ENOUGH!&quot;</span> Mathias abruptly commands, I stop spellcasting to listen, but I still face Moonstone, watching him closely.<br /> <br /> So they go through with the Duel Arcane, Mathias offers reasonable, if rather light terms. But whatever, they're not my terms. Then it's Moonstone's turn, and my blood boils. You saved us? You almost got me and Ragnar killed! I did the heavy-lifting anyways, you simply landed the final blow. Putting your life on the line? We were all in danger, no thanks to you. In fact, while I was beating that freak into a bloody pulp, you hid in the shadows. <i>You</i> will teach <i>him</i> discipline? You just abused your magic on Ragnar, don't you dare talk of discipline like you know what it is!<br /> <br /> This guy is a ticking time bomb. No way I'm letting him have my staff now. But I'll have to wait after the duel.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's fairly obvious to anyone who looks that he is outright furious with Moonstone.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T02:51:02-07:00","id":985329,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 5/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I am not your student, Mathias. I am not your servant, or your disciple, or your friend. I am your equal. I will teach you discipline. I will show you the fear I feel when a white man twice my size shoves my queer brown ass against a brick wall in a dark alley and insults me for the crime of saving his life, and the people I saved watch and do nothing. I will show you the power of my magic. Defeating and humiliating you in front of your own cabal will give me special pleasure.<br /> <br /> This is my gift to you. This is how I display my Wisdom. Are these terms agreeable to you?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Moonstone's words trigger something in Lynx. A small tinge of rage - no - a raging river of it. He clenches his fists, and when he speaks, his voice is a roar. His own Nimbus flares - the hallway's shadows twist into that of lions and tigers, all pacing around the group with anger in every stomp.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx triggers his Immediate Nimbus by spending a Mana. Probably by accident.</b></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">...Really? <b>REALLY!?</b> Ragnar hurling himself in front of that Gulmoth thing to distract it is 'watching and doing nothing'? Phoenix punching the absolute <i>shit</i> out of that...that <b><i>THING</i></b> is <b><i>doing NOTHING</i>!?</b> How deluded are you!? Discipline my bloody arse, I don't know if you summoning that Gulmoth was a mistake or not, but right now you are being a self-obsessed <i>twat</i>, so indulged in your own fucking pride that you're disrespecting everyone around you helping you rectify your mistake, just so you can have the pettiest piece of 'vengeance',</span>&quot; Lynx's voice drips with exquisite sarcasm, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">that I have ever heard of!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Deep breaths.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Is this what mages do?</span>&quot; He asks frantically, lowering his voice. His Nimbus weakens, but his anger doesn't subside. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Or is this the exception to the rule, Boomer? Valentine?</span>&quot; He glances at Mathias. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Is pride so bloody important in this world? We're, what, three people? Four?</span>&quot; He glances at Ragnar and Phoenix, and looks for Binder, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Who have just taken our first step into this wonderful world, and you think <i>this</i> is the perfect way to show me - show <i>us</i>&quot;, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">he corrects himself,</span><span style=\"color:#800000\"> &quot;That this is <i>magic</i></span>?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Calm down! Come on...</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx bites his lip as he looks at the lot of them, bites it until he draws blood. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">If you'll excuse me,</span>&quot; he grumbles through gritted teeth as he turns around, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'll remove myself before I yell some fucking more.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He strides back to the room where they gathered, and once out of sight, buries his face in his hands. <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Today's too much.</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:38:31-07:00","id":985363,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar looks around in desperation. Everybody is angry, particularly Moonstone.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i> He's lashing out at anybody and everybody in sight. It's almost like he... </i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar attempts Perception to work out what Moonstone's feelings towards Hakim were. Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444519\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The truth hits him like a lightning bolt. <i>He loved him.</i><br /> <br /> He needs to act. The situation is hitting something of a tipping point- he doesn't need Fate or Time to know that, and so he reaches out for magic once more, for the spell he first knew when he Awakened, and tries to draw the threads of Fate around himself. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar attempts to cast his Exceptional Luck Praxis on himself. He has one free Reach, which he spends on Instant Casting. Gnosis 1 + Fate 2 + Path Tool 1 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444524\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. He will grant himself a boon of dice equal to Potency (2) on Empathy rolls.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ragnar speaks up once again. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Please, both of you! This is pointless. It's nothing more than two grieving men clawing at each other.&quot; </span>He turns to Mathias. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Mathias... you're dealing with the deaths of two cabal mates due to the Deathstorm. You're obviously going through a lot of pain right now, but is this what they would've wanted?&quot; </span>He then turns to Moonstone. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200b&quot;Moonstone... I could be really off base here, but you loved Hakim, didn't you? And more than just the love of an apprentice for his master. Is this really the best way you can honor his memory?&quot; </span>He pauses, and then continues. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;But if that's not enough, then please, honor my first request as your apprentice,&quot; </span>he bows slightly to Mathias,<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"> &quot;and as your </span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">cabalmate,&quot; </span>he bows just as deeply to Moonstone,<span style=\"color:#0000cd\"> &quot;to drop this. Please.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Ragnar is attempting to talk Mathias and Moonstone down from the Duel Arcane by appealing to their emotions. Manipulation 3 + Empathy 1 + Exceptional Luck 2 = 6 dice -&gt;<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444529\" target=\"_blank\"> 0 successes</a>. I tried.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:58:05-07:00","id":985449,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LL</b>OOOOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 4</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I actually think we've seen you before, Binder,&quot;</span> Valentine chimes in. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Mathias came and dropped off some books at your store that had some rituals and theory about Supernal magic.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder blinks at the implication that Mathias may have essentially caused his Awakening. He's... not sure what to think of that. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Really? Do you recall their titles?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Should one of the texts be the book with the demon summoning ritual, he'll ask: <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Mathias, were you able to tell that book would trigger my awakening? Unfortunately, I seem to have, ah, misplaced it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> If it isn't, he'll promise to give those books a closer look, but keep his thoughts about the mysterious summoning tome to himself.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;My experience with the Supernal seems to suggest that it is neither good nor evil, just true.&quot;</span> He shrugs. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Is the teacher who informs you of the existence of evil complicit in it's existence?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">+1 Arcane Beat for participating in the discussion! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm older than I look.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>That</i> gets a double-take from Binder. <i>Magical life-extension? Is it possible that I've been thinking of him as a kid when he's actually my age? Or older?</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;We...We lost two of our cabal members in the Deathstorm. Our Thyrsus and Moros mages. I'm sorry.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There's so much death, so much pain. And if those numbers are right - a third dead in this Deathstorm - this isn't the exception, this is the rule. <i>The world that we're entering is in mourning.</i><br /> <br /> Marlin is suddenly struck by how much he has to lose. The thought is terrifying.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;This isn't normal, right? This amount of danger and death - it's unprecedented?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Now. My stakes....&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder listens to Moonstone's diatribe, trying to fit it with what he knows of him. <i>I know I only met him a short while ago, but he seems like a different person almost minute to minute...</i><br /> <br /> <i>Separate. Allow time to cool down. Talk over emotions with a sympathetic party. Exchange apologies. That's what you do. But I don't have any authority in this situation. And I don't think Moonstone would react positively to any perceived condescension...</i><br /> <br /> While Binder is paralyzed by indecision, Ragnar acts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;Please, both of you! This is pointless....&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I agree with Ragnar. At the very least, let's allow for some time to cool down,&quot;</span> (significant look at Moonstone) <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;and think this over.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":".  Wow my spelling is bad. 10-13-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:28:35-07:00","id":985911,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I like the idea of goading him into attacking, and approve of that tactic. You're absolutely right that Mathias would be infuriated.<br /> <br /> I am not okay with making a Teamwork action with yourself, even despite the spell. Teamwork is based on two people doing the same action at the same time; your spell is about one person doing different actions at the same time. That seems like a convoluted way to give yourself bonuses. Consequently, I will subtract 2 dice from your primary roll; however, it's a moot point because it still gets an exceptional success. You can take Determined as suggested.<br /> <br /> Mathias' Vice is Pride, and I think accepting your terms for these stakes is something he would only do because you're calling him out on his ego. But he's not going to blindly attack the whole time; he's smart and wants to win, and his Vice isn't Wrath or Hatred.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With each word, Mathias' body tenses more. He seems to be absolutely <i>seething</i> with barely-contained fury. When you finish, he doesn't move, simply staring at you with contempt. <br /> <br /> Lynx's display of his Nimbus draws Boomer's gaze, and Ragnar's appeal gets a raised eyebrow from Valentine. But Mathias' eyes are fixated on Moonstone in a glare. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I accept,&quot;</span> Mathias suddenly replies. His voice is a blade, cold steel quietly being pulled from its sheath. Boomer looks like she wants to tear her mohawk out in annoyance; Valentiner just stares intently at Moonstone with unblinking eyes, as if trying to read you. When Lynx leaves the room, Boomer gives a questioning look to Mathias and leaves the room. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Shortly after you leave the room, you hear quiet footsteps, and then your realize that Boomer is there. She sits down on a chair near you and lounges back, crossing her arms across her chest. At first she says nothing, just trying to give you space. Then, after a few minutes, she says, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Mathias always had a rough time backing down from a fight when someone insulted him,&quot;</span> she sighs. The punk woman runs a hand through her hair. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;And I know it doesn't look like it, but Mathias cares about helping you all, even Moonstone. He...&quot;</span> She pauses, seemingly conflicted. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Mathias...lost someone once, someone close to him, from the effects of Paradox and hubris. He has dedicated his Awakened life to make sure it never happens again, if he can help it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer smiles at you, although it's tinged with worry. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;The Duel Arcane is actually a safe and reasonable alternative here. It allows mages at conflict with each other to cast magic as <i>if</i> they were about to attack, but without causing actual physical harm. It kinda feels like being socked to the gut and pulled through a white water rapids by a hook in your nose,&quot;</span> she grins, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;but it won't actually cause wounds. Not the kind you can see, anyway.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer stands, then turns to you and offers her hand. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I think you'll really want to see this,&quot;</span> she suggests. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Who knows. Some day you may very well be fighting in one of these.&quot;</span> Her smile tells you she's trying to make light of the situation, but she also means it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You twist Fate and pull it around you like a cloak. You say the perfect words, but they don't strike true this time, falling on deaf ears. Mathias has made his mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> <i>Earlier:</i><br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;No, I'm sorry, I don't remember them exactly. I used to pick the topics at random after using a Fate spell to maximize my efforts, but it never seems to make a difference. Still, I figured it never hurt,&quot;</span> he smiles.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;This level of catastrophe from one Highstorm cannot be a coincidence,&quot;</span> Valentine says. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;There are several hundred mages in Chicago, perhaps 300 or 400, at any one time. To lose almost 10 percent in one storm is unheard of. It has everyone on edge, out of fear that it will happen again, even though no one knows why, how, or even <i>what</i> precisely happened.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;A small few go missing after each Highstorm, but the rewards are excellent, too,&quot;</span> Mathias points out.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>Now:</i><br /> Your reasoning falls on deaf ears, too. Neither man is willing to listen to you. <br /> <br /> Mathias speaks again. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Come. Let us be done with this foolishness.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b> (or minus Lynx if he doesn't come)<br /> Valentine leads the group down a long hallway towards a very large, empty room with hardwood floors and a tiled area in one corner. It somewhat resembles a gym, but there are scuff marks on the floor that look like they're from a piano and bench. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;It's a multi-purpose room,&quot;</span> Valentine grins.<br /> <br /> Mathias reverently sets down all of his tools, extra charms, and his old silver coin on a bench along a wall. Boomer orders the spectators to line up on either end of the room around the perimeter, and asks Moonstone and Mathias to face each other. Mathias offers a formal, if stilted, salute, and then he adopts a stance that resembles a fencing position.<br /> <br /> When the duelists signal their readiness, she clears her threat and intones loudly, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;The words have been spoken, the terms agreed upon.&quot;</span> Boomer kneels and places both palms on the floor. There is an explosion of light and a ringing of bells, and a pure white light extends in a perfect circle around the room, drawing itself to create a loop surrounding the two combatants. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Let the Duel Arcane commence.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias narrows his eyes, preparing to strike.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Moonstone, roll Initiative with a modifier equal to Wits + Composure (so +7 for you).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444751\" target=\"_blank\">Initiative</a>: <b>7</b>. Looks like you go first!<br /> <br /> As far as the actual rules, I feel like the core book is really vague here. I think it's just Attribute + Arcanum roll, and you only need one success. Each extra success will add to your next dice pool used in the duel, whether for defending or attacking. You can only open one Door per attack. Your actions allowed are either attacking, defending, or negotiating (so it takes up your attack/defense option for that round). No other modifiers allowed to the roll because you're already representing your Willpower as Doors.<br /> <br /> If you want to defend, announce it as soon as the corresponding attack roll is made. Ties count as success for the defender. (Per normal rules, I think you technically reroll, but I want to make this move quickly so we can get back to the narrative action for everyone else.) If you successfully defend, the attacker needs to pick a new Arcanum until you break through the current Door.<br /> <br /> Make sense? Let me know if there are other rules or guidelines I'm forgetting.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-11-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:17:20-07:00","id":985960,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: One Mind Two Thoughts (Potency 1, scene) [Wards and Signs, Potency 5, scene]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 8/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 2/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b><br /> </div> Lynx detonates. Moonstone flinches, shame-faced, and can't find the words to respond before the young man leaves. This isn't how he imagined it would feel. They'll have to have words later. If he gets a chance, at this rate.<br /> <br /> Ragnar and Binder advise caution, and his words are well-chosen. Moonstone listens to them, sincerely, and drops his guard a little to glance at both. One line almost makes him melt: <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone... I could be really off base here, but you loved Hakim, didn't you? And more than just the love of an apprentice for his master. Is this really the best way you can honor his memory?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> When they offer a way out, he shuts his eyes and breathes. Quiet, but loud enough to hear: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;everything i did, i did for him. now he's gone. but i'm still here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He rests a hand on his forehead. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;i don't know what he wants from me. but i have to believe this is what he would do. he always had to be right. since he died, i'm not thinking straight again. i'm sharp and then i'm dull, over and over. i need help. i need him, to tell me what to do. i'm useless on my own.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moment of clarity. He narrows his eyes as a lightbulb goes off: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;This is exactly how we lost his cabal, isn't it? Hubris.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His whole body is tense as Mathias accepts. One last word to Ragnar and Binder: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Too late.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Q: Is this really happening?<br /> A: This is really happening.</i><br /> <br /> He follows the others into the multi-purpose room. His doubts are dismissed for his own security, as are his spells. He lets his two thoughts merge back into one, and feels whole again. He unclasps the death's-head moth on the Cloak and lets the magic fade. Sheds his leather jacket, his ballcap, and his gloves, and reverently folds the Cloak- clearly taking a second to smell it and hold it close and sigh before setting it down on another bench. Gingerly sets his precious mirror and messenger bag on top of the pile. He's standing in boots and jeans and thick-framed glasses and bandaged hands and a racerback top. With fewer layers covering his body, it's more clear that he's not cis and that he's really quite fit.<br /> <br /> When instructed to do so, he stands opposite Mathias and offers a similarly unenthusiastic salute. His ready stance is more like an opening pose in ballet. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Ready.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The bells ring, the light bursts, he opens his Sight to the Supernal World. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Let the Duel Arcane commence.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xh7yNwdKaqo\" target=\"_blank\"><b>[BATTLE START]</b></a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444838\" target=\"_blank\">13</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone<br /> Turn 1 | Initiative 13 | Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined<br /> Doors:</b> OOOOOOOO<br /> <br /> It feels so different as a duelist than a spectator. Not even close. He really and truly has no idea what he's gotten himself into. But he can't let it show.<br /> <br /> He forms an Imago, and the runes and symbols shine around him, announcing what he <i>could </i>do. <i><b>SPACE - COMPELLING - ISOLATION - TRAP</b></i><br /> <br /> The Imago of his intended spell suggests Mathias trapped in an infinitely large room, with an impenetrable crowd of anonymous people who can't hear him shouting at them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Wits+Space: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444844\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:57:04-07:00","id":986031,"title":"","content":"<b>Everyone</b><br /> To your mundane eyes, there's nothing really happening here. Moonstone and Mathias are simply...staring each other down. Beads of sweat begin to form on their faces, but otherwise nothing noteworthy happens. <br /> <br /> Boomer instructs, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Open your Sight to the Truth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Anyone who does so sees the Imagos forming vividly, the potential for spells that could happen but the mages have not actually cast. Waves of emotion and mana are swirling in a torrential storm before your eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mathias<br /> Doors: XOOOOO</b><br /> <br /> The older mage yells in anger, shaking his head to clear his mind. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You think that I owe you for saving <i>me</i>?&quot;</span> he chides you. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;It was your hubris that brought that creature into this world, your <i>arrogance</i> that nearly cost your companions their lives!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He extends his hands and intones in High Speech. The words are foreign to you all, but the meaning behind them is clear all the same as they ring with Supernal truth. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;<b>Behold your Destiny if your path continues.</b>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The room darkens. A scene reveals itself from the Imago, of Moonstone standing alone, everyone he cared for around him dead and destroyed at his hand. The form of the mage stands in the center of the carnage, laughing. <br /> <br /> But the Imago flickers, and the image of Moonstone that Mathias creates isn't quite right. Mathias' emotions interfere with his willworking. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attacking with Presence + Fate: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444865\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:55:04-07:00","id":986051,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate and Time)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> Ragnar feels crushed when Mathias and Moonstone refuse his offer. Out of morbid fascination, he follows the others down the hall, he heart somewhere down around his ankles. <br /> <br /> He receives a pleasant- and embarrassing- surprise when they appear to simply stand their and work their wills. At Boomer's suggestion, he opens his eyes to the Supernal, studying the proceedings through Fate and Time. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Of course. Agonistic behavior. There's too few of us to be going around having duels to the death. </span></i>Images of bighorn rams butting heads, and male lizards grappling with each other, spring to mind. <br /> <br /> He looks over at Boomer, suddenly red-faced. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I'm sorry,&quot;</span> he whispers, so as not to distract the duelists, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I didn't really understand what the Duel Arcane entailed. I thought there was a chance they would kill each other. So they're just trying to intimidate each other, right? Show each other how they would kill him if he really wanted to?&quot; </span>He watches for a moment, and then frowns. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Still... it's going to be pretty awkward for me.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:20:28-07:00","id":986114,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 5/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> When Boomer arrives, Lynx is sitting cross-legged on the floor, eyes closed in thought. He twitches at the sound of her arrival. He listens to her talk about Mathias's story and the Duel Arcane.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I know Mathias cares - you do too, and I appreciate that - but after that incident with the Gulmoth, hearing Moonstone talk about Ragnar and Phoenix like that... I couldn't hold it back.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He gives a small smile, which then turns solemn.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I feel misplaced,</span>&quot; he says with a heavy sigh. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">My four to-be... well, Ragnar called Moonstone a cabalmate already, which... I don't know, sounds hasty? Anyway, the four of them all resonate with you, don't they? You and Phoenix, and Mathias and Ragnar... Valentine, Binder and Moonstone, even though the way Valentine looks at Moonstone is hostile. When you talk about the arcana, it doesn't feel right for me. When it comes to the Wild, the way you talk about Thyrsus and... and Shaman and whatever names we Thyrsus...Thyrsi? and how they feel it... it's textbook. Recited. Not... not real.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx rubs his beard. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">It's silly, I know... there's this huge world out there of magic, of ... tradition, and paths and aspects that we Mages can share in common... but there's this nagging feeling of...why am I here, exactly, with the seven of you? Is there a purpose? Only I feel like a... a pet animal. Or an intrusion. Depends on how melodramatic you want it to sound.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> As Boomer gets up from her seat, he, too, gets up. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Sorry, it's just with everything today, I am utterly drained. And I know I can use my Life magic to perk up and be refreshed... is it strange that I don't want to do that?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> When Boomer offers her hand, he grasps it willingly. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Can a Duel Arcane cause physical harm if the participants go too far?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Lynx arrives with Boomer, who lets go of his hand and immediately goes off to referee the Duel. He moves quietly to the group, opening his Life Senses instinctively as the Duel begins.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Still... it's going to be pretty awkward for me.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Nah,</span>&quot; Lynx says as he puts an arm on Ragnar's shoulder from behind, with a bit of a laugh in his throat. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">They'll appreciate the gesture. You're brave, Ragnar. At least you didn't throw a tantrum and storm out. Who are you all cheering for?</span>&quot; He asks his fellow ... <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">friends? I think that's where we're going...</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:42:12-07:00","id":986262,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone<br /> Turn 2 | Initiative 13 | Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined<br /> Doors:</b> OOOOOOOO<br /> <br /> High Speech- wait, he <i>understands </i>High Speech now. The meaning rings through clearly, not just mystical glossolalia. But the image Mathias created to match them falls short.<br /> <br /> Moonstone twirls on his heel in the physical world, gracefully clearing the air. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That isn't me. This is me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He parts Time, and keeps his cool by conjuring up an image from Postcognition, accompanied by <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/aivisura/steven-universe-roses-fountain\" target=\"_blank\">peaceful music</a>: Moonstone and Hakim standing intertwined together in ritual garb, until the mage points ahead and the Sleepwalker lunges outward for battle with a smile on his face. Moonstone matches his copy's pose, with Supernal symbols arrayed around himself.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Composure+Time: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444923\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> Actually I should have rolled +1 die there from my last success: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444925\" target=\"_blank\">no additional success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:00:48-07:00","id":986322,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> Boomer shrugs, while keeping her eyes on the duel. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It depends,&quot;</span> she whispers. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Some Duels Arcane can indeed end in death. Although the match generally ends with no physical violence or bloodshed, it is incredibly exhausting. Some choose to continue to the point of death. Most just use it to settle petty arguments.&quot;</span> She snorts and shrugs. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I try not to get myself into the ring too much, although I'd be lying if I said I was a poor duelist,&quot;</span> she winks.<br /> <br /> She pauses at your comment about killing. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;This isn't just about harm or threat of harm. It's a magical extension of emotion and pure will. It's just cleaner than actually slinging spells, and it doesn't risk Paradox or danger to anyone else. It's a more...civilized way of settling arguments and putting them to rest.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Boomer nods understandingly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Totally get it. Until I found the right mentor, I felt really misguided myself. And we can help you find one. We know some people,&quot;</span> she grins. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It depends in part on which Order you might be interested in. They really do their best to attract the interest of newly Awakened mages. It's in your best interest to join one, but we rely on membership to gain political strength, too. It's a mutual relationship that helps us to keep our society healthy, and provide opportunities to explore greater Mysteries.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer looks at you again, not in the same way she appraised you upon first meeting you, but as if trying to assess your skill. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Honestly, I get the sense that the Adamantine Arrow probably isn't what you're looking for, and I'm not going to try and convince you otherwise. But if you want to learn more, I can bring you to some of our meetings. The Arrows are about mastering yourself as a way to master the Supernal. It's about discipline, loyalty, and confidence, and exerting those things in very tangible and practical ways. You have some of those qualities. Let me know if you're interested. But know that you are absolutely welcome in this place, even if we don't have any Thyrsi available for you to meet.&quot;</span> She places a hand gently on your shoulder and smiles.<br /> <br /> As you begin to leave the room, she shakes her head at your question. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;There's a real temptation there, and I think you're understanding why it can be problematic for some. Magic can let us do some incredible things. But the more we use it, the more we give in to our pride and hubris, the more we lose self-discipline and give in to temptation. It's a really bad downward spiral. There's nothing wrong with using magic to help yourself. Just follow your gut and don't be an asshole to people, and generally everything will sort itself out,&quot;</span> she grins.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Obviously, I'm rooting for Mathias here,&quot;</span> she mutters dryly. She frowns, though. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Moonstone is more capable than he first appeared, though. I'll give him that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mathias<br /> Doors: </b>XXOOOO<br /> <b>Turn 2</b><br /> <br /> Mathias is momentarily distracted by your Imago, and it causes him to falter more. Hesitation shows in his eyes, but he shakes it away. The mage reaches out with his mind and forces his Imago into place.<br /> <br /> As Moonstone watches, the idyllic scene he has created is suddenly interrupted; the peaceful music halts, replaced by sharp melodies with dissonant tones. Alux appears. The Gulmoth roars, gnashing its teeth at the young mage -- both the imagined one and the real one standing in the dueling circle. Tangible cords of Fate wrap around and between Moonstone and the Gulmoth. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Your 'help' attacking the creature simply discorporated it. With time, it will reform its corpus and spread terror, both in the Shadow and the Fallen Worlds.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Wits + Fate: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444933\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. +1 on next roll.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:29:21-07:00","id":986347,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone<br /> Turn 3 | Initiative 13 | Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined<br /> Doors:</b> XOOOOOOO<br /> <br /> Seeing his memory-fantasy dissipate stings, and his confidence wavers. He shouts back: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm a Warlock! I dealt with demons to earn my Awakening, and I'll master this one, too!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Memories and images from his Awakening sparkle in the background like reflections in a shattered mirror: being trapped by his own Mind in a full-on nervous breakdown, creating his own road to escape outside of Space, being harried and mocked by demons with familiar faces, and finally binding a pack of wraiths in the shape of Hakim and his parents and other figures, trapping them in a mirror as they pleaded for mercy, and shattering the mirror (hence his bandaged hands) to create a portal to the Iron Gauntlet itself.<br /> <br /> They all condense into an Imago: <i><b>MIND - RULING - DOMINATION</b></i>, and his projected self quickly and carefully wraps Alux in their shared cords of Fate like a noose, or a leash. The bound Gulmoth falls under his sway, and goes charging back toward Mathias.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Dexterity+Mind+1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444957\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:18:10-07:00","id":986377,"title":"","content":"<b>Mathias<br /> Doors: </b>XXXOOO<br /> <b>Turn 3</b><br /> <br /> Mathias grits his teeth, but there are very clearly beads of sweat dripping down his face. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;NO!</span> he shouts in defiance. He raises his hand and intones in High Speech again. Alux falters in place, slows, and turns to dust as Mathias' Time magic swirls around the creature like a desert wind.<br /> <br /> The weight of Time extends forward, whirling around Moonstone, threatening to crush him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Presence + Time + 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444964\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:44:26-07:00","id":986398,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate and Time)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Obviously, I'm rooting for Mathias here. </span><span style=\"color:deeppink\">Moonstone is more capable than he first appeared, though. I'll give him that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar gives a half-smile. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well, seeing as Mathias is probably going to be my master, and the bunch of us are probably going to end up as cabalmates, I don't think it's going to be to my benefit to take a side at all.&quot; </span>He watches the back-and-forth for a moment, and furrows his brow slightly. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;But is it just me, or is Moonstone actually winning?&quot; <i>Note to self: never piss off Moonstone. </i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:59:46-07:00","id":986410,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone<br /> Turn 4 | Initiative 13 | Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined<br /> Doors:</b> XXOOOOOO<br /> <br /> The fighting continues this way for several volleys. The air crackles with dueling Nimbuses.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;After everything I've lived through- I'll endure this, too!&quot;</span> He forms a similar counter-Imago of himself remaining youthful and eternal, untouched and untouchable, while Mathias fades away. <i><b>TIME - SHIELDING - AGELESS</b></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Resolve+Time: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444968\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Feel free to modify the bonuses for the following rolls if Mathias Defends.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Turn 5</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;And <i>you-</i> ha- you'll just be a memory! <i>You. Ain't. Nothin'.&quot;</i></span> He undulates and dances into existence a labyrinth made of mirrored walls, a symbolic representation of his own evasion of responsibility, defying Mathias' efforts to find a way through. <b><i>SPACE - VEILING - (NO) EXIT</i></b><br /> <br /> The physical Moonstone reinforces the message by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=efttzj5VtXE\" target=\"_blank\">styling on him in the most elegant way</a>, drawing on his skill in both the mystical secrets of the Space Arcanum and modern dance.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Wits+Space+1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444969\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes!</a><br /> <br /> If I can, I'd like to apply a custom Tilt to Mathias, giving him -2 to Defend rolls this Duel, resolved when he successfully Defends.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Turn 6</b><br /> <br /> Having seized the initiative, he expands on the Imago: his own hands reach out from the mirrors in every direction, turning Mathias around and stealing the threads of his Sympathy one by one. Finally he stands threadbare and alone in the middle of the labyrinth, watching as his friends and family greet and welcome Moonstone as if he were Mathias. <b><i>SPACE - RULING - THIEF-OF-NAMES</i></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attacking with Dexterity+Space+4: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444970\" target=\"_blank\">1 success, of course.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-12-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:22:00-07:00","id":986431,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Active Sight</b>: Prime (Peripheral at end of Duel) | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 0/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Open your Sight to the Truth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Doing as instructed, the two duelists wills reveal themselves. So this is what a wizard's war looks like.<br /> <br /> Mathias is fighting hard, but it's an uphill battle for him. Moonstone has a clear advantage, at least for now. Moonstone mustn't win, I wish I could do something instead of clenching my fists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:14:38-07:00","id":986480,"title":"","content":"<b>Mathias</b><br /> <b>Turn 4</b><br /> <b>Doors:</b> XXXXOO<br /> <br /> Mathias cries out in surprise as the Duel wears down on his psyche. He throws a look at Moonstone that is a mixture of outrage and shock. He simply seems like he cannot fathom how he is losing. <br /> <br /> Wordlessly, rather than attacking, Mathias holds up his arms defensively. Cords of Destiny extend outward from him and lash on to the ground around him, desperately clinging to the version of himself here rather than submitting to Moonstone's Imago. But the threads falter, and he slips to one knee.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Defending with Resolve + Fate: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444992\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Mathias' 4th Door opens, but you only exceed his total by 1 (minimum to win), so no bonus on the Turn 5 roll. As a result, your Turn 5 only gets 4 successes, so makes the discussion about a Tilt a moot point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Turn 5</b><br /> <b>Doors:</b> XXXXXO<br /> <br /> Mathias is clearly on the defensive now. He is creating Imagos out of pure instinct, reacting to Moonstone's rather than crafting nuanced effects. His Imagos have more weight behind them, and create larger and more dramatic effects, but somehow Moonstone's sheer force of will presses harder and harder than Mathias can tolerate. <br /> <br /> The older mage closes his eyes and intones in High Speech, forcing his face to a look of focused serenity. Mathias creates an Image of himself deftly navigating the endless maze, letting chance and random decisions guide his feet to the exit. But the exit never appears, and Mathias' calm facade cracks.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Defending with Dexterity + Fate: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444996\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Well, the dice are on your side tonight!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Turn 6</b><br /> <b>Doors:</b> XXXXXX<br /> <br /> Mathias makes one last effort to defend himself, hoping to knock away your grip on your Sword to buy time to rethink his path to victory. But his final Imago, of threads of Fate wrapping him in a cocoon of Destiny to shield himself from the future Moonstone tries to bring to pass, fails. <br /> <br /> Mathias falls to his knees, gasping. He is at a loss of words. <br /> <br /> Silence fills the room. The dueling circle disappears, and Boomer shakes her head in disappointment. Valentine looks down, not looking at Mathias. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Moonstone wins,&quot;</span> Boomer announces quietly.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Defending with Presence + Fate: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/444999\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes again</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T18:11:28-07:00","id":986503,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate and Time)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar is verklempt. The sight of Mathias losing to a newly-Awakened mage is stunning. He looks over at Moonstone. By all accounts, Mathias should have had no difficulties defeating Moonstone. But the Warlock conducted himself well. True talent, or just a fortuitous eddy of Fate? <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Mathias the Witch. Will he bear a grudge against Moonstone for this? Will this color his attitude towards me? </i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is casting Divination (Time 1) as an Improvised Spell. He has two free Reach, one of which he spends for Advanced Range, and the other for Specific Answers. Gnosis 1 + Time 2 + Path Tool 1 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445011\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:31:17-07:00","id":986545,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> You tap into the streams of Time swirling around you. Images flash through your mind, glimpses of the future -- or at least a likely future.<br /> <br /> You see scenes of Moonstone and Mathias speaking cordially but curtly, flashing again and again, but none of outright hostility; you sense that Mathias will indeed bear a grudge, but not something that would be so strong as to form a lasting hatred or blood feud.<br /> <br /> The scenes fade, only to be replaced by mental snapshots of your own interactions with Mathias -- ones filled with understanding, patience, and generosity from Mathias. Clearly, he will not hold any ill will towards you specifically because of Moonstone's actions, even if you continue on your current path.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> For a long pause, Mathias stares at the ground, unable to lift his gaze to any of you. His breathing begins to slow to a steady rhythm, and he wipes the sweat from his forehead.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Mathias rises to his feet and lifts his gaze to meet each of the mages -- except Moonstone's. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;The Duel Arcane is a system of combat for settling wrongs and claims by opposing parties,&quot;</span> he says wearily. All of the heat has left his tone, and his voice sounds hoarse as if he has been yelling for hours. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;By right of force and will, the winner is granted exclusive rights to the stakes and claims over which the Duel were held. It is steeped in millennia of tradition, passed down from generation to generation of mages. The magic of the Duel is such that it leaves the loser mentally and spiritually exhausted, such that failing to accept the terms of losing is incredibly difficult.&quot;</span> His voice does indeed sound exhausted. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;And even if that were not the case, the code duello and the Lex Magica -- the laws of the Duel Arcane and mage society overall, respectively -- clearly indicate that failing to accept terms of losing after a Duel is a severe crime.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And, as if to demonstrate his compliance, Mathias finally makes eye contact with Moonstone, if briefly, and walks towards him. The Mastigos mage slowly kneels before him, takes a deep breath, and nods. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Moonstone, I wish to formally...<i>thank you</i>...&quot;</span> The words are slow in coming, as if being dragged out of him. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;...for saving my, and these mages', lives from the Gulmoth known as Alux.&quot;</span> Pause, followed by another longer, slower breath. Mathias' eyes are fixated on Moonstone, but they still lack the heat they held before the Duel.<br /> <br /> He sighs. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;As I already said, it was wrong to strike you out of anger. I ask for you to forgive me for harming you, insulting you, and disrespecting you after you...put your life on the line for my sake.&quot;</span> By this point, Mathias' eyes are starting to pick up more of the intensity they held before his loss, but his tone remains decidedly neutral. Mathias takes one more ragged breath, as if preparing himself, and then he leans forward and kisses Moonstone's hand. His lips twitch, and he quickly removes them, as if tasting something unsavory.<br /> <br /> His required tasks completed, at least for now, Mathias quickly stands to his feet. However, he continues to speak. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You truly are a remarkable mage, for one so newly Awakened. In my pride, I underestimated you.&quot;</span> He laughs bitterly at the irony. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;But I <i>must</i> impress upon you again that you have been blessed by Creation with incredible power, but also an equally incredible responsibility.&quot;</span> He closes his eyes and intones softly in High Speech, creating a pulse of energy visible to your Sight or diffusely sensed on your Periphery. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;This I prophesize: Alux will return, and it will <i>murder. </i>Your actions have set ripples in motion that I believe cannot be prevented now. So, while I <i>thank you</i> for your efforts to defeat the Gulmoth,&quot;</span> he says bitterly, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;you must forgive me for lacking satisfaction with the outcome.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias turns and walks slowly away. He pauses at the treshold, then half-turns his head over his shoulder to say, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;The Consilium meets in downtown Chicago on Saturday at noon, sharp. I will complete our terms then.&quot;</span> With that, he walks away, footsteps muted on the carepeted hallway leading away from this room","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:44:28-07:00","id":986551,"title":"","content":"<b>^BUT BEFORE THAT HAPPENS...^</b> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Spells: None<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined, Triumphant<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 8/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 2/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Moonstone is flying. It's not the fractured heat of delirium, or a manic episode, it's just pure blissful joy. He watches Mathias' defenses fail, and the elder mage falls to his knees. His own mouth hangs open, his eyes are wide.<span style=\"color:#008080\"> &quot;I...won?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He feels his face. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I...won.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> A huge smile spreads across his face, impossible to hide. He jumps up and pumps his fist and just starts laughing- certainly the only one to do so- and hugs himself tight and twirls on his heels and makes a spectacle of himself, literally crying with joy. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I won, I won, I <b>WON!</b> Babe, I did it! I won! I told you I could!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The sound of uncontrollable cackling (plus hiccups and snorts and sobs) fills the sparse utility room, boots scuffing on the floor as he jumps up and down, presumably met with stunned silence from everyone else. He holds up a finger and turns to the audience, smiling ear to ear, shifting his weight between his feet: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;And before <i>anyone </i>calls that luck- let me remind you, the great Mathias is an <i>Adept of Fate.</i> Isn't that right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He snaps his fingers. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Wait! Wait! Before you answer-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He hustles over to the bench, <i>skips</i> some of the way, digs through his messenger bag and pulls out his phone. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hang on, everybody hang on, let me find it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone, feared sorcerer and Warlock sworn to Pandemonium, navigates through his iPhone menu with trembling fingers until the tinny voice of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7p7sjrabPMM\" target=\"_blank\">Nicki Minaj</a> plays through the low-quality speakers, echoing in the otherworldly Sanctum of the Shields of Dawn. <span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\"><i>&quot;Get on your knees get on your knees get on your knees, baby just get on your knees...&quot;</i></span><br /> <br /> Moonstone kicks off his boots and struts back, high femme, preening and holding his iPhone (the music is shaky and bouncy) as he approaches the dumbstruck Mathias. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hold that pose, it's perfect.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He snaps a quick photo of Mathias and smiles. He's <i>glowing </i>with pride and joy and maybe a little spite. Magnanimous in victory he is not. Nicki Minaj continues to taunt against a backing track: <span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\"><i>&quot;Yeah, it's gooder than Meagan, you look good when you're beggin' / I be laughing when you begging me to just put the head in...&quot;</i></span><br /> <br /> One last thing. He marches toward Phoenix on the sidelines, stepping in time with the rhythm, and speaks in a sickly sweet voice: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hey buddy?&quot;</span> He reaches out his hand as if he's about to slap him-<br /> <br /> ...But instead, he softly caresses Phoenix's cheek and tickles a little under his chin. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Don't ever do that again,&quot;</span> he coos, and skips back toward his defeated opponent. Moonstone gestures toward the spectators, covering his laughter with one hand. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Oh- don't get up. Tell the people what he's won, Mathias.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Savoring this so hard. May I count this whole spectacle for my &quot;Perform for a crowd&quot; Aspiration?<br /> <br /> edit: apparently yes! +1 Beat, and I'll replace it with &quot;Gain a Familiar.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rest of this is after the previous post:</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By this point, Mathias' eyes are starting to pick up more of the intensity they held before his loss, but his tone remains decidedly neutral. Mathias takes one more ragged breath, as if preparing himself, and then he leans forward and kisses Moonstone's hand. His lips twitch, and he quickly removes them, as if tasting something unsavory. </div> </div> </div>It's actually more uncomfortable than he expected- it's not very much fun to demean someone in such a personal way. But then, it's not very fun to get slapped and shoved against a wall, either. Once Mathias finishes kissing his outstretched hand, Moonstone is blushing, but he bows his head and reverently says: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You are, uh, most welcome. In my mercy, I forgive you. You may rise.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Just to be completely clear, &quot;Get On Your Knees&quot; by Nicki Minaj and Aria Grande continues to play loudly from Moonstone's shitty iPhone speakers during this entire exchange, including and especially <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;This I prophesize: Alux will return, and it will <i>murder.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone mutters <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;killjoy,&quot;</span> but the prophecy does make him rather sick to his stomach. He offers a retort: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm better than my mistakes- and if you work as hard as I do, you might be, too. I already did the impossible by humbling an Adept. Stopping Alux before it hurts anyone else is a much more worthy use of my talent, and I bet saving those lives is gonna feel even better than defeating you! I'll take your prophecy as a challenge!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He turns to the other Nameless- gonna have to get on their good side sometime- and raises his fist. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;No more deaths. No more Alux. Everyone lives! Who's with me?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-13-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:37:55-07:00","id":986592,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 0/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> Damn, looks like Moonstone won. I crack a little smile as he jumps for joy like a little spaz. Oh sure, you beat Mathias, but you're gonna crash sooner or later. Then the motherfucker starts gloating hard, getting a friggin' Nicki Minaj song to mock him. I mean, you already made the man agree to get on his knees and praise for a bunch of bullshit, but then you have to go and rub it in his face, too? What a fucking bitch.<br /> <br /> As if all that wasn't enough for him, he decides to stroll up to me and-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hey buddy?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> In your dreams, asshat. But it's time to wake up. I grab the pissant by the cuff, forcing him to his toes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not initiating a grapple or anything, More of a role-playing thing than anything else. Moonstone can contest it if he wants, so here's the roll for it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445058\" target=\"_blank\">Strength 3 + Brawl 4 = 7 dice \u2192 3 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I hunch down and look him right in the eye, letting my anger flow through my eyes. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;You may have beaten Mathias, but that doesn't change the fact that you summoned the Gulmoth, and the Gulmoth almost killed me, so you almost ended up killing me,&quot;</span> I deeply growl, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Just because you delivered the final blow to that thing, doesn't mean you saved us. You just helped, along with all of us. And frankly, I did the heavy lifting for you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;You think on that,&quot;</span> I demand as I thrust him out of my grasp. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Also, I'm taking the staff. If you're willing to control Ragnar's mind, then you're willing to control mine, so I ain't letting you have anything that could help you with that,&quot;</span> I state as I head over and retrieve the staff, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;And if you want it, then you can fight me. With your fists, man to man.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:02:50-07:00","id":986685,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> Ragnar rolls his eyes at Moonstone's gloating. He's consoled by his vision that Moonstone's antics haven't ruined his chance of being mentored by Mathias. Then they threaten to roll out of his head at Moonstone's and Phoenix's spat. He walks over to them and claps a hand on each man's shoulder, trying to be jovial. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200b&quot;Yeesh, guys. There are better ways to resolve this. Phoenix, let Moonstone have the staff for the time being. Then, the next time there's a Highstorm, we can go hunting for artifacts. If we find something attuned to Stygia, Moonstone gets it, and then he'll hand the staff over to you, Phoenix. And if we find something attuned to the Aether, you'll keep the staff, Moonstone. Deal?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:53:11-07:00","id":986730,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LL</b>OOOOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 0</div> <br /> <br /> <i>Huh, I would've thought a wizards' duel would be more heavily weighted toward the more experience wizard... Is it that Moonstone is just that good? Or was it just a fluke? I feel like I could've accomplished similar things with my magic.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Yeesh, guys. There are better ways to resolve this...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder will cast a quick spell just to verify the staff's ownership, more out of curiosity than anything.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting <i>Correspondences </i>(Space 2)<br /> Reach: 1 Free; Spending for instant speed and sensory range<br /> Paradox (containing): 1 vs Wisdom 7 = 1 vs 7 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445097\" target=\"_blank\">1 </a> vs <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445098\" target=\"_blank\">0</a>... <u><b><i>amazing</i></b></u><br /> <br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Space 2 = 3 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445099\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Potency is 2, so that should show me the staff's two strongest Sympathetic links.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:18:05-07:00","id":986855,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight: Mind/Space | Spells: None<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Determined, Triumphant<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 8/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Strength 3 + Brawl 0, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445155\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Resolving Determined to win the contested roll and evade the grapple. Please stop doing attack rolls &quot;for roleplaying reasons,&quot; okay?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Moonstone gracefully spins out of Phoenix's grip and moves outside his range, still flush with victory. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;<i>God,</i> I love styling on masculine dudes. This is like the third time today you've tried to hit me, Phoenix- if you want a kiss, you can just ask! I hope you get that temper under control, for your girl or boyfriend's sake.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He giggles and flexes for show as Phoenix picks up the staff. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Oh, <i>man to man.</i> That's where the real power is, right? Fists, not the Awakened will. The Duel Arcane is a symbolic battle fought by people who make symbols real. My victory is more pure than a locker room brawl could ever be.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> But Ragnar's diplomatic efforts pay off. He bows with a flourish and opens his palms. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'll give it to you as a gift, freely and with a glad heart. You'll make better use of an Aetherial artifact than I would, anyway. No need to thank me! You can think of it as a gracious surrender. I hereby consider our hatchet buried.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:52:58-07:00","id":986901,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 0/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;<i>God,</i> I love styling on masculine dudes. This is like the third time today you've tried to hit me, Phoenix- if you want a kiss, you can just ask! I hope you get that temper under control, for your girl or boyfriend's sake.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Ha! Don't flatter yourself,&quot;</span> I retort.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Oh, <i>man to man.</i> That's where the real power is, right? Fists, not the Awakened will. The Duel Arcane is a symbolic battle fought by people who make symbols real. My victory is more pure than a locker room brawl could ever be.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I simply scoff. More pure, eh? Just shows you don't understand physical fighting one bit. Why am I not surprised? What does surprise me is Ragnar's efforts to negotiate. Dude, you're talking about someone who just a few minutes ago reached into your mind and commanded it! He hijacked you, would you be willing to let him have anything that could help him do that again in any way? I'm about to open my mouth when-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'll give it to you as a gift, freely and with a glad heart. You'll make better use of an Aetherial artifact than I would, anyway. No need to thank me! You can think of it as a gracious surrender. I hereby consider our hatchet buried.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Oh how I'd like to abuse this staff...<br /> <br /> Instead I just grip it tighter, anger twisting my hands around it. I don't even say anything, I just leave the room. I return to the room where the main discussion took place and sit down. I take a look at the staff, testing it's balance, admiring its craftsmanship (if it had and, that is. I think they said Artifacts came from the Supernal itself, so I get it wasn't crafted by human hands. Doesn't matter, I still like it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:52:04-07:00","id":987046,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar waits until Moonstone walks away or shifts his attention, and then turns to Phoenix and whispers. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I know Moonstone's an... interesting character. But honestly, don't mess with him. He obviously doesn't take well to being manhandled. And if he can take on somebody as skilled in magic as Mathias and win...&quot; </span>He looks Phoenix in the eye. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;It might just be posturing, but something tells me he could eff any one of us up <i>badly </i>\u200bwithout laying a finger on us. Call it a hunch or Fate, but something tells me that he's got a Destiny with a 'D.' And those kinds of things are rarely preordained to end just for good or ill. But if you, Binder, Lynx and I work together, I think we can swing it in favor of his Destiny turning out well.&quot;</span> <br /> <br /> With that, he walks over to Valentine. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Mathias mentioned the Consilium meets downtown at noon on Saturday? Can you tell me where, exactly?&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T22:55:31-07:00","id":987113,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> It's pretty clear that he's just about worn out his welcome with the Shields of Dawn for the moment, so after the MP3 ends and he and Phoenix conclude their business, Moonstone goes to the bench on the far side of the room to put his clothes back on (whispering <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;i did it!&quot;</span> one more time into the Cloak) and secure his magical belongings. This doesn't seem like the best time to break bread with the other Nameless, although the urge is there now that the storm clouds have passed.<br /> <br /> Unless something big happens, he's going to keep his joy to himself and keep a low profile until they can leave. His Paradox-induced wounds are aching again after the Duel. He sends a few texts to Arrow mages he knows, looking for a crash space. He doesn't really want to sink his mood by heading right back to the empty apartment after this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I dunno what the plan is for the immediate future, but if it's doable, I'm going to use my Allies (Adamantine Arrow) 3 favor for this Chapter to request access to a communal Order Sanctum (either in Chicago or La Grange) for a couple days until the Consilium meeting. Gotta recover from that resistant Lethal damage somewhere comfortable, and maybe link up with the Knights of Alhambra offscreen.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T01:25:18-07:00","id":987148,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> You reach out your consciousness and study the staff, focusing on its connections to important people around it. Just as Valentine suggested, the staff has a Medium connection to Phoenix, which you can sense as a thick thread stretching from the object straight to him here in this room. And although it is very faint, there is also a Weak connection to Moonstone, which formed from the young femme's interactions with the weapon after leaving the Highstorm.<br /> <br /> As you cast your spell, you notice a small bubble of Paradox rising inside of you. It's a good reminder that even the simplest of spells can threaten to infect you or the area when pushing beyond the safe limits of your abilities. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gain the Abyssal Backlash condition, granting +1 to your next Paradox roll this scene, if relevant.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> Boomer watches your exchange with Phoenix with crossed arms. She walks up, boots clicking on the tile, and stands with her hands at her hips to face you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;You're being a dick,&quot;</span> she says bluntly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Savor your victory. You're a skilled mage to beat Mathias, and I think you knew exactly which buttons you were pushing to goad him into that Duel. He should've seen that for what it was. But keep it to yourself. Gloating and antagonizing is a piss-poor move, and it's definitely not the Arrow way.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer pauses and groans to herself, face palming. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;And I swear to God, if you play one more fucking <i>Nicki Minaj</i> song in front of me, I will fry your phone faster than you can say 'Bang Bang.'&quot;</span> She turns away, but you can hear her mutter, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Seriously, no one has any good taste in music anymore...&quot;</span> Valentine laughs out loud, grinning at Boomer, who casually flips him off as she heads after Phoenix.<br /> <br /> After the room settles, you send your texts to your Arrow contacts, asking for your favor to crash at a sanctum. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sure, that makes a lot of sense to me. I'll respond to it more when this scene ends.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> The staff gives off a warmth that you find comforting as you inspect it. The weapon is excellently crafted, perfectly balanced, and supple with a slight bend when you push on it.<br /> <br /> You hear boots clicking on the hardwood floor again as Boomer walks into the room. She nods at the artifact in your hand. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It has the makings of a solid weapon, and a useful Tool,&quot;</span> she comments. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Mind if I join you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer hops onto a couch adjacent to yours. After a moment, she says, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Look, Phoenix, I've watched you since you came in here. I think you and I have a lot in common. You've got passion, and strength, and I respect that. You aren't afraid to say what you feel is right. And yeah, you could maybe still use some work on restraint when being provoked, but you were standing up for others being challenged or trying to stop people from causing harm.&quot;</span> She smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I think it's wiser not to throw a punch at someone who may join your cabal, but I think it shows restraint for you to come out here instead of giving in to his jabs.&quot;</span> She doesn't need to explain whom she's talking about. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;If you're interested, I think you might be a good fit for the Adamantine Arrow. I don't know what your personal goals or interests are, but I think you'd find yourself in good company. Just wanted you to know.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Valentine nods at your request. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Yes, Mathias was going to talk more about it, but he seems...preoccupied at the moment.&quot;</span> His eyes shift towards Moonstone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The meeting is being held in Saint John Cantius Church, near I-90 a little west of Navy Pier. Right by a metra station. When you get there, tell the guard that you're there to 'open your eyes to the truth', and they'll let you in. Try to get there a little early so you don't miss anything and we can touch base about the meeting.&quot;</span> Valentine addresses the rest of you in the room with a firm, serious expression. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;There's something you need to know about these meetings. It is absolutely imperative that under no circumstances are you to use <i>any</i> magic during this meeting or on the church premises without express permission from the Council. Guardians will be closely watching for it. As a first time offender, you will be severely reprimanded. There won't be a second time. This is a critical safety precaution we have been required to follow for a long time, for reasons that I really think it's best to save for another day.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine pulls out a piece of paper and pen, and writes down several phone numbers. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;This is contact information for the three of us. Call or text if you need something important.&quot;</span> You realize that he doesn't ask for contact information in return. As if reading your mind, he smiles and says, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;If we need to contact you, we'll find you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Finally, Valentine says, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I'm sorry for not saying it earlier, but we were distracted. There is another mage who has recently Awakened whom we think would be an excellent addition to your cabal. He is a Moros mage, a physician who goes by the name Ouroboros Ophis. Having someone with his Path and talents in your cabal will give you a well-rounded group and help you explore more complex Mysteries. The choice is of course yours as a group, but he will be at the meeting beforehand and can talk to you then. You might also be able to reach him before Saturday.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine looks around. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Please pass the message to the others. We're done here, then, unless anyone has any questions.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Everyone: I think I forgot to say it, but if you haven't already, you all gain an Arcane Beat for witnessing (or participating in) the Duel Arcane and learning about its role in mage society.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:06:30-07:00","id":987177,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: <br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 0/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Beats: 1 - Arcane Beats: 1</b></div> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">All of this is Awakened Society, huh...</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx rubs his beard passively, as Phoenix and Boomer voice their opinions to Moonstone and Mathias pays the price for his loss. He listens to Valentine's warnings, perks up momentarily at the mention of another Awakened, and falters when it's not a Thyrsus. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Stupid envy.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#808080\">Please pass the message to the others. We're done here, then, unless anyone has any questions.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I have three,&quot;</span> Lynx says as he steps forward a. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't like that... that mind reading omniscience thing you're doing. It's intrusive. And rude. Could you not do that?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">You said we're not allowed to use <i>any</i> magic... does that include our Awakened Senses? Or... Sight, I guess. And...</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> Lynx rubs his beard, gazing into Valentine's eyes. His expression is solemn, worried, almost apologetic. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Do you regret having us over?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>During all three questions, Lynx observes the Shields' reactions to each of his question with an Empathy Roll, gaining 3 successes.</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/445411\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Empathy \u2192 3 successes.</a><br /> <br /> He resolves his Inspired Condition so it becomes an Exceptional Success, and he gains 1 arcane beat for resolving the condition, and 1 Willpower as part of Inspired's Resolution. Is this correct?</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:22:14-07:00","id":987224,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> LOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 0/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Irritable | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> [Before exiting Duel room]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I know Moonstone's an... interesting character. But honestly, don't mess with him. He obviously doesn't take well to being manhandled. And if he can take on somebody as skilled in magic as Mathias and win. </span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">It might just be posturing, but something tells me he could eff any one of us up <i>badly </i>\u200bwithout laying a finger on us. Call it a hunch or Fate, but something tells me that he's got a Destiny with a 'D.' And those kinds of things are rarely preordained to end just for good or ill. But if you, Binder, Lynx and I work together, I think we can swing it in favor of his Destiny turning out well.</span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I understand your concern, considering what happened,&quot;</span> I whisper back, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;But I was able to take out a spell of his right after it was cast. If he really was truly talented, wouldn't he be able to easily counter it or something? I think he got lucky, and the victory's gone to his head in either case. Maybe he does have a destiny or something. Don't you know Fate magic? Maybe you could try to find out.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> [After exiting Duel room]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It has the makings of a solid weapon, and a useful Tool. Mind if I join you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Not at all.&quot;</span> I reply as I scooch over to give her room for a seat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Look, Phoenix, I've watched you since you came in here. I think you and I have a lot in common. You've got passion, and strength, and I respect that. You aren't afraid to say what you feel is right. And yeah, you could maybe still use some work on restraint when being provoked,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I chuckle at that. She ain't wrong. I'm a 100% certified hothead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;But you were standing up for others being challenged or trying to stop people from causing harm. </span><span style=\"color:deeppink\">I think it's wiser not to throw a punch at someone who may join your cabal, but I think it shows restraint for you to come out here instead of giving in to his jabs.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;To be honest, after hearing about the significance of the Duel Arcane, it seemed like it would be a big low blow if I hit him for his victory,&quot;</span> I state dryly, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;That, and I just wanted to get away from the bastard.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;If you're interested, I think you might be a good fit for the Adamantine Arrow. I don't know what your personal goals or interests are, but I think you'd find yourself in good company. Just wanted you to know.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hmm, the Adamantine Arrow...&quot;</span> I repeat as I ponder about it, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Protectors of Awakened and Sleepers alike who master the self...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Definitely something worth thinking about,&quot;</span> I say with a nod and smile, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;So if I wanted to, where would I need to go?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:52:22-07:00","id":987455,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: None<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 8/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;You're being a dick,&quot;</span> Boomer says bluntly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Savor your victory. You're a skilled mage to beat Mathias, and I think you knew exactly which buttons you were pushing to goad him into that Duel. He should've seen that for what it was. But keep it to yourself. Gloating and antagonizing is a piss-poor move, and it's definitely not the Arrow way.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Well- he doesn't have a lot to say to that. He<i> is</i> kind of being a dick. Somehow, being called out on his bullshit by a more experienced mage resonates more, especially an Arrow. He frowns as he puts the Cloak back on. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I guess it isn't. It just feels good to <i>win </i>for once. I thought the Arrow was about honor and victory, but...maybe it looks different from the outside. What Mathias said about Alux- this doesn't feel like the best way I could be using my magic. It didn't feel good when he kissed my hand.&quot;</span> That's something to think about, isn't it? <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I made my point, I'm done. I'll, um- stay out of you guys' way for a while.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> But throwing shade on Nicki? That's too much. He calls back: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Haters give me strength! What do you want, Black Flag?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> What she <i>wants </i>is probably for him not to Duel over stupid shit. Message heard, may or may not be internalized.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:25:11-07:00","id":988090,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> Valentine blinks and then laughs unexpectedly at your first question. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I'm sorry to disappoint, but I'm not actually reading your mind. I'm just making educated guesses. Being able to read people is a strength of mine. As for the meeting, you are allowed to do anything that won't set off others' magical senses. So, yes, you may use your Sight as needed at the Consilium meeting. Excellent question.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> In response to your third question, Valentine shakes his head and smiles. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Absolutely not. I suppose Mathias will be quite humbled and irritated about the outcome of today, but such is the case for anyone who loses a Duel Arcane under such terms. Even with that, he believes he needed to be with you tonight or he wouldn't have sought you out. I can't speak for Boomer, but she has always worn her emotions on her sleeve, and she seems pretty pleased with tonight.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, that all sounds good! Nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It <i>is</i> about honor and victory,&quot;</span> Boomer replies, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;but winning a conflict doesn't inherently make it honorable. Self-discipline, which cultivates enlightenment and harmony, may mean having restraint rather then fighting in some cases. And victory without consideration of the means to obtain it can be dishonorable. Honor comes from mastering oneself and, in turn, mastering all.&quot;</span> Despite some of the lecturing words she uses, her voice is softer than before. And when you mention Nicki Minaj, there's a small grin accompanying that middle finger.<br /> <br /> After Boomer leaves, Valentine crosses his arms and finishes drinking the Scotch he has been holding since you met him. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I know you think the Arrow is the right choice for your Order, but the Guardians could use someone with your temperament,&quot;</span> he suggests. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I know you used your knowledge of Mathias as a tool and leveraged it against him. That shows you can read others and use that knowledge to your advantage. I know you have a greater appreciation now for the risks of releasing Paradox. And I also know you aren't afraid of Supernal conflict with mages whom you believe are engaging in unsavory or immoral actions.&quot;</span> He shrugs. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Think on it. If you want to talk more, we can discuss it on Saturday.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Boomer nods as your summary. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Yes, great question. Any prospective mage who wants to join needs to pass a thorough series of assessments and testing. First, I would suggest you think on it or talk to me more over the next few days. If you want to move forward, you'll need to make a petition before a ranking Arrow at a Consilium meeting. From there, you'll be evaluated on a number of skills, including magical and physical prowess -- not to determine if you're in, but to figure out your strengths and weaknesses, and what remedial areas need to be improved, if any.<br /> <br /> &quot;Then, you'll get training to flesh out your skills, and then tested over a prolonged period. If you pass, you're in. If you struggle, you go back to more training, or possibly let go. The Order can't afford to be too choosy -- there are only so many mages, you know? -- but they need everyone to meet minimal standards.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer leans back and smiles. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Frankly, I think you'd do great. And I'm a Thunderbolt Guardian, one of our ranking officials, and I help oversee recruitment and some other Order business. So I may be your sensei if you decide to move forward with it. Just let me know by noon on Saturday if you have a clear answer.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:43:40-07:00","id":990236,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>* NEW SCENE *</b></div> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> Your meeting with the Shields of Dawn draws to a natural close. After you each have the chance to get answers to your questions, Valentine and Boomer escort you back to the foyer where you first entered. You briefly see Mathias look down at you from a balcony upstairs, but he quickly walks away as you approach.<br /> <br /> Boomer reminds you to contact any of them with any questions before the meeting. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;If you do text or call,&quot;</span> she instructs you, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;be smart about it. Don't talk about magic where someone might overhear you. If you think you're in danger for some reason, go to somewhere public -- it's your safest place to be if another mage is trying to harm you. But that means you need to be careful about your own spells, too,&quot;</span> she reminds you. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Crowds of Sleepers strengthen the Lie, which means Paradox is increasingly stronger.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> You feel two quick pulses of energy on your Periphery as Valentine raises his hands, which he uses to smoothly make rapid synchronized motions before pointing at the door. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;This way will lead you back to Chicago, out to the alley where you first came here. With enough advance warning and preparation, I can help relocate you to other places.&quot;</span> He reaches into his pocket and pulls out a small stack of business cards, and gives one to each of you; they are plain, with nothing but the word &quot;Valentine&quot; written on one side. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Holding onto this will make it easier for me to find you in an emergency. We'll see you on Saturday, if not sooner. Try to get there around 11 am, if possible. Contact us if you require any assistance.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> With that, he opens the front door and nods to each of you as you walk through the door. You find yourselves in the streets of Chicago, exactly where you first entered the mysterious mansion. When you look behind you, there is no sign of a door, just a plain brick wall.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It is currently late afternoon or early evening on Tuesday, 9/6/16 in game time. You have until Saturday, 9/10 around 11 am during which you are welcome to do as you please. Due to the natural passing of time, each of you regains 3 WP and heals 3 lethal damage (if relevant), which could obviously be accelerated should you choose to use magic in some way to heal yourself or others.<br /> <br /> You are welcome to spend any XP or Arcane XP (AXP) during this down time as well. I'm not personally tracking your Beats or XP, and won't be monitoring that -- I trust you all to handle that on your own. Please keep an eye on them and make sure you're tracking accordingly. If you do buy something, though, please make a note of it in the OOC thread just so I can be updated on the changes you're making to your character. And as always, please feel free to post or PM me with questions/concerns.<br /> <br /> Please make a post including the actions you would like to do between now and Saturday. If your character's actions would depend on results from a certain roll or are otherwise situational (e.g., if you want to meet someone and your follow-up actions would depend on what they tell you), describe the actions leading up to that situation and let me know what information you would need to know how your character would act. If you know what rolls you would need to make, like spell rolls, include them in your post.<br /> <br /> In addition to your own actions, the following would happen. Please incorporate these actions/situations into your post based on the info below.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> When you return to your apartment in La Grange that evening, you find the door locked and assume that you're alone. The place is quiet and peaceful as you enter. As you set your things down and lock the door behind you, however, you hear someone walking down the hallway. You turn around to see your roommate, Ewan Byrne, walk out of the bathroom naked. He's drying himself off with a towel when he suddenly realizes you're there. He quickly covers himself with the towel and ducks into his bedroom as he shouts out angrily, <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;What the <i>fuck</i> man, didn't you ever hear of knocking or something?&quot;</span> He comes out a minute later after throwing on a muscle tank-top and some jeans.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://4.bp.blogspot.com/-8pjKqdcywgI/VKm2m_7BMYI/AAAAAAAAFvc/6aHLru_ACYs/w506-h356/black-white-bicep-flexing.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Based on your limited interactions with him to date, Ewan is a friendly enough guy. Like you, he is a freshman at the University of Chicago, except that he grew up in the greater Chicago area. You arranged to rent an apartment together via email and social media before you came here. He has shared interests in hiking and sports, but you've quickly realized that he gets very angry in response to awkward roommate situations like this.<br /> <br /> Ewan's temper tends to cool off pretty fast, however. Within a few minutes he acts like nothing has happened. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;So what's up?&quot;</span> he asks nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You realize that you don't have any contact information for Dr. McCallister besides her work phone and email. When you call her, it rings several times and goes to a voicemail. Email attempts to reach her don't get a reply, either. This isn't out of the ordinary for many professors, who can get bogged down with administrative or research obligations.<br /> <br /> When you show up to your next FYS class on Thursday, however, you and Ragnar see an unfamiliar face at the front of the room. It's a middle-aged man who explains that he was asked to fill in unexpectedly for the rest of the semester, as Dr. McCallister has unexpectedly requested emergency medical leave.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If you want to explore the woods in La Grange, the local LGBT community, or anything else with the other PCs you've met, please state your intentions here and include what day and time of day you'd go and what you'd be trying to do or look for. I'll also say that you can gain a Beat for accomplishing your Aspiration to &quot;get the know the rest of the group&quot;, as you've had more time today to meet and learn about each of them. Pick a new one. You may also engage in your Gluttonous Vice if desired; there's plenty of time to do something creative that might accomplish it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You are able to reach each of the surviving members of Hakim's old cabal. The Knights of Alhambra communicate with you via phone calls and texts, but prefer at this time not to meet with you in person; they suggest instead to meet at the upcoming Consilium meeting. You can tell from their language that they are shocked to hear of your Awakening, and they are certainly cordial and polite, but you get the sense that you're not sure how they feel about talking to you. Your connection to Hakim brings up old hurts for them, and you made your choice to follow Hakim rather than serving the cabal. They haven't forgotten that. Still, they help facilitate your request for an Arrow sanctum for a few days.<br /> <br /> You spend some time crashing for a few days at an Arrow safe house, a sanctum available to traveling Arrow members who come into Chicago for local Consilium business when a caucus meets here. You have the place to yourself for the next few days. The sanctum is located in the upper level of a duplex home in La Grange. It has a few wards in place, mostly some basic Mind spells, that make Sleepers feel an urge to avoid the entrance to your floor.<br /> <br /> You don't manage to make any contact with a Mind Adept who is immediately available to see you, at least one who would be willing to help. But Rose of Sharon does know of someone, an Arrow colleague and old friend, who <i>might</i> be willing to help you. She suggests talking more about it at the Consilium meeting.<br /> <br /> Rumors Nightclub is a modern, upbeat LGBT hangout. With a little bit of persuasion (and possibly some Mind magic?), you're able to arrange for a brief meeting with the club manager on duty. It's an attractive African American woman in her late 30s or early 40s named Erica. She seems open enough to the prospect of seeing what you have to offer, but she's very business-like about it. &quot;We have a lot of people coming here interested in work,&quot; she explains. &quot;Make a good case for why I should consider you, and I can give you a call if we have an opening or if I have any other questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Make any rolls you want for spells as discussed in the OOC thread. If you want to start the Social Maneuvering process at the bar, first let me know if you'd be doing any Mind spells that might influence the rolls before we get into that. Otherwise, she starts at an Average impression and has 2 Doors. You can make any Attribute + Skill roll that seems appropriate for how you'd like to try and open a Door. Engaging in Social Maneuvering will also grant you a Beat for your Aspiration, so pick a new one.<br /> <br /> As for finding sacrament Yantra, the possible issue is that Moonstone doesn't have any dots in Resources. So, without some magic or help, he can't just procure whatever he wants. You may be able to use the Infamous Mentor merit, but will need to roll for that -- let me know which route you want to go and we can talk logistics.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You return to your small La Grange apartment and find your roommate, Patty LeBlanc, a UofC computer science major. She's in the middle of heating up some leftover pad thai and has her laptop open on the kitchen table, where she's rapidly typing away.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/26/71/7d/26717dc8c0099e692d629de07c45604e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>(Is this close to what you had in mind for her appearance?)</i><br /> <br /> Patty looks up and smiles. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Hiya Simon, how's it going?&quot;</span> she asks in a cheerful tone. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;How'd things go with your FYS class? Any cuties in there?&quot;</span> she winks.<br /> <br /> After the day you've had, you feel an urge to pull out one of your hookup apps and look for some casual, refreshingly uncomplicated sex. Part of you wonders if the pleasure will feel as good as your newfound appreciation for magic, though.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You receive a phone call on Wednesday from Dr. Gray, the Dean you briefly ran into at school yesterday. He explains that Dr. McCallister has unexpectedly requested emergency medical leave and won't be able to continue with the class. He seems irritated and a bit stressed from the sudden change of plans. He apologizes profusely for the change in plans, but says not to worry -- they've found a replacement who will be willing to help out for the semester in a pinch. When you show to class on Thursday, he's there at the front of the room.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Let me know specifically what rolls you'd like to make or how you'd like to try pursuing your aspirations/Obsession, or what spells you would like to cast. If you take some time to use Mage Sight or some Unveiling spells, you can pretty easily accomplish your Aspiration to investigate your apartment complex for supernatural disturbances, or make progress towards your Obsession.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dr. Marvin Bates receives a phone call early on Wednesday morning from Dr. Gray. You don't know him personally, and it's been a while since you were in contact with someone at the undergrad side of UofC. But Dr. Gray knows from talking to his network of colleagues that you have enjoyed working with and mentoring students early in their academic career, and he is reaching out to you specifically for that reason.<br /> <br /> He explains that the precious instructor unexpectedly filed for emergency medical leave, which has left the class and department in a very difficult spot, as the students need the class to graduate. He says that he knows it is a very large favor, but he offers a salary bonus and emphasizes how much it would help the students. He asks you to start coming to the classes on Thursday, emails you the course syllabus Dr. McCallister had created, and ultimately thanks you repeatedly for your willingness to help. <span style=\"color:dodgerblue\">&quot;This means so much to me,&quot;</span> he says to you. <span style=\"color:dodgerblue\">&quot;Really, thank you for your help.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Please clarify whether Ophis would introduce himself by his sympathetic name or some other pseudonym. Also let me know if there is anything else he would do, either at the class or during the week.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Shortly after leaving the mansion, you pull out your cell phone and realize that you have two missed calls and several texts from your wife Daisy. Your phone says that it's 4:30 pm, but you were supposed to pick up Forest from elementary school a little before 4 pm. Her messages have a mixed tone of fear and irritation, asking why she's getting calls from the school asking who is going to pick up Forest. The later messages are asking whether you're alright and urging you to call her when you see this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Please include what you'd tell Daisy about your tardiness. If you want to cast any spells around the shop or change its name, feel free to include that in your post, too.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> After you depart from the group for now, you find yourself in downtown Chicago and once again wonder where Anubis is. A number of people eye you and the staff you're carrying, most of whom give you a wide berth; no one wants trouble, and it's easier to not ask questions. The encounter with the Gulmoth and subsequent meeting with the Shields of Dawn cost you the better pat of the afternoon. Rush hour is going to be here soon, creating waves of people that Anubis could easily hide in. You know enough about Supernal magic, real magic, to know that he could probably hide in plain sight -- which makes you wonder if invisibility is out of the question.<br /> <br /> Still, you're a Hunter. At least, you used to be. You aren't one to quit just because the mission is hard. You don't quit until justice is served, the rival vanquished. And so you keep looking for Anubis.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The staff sings in your hands.<br /> <br /> It feels <i>right</i> to you. You flow through your staff kata, and the staff swings swiftly through the air to your rhythm. It feels well-crafted, more so than the average bo staff you've used in your classes. None of your students seem suspicious or overly curious about the weapon. A few give compliments on it, ask if you made it yourself or where you found it, and several ask to use it themselves for a little while to test its balance.<br /> <br /> The longer you train, the more you feel the tension in your body slowly melt away, as if you're working out aches in your bones that you didn't realize were there. <i>This</i> is what you're good at. This is your calling. Decisive, efficient action.<br /> <br /> When you go home from training, there's another bill notice in your mailbox. Electricity is past due. The letter has some very unkind words in it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Clarify how, specifically, you want to try looking for &quot;Anubis.&quot; If you want to use any magic to help, include those rolls. Otherwise pick an Attribute + Skill that makes sense based on your approach (e.g., Wits + Streetwise, Intelligence + Investigation).<br /> <br /> Let me know if you want to do anything else in the down time, or any other rolls/spells you'd like to attempt. If you make intentional effort, you can also find a way to satisfy your Rigid Vice -- perhaps by missing out on some opportunity by sticking to a schedule, gettign in an argument with another student over something, whatever. Just clarify how you'd try to accomplish that, if relevant.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Clarified that this is a new scene 10-20-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T00:46:59-07:00","id":990321,"title":"","content":"[duplicate post]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:11:32-07:00","id":990416,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant<br /> Health: LL</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 8/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Moonstone thinks hard on Valentine's words about the Guardians, and is tentatively open to talking more about it on Saturday.<br /> <br /> Things are tense and awkward with the rest of the Nameless, and he's relieved to have a portal opened for them so they can be on their way. He's not ready for apologies yet and he doesn't provide his contact information or anything for right now, but expresses that he'll see the others on Saturday. He does take a minute to thank Marlin/Binder sincerely for his Clear Thoughts spell earlier that day, and requests to stop by the bookstore this week if he's available.<br /> <br /> Briefly thinks about destroying Valentine's card in the name of security, but decides that it would be rude, and a more powerful Mastigos could easily get Sympathy to him anyway.<br /> <br /> He goes straight to the sanctum in La Grange for now, doesn't even go back to the apartment. That's too big for today. Once he gets settled in, he immediately sleeps for 12 hours straight and dreams fitfully.<br /> <br /> <b>Wednesday</b><br /> <br /> He does a Divination to find the best date and time to visit Rumors this week if he wants an audience with a manager.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">gnosis 1, time 2, personal tool 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447474\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a>, then later tries again for <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447475\" target=\"_blank\">another failure</a>. I'll make that a dramatic failure for an Arcane Beat, because Moonstone is clearly just terrible at using his Praxis and <i>really </i>needs to get some rote training from an Order instead of winging it with a non-Ruling Arcanum. Maybe a custom Condition that penalizes Time magic would be appropriate since he just keeps getting it wrong?<br /> <br /> Also, Moonstone does Pattern Scouring every day this week, taking a -1 Strength penalty for 3 Mana each day. I'll balance the scales at the end of this scene, just mentioning it for now.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But it doesn't work. He throws up his hands in frustration and almost gives up, but writes down what he's thinking to get it out, and eventually decides he'll just go in tomorrow when they open and wing it. For now, he has some acquaintances to hit up.<br /> <br /> He visits a middle-aged white woman who goes by <b>Seldarine </b>in occult circles, an artist (and frequent patron of Marlin's bookstore) who split from the local Dianic Wiccan coven over an obscure but deeply felt theological dispute and now acts as an independent &quot;low pracitioner.&quot; She knows him as Moonstone, a ritualist from a different enough tradition to not be a rival. As far as he knows, she has no knowledge of the Awakened. But she does have knowledge of ritual trappings, which sometimes reflect the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Here's what I'm thinking for the sacraments. I'd like to use my Contacts (non-Awakened Occultists) to find some good sources, then harvest some immaterial stuff and just steal some physical stuff.<br /> <br /> Moonstone straight up tells her that he's looking for sources for &quot;found/secondhand&quot; ritual material resonant with Mind, Space, and Time. But he presents it more as props for a performance art piece than an Awakened magical working. Manipulation+Subterfuge+1 because this seems highly relevant to the Contact area: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447482\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> I'm just going to run with this myself if you don't mind, feel free to adjust or edit anything. I'd like to say that she gives him the name of a curio/antique shop in La Grange, and a paranormal message board.<br /> <br /> First, he posts on the message board and requests that people post their dreams. He makes it clear that he intends to glean mystical significance from them, but posters will not be harmed or touched in any way. His theory is that this will work better if people give him their dreams directly, rather than him reading some other dream journal passively. Manipulation+Occult: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447483\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Presumably he gets one good detailed response to the thread, and he writes it out with pen on fine paper and folds it away for later.<br /> <br /> Second, he scopes out the curio shop. This is far, far from the first time in his life that he's committed mundane theft for personal gain, although he's a little out of practice and his days of pawning Mom's jewelry are long behind him. He (barely) justifies today's crime to himself on grounds that they're Sleepers and he's using it for a better purpose than they ever could, and besides, it's not like he's robbing them blind. Then he casts Incognito Presence.<br /> <br /> 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for scene duration. Paradox 1, -2 from dedicated tool, chance die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447489\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2, personal tool 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447490\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. Spending 1 Mana from the Cloak (now 5/10) to activate.<br /> <br /> Once he's made himself forgettable, he goes in and peruses the store for a bit, savoring the sensation of invisibility, and picks out a handful of interesting but cheap curios that &quot;no one will miss.&quot; Old maps, vintage watches, dusty spyglasses. Wits+Stealth: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447496\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> If it's alright, I'll assume that Moonstone has one +2 Time, Space, and Mind sacrament each.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After he's quite unethically and illegally acquired some knick-knacks and occult curios, he's still in a Yantra-contemplating mood, so he heads back to the duplex Sanctum and thinks about Sympathy for a while. He knows some things secondhand, but wants to feel out Space himself. After hiding Valentine's card in a closed book, he spends about an hour in front of a floor-length mirror trying on clothes and accents and ways of walking and moving. He's trying to caricature Mathias, and develop a recognizable impression of him, even if it's a broad one. When he thinks he's got something, he stares daggers at his iPhone and says in an affected accent: <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I, Mathias, <i>Adept</i> of Fate, Disciple of Time, Apprentice of Forces, th\u00e9arch of the Silver Ladder and sworn to the Lunargent Thorn of Arcadia, accept your challenge to the Duel Arcane.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Then, he snaps a selfie.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Trying to see if this is sufficient to create a Symbolic-level sympathy yantra. Manipulation+Expression to caricature Mathias: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447503\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-20-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:12:26-07:00","id":990417,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone - Thursday</b><br /> <br /> Without the benefit of Divination, he's going to Rumors the old-fashioned way: early evening when they open. He briefly stops by his and Hakim's apartment to get some of his more comfortable and appealing dancewear, a mix of the skintight and the soft and flowing, veils and bangles and the like.<br /> <br /> When he gets to the venue and asks around a bit- perfectly polite, it's really very sweet- he's eventually pointed to Erica, the manager on duty. He surreptitiously snaps a pic of her on his phone, just a quick shot. But still enough for the camera to capture a piece of her soul, as cameras do. He looks down at the picture and attunes himself to the environment of the club as he walks toward her, smiles sincerely, and completes his Imago of warmth and good feeling as they shake hands. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Erica? I'm Roger. Lovely to meet you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using my starting equipment, dance/performance Fashion with a +2 bonus to relevant rolls.<br /> <br /> Wits+Stealth to take a picture unseen and get a suitable Material yantra: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447516\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> <br /> Casting Mind 2 &quot;Emotional Urging&quot; to open one Door. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for scene duration. 1 paradox: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447518\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2, Material sympathy +2, friendly and open club Environment +1, willpower +3, raising Potency -4. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447520\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a> Potency 4, one Door opens if Erica has Composure 3 or less.<br /> <br /> Also making a totally mundane Manipulation+Expression (Dance) roll, hoping to raise her impression level to Good by talking shop about dance and clearly coming prepared and ready to perform. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447524\" target=\"_blank\">no success.</a> forgot to add +2 equipment bonus: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447525\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He gives a bit of semi-true, semi-false background that makes him sound only a little older than he looks. Did a Modern Dance program at UCLA, lived in the area for a little while, used to perform with <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;a small artistic troupe, kind of an experimental performance cabal&quot;</span> but now looking to get out of his comfort zone and meet and perform in front of new people. He's not a good enough liar to hide the implication that he recently lost a loved one and he's trying to cope with the grief by exploding outward instead of retreating inward, so it just sits there between his smile and pleasant laugh and carefully applied makeup and nervous need to do something with his fingers. He doesn't really <i>talk </i>to Sleepers about himself like this, it's been a long time since he's been part of their world.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm sure you don't have the time for a full routine. Is there an open pole I could work with, just to give you an idea of my skill level?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Planning to open the Door using Dexterity+Athletics to show off some more advanced moves. Would any environmental or equipment bonuses/penalties apply?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:57:22-07:00","id":990444,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 2</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>TUESDAY AFTERNOON - HOME</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#B8860B\">What the <i>fuck</i> man, didn't you ever hear of knocking or something?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I live here,</span>&quot; Oscar replies flatly, pocketing his keys. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">And the door was locked.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> With a shrug, Oscar goes to his own room. In one corner on a study desk stands his laptop, a cup of pens, a lamp, a mess of papers and a geography textbook. His bookcase has a small assortment of statuettes and idols of various miniature animals, some computer paraphernalia, and some of his other textbooks. He throws his backpack on the bed - a mess of two pillows and a duvet - his body eager for some rest. Yet his belly grumbles, and with a sigh, he goes to the kitchen.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#B8860B\">So what's up?</span>&quot; Ewan asks nonchalantly as he returns from his own room, now dressed.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Long day,</span>&quot; Oscar shrugs as he starts preparing a sandwich. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Classes. New people. Still getting used to the world and this life. What about you? How'd your day at Uni go? You want one?</span>&quot; He gestures to his food-in-progress.<br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>WEDNESDAY</b></div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Lynx will go to his classes as normal. After Uni, he will go check out the closest Zoo to where he lives to observe the animals. While there, he will cast Spirit 1 &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot; with prolonged duration. Any Mages in the area should feel their Periphery go off. If Lynx sees any spirits, he will communicate with them if possible.<br /> <br /> After that, he will spend most of the evening in the woods and with the wildlife, still with &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot; up, to communicate with spirits.<br /> <br /> He'll interact with spirits, in particular feline ones, wondering if they might know of the &quot;Great Lynx&quot; he's looking for, through a Socialise roll.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>ACTION: Lynx casts Spirit 1 &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot; and gains 1 success.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Self.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Advanced, 1 week.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice)<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Spirit 1 &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot;: Spirit (2) + Gnosis (1)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 2 Free Reach: 1 spent on Instant Cast, 1 spent on Advanced Duration. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447643\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Spirit 1 &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot; \u2192 1 success.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ACTION: Lynx socialises with spirits he finds in the Zoo and the woods and garners 1 success.</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447647\" target=\"_blank\">Socialise roll to chat with spirits \u2192 1 success.</a><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>THURSDAY - FYS CLASS</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Simon!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Oscar hurries over to Ragnar - <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Simon in public, Ragnar when ... alone? That doesn't sound right...</span></i> - and claps him on the shoulder. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">How're you today? Have you heard from Dr. Asp... Ah, McCallister?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Faen.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm a little worried,</span>&quot; Oscar says quietly as he looks down to the podium, at the middle-aged man. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I mean... Do you think something's bad happened? I mean, Tuesday-kind of... bad?</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:27:40-07:00","id":990732,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 0/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> Ragnar waves at Patty wearily. Suddenly, he feels very, very tired. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Oh, hey Patty. Well, there is... one guy. He's pretty interesting.&quot; </span>But he needs something quick and easy <i>right now. </i>Once he eats, he hops on a hookup app and solicits the first non-creepy guy he can find: some muscly closeted guy who's going to UChi too. They meet in an isolated spot on campus and Ragnar lets himself get taken for the first time in ages. And it feels good, damn good, to surrender and feel overpowered again... but its the first time he's been with somebody since he Awakened, and part of him feels disappointed with himself. Anonymous, up-against-the-wall flings were how Simon Collins satisfied himself. There's no need for <i>Ragnar </i>to subside like this. And two thoughts sully the encounter further: one, that sex, at least with Sleepers, doesn't seem to satisfy like it used to. Not that he knows magic now. And second, that he more than anything right now to hear somebody to whisper his <i>real </i>name in his ear while doing this. They hardly speak throughout the encounter, and the other guy is vague about meeting up again. Ragnar's not sure he wants to.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar regains a point of Willpower. He'll be spending it Thursday. That way, he'll be able to do some magic and still have max Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> On Wednesday, Ragnar spends some time looking around the apartment complex in the morning, and then in the afternoon after classes. He opens his Sight to Fate and Time, examining every nook and cranny of the exterior and interior. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar uses Fate and Time Sight to search for signs of supernatural activity. Let me know if there's any Opacity so that he can go for Revelation and Scrutiny at a later time, preferably with some backup as appropriate by Arcana.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Thursday comes, and he reunites with Lynx- <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Oscar, for now- </span></i>and meets Dr. Bates. He considers Lynx's question. When they have a second, he whispers, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;We'll have to ask at the Consilium meeting. I'll bet you dollars to donuts that Dr. Asphodel was a Moros; Mathias mentioned that the mage he wanted to join our cabal is one. We'll have to be careful how we ask. We might be able to ask if 'Dr. McAllister' is okay, but we can't just clue everybody in to Dr. Asphodel's sympathetic name.&quot;<br /> <br /> After class,</span> Ragnar decides to review the events of the fight with Alux, and their immediate aftermath. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar attempts to cast Postcognition (Time 1). He has two free Reach, which he spends on Advanced Duration and on the option to &quot;scrub&quot; the memory. <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Time 2 + Concentration 2+ Willpower 3 = 8 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447787\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ragnar pours over the events of the fight and the conversation after, watching it from the perspective of everybody present, trying to glean some information that he may have missed in the confusion and chaos of Monday. He winces every time Mathias throws Moonstone up against the wall, and he stupidly snarks at him immediately after. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><i>Moonstone seems like he has some talent at Time. Hopefully he's reviewing this, too. And the next time we fight that thing, Lynx really does need to take a look at it with Spirit. </i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:18:37-07:00","id":991332,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight:</b>Periphereal/Active(Death/Matter) | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 10/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY</b><br /> <br /> Thunder.<br /> <br /> Lightning.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\"><i>Wasn't the other way around?</i></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Thunder.<br /> <br /> Lightning.<br /> <br /> -&quot;<span style=\"color:#FFA07A\">MAAARVIIINNN!!!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> That silent thunder again, followed by a flash of dark lightning.<br /> <br /> -&quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\">Melissa? Melissa. MELISSA!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Thunder.<br /> <br /> Lightning.<br /> <br /> Marvin Bates woke up in his appartment covered in cold sweat, his heart racing and his eyes red with tears. It took him a good couple of minutes to focus himself enought to realize that the phone was ringing.<br /> <br /> -&quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\">Bates speaking</span>&quot; - he listens in a daze to a certain Dr. Grey mumbling about a sudden medical leave and a syllabus that needs to be taught. He agrees to do it without really thinking about it, still recovering from the nightmare.-<span style=\"color:#1E90FF\">&quot;This means so much to me,&quot;</span>- he says-<span style=\"color:#1E90FF\">&quot;Really, thank you for your help.&quot;</span>-Marvin doesn't remember even hanging up.<br /> <br /> Was it really a week since all that happened? It seemed like ages. It seemed like yesterday.<br /> <br /> He gets out of bed and goes straight to the shower, letting the cold water clean away his skin and his nightmares, numbing his muscles and conscience. He looks in the mirror and barely recongnizes the man looking back to him. He sighs and takes a comb and sccisors, trimming his beard and moustache, and cutting what hair is left in his balding head short. Much better, he allows himself a quick smile of something resembling satisfaction before he suits up and goes to his laptop.<br /> <br /> How efficient. As expected the notes from Dr. Mc Allister had already been sent his way. He starts reading while his cofee starts to boil in the kitchen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>THURSDAY</b><br /> <br /> He really thought it would be harder to adapt, but Marvin could feel himself getting better the moment he entered the campus. The loud activity and life filling the air, lifted his spirit, he was starkly reminded why he loved to teach the young generation.<br /> <br /> He was early so he could afford a walk. He barely even felt the snake coiling around his heart.<br /> <br /> Once he humored himslef he went to what would be his department for the time being and made the last preparations for his first class.<br /> <br /> He entered the classroom and was greeted by a chorus of whispers and some confused looks as he put his papers on his table and wrote his name on the board.<br /> <br /> -&quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\">Welcome. My name is Marvin Bates, Dr.Bates if you wish. As some of you may already know, Dr. Mc Allister had to take a leave unexpectedly due to medical complications. Nothing particularly grave, I was asured. I will take over her class until she is ready to resume teaching herself, and I hope we all can make this transition as smooth as posible. I know all of you need this class to graduate, and I will make sure all of you do if you are ready to work with me</span>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Trying to make a good first impression with the class: Presence + Socialize = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448270\" target=\"_blank\">2 Successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He decides to make a quick recap of what they had seen up until now, to be sure he can move forward with the syllabus next day. He tries to make things as simple and comprehensible as posible, making sure no one is left behind and that all possible doubts are dispelled before they actually start with the meat of the course.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Magistral Class: Intelligence + Expression = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448273\" target=\"_blank\">3 Successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It goes well. Better than he expected giving his latest circumstances. But the slithering is still there on the background, Ophis wants to take a look at the class too. He figures that there's nothing wrong to Open His Eyes, just a little bit, not that he expects anything relevant to show up.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Activating Mage Sight (Death/Matter)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:33:35-07:00","id":991336,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Your sleep is indeed fitful. You fall asleep quickly out of sheer physical and mental exhaustion, but find yourself tossing and turning during the night. Most of your dreams include Mathias, Alux, Hakim, or some combination of the three. In some, you conquer Alux; in others, your body and mind are ravaged by the Gulmoth while the other mages watch with disgust, apathy, or eagerness.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Your inability to read the future places a crack in your calm fa\u00e7ade. You find yourself growing irritable, as it brings up thoughts about your encounter with Mathias yesterday.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for the dramatic failure on a spell roll. While I like the idea of a custom condition related to Time magic, I think it's too circumscribed and doesn't add much drama or conflict to this scene. Instead, I'm again giving you the custom condition I used before, and tweaking it a bit now that I've actually read the rules on Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <b>Irritable</b>. Like a lion lashing its tail and looking ready to pounce, your character is feeling on edge and thinking about lashing out. Small things that you might normally ignore or brush away have a tendency to get under your skin. Take -2 to Composure rolls. In addition, add 1 Door to Social Maneuvering encounters, as others pick up on your mood and it puts them on edge.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution</u>: This Condition is resolved when your character's anger causes you to do something that you might later regret about yourself or someone else, such as saying or doing something that might cause harm to a significant relationship (e.g., spreading a negative rumor, breaking something you or someone else owns). Alternatively, you can take a dramatic failure on a Social Maneuvering attempt to resolve this condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Beat</u>: N/A.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Your meeting with Seldarine is as fruitful as you expected, if not as much as you could have possibly hoped for. Her advice leads you to resources that can provide some useful sacraments. You ponder the significance of the dreams, and nature of dreams themselves, as you write down the journal entry.<br /> <br /> You definitely are comfortable with taking things from others, whether out of necessity or when you've found ways to justify it. Something's a little different this time, however: The act of using Mind magic to intentionally take things without drawing attention from Sleepers, however, gives you a thrill that you haven't felt before. You think once again about the things you can do now with magic that society has kept out of your reach. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Really love the depth of detail you've provided here, and I want to reward you for it. No changes to the actual rolls/actions, so go ahead and take the +2 sacraments. I do think that the items you're seeking are probably more realistically +1 sacraments, but I will allow you +2 given the RP effort here and multiple steps taken to find them.<br /> <br /> I do think that intentionally using magic to allow you to steal things will constitute an act of hubris and risk a degeneration roll at the Understanding level (3 dice). Although it's not at the same level as premeditated violence per se, it's still allowing you to engage in an act that could become a slippery slope. However, because Moonstone feels justified and is being very confident and intentional about this, I'll say that it relates to his Bold Virtue and add 1 to the roll. So roll 4 dice and take another Arcane Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Later, you snap the photo of your impression of Mathias and immediately review it. Studying the picture evokes a mixture of accomplishment and annoyance towards the mage who dared to humiliate you in public. When you flip over to the picture you took of the actual Mathias, the emotional reaction is stronger. You can sense that your impression of Mathias is symbolic enough to work as a Yantra, but the actual photo of him is clearly a more powerful connection.<br /> <br /> Next, you study your own Sympathetic connections to Alux by casting a weave of Space magic around yourself. You sense a Medium connection to the Gulmoth, and know that Alux is its true sympathetic name.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> On Thursday, you head to the club and use your burgeoning mastery of the Mind Arcanum to sway the mood around you. You snap the photo of her, which you then subtly delete on your phone just as you cast your spell, as you know that you must destroy the sacrament you've collected in order to fuel your magic. You can actually see the spell settle on her; her pupils dilate just a little, and she smiles at you as she speaks in a tone that's a little more pleasant than it had been a few moments ago.<br /> <br /> Erica seems impressed enough with your background and outfit; combined with your spell, she seems somewhat impressed. &quot;Sure, let's see what you've got.&quot; She walks you over to the main stage in the club, which is currently empty of patrons; there are miscellaneous bartenders and staff members washing dishes, setting up decorations, and overall making the place ready for another fun night.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So originally she was at Average impression and 2 Doors. Due to the Irritable Condition I added, she's at 3 Doors. But with your rolls and spell, she drops back down to 2 Doors and bumps up to Good impression. You can roll Dex + Athletics + 2 (bonus from professional dancing attire) to open one Door, and can make another new attempt the following day if you like.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Ewan shrugs. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;Eh, about the same,&quot;</span> he replied. He nods at your offer for food; he's been eyeing your sandwich and is quick to take up your offer to make one for him. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;I've been doing this new work-out routine that kicks the shit out of me. Feels fucking great, but I've been crazy hungry, you know?&quot;</span> Ewan wolfs down the sandwich and grabs some extra helpings of protein out of the refrigerator: some hardboiled eggs, beef jerky, and a protein shake. He plops down on the living room sofa and goes to town on the rest of his food. Between bites, he shares random thoughts about his day. He talks about a cute girl he saw at the gym earlier whom he's convinced was checking him out. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;Not my type, though. Too easy for sure.&quot;</span> He's mostly taking a few general classes for graduation requirements, as well as some business classes -- he's planning to major in business administration.<br /> <br /> Ewan pulls out his phone and gets a bit distracted. He's tapping away for a while, and a little after dinner time, he shares that he's going to meet up with a friend and says he'll be back later. He leaves abruptly, leaving you in an empty apartment.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You never realized how strange the zoo could feel when you look at it from a completely different view. You're at the Brookfield Zoo northeast of La Grange, a popular tourist attraction in the area. Even before you cast your spell, you feel things on your Periphery, as if the hairs on the back of your neck are rising in response to being watched.<br /> <br /> Instinctively calling upon the Spirit Arcanum, you Unveil your eyes to the ephemeral quality of spirits around you. You see them, really see what's there in a way you haven't before. There are...creatures...around the zoo in Twilight. There aren't as many active spirits as you might have suspected -- but then again, you probably aren't sure what a &quot;normal&quot; population of spirits in any area might be. Either way, this is the first time you've been able to truly study spirits without being pressured for time.<br /> <br /> Some you can identify immediately, because of their reflection in nature as you know it. Spirits of several animal types roam the zoo: A bear spirit chases a trout spirit, a lion spirit prowls in Twilight chasing down other smaller prey. Most seem to lack any clear sentience beyond instinctive behavior to &quot;eat&quot; Essence or avoid predation. Some &quot;sleep&quot; within things. You touch an old tree and sense a dormant spirit of life within it; you're not sure why or how these things hibernate, but some are. As you watch, the bear spirit outpaces the smaller trout one, and it claws away at the thing, stealing its Essence. It's a very primal experience suggesting that in the world of spirits, you hunt or are hunted. <br /> <br /> Some of the spirits are hard to identify, weird mixtures of colors and shapes. They remind you of primal urges, of symbolic representations, but you don't always know what they are just by looking. One, resembling a chain in loops, evokes a sense of sadness that you interpret as a spirit of captivity. It seems to be feeding on the emotional qualities of some animals nearby.<br /> <br /> When you approach them, the spirits seem very cautious of you. Most ignore you entirely or quickly scuttle away as you approach. But the lion spirit you saw earlier studies you curiously and is willing to speak to you, uttering sounds in a flowing language that sounds only very loosely related to High Speech -- the language of the Supernal Realms that you have learned through Awakening.<br /> <br /> The lion spirit seems to be sizing you up, determining if you are predator or prey. <i>&quot;What are you seeking, little cub?&quot;</i> the spirit says to you. As you watch, it suddenly pounces on a minor, unintelligent spirit and consumes its Essence.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for your first chance to really study spirits and attempts to interact with them.<br /> <br /> If you want to obtain more information about the Great Lynx spirit, you can attempt to make a social roll or use a spell to influence the spirit. But it is not inclined to help you, as most spirits offer grudging respect to mages at best, especially if/when you ever encounter some in the Shadow World.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Later, you go to the woods in La Grange. After your experiences at the zoo, you are surprised to see an even greater population of spirits here. You suspect that it has something to do with the Gauntlet, that barrier between the Shadow World and the Fallen World, but you can't tell without exploring things more with your magic.<br /> <br /> You again have the sensation of being watched. And then, more clearly, you feel a pulse of energy, of something odd happening on your Periphery.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Roll Wits + Composure for a Perception roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Patty is quick to pick up on your mood. She smiles warmly and pats you on your arm as she walks by. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I know that look, sweetie. Take a break tonight, do something fun for yourself. Or get some sleep. Either way, take it easy tonight.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And so you find yourself hooking up with the muscle head, who's got a firmly toned body with a broad chest and shoulders, and thick biceps and calves. You realize quickly that he is very paranoid about being seen; he's wearing dark clothing and insists on not using any names. He also insists on being the dominant partner in this encounter, which you oblige. Despite his nervousness, once you start he is eager to perform for you, and although he's awkward about it and hardly says anything, he seems to enjoy himself. He takes off shortly afterward.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You open your Sight to the influence of Arcadia in this Fallen World and begin to study the apartment. You're tentative at first, but quickly find yourself intensely curious and excited. With no urgency or time limit to your efforts, you can finally study Fate and Time at your leisure. <br /> <br /> Most of the building is disappointingly boring, although you find a few things interesting. You can discern which parts of the building have been recently repaired; you hadn't noticed with your mundane vision, but a few sections of the walls here and there are newly patched and painted.<br /> <br /> At one point, you see a young man walk by, probably 15 or 16 years old. You don't know who he is, but as you look at him you see his Destiny -- that's the only way you can describe it. You sense that he is destined to invent something, a tool or device that could be incredibly influential and helpful for millions. He's carrying a backpack, and you see a math textbook in his arms. You also see a potential Doom in his pattern of Fate, a cloud of depression looming in the future that could dash his dreams and cripple his ambition. The boy is smiling right now, though.<br /> <br /> You're almost done exploring when you notice a door in the apartment complex basement that carries a touch of the Supernal. You see wisps of energy around the door through the lens of Time, but you're not sure what to make of it. They seem frozen in place.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You'll need to use a WP to keep Active Sight for more than 1 minute, if you intend to study the whole building. This Mystery has Opacity 3.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> You find that you're naturally able to build rapport with the students. Because this is only their second class period of the semester, and you don't have Dr. McCallister's stutter or dry personality, you're able to quickly review the basic info in the course and draw the students in.<br /> <br /> When you open up your Sight, you can quickly tell that the students seated before you are all, thankfully (and expectedly), still alive. <br /> <br /> But in the back of the room, seemingly ignoring all of you, is a ghost. She appears in Twilight, not moving, staring around the room. She looks like she is wearing clothes from the early 1940s, very conservative dress, and thick frames glasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-22-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:10:59-07:00","id":991382,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 3/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <b>Tuesday</b><br /> <br /> Ho, I'm seriously late for work. In fact, I've missed the entire day by the time I get there. This is not gonna end well, but I'm gonna go there any way and receive my punishment. Least I could do, honestly.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Sorry, Master Jeon. I won't let it happen again,</span>&quot; I apologize, bowing my head. Glad to have that over with. Unfortunately, I forgot to change my clothes, my newly hole-ridden clothes from the fight with the Abyssal. It's also stained with blood, too. So naturally, many of the staff inquired about it. I gave them the hint that I really didn't want to talk about it. All that is, except for one of the instructors ((OOC: Not Jeon, though)). They keep pressing, trying to find out what happened exactly. They wouldn't let up, either. I know they were simply trying to help me, but the prying got a bit much after awhile.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>SHUT THE FUCK UP, ALREADY!</b></span>&quot; I snap in their face. Everything's silent for a minute, then I just finish my duties and leave.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448287\" target=\"_blank\">Presence 3 + Intimidation 2 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a><br /> <br /> This seems an appropriate point to resolve Irritable.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I come home to find a not-so-good letter for the electricity. Welp, no TV for me for awhile, and I'll have to skimp on meals as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Wednesday</b><br /> <br /> First order of business, find a roommate, I can't support the bills on my own. Not without working at another part-time job, and that'll eat up my time for more important things. I network with some people in the streets to find someone. Takes all day, but I actually manage to find someone who might be interested. Now I just need to convince them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448295\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligence 2 + Streetwise 1 = 3 dice \u2192 1 success</a><br /> <br /> Would this count towards fulfilling &quot;Solve the bill problem&quot; Aspiration for 1 Beat? The Aspiration wouldn't be completely fulfilled, but simply a step towards it. Possibly go for some Social Maneuvering now?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Thursday</b><br /> <br /> The trail's almost cold, but I've still got a few places to check, especially with my new-found Sight.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Looking for Anubis with Active Mage Sight used sparingly throughout.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448298\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligence 2 - 3 Untrained Investigation = Chance die \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I manage to get a lead, but it's not much. I'll definitely need to...get some help with this tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <b>Friday</b><br /> <br /> Alright man, you have to swallow your pride to these assholes. You need their help with the lead, and that means stroking their egos. Just take their jabs and jives. For your comrades. You owe them that justice be served.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I got a lead, but...I can't find Anubis...on my own,&quot;</span> I choke up to the Hunters, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I...need, really...need your help.,,please.,,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Damn, this is painful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:43:08-07:00","id":991693,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> Your outburst creates a deafening silence in the martial arts dojo. Students and colleagues alike stop in the middle of their exercises. Some look at you with shock, others with anger or irritation. A few avert their eyes, obviously not wanting to get involved or incur your anger. Master Jeon shakes his head slowly but says nothing. He doesn't need to; his face speaks volumes about his disappointment and disapproval.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You track down some leads on a roommate by surveying a few local shops and restaurants, as well as searching ads online. You find a sign in a coffee shop down the street from your apartment with a description and phone number, and set up a meeting.<br /> <br /> Ken Tanaka is a second-generation Japanese American young man going to college at the University of Chicago. He is currently an undergraduate sophomore pursuing his Bachelor's degree with double majors in economics and political science, but he explains that what he really loves is music. He is a talented viola player and often plays as a street performer in Chicago and downtown La Grange. He says his income is limited but that he is good enough to make rent, and he works a stable part-time job at the university bookstore. But he is looking for someone who won't mind if he practices in the apartment, and he's a little shy. He's looking for a new roommate because his last one unexpectedly dropped out of classes for the semester at the last minute.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Finding a roommate will let you resolve the Aspiration, but I'm going to say you won't do so until you can succeed on Social Maneuvering. You start with Average impression and only 1 Door; he has average Resolve/Composure but he is motivated to find a roommate. You can make a roll to try and improve your impression, so if you fail you can try again one day later, and then some roll to open the Door. If you succeed on opening the door, you gain a Beat and pick a new Aspiration.<br /> <br /> I assume you go by Garrick Royce with him and people at the dojo, right?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You've been searching all over for any signs of Anubis. The desperation to find something, anything, has long since settled into your bones. With limited ideas on what to do, you decide to retrace your steps (again) and return to where you first found the lich who attacked you, and where your Hunter allies met you. As you walk outside of the building where you nearly died, you open your Sight -- and freeze as you see a mage casting a spell of the Death Arcanum. He's walking out of the building, fingering something small in his right hand that you can't see immediately, and you have a feeling like you've seen him before.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s5.favim.com/orig/51/guy-boy-punk-rock-style-skater-Favim.com-470960.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> If you're right, there's a possibility that this mage has some association with Anubis, or the lich cult you tried to take down while you were a Hunter. Or he could be someone in the wrong place at the wrong time. You realize that you know enough about magic and mage society now to get yourself in trouble, but you aren't fully sure what to make of this event.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Before I comment on the Hunter cell and how they fit in, I would like to know how Phoenix would react to this potential lead. Does he decide to tail the guy, or leave him to find the Hunter cell and ask for their help?<br /> <br /> How does Phoenix feel about these other Hunters? From your back story, I thought he was trying to avoid running into them out of concern they'd realize he is a mage now or spending time with mage allies. Does Phoenix feel guilty about his past, annoyed with these guys, or what? Please help me understand their relationships with you so I can incorporate them correctly.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Added picture for the mage Phoenix runs into 12-09-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:39:52-07:00","id":991825,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Focused (Fate, Time)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> <br /> </div> It takes some mental effort to keep his Sight active for more than a minute, but Ragnar carries through with it. The frozen wisps pique his interest, and he attempts to investigate further, dropping the lens of Fate to channel all of his attention into Time. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is going to try Revelation on the Mystery. Gnosis 1 + Time 2 - Opacity 3 = chance dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448633\" target=\"_blank\">oh thank god</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:13:25-07:00","id":991842,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> You're surprised at how quickly you are able to make sense of this Mystery, at least at a surface level. Perhaps your practice yesterday helped you to better hone your basic understanding of how to use your Sight effectively. <br /> <br /> You glean a few curious things from these wisps of magic. First, they are definitely the source of the Time Arcanum, and clearly created by Supernal magic. You believe that they are due to the Ruling Practice, based on how they rest around the door frame: There appears to be another spell, a second Time spell, intricately woven in the wisps before you. It makes it hard to see what it could be without further study. <br /> <br /> You also notice that you can't recognize a distinct Signature Nimbus to this spell. You've noticed even in your brief time Awakened that virtually all spells carry a uniquely personal quality corresponding to the mage who cast it. This one doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typo 10-23-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:34:20-07:00","id":991845,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: Exorcist's Eye (Spirit 1;Potency 1; 1 week duration; Can see and communicate with spirits in the Physical World)<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (2/5 on Thursday, 4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 3</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TUESDAY EVENING - HOME</b><br /> <br /> Ewan's sudden departure leaves Lynx a little bemused at first, yet the solitude eases into him as he stretches and rubs his beard. Humming, he takes off his t-shirt - <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh, right, this is Mathias's shirt... I should give it back to him. Should tell him future shirts need to be a size or two larger.</span></i> - and he heads to the bathroom for a warm shower.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Lynx lies still in bed as he gazes up to the ceiling.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar... He's good. His voice is soothing. And he's nice. And smart. And good with words. A good friend.<br /> <br /> Dr. Asphodel... What happened to her? I'm worried. I dragged all of us into... into what again? I remember being wet, and then ... pavement and Mathias? I feel like we were drowning. Were we? Why do I feel so... apologetic?<br /> <br /> Phoenix is... Fierce? Definitely fierce. Blunt. A little angry and bitter. A little self-righteous. And dangerous. Is that a bad thing, though?<br /> <br /> Moonstone... I have no idea. I don't think he's a bad man, but he smells of everything at once. Anger and sadness and happiness and regret and... Dangerous. Really dangerous.<br /> <br /> Binder... I don't know. Too quiet, I think... Didn't say much.<br /> <br /> Valentine... Handsome, but a little... disturbing. Educated guesses? I guess, but it didn't feel like that. Something feels off about him.<br /> <br /> Boomer... Definitely my favourite. Looks wicked. And she seems to like me. So does Ragnar. And the look Phoenix gave me...<br /> <br /> Mathias... I don't know why, but I can't bring myself to rely on him. Losing his temper and attacking Moonstone like that? I mean, people did get hurt, but he did apologise, didn't he? Isn't that good enough? </span></i><br /> <br /> He sighs as the front door is unlocked. Heavy footsteps follow with some panting and the smell of sweat and... something else?<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">What is that...?</span></i><br /> <br /> Ewan's walk through their apartment is surprisingly quiet, though he's unable to muffle his heavy footsteps. Quiet profanity leads the way into the room opposite Lynx's, the door closes a little too angrily, and there is another sound of a door being locked. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - ZOO</b><br /> <br /> His hackles on edge, the world of Twilight within the zoo has Lynx in awe with every step. Much like a child's first trip to the Zoo - and incidentally, this is Lynx's first visit outside of Twilight - he stares in wonder at beast and spirit alike. Mostly the spirits. It is when the lion speaks that he is overwhelmed with giddiness.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>What are you seeking, little cub?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">What</span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\"> am <i>I seeking? It's all so new still... Ah!</i></span><br /> <br /> Lynx ponders for a moment as he studies the leonine spirit, and he takes a step forward. When he speaks, his voice is the same strange sound. &quot;<u><i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah, hello! Greetings, I mean! I was wondering if you might know of something like a... <b>Great Lynx?</b></span></i></u>&quot; He puts careful emphasis on the latter words. &quot;<u><i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Or other... <b>Great</b> spirits? Are you the <b>Great Lion</b>? Or... a <b>Great</b> one?</span></i></u>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Do spirits have titles? Can there be more than one Great spirit? Why does referring to a spirit as</span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\"> Great <i>sound stupid on repeat?</i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Lynx attempts to persuade the Lion spirit for information, and garners 1 success.</span></b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448639\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Persuasion \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - FOREST</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448641\" target=\"_blank\">Perception roll in the forest \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-23-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:59:42-07:00","id":991854,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight:</b>Periphereal, Active (Death/Matter) | <b>Active Spells: </b>Able to interact with Death Twilight<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>5/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY (LATER)</b><br /> <br /> Marvin waits a while after the last student leaves the classroom, he doesn't want to spoil a good start by developing the reputation of being out of his mind if any were to see him talking to what would look essentially like thin air.<br /> <br /> He packs his belongings quietly, keeping an eye on the ghost woman while doing so. He focuses on keeping his Sight on, despite the effort and channels Mana through his pattern to be able to interact with this misterious lady. She is his first ghost, and he is both excited and terrified of the posibilities.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1 Willpower to keep Active Sight for the Scene, 1 Mana to activate Death Eyes Attainment to interact with Death Twilight</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\"><i>Who could she be?</i></span>&quot;-he wonders, walking slowly and hopefully not threateningly towards her in the back of the room. He makes a point of looking her in the eye, so she realizes he can actually see her before she starts to speak:<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Good morning, my lady, I am Dr. Bates</span> (no point in not using his name now after sharing it with the whole class) <span style=\"color:#006400\">may I ask you your name and if I may do something for you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First, could I change my vague &quot;Regain his life&quot; Aspiration for &quot;Helping Lady Ghost&quot;? Second: Interacting with Lady Ghost= Presence + Perssuasion (9-Again) =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448649\" target=\"_blank\">0 Successes,Ouch!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:59:28-07:00","id":991933,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Irritable<br /> Health: L</b>OOOOO | <b>Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 2/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 2/5</b></div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, Irritable is a lot more interesting than the mechanical penalty I suggested. I just wanted to introduce something a bit more arcane for a spellcasting problem.<br /> <br /> I figured this kind of petty theft would count as &quot;innocent bystanders are affected by your spells or actions,&quot; which is only a sin at higher Wisdom, but let's run with it. Act of Hubris, 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448403\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Moonstone continues to enjoy &quot;beginner's luck&quot; with this whole Wisdom thing.[/url]</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It <i>does</i> feel good to be unseen and untouchable. But there's a moment when he's turning over an antique watch, and the old woman who runs the shop looks at him, about to say something...and then immediately forgets that he's there and returns to her work. He thinks about the trouble she must have gone through to acquire the thing, and the whole thing feels exploitative.<br /> <br /> Not enough to return the things he stole from her shop, of course. But he turns the matter over in his mind and resolves to be more considerate of the livelihoods of Sleepers in the future, if not necessarily their property.<br /> <br /> When he goes to bed on Wednesday night, he tries to give himself better dreams, meditating before bed in an attempt to induce lucid dreaming.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Meditation roll to enter lucid dreaming (p.248), Resolve+Composure-2 from Irritable: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448683\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Only on Thursday morning does he realize it didn't work.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He's still pissed off and edgy about his failed Divination, and it's affecting his cool. Erica is clearly picking up on it. Performance anxiety is buzzing in his mind, but he's feeling refreshed and whole. It doesn't overwhelm him. He stretches and warms up, tests the pole, centers himself, loads some unobtrusive club music on his phone and goes through a condensed routine. He circles the pole and lets his fingers trace it, sidles up against the unfortunately cold metal, hops up and mounts it, climbs like a spider. Soon he's inverted, holding on with just his thighs, bicycling in the air, or gripping the pole with one hand and one knee and holding a pose, reaching his whole body out towards the heavens (or just the nightclub ceiling.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dexterity+Athletics+2: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448492\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes!</a> That should open 2 Doors. I'll take the Informed Condition related to Rumors, and perhaps draw the attention of a ghoul or some other vampiric agent...Also taking a Beat for resolving my Social Maneuvering Aspiration. New Aspiration: formally join a cabal.<br /> <br /> Minor point of order: Sympathy and Sacrament are two different types of yantras, and I was using the photo as the first one. You don't need to destroy a Sympathy item to get its bonus, although you can choose to destroy it and use it as a Sacrament as well. I'll say that Moonstone deleted the pic and used it as that.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He didn't actually intend for it to be an artistic performance, just a purely athletic demonstration of his skill level. But the new atmosphere of a modern nightclub rather than a Supernally-charged ritual space, this thing that caused him so much fear at first, instead leads him to bloom. His style is graceful, controlled, unique- he's adapting his movement to the pole, but he's channeling something otherworldly and ancient. As he dances, the generic club music and the atmosphere of the club and Erica and the dishwashers, they all melt away and become one with him and the pole becomes a line extending infinitely, and everything of consequence is a single point in Space. In the middle of the performance he visualizes exactly what his Correspondence ritual the next day will look like. Maybe there's something real when the Free Council talks about Supernal truth arising from human craft.<br /> <br /> He follows his own imagined rhythm after the music ends, climbing higher and corkscrewing around the pole, letting his bangles clatter and his veils hang low, and finally he inverts and grips the pole between his knees and slowly lowers himself backwards into a handstand on the floor, holds it, and somersaults into a standing position. He breathes hard as he comes down from the unexpected intensity of it. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;So...you know, that kind of thing.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-23-2016, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:00:35-07:00","id":991935,"title":"","content":"[duplicate post]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:01:37-07:00","id":991936,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone - Thursday Night</b><br /> <br /> As soon as he gets back to the sanctum, Moonstone uses his spark of inspiration and writes out a detailed ritual plan for tomorrow. He checks the star charts, sketches out the choreography, picks out the proper candles and incense from his collection, and stops by the old apartment to get what few Space-related icons and sigils Hakim had. He's done this many times before, with Awakened help, but it's the first ritual he's designed for himself. He instinctively refers to himself in the third person in his plans, as if this &quot;Moonstone&quot; was some other mage he now served.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Li'l Intelligence+Occult (Awakened Magic) roll to justify Moonstone performing an all-day extended ritual casting for the first time: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448497\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> <br /> edit: keep forgetting that I get 9-again on Occult rolls, and that's a lot of 9s. Rerolls: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448822\" target=\"_blank\">2 more successes</a>. That makes it an exceptional, I'll take Steadfast related to the Correspondence ritual.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With that taken care of, he has several less complex spells to cast. So he polishes his trusty mirror, goes to a quiet place, and gets to work.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First, my praxis Divination with a Space requisite. Withstand 2 for Medium sympathy to subject. 1 reach for instant, 1 for sensory range, 1 for detailed answers. Going to contain any paradox, 1 die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448500\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Wisdom 7: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448501\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>, 1 bashing damage for Moonstone.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Time 2. Yantras: path tool (+1), speaking the unspeakable name of Alux (no bonus). -2 to raise Potency to 3, +3 for spending 1 willpower. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448502\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> 1 Mana from the Cloak (now at 4/10) to cast sympathetically. Moonstone loads a street map of the Chicago area and asks: <i>Exactly when and where will Alux rematerialize?</i><br /> <br /> Next, going to try to use Mind 1 Perfect Recall for things that happened in the portal. 1 reach for instant casting, 1 for advanced potency. Gnosis 1, Mind 2, path tool +1. 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448503\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a> Per your rules, I'm gonna &quot;take 1&quot; and assume Moonstone tries again until he gets it right. With Potency 2, trying to recover 2 memories: <i>how exactly did I summon Alux? </i>And<i>: how did I get back to the real world?</i> I don't know whether this will be more difficult because of the magic of the portal, but here's a Clash of Wills roll (Gnosis 1+Mind 2+advanced potency 1) in case one is required: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448506\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Then, going to try a similar approach with a different Arcanum. Time 1 Postcognition to review what happened during the scene he and Phoenix were in the portal. 1 reach for instant, 1 for scene duration. Spending 1 Mana from the Cloak to activate (now at 3/10). Gnosis 1, Time 2, path tool +1, generic sacraments (memory-aiding incense and crystals) from my starting equipment +1. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448510\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Again, Gnosis/Time Clash of Wills if necessary: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448511\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-23-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:03:16-07:00","id":991937,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone - Thursday Night, cont.</b><br /> <br /> After taking a break to cook some dinner and walk around outside for a while, he returns for some more magical mystery. He's going to attempt some Scrutiny across Space and Time. He opens his Sight fully to the Supernal World, peers into his mirror, and reaches into the past.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Turning on Active Mage Sight with Mind, Space, and Time (spending 1 Mana from my own supply). Then casting Postcognition, also with 1 Mana from my own pool. 1 reach for instant, 1 for scene duration. Moonstone is reaching to the moment he, Phoenix and Alux returned to the physical world. That gives him 3 turns worth of Scrutiny by my count before Alux discorporates.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Time 2, tool 1, generic sacraments 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448514\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Going into Focused Mage Sight, centered on Alux. Spending 1 willpower to do Scrutiny using Mind, Space, and Time. That means I get 1 roll before my failures start getting dangerous, normally I would get 3 but my additional Arcana lower that by 2. Let's do this.<br /> <br /> Turn 1 Scrutiny, spending 1 Mana. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448655\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> +1 from Mana.<br /> <br /> Turn 2 Scrutiny, spending 1 Mana (Cloak now at 1/10). <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448657\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a>. I'll turn that into a dramatic failure for...a beat? An arcane beat? Nothing? IDK. But the Mystery gains 2 Opacity <i>and </i>an entity from Pandemonium takes notice and can affect me with its powers as long as I maintain Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Turn 3 attempting Revelation. Gnosis 1, Arcanum 2, Willpower 3, 6 dice minus whatever Opacity: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448670\" target=\"_blank\">9,9,1,4,9,5</a><br /> <br /> Following whatever magical experience surely ensues, Moonstone closes his Mage Sight. If he's somehow being tricked or trapped or enticed or something, he'll at least close it after 1 minute when he'd have to spend WP to keep it active.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Before he goes to sleep, he reads the stranger's dream journal that he wrote out on fine paper, then neatly folds it up into a paper crane to carry him into dreams and places it on a bedside table. He loads the picture of the defeated Mathias on his phone, studies it for a few minutes, and meditates on the image as he drifts off to sleep.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Another attempt at lucid dreaming, Resolve+Composure-2: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448685\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone's Dream</b><br /> <br /> He's sitting on Santa Monica Beach in LA, the spot he used to go when he was a kid. His toes are in the uncomfortably cool wet sand. The other people on the beach are a mix of faces from high school and the Shields of Dawn. He's aware that he's dreaming.<br /> <br /> He looks different in dreams, or rather, he looks different when he's awake from how he imagines himself to look, and in dreams he matches his self-image. There should be a beach-house near here, and indeed, there is. He climbs up the quaint little stairs cut into the cliffside and enters through the side door. He has made it look like a <i>Scooby-Doo </i>style hallway with dozens of doors on either side. He wants to feel the familiar weight of his dedicated mirror in his hand, and so there it is.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Time 2 Choose the Thread to improve my chances. Spending 1 Mana from my own supply. 1 reach for instant, 2 reach to affect spellcasting rolls. +1 paradox dice for risking earlier in the scene. 3 paradox dice, gonna contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448692\" target=\"_blank\">no successes.</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Time 2, path tool +1, environment +1, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448693\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The doors all lead to the same place, but in different ways. This is going to be a difficult working, so only one of the doors will lead to success. Looking at their reflections in the mirror, like a lens of truth, helps him identify the right path. He picks a black oaken door with an ornately carved brass handle and steps through, and now he's in the room where he dueled Mathias. The Acanthus is on his knees, exactly as he was in the picture Moonstone meditated on. He picks up the folded paper dream-journal-crane from the floor, sets it on balefire with a thought, and blows the smoke from the sacrament into Mathias' nostrils.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And finally casting Mind 2 Dream Reaching on Mathias sympathetically. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for sensory range, 1 reach to change primary factor to Potency, 1 reach for scene duration, 1 reach for casting a spell beyond my spell tolerance. +2 paradox dice for risking already this scene. 6 paradox, spending 3 of my own Mana to get that down to 3 dice, going to contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448700\" target=\"_blank\">no successes.</a><br /> <br /> Alright. I have to overcome Withstand 4 (Composure 3+1 for the lower Sympathy Withstand), so I need Potency 5, and I'm using one of my yantra slots on the Sympathy itself. Base Potency is 2. Spending 1 Mana from my supply for the sympathetic range. Gnosis 1, Mind 2, sacrament +2, willpower +3, Potency -6. 2 dice, and I roll it twice with Choose the Thread: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448703\" target=\"_blank\">first roll fails, second roll succeeds!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He chose the right door. Moonstone rides the sacrificial smoke into Mathias' mind, leaving his own dreams and entering the Other. He's not going to interfere or even embody himself, but he will try to subtly shift Mathias' dream to focus on prophecies and fates that are on his mind. He's not interested in spying on the mage's personal life, he wants to learn about the things that concern him magically, and especially what the prophet sees over the horizon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:04:52-07:00","id":991938,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone - Friday</b><br /> <br /> Friday is ritual day. He gets up at 5, shreds the dream journal, makes a spinach-and-pomegranate smoothie (the perfect mix of sympathetic power and healthy flavor), stretches and warms up, purifies his body, puts on makeup and silks, and enters the ritual space he prepared in the sanctum's utility room last night. At exactly 6:26 AM, when the sun first shines through the east-facing window, he rings a singing bowl and begins.<br /> <br /> It's a grueling, 12-hour ordeal that involves him traveling to various points in the room assigned astrological correspondences, dancing in place and in motion, ringing the bowl, reciting verses of Japanese death poetry, lighting carefully chosen candles and incense, symbolically wearing and removing the Cloak of Night, that sort of thing. He allocated time for a 5-minute break every 3 hours to rest his muscles, but he never leaves the room. It's not his first all-day ritual, but it <i>is </i>his first as the primary actor. Actually <i>knowing </i>the Truth of the occult correspondences he set out, <i>feeling </i>the rush of power as he draws his own performance into his Imago- it's completely different from everything he's experienced, even beyond what he imagined in his inspiration on the pole. When he reaches 3:33 PM and begins a prolonged waltz with Hakim's cloak, the sensation of magic is so strong that he doesn't realize how hard he's crying.<br /> <br /> At exactly 6:41 PM, after walking backwards from the edge of the room in a clockwise (symbolizing growth and perception) vertex (symbolizing privacy and secrets) spiral, and finally a vertigo-inducing dervish dance at the very center, he declares his Imago into the Fallen World by whispering: <span style=\"color:#008080\"><i>&quot;show me Lamont Torres-Wilson.&quot;</i></span> The room warps and shatters like a mirror, Time stands still, and his awareness expands throughout the universe. The only thing he perceives is Hakim, shrouded in the Cloak of Night, and the Deathstorm rumbling in the distance. There are threads to be followed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Broke out my Ars Magica books to get in the ritual symbolism mood, haha. Space 1 Correspondence! Subject is Hakim. 1 Reach for sensory range, 1 Reach to follow a trail of connections, 2 Reach to specify the type of connection. 2 paradox dice, gonna contain it: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448748\" target=\"_blank\">nothing on first die,</a> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448750\" target=\"_blank\">1 success on second die.</a> Wisdom 7: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448752\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>, 1 bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Moonstone has Strong Sympathy to Hakim, so it's Withstand 1. Using one of my yantras on Sympathy using the Cloak.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Space 2, generic sacraments +1, four ritual casting intervals +4, willpower +3, raising Potency -10. 1 die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448756\" target=\"_blank\">no success.</a> Resolving Steadfast to make that a success and gain a Beat.<br /> <br /> I have a final total of Potency 6. Specifically searching for those sympathetic links created, strengthened, or modified by the Deathstorm, and wanting to learn the strength of those links. I should learn: Hakim to A, A to B, B to C, C to D, D to E, E to F.<br /> <br /> Moonstone has four theories about what he might discover, to give this some structure.<ul><li>Every person killed in the Deathstorm has Sympathy to every other victim.</li> <li>Every victim has Sympathy to one other victim, possibly the next or previous person to die.</li> <li>Every victim has Sympathy to one single subject that represents/embodies/caused the Deathstorm itself, and that subject has Sympathy to every victim.</li> <li>Null result; the Deathstorm did not uniquely create Sympathy. If this were the case, he would expect to discover Hakim's connection to Moonstone (the nature of which was of course modified by the Deathstorm), Moonstone's connection to Hakim or some other connection (perhaps to Mathias or Alux) that was created or changed by the mundane fallout of the Deathstorm, and so on.</li> </ul><br /> His ideal outcome from this Obsession would be using Borrow Threads to gain Sympathy to other victims via Hakim, compiling a complete list of everyone who died because of the Deathstorm, and then using that knowledge. It could tell him whether someone died in the storm that no one else knows about yet or was covered up. It could tell him whether a death that appeared Deathstorm-related was actually for unrelated reasons (because the victim wasn't part of the Sympathy web), like an assassination using the storm as cover, or the supposed death might not have happened at all.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-23-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:53:36-07:00","id":992254,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> You make sure to wait for other people to wander past you before you try and speak to the lion spirit; you know that others would give you strange looks if they saw you talking to no one, especially uttering sounds and phonemes that don't exist in any human language.<br /> <br /> At your questions, the lion spirit seems to sit up and puff out its chest. It replies, &quot;<i>I may know of this spirit of which you seek. But you will not find it here. Few of our kind traverse to your world.</i>&quot; The lion spirit does not explain, however, why it chose to come to this side of the Gauntlet. &quot;<i>I am indeed a Great Spirit.</i>&quot; Despite its words, you sense that this spirit is not being honest with you. He doesn't seem particularly &quot;great&quot; under your scrutiny, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No need to make a social/perception roll of any kind to detect that it's not being fully honest. The lion spirit does a poor job of lying to you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The woods are dark this evening, but there's enough light shining down from the waxing crescent moon to let you see that there is a dark bird, some kind of raven or crow, staring at you. It fixes its beady eyes on you and quietly hops from tree branch to tree branch above your head as you move through the woods. When you watch it more closely, it looks away as if averting eye contact, then slowly turns its head back towards you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may roll Intelligence + Science or Animal Ken to discern more about this creature, if you like.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> The woman turns towards you, facing you when you speak to her. But something is not quite right about her gaze. Her eyes don't quite look into yours, giving the impression that she doesn't comprehend who you are or what you're saying. &quot;Henry? Where are you?&quot; she asks. &quot;I'm so cold. Henry?&quot; She wanders aimlessly, moving in your direction. You notice that she has a name tag clipped on the front of her blouse, which reads &quot;Mrs. Parks.&quot;<br /> <br /> At one point she passes directly through you. You feel a chill pass down your spine, and then she continues walking around the room and towards the classroom door.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Let's say you go with the Aspiration &quot;Attempt communication with a ghost,&quot; which I'll say you resolve now and earn a Beat. Pick a new one as a replacement. Also, can you indicate on your character sheet which you intend for your long-term aspiration? I'm assuming it's the one about your wife? Just want to make sure I know for purposes of storytelling and giving Beats.<br /> <br /> You may also roll Wits + Composure for a perception check.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I agree it's kind of in a gray area here for the act of hubris, but you're using magic to let you actively prevent someone from interfering with an action they would otherwise want to prevent out of self-interest (i.e., stealing their stuff they would rather sell). The innocent bystander would be if the Gulmoth you summoned killed someone who was in the wrong place at the wrong time.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the sympathy/sacrament yantra, I misread that when reading over your post. We can say you still have a photo of her, it's easy enough to snap another any time.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You excel at your dance routine. You hear a shattering of glass followed by muttered curses as a boyish looking bartender ogles you in awe and accidentally drops a martini glass while you're performing. A woman next to him laughs and pokes him in the ribs, teasing him for getting distracted, and he blushes.<br /> <br /> You know long before you finish your routine that you nailed at your performance. To her credit, Erica manages to not go slack-jawed in awe like the bartender; that wouldn't be professional. But she does whistle in pleasant surprise and offer a genuinely warm smile. &quot;You're hired,&quot; she says simply. &quot;How soon can you start?&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll allow the Steadfast condition from the exceptional success on that roll, but I do want to point out that in scenes like this when you're taking an idea and running with it, especially when I'm not asking for or implying a need for a roll, rolling isn't necessary. By extension, getting extra beneficial conditions by opting to make a roll you're very good at seems inconsistent with the spirit of these mechanics, which is to provide a way to quantify your success in the midst of struggle during a dramatic scene. So, unless I'm missing a rule suggesting that a roll is needed, or if you could clarify why you think a roll is needed in a certain situation, these kinds of rolls seems unneeded to me.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You focus your mind's eye on Alux, close your eyes while you prepare your Imago, and snap them open as you stare into your mirror. You see an image of the sun and the moon flying across the sky repeatedly, then snap into place. He will return on the evening of Saturday, September 17. Its location eludes you.<br /> <br /> You make multiple efforts to summon forth your memories of the events that occurred within the Highstorm. You comb through your mind, and try to read the past, but continually find yourself at an unexpected and maddening impasse. Even for memories that you vaguely retain -- like the knowledge that you somehow summoned Alux from the Abyss through your hubris -- seem imperturbable when you attempt to investigate them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unless I'm missing something, because your spell is Potency 3 and it is Withstood by 2, you only have 1 remaining question. &quot;When&quot; and &quot;where&quot; are two questions, so I answered the first question.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Next, you focus on the spells necessary to review the fight with Alux. The stream of Time around you pauses, and then you feel a dizzying sensation as everything spins around you...and then you're back in that street, facing down the horrible monster you inadvertently summoned. But this time, you don't need to focus on fighting it or even surviving; you just need to study it. You intensely scrutinize it with your Sight, pouring out mana from your soul and your Cloak to study the way your Arcana flow around this Gulmoth.<br /> <br /> But you push too hard, study too intensely, and it gives you a terrific headache that dazzles your Sight. When you try to glean something useful about the Gulmoth, the arcane &quot;glare&quot; is too strong, obscuring your view. At the same time, you immediately have the sensation of being watched, and the hairs on the back of your neck rise.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Opacity was 4, became 6 upon your dramatic failure. You take a regular Beat because it's not a spellcasting roll. Your Revelation roll is reduced to a chance die, so you get no successes.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You settle into a peaceful slumber, and quickly find yourself in a dream of your choosing. However, you have a strange feeling still of being watched. You scan your eyes along the crowd at the beach, and see nothing unusual there. Old friends, Boomer, Valentine --<br /> <br /> And then Alux is there. The Gulmoth roars in fury and leaps towards you, shadows threatening to engulf you. The crowd laughs as Alux swallows you, teeth ripping you apart --<br /> <br /> And then, suddenly, everything flashes back to normal. No Gulmoth in view. Everything is how you want it to appear. But you occasionally see unbidden shadows on your periphery, and still have an unsettling feeling of being watched. <br /> <br /> Still, you move on. You have a mission here. You seek out your connection to Mathias. The older mage is not hard to conjure up here; having lost the Duel Arcane to you, you sense a Strong sympathetic connection to him. You throw all of your will and mental force into your Imago now, driving yourself past his supernatural defenses. And, to your glee, it works.<br /> <br /> You silently slip into Mathias' dreams. Like you, he appears to be dreaming lucidly. When you first arrive, you're shocked to find that the mage is in the thick of battle against a supernatural being -- a Gulmoth that rises up from the ground like a large wall or tower of unholy fire. Matthias appears to be fighting with all of his strength, weaving Imagos that appear like he did in his Duel, causing him to sidestep the creature's attacks and create a Doom hanging over its form. You hear two screams, belonging to a woman and a young child, and suddenly Mathias collapses to his knees. When he does, the Gulmoth vanishes, and the entire scene before you is replaced with nothing but an endless sea of white light.<br /> <br /> Mathias draws a ragged breath and then stands. You notice a tear on his cheek, which he wipes away. And then he watches silently as an image of Chicago appears, starting as a dot and then rapidly expanding with vivid colors to fill your vision. The sky is pitch black, even though you somehow know it should be midday, and the scene now appears apocalyptic. Pillars of swirling fire rip across the streets, causing abandoned cars to explode along Lake Shore Drive and near the city streets. Lightning streaks across the sky, over and over again. Mathias just stands there and watches, shaking his head as if refusing to believe what he sees. The scene repeats again and again, and Mathias paces, rubbing his forehead and ignoring the tears streaming down his face.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You feel utterly exhausted and exhilarated at once as you complete your ritual. The day is brutal to you, physically, mentally, and spiritually draining. But everything is worth it when you finish that last step and the world warps around you in tune to your personal rhythm. <br /> <br /> This is the most potent spell you've created since your Awakening, but for being a simple Knowing spell, you find that you have to throw your entire will behind the Imago to obtain anything from your efforts. <i>Something</i> you can't perceive tries to push against your spell, stripping away its potency, but you persevere. <br /> <br /> You instantly learn the Correspondence to a single subject, but have difficulty understanding what it could mean: <i>The Destroyer</i>. Hakim never spoke of this term or name. And yet somehow, for reasons you cannot fathom, the link to this symbol or being is metaphysically <i>Connected</i>. It's stronger than any link you've seen or studied yet. You believe, based on your research about recent events, that this has to somehow be related to the Deathstorm and Hakim's death.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gain an Arcane Beat for making significant headway towards your Obsession. The name can be used when invoked as a Symbolic sympathy yantra, but does not count as the sympathetic name.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T02:15:35-07:00","id":992301,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight:</b>Periphereal, Active (Death/Matter) | <b>Active Spells: </b>Able to interact with Death Twilight<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>5/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>1 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 0</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY</b><br /> <br /> Marvin doesn't know what is more shocking, the freezing sensation of ectoplasm going trough his body or the pitiful remarks of &quot;Mrs Parks&quot; before that. It is really sad to see how lost and confused this poor soul is, despite the momentary rush of discovering his first ghost. He inmediately decides he is going to help her.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perception: Wits+Composure =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448992\" target=\"_blank\">5 Successes!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He leaves the college grounds and contacts other Libertines, perhaps the Lorehouse has anything about ghosts that might be of help. Anything will do at this point, given his total ignorance on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using my Status 1 to get access to a Library 1 (ghosts) is feasible? If it is: Ghost Research (Intelligence +Occult/Investigation+1)=<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448994\" target=\"_blank\">1 Success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He keeps building rapport with his new students, taking notes of the strengths and weaknesses of the class overall. He is quite pleased to see most of them are actually interested in the matter besides the graduation requirements.<br /> <br /> His mind is other place though.<br /> <br /> As soon as the classes end he goes to the library, looking through old archives of students and teachers looking for a Mrs. Parks or a Henry (Henry Parks, perhaps?)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Research Intelligence + Academics + 2 (I'm assuming a bonus for the college library) =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/448993\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-24-2016, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:11:09-07:00","id":992407,"title":"","content":"<b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Your keen eye picks up several other helpful pieces of information about Mrs. Parks. With your medical training, you notice facial drooping on half of her face, suggesting that at some point in her life -- perhaps the very end of it -- she suffered a stroke. You also notice an obvious mole on her left cheek, which provides a defining feature to help you identify her in pictures. Combined with her fashion and age, you can reasonably estimate the apparent age of this woman at about 50-55 years old, which will help you narrow down a search for her obituary.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can gain a beneficial condition of your choosing (e.g., Informed, Steadfast, Inspired), or suggest a custom condition relevant to this roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When you follow her out into the hallway, you notice sometime else startling: There are actually several ghosts, about 5 or 6, all walking up and down these hallways. They vary in approximate age, attire, and gender. You've never heard any rumors about this university or academic building being haunted, which makes you wonder what this means about the common occurrence of ghosts here. Perhaps there are many more ghosts than you thought? Regardless, none of the ghosts really seem to interact or converse with each other.<br /> <br /> You have met two mages so far since your Awakening, and they've both been eager to offer knowledge about Awakened society and encourage you to consider joining their Order. Mathias, a th\u00e9arch who found you shortly after you Awakened, doesn't answer your call when you try to reach him; you assume that he's busy. But you are able to contact Dante, a Libertine man who is glad to meet you at a caf\u00e9 not far from campus.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/66/ff/63/66ff631eaed1c4961259f553fec3854b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Dante draws more than a few stares and eye rolls from people around him. But despite his classic Goth attire, he's a surprisingly excitable man. He clasps your arm with both hands in a warm handshake as you meet. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Well met again, my friend, well met indeed!&quot;</span> He suggests ordering to go, so you can find a place with more privacy, and he orders a lavender and chamomile tea (<span style=\"color:red\">&quot;It's deliciously refreshing&quot;</span>).<br /> <br /> While you walk towards a more secluded area of campus, Dante quickly falls into a story, using vague enough language that there is no harm in Sleepers overhearing him, about his recent efforts to find Supernal truth in music. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;I have been exploring some <i>fascinating</i> genres, and mixing them to see whether anything resonates with the Undead when I transmit it to them,&quot;</span> he shares. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Many of our kind believe that most of these beings lack initiative of thought, but I wonder if they are simply missing the wrong stimulation. I have seen some very surprising results that my colleagues have not been able to explain...but perhaps more on that some other time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Once you find an empty park bench a little removed from busy streets or sidewalks, Dante asks, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;You seem as if something pressing is on your mind. How can I assist you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">FYI, the class is only held on Tuesday and Thursday afternoons, so I'll assume you're either doing this research on Thursday or coming back in on Friday to check out the facility.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You eagerly search through the library archives, both the electronic and printed databases. You initially struggle to find what you're looking for on the computer, because there are too many hits initially. &quot;Parks&quot; accidentally hits searches related to the school park, and parks in Chicago, and Henry was a common name for that time.<br /> <br /> After a bit of digging, you find mention of a Mr. Henry Parks, who taught statistics at this university. A widower, from what you can find, he passed away in the late 1990s after a long and successful academic career. His wife, Margaret Parks, worked as a secretary for the university. You find mention that she passed away suddenly due to a fatal medical condition, which you presume was a stroke based on her appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:26:05-07:00","id":992525,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Irritable, Informed (Rumors)<br /> Health: </b><b>LB</b>OOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/8 | Mana: 6/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b><br /> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">bookkeeping: updated my resource stats based on sleep and pattern scouring for the past couple days.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Despite everything, the first thing Moonstone thinks of after his Knowing spell is a quote from <i>Ghostbusters</i>: <b>CHOOSE THE FORM OF THE DESTRUCTOR!</b><br /> <br /> Or rather the Destroyer. Apparently someone chose the form of a Deathstorm. Whatever this baleful thing is, the prospect of it being so intimately connected to Hakim on a mystical level feels like lead in his stomach. He leaves the ritual space, paces around the sanctum, digs his fingers into his hair, narrowly averts a panic attack. After the serenity of the ritual, he feels himself spiraling into thoughts of Alux and Hakim and the Destroyer and what he's done to Mathias. It's a sense of not only being in <i>way </i>over his head, but drowning the other swimmers with his panicked flailing.<br /> <br /> He does what he's quietly done almost every day this week: turns his frustration inward. There's one thing he can do to take control, and that's purge his guilt and fear by scouring his own Pattern for pure Mana, the same way he purged the taint of Paradox. His muscles burn as he fires the internal athanor, much worse than they hurt already after the ritual. He knows intellectually that this really isn't healthy, but it's hard to resist the allure of Mana blooming within his Pattern. As long as he doesn't tell anyone, it should be okay.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Pattern Scouring for 3 Mana, -1 Strength until Saturday evening.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, no, hang on, that doesn't sound right.<br /> <br /> Who could he even talk to? Not Binder or Ragnar or Lynx or Phoenix, or any of the Shields of Dawn, certainly not, he's burned his bridges with them and they want nothing more to do with him. Maybe...Ace?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/gmB3sCS.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Of course, <b>Ace</b>! Another Sleepwalker in the service of the Adamantine Arrow. Formerly a professional athlete, now working as a physical trainer for Arrow mages and others in their net. Before he and Hakim split from the Knights, he used to assist her with training sessions, and he's occasionally come to her for honest talk when things were really bad with Hakim. He's pretty sure he still has her number...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using my Contacts (Sleepwalker Servants) to get some info. Manipulation+Expression: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449095\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Still sitting on the floor in ritualwear with his makeup runny, he folds his legs and puts on a sunny disposition and gives Ace a call. He briefly catches her up: (&quot;i'm awakened now! wild, right? also hakim died&quot;), and gushes about defeating a more experienced mage in the Duel Arcane and how amazing it felt and so on. But he's finding it difficult to get to the actual reason he called. He asks two big questions:<ul><li>&quot;What should I expect from the Consilium meeting tomorrow?&quot;</li> <li>And after much hemming and hawing: &quot;I'm feeling a huge amount of guilt and dread and grief I haven't processed properly. Possibly related, I'm having trouble distinguishing between the ritual sacrifice of Pattern Scouring and mundane self-harm. As you know, this is a problem for me. Are there Awakened mental health experts in the Consilium? Is that a thing that exists?&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-25-2016, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:15:56-07:00","id":992660,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Focused (Time; ended this turn)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> </div> <br /> The quandary of the Mystery before him makes Ragnar tilt his head in puzzlement. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>No Signature Nimbus? What is going on here?</i></span> He zeroes in on the Mystery, feeling an effect as if a pair of lenses have been placed over his eyes, and he feels as if Time stops around him as his focus zeroes down to the echo of magic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar spends a point of Willpower to enter Revelation. Gnosis 1 + Arcana 2 = 3 dice. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449187\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449189\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449190\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. Opacity has dropped to 2. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449193\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Opacity is back up to 3. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449196\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Opacity is now at 4. Ragnar's going to quit while he's behind disengage Focused Mage Sight.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ragnar grits his teeth. He knows he was starting to zero in on the truth of the Mystery, but he got lost somewhere in the puzzle and not only undid all his progress, but now the Mystery is even murkier than it originally was. He glares at the magic for a moment, but then takes a deep breath. This Mystery won't be going anywhere. And he doesn't think there are any other mages in the area who could possibly interfere with it the Mystery and increase its Opacity further. He has time. And hey, he's an Acanthus, he can make time if he needs to. He leaves, resolving to return once his understanding of Time or his Gnosis increases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:07:04-07:00","id":992687,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> The act of scouring your Pattern for mana causes not just physical pain, but emotional and mental pain; at the same time, it partially fills the well of mana within your soul, helping you feel satisfied. You're nervous about admitting how much you like this feeling, so you justify it as a necessary action to replenish your magical fuel. You need to find mana somehow, right?<br /> <br /> When you contact Ace, she seems surprised to get your call. She hasn't spoken to you in a while, and definitely not since the Deathstorm. When you blurt out that you have Awakened, her breath catches and her voice falters for just a moment, and you catch it. &quot;Wow,&quot; she replies awkwardly, &quot;I can't believe it! Wow.&quot; Whereas before you and Ace shared an odd bond, now you're a <i>mage</i>. You can tell that she tries to stay cool with you, but she sounds jealous. That much is clear when you share about your recent &quot;adventures&quot; and successes. She does seem genuinely impressed, but as an Arrow servant, she doesn't know Mathias that well, at least not personally.<br /> <br /> The more you talk, Ace starts to slip into her servant role, the position that's the most natural for her when talking to an Awakened mage. By the time you're ready to ask your questions, she is speaking more as an advisor and less as a friend.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's the first Consilium meeting that's been held since the emergency meeting in which Cielo assumed the role of Hierarch,&quot; Ace explains. &quot;My guess? Everyone's going to want to keep things feeling as normal as possible. The council seems like it wants to play things cool, make sure everyone is still doing well with the transition, and move on with more important matters. Cielo will speak, for sure, and then...who knows? Probably some of the Councilors. Might be a few more newly Awakened mages to talk about, so they might encourage them to form a cabal or something. But I definitely think everyone's been awkward around each other here lately, so I expect it to feel awkward.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's another awkward pause after your second question before Ace replies. &quot;I...can't say it's an area I'm really knowledgeable about,&quot; she admits, &quot;but I do know of some Mind Disciples who have worked with the Arrow to help them cope with the traumas they've seen. One or two seem particularly interested in understanding how to facilitate long-term mental health recovery. But I'm sure they'll require a favor of some kind, or artifact or service, as some kind of payment.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You initially try to be careful with your scrutiny of this odd spell, but the more you study it, the more you crave the information hiding behind this Mystery. You get eager, and it makes you sloppy. The magic seems to wind tighter, obscuring your view even to your Sight.<br /> <br /> You stand straighter as you challenge yourself to uncover the meaning behind this magic, and what it is doing on this door in this apartment. The craving to uncover this Mystery leaves you feeling hungry for more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:07:45-07:00","id":992832,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Irritable, Informed (Rumors)<br /> Health: </b><b>L</b>OOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b><br /> </div><br /> He nods along to Ace's counsel, and makes a note to talk privately with this Mind Adept that Rose of Sharon mentioned, as a potential source of help- or would it be better to find someone unrelated? Possibly he and the Nameless will be publicly highlighted during the Consilium meeting as new Awakenings, so that's something to warn them about. Mathias fulfilling his terms is probably going to be even more uncomfortable than he expected, which only wrenches his guilt over Alux harder, especially after he observed the thearch's dreams. But would &quot;showing mercy&quot; by asking him not to speak be helpful, or just a further insult? And doesn't Hakim deserve to be honored and recognized somehow?<br /> <br /> He's been Irritable all week, and the alienation and deference in Ace's voice grates on his aching nerves. He's wrapped in the Cloak, cheeks flushed, ears hot, voice gravelly and hoarse. <span style=\"color:teal\">&quot;I hear what you're doing, Ace. I'm not a different person. Do you think I wanted- no, of course I wanted to Awaken. We all do. But not like this! You know that if I could undo all this, if I could have him back for a <i>day</i> by going back to Sleep, in a heartbeat I'd...you know...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Dead air. He'd what? He can't actually bring himself to say it honestly. He knows he wouldn't.<br /> <br /> <i>You traded the life of the man you loved for power, and all the magic in the world won't let you take it back. [yes, loved, we can say it here, it's just us.] Choked to death by the Ironic Gauntlet. That's what happens when you make a deal with the devil. Utter Pandemonium, baby!</i><br /> <br /> Facing his own selfishness and hypocrisy only makes him more angry. Even without the mirror handy, he can't stop seeing his reflection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T02:24:25-07:00","id":992859,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight:</b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>5/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>1 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 0</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ouroboros Ophis listens carefully to everything Dante says, one could never known which detail could be of use later. In the end, he is pleased, it seems he is the right man for the job.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;I think our objectives align. I wanted to see you because I have discovered that there are a large number of ghosts roaming the campus. One in particular, a certain Mrs Parks, is in one of my classes. None of them have been an actual problem, mind you, they limit themselves to walk around in their own solipistic universes. I do not think any of them is even aware of the existence of the others. It was... a rather pitiful sight, to be honest. Is that everything there is after death?&quot;</span>-he pauses and thinks of Melissa, he feels a sudden weight on his chest-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Maybe you can help me comunicate with them, if that music treatment of yours can actually make them aware&quot;</span>-he takes a long sip of his cofeee-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;I will try to find out more information about Mrs Parks, hopefully that help us reach her and maybe solve his atachments. It is posible to help them move on, is it not?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>FRIDAY</b><br /> <br /> Ouroboros meets again with Dante the next day, now knowing more about Mrs. Parks (Margaret) and her late widower, Henry. He figures he can help the ghost lady if only Dante can manage to put him in contact with her, he deferes to the most experience mage to take care of that detail.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Good evening, Dante&quot;</span>-he greets the younger mage with a firm handshake-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;I found a couple of things that may be useful&quot;</span>-he shares his findings regarding the dead couple-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Are we ready to proceed?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-25-2016, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:26:49-07:00","id":992936,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 0/7 Mana: 0/10 Health: <b>LL</b>OOOOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken] [Abyssal Backlash]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 2 Arcane Beats: 0</div> <br /> First things first; Marlin will call the school and let them know he's on his way. (If he doesn't have a missed call from the school, he will pointedly request they call him first in the future).<br /> <br /> After giving them his best estimate for arrival, he'll start to consider what to tell Daisy. Years of honesty bubble to the surface. All he can imagine is &quot;You'll never believe what happened! There were other sorcerers, and a portal, and a teleporting mansion, and a wizard's duel!&quot; He sighs and shakes his head, but is unable to rid himself of the imaginary conversation.<br /> <br /> <i>I'll have to force it out.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting <i>Alter Mental Pattern</i> (Mind 2)<br /> 2 Reach available: spending for instant casting and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Potency 3, Duration scene<br /> Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 = 4 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447663\" target=\"_blank\">0</a> successes<br /> <br /> Trying again<br /> Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 - 1 (successive attempt) = 3 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447664\" target=\"_blank\">0</a> successes<br /> <br /> Ugh. I guess magic doesn't want Marlin to lie to his wife, lol. Trying again.<br /> Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 - 2 (successive attempt) = 2 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447665\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> <br /> <br /> +3 to Subterfuge rolls for the scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Once the spell is in place, he'll call up Daisy to apologize, assure her that everything is all right, and let her know he's on his way. Forgoing any complex story, his general excuse is that he started rearranging some shelves, left his phone in the other room, and &quot;I guess I haven't fully transitioned to the fall schedule yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Manipulation 2 + Subterfuge 1 + 3 (<i>~*magic*~</i>) = 6 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447668\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes!</a> <br /> That's probably enough to overcome any contesting roll she would make?<br /> +1 Beat for &quot;hide magical activities from family.&quot; Replacing that Aspiration with &quot;join an Order.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Conversation over, Daisy irritated but at least satisfied that nothing strange is going on, Marlin hangs up the phone. He cancels the spell. It's not the first time he's lied to his wife; it's not even the first time he's lied about magic. But it hasn't become routine. Yet.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Wednesday</b> (+1 WP!)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Taking a page from Caladriu, I'm going to be scouring for Mana since I'm out and don't have another source of it. -1 Str, +3 Mana</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When Marlin gets to the bookstore, he hangs up a sign that says &quot;Closed for Inventory&quot; and draws the curtains. Satisfied that it will take serious effort to peer inside, he opens a satchel full of ritual components: candles, chalk, incense, and a mirror. Under the flickering candlelight he creates a ritual space focused on the door to the upstairs section of the store.<br /> <br /> He visualizes the door becoming like the mirror, deflecting attention from itself. He visualizes the smoke and scent of the incense shrouding the door, shielding it from scrutiny.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting <i>Secret Door</i> (Space 2)<br /> 1 Reach available: spending for advanced duration<br /> Yantras: Mirror, incense (sacrament)<br /> <br /> Potency 1, Duration week<br /> Gnosis 1 + Space 2 + Yantras 2 = 5 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449342\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After three hours of casting, the spell takes hold. Marlin wipes sweat off his face, then for good measure, hangs an &quot;Employees Only&quot; sign on the door.<br /> <br /> The ritual components are relocated upstairs, where he begins to cobble together a proper sanctum.<br /> <br /> <br /> At some point that evening, Marlin feels the abyssal taint finish working its way into his pattern. He checks his nimbus under mage sight, examining the taint. Disgusted, he scours it out. (+1 Lethal, +2? Arcane Beats)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Thursday, Friday</b> (+2 WP, -1 Lethal, +6 Mana)<br /> <br /> Marlin will make arrangements to change the name of the bookstore as it appears on the door to &quot;Bound Books&quot;.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, he'll spend the days resting and attending to whatever customers wander in. Trying to be normal.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Saturday </b>will find Binder will the following status:<br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO [Shaken] Beats: 3 Arcane Beats: 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:32:26-07:00","id":992938,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Meeting with Tanaka (Wednesday-Thursday)</b><br /> <br /> Looks like I found a college student who's also a little desperate for a place to stay, that's good. We decided to meet at my place so he could have a good look at the place he was going to stay. He's into music, so I kick off the meeting with that, asking what music he likes, what instruments he plays, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix will try to improve his impression by starting the conversation with Ken's interests.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449348\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligence + Expression 2 = 4 dice \u2192 2 successes</a><br /> <br /> The reason for 5 dice is that I originally used Presence + Expression, but Intelligence makes much more sense, so 4 dice. Even so, that doesn't change the result. And yes, he would introduce himself as Garrick Royce. The dojo also knows him as Garrick.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That went well. Looks like this guy is really passionate about music, so that was a smart move. Alright then, now for the hard part: Talking business enough that we're on the same page, but not going so heavily into it that I alienate the guy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449344\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 - 1 Untrained Socialize = 2 dice \u2192 0 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well that was awkward. Talked way too much business and sucked the fun right out of the air.<br /> <br /> Shit.<br /> <br /> At least we could arrange another meeting same place tomorrow. Since most of the business talk was settled yesterday, This time, I decide to play to my strengths. I put on some music from one of his favorite genres and giving off a more friendly vibe.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix will present a much more friendly demeanor than talk strictly about business like yesterday.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449333\" target=\"_blank\">Presence 3 + Expression 2 = 5 dice \u2192 2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And we have liftoff from unpaid bills! And I still have time to pursue Anubis afterwards.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This does occur on the same day as when Phoenix tries to find a lead on Anubis. I don't think that's too much of a stretch considering most of the legwork in the arrangement was already done.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Finding a Lead (Thursday)</b><br /> <br /> I return to my former grave. The burn marks are still there, and so is the burst of magic my Awakening generated. But then, I sense some other sort of magic that reeks of Death. I discover the source to be from a fellow mage about to leave. Why does he look familiar? Doesn't matter, I need to see if he knows anything.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hey!&quot;</span> I shout for his attention as I approach, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I'm trying to find someone who's Awake, can you help?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For the other Hunter cell, they're good at networking and knowing who's who (and even what, sometimes), but aren't too hot at actually taking out the targets and have no supernatural abilities to discern supernaturals, Because of this, Phoenix didn't see much use for the collaboration because not only did he have an ability to sense magic, but he could also take out the targets, too. He also vocalized his feelings towards the group, which is why he would be coming back to them with his tail between his legs. He made an ass out of himself, and he would be paying for it.<br /> <br /> As for keeping them away, while it's true he doesn't want them finding out that he's a mage with mage friends, they don't have any reliable means of finding out unless he makes it obvious in some way. At least, that's what he believes anyway. Remember, the Aspiration is &quot;Fail to keep the other Hunters away&quot;, and they are an information-gathering cell. Phoenix still needs to learn to truly appreciate the importance and power of information.<br /> <br /> Although I do agree we should focus on this other mage before proceeding with that angle.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-26-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:43:56-07:00","id":993047,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 3</b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - ZOO</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Well, of course he'll think he's great, pride and all.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Thank you for the help,</span>&quot; Lynx bows his head to the lion, before he leaves the feline in peace. He mulls over the lion's words as he wanders throughout the zoo, his observations of the spiritual fauna having taken a back seat momentarily...<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - FOREST</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449463\" target=\"_blank\">Animal Ken roll to observe and discern raven or crow-like creature \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:33:35-07:00","id":993077,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Ace sounds a little taken aback at your change in tone. Her reply is somewhat more clipped, although she seems a little hurt, too. &quot;Right. Whatever. Talk to me on Saturday if you want to learn more. Bye.&quot;<br /> <br /> The call ends shortly after that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante looks excited for a moment. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;A ghost, <i>attending</i> your classes at the university? Oh, how delightful indeed!&quot;</span> When you clarify that she's merely wandering mindlessly, he seems disappointed but smiles at your na\u00efvet\u00e9. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Ah. I see. Well, actually it's quite a bit more <i>exciting</i> than that, depending on the circumstances. You see, when most people die, they leave this world, passing onto the Underworld -- a realm Beyond. Their souls can find peace, and continue to flourish in the afterlife.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometimes, though,&quot;</span> he explains, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;when someone has a strong reason for remaining -- perhaps unfinished business, a strong connection to a living being, or maybe vengeful feelings towards their killer -- they linger in this world as a ghost.&quot;</span> He sips from his tea, letting you process his information. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Now, most ghosts appear to be non-sentient reflections of themselves, like this dear Mrs. Parks. But some of them retain their sentience, and have more power and influence over the living world as a result.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Dante smiles at your eagerness. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Now, that is a <i>fantastic </i>question. We believe that the ghosts are Anchored to this world, creating attachments to meaningful people, places or things upon their death. These Anchors provide sustenance that they need to remain sentient in this world. If they lose their connections, they are pulled into the Underworld. Removing or suspending her Anchors will ease her passing. Alternatively, you can try to lead her to an Avernian Gate, a portal to the Underworld, if you find one here in this world. Why, with the right spell, you can even create a portal directly to the Underworld itself! But alas, that requires Mastery in Death, which both of us lack.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The mage smiles and asks curiously, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;You...do realize that ghosts are quite common, yes? Especially in largely populated areas such as this city. Why, look around you.&quot;</span> He casually waves his hand, and you feel a chill pass down your spine as you sense magic on your Periphery. If you look down the sidewalk in any direction, you see a handful of ghosts wandering aimlessly. They range in gender and apparent ages and clothing styles. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;As you learn to master Death, you will grow more accustomed to working with them. It is a <i>delightfully </i>interesting focus of mine. Do let me know if you wish to learn more. However, if you were to pursue initiation with the Free Council, I can assure you that you could find additional likeminded colleagues. I could point you in their direction at the Consilium meeting this Saturday, if you are interested.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You reconvene with Dante on Friday, this time on a bench in Millennium Park. Although it's a populated area, there is enough ambience noise that no one seems to be able to listen to your quiet conversation. You and Dante do still get a number of odd looks, though.<br /> <br /> The other Moros mage rests his hands in his laps with fingertips of either hand touching each other. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Excellent! Tell me what you have found, and how you would like to proceed.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> You reach the school and speak to a cranky secretary, who is sticking around late until you're able to stop by and pick up Forest. Mini-crisis averted.<br /> <br /> You deftly construct an Imago that allows you to sift through your thoughts and pull away any about the truth you would like to discuss. It's an odd sensation, but gives you the temporary mental clarity needed to lie to Daisy effectively. You know that telling her the truth could cause incredible damage to your family, and are able to rationalize the lie without pause. Part of you wonders if you know where that boundary is, though, and whether you'd be able to tell if you ever cross it.<br /> <br /> Daisy sounds annoyed but understanding. She sighs. &quot;Ok, Marlin. Well, try to remember next time. Poor Forest was probably worried. <i>I</i> was worried. I'll be home soon, just need to run some more errands. Love you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You actually have that Aspiration as a long-term one, don't you? You're allowed to change it if you want, but you need to have at least one long-term aspiration -- something that would take weeks to months to accomplish, or a complex or multi-step task that won't happen in one scene or chapter. Please adjust your Aspirations accordingly so you have something that fits that criteria<br /> <br /> My recommendation would be to keep the same long-term aspiration, but then you can take a Beat for making significant headway towards it -- you're using magic to keep your family ignorant of your new Awakening, despite missing out on an important role as Forest's dad. But if you want to pick a different long-term Aspiration, you can do that, too.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> It's strange, really. You're doing another ritual. But this time, it's your first ritual casting since you Awakened. In the past few days, your fledgling control over Supernal magic, <i>real</i> magic, has developed enough that you are able to construct a useful Imago that serves your purpose. The &quot;rituals&quot; you studied and attempted prior to Awakening seem like pitiful attempts at child's play in comparison. This, <i>this </i>is the real stuff. Sure, it's emotionally and physically tiring, but it is so worth it.<br /> <br /> You study your handiwork and nod to yourself. You make a mental note that it would probably be best to have a lie ready to tell customers who used to know about the door why there isn't one there anymore.<br /> <br /> You feel the Abyssal energy seeping into your soul. It's a really nasty, disgusting feeling. You somehow mentally pry at it and pull it out like a poisoned barb, but you feel a spike of pain in your gut and suddenly cough up a little bit of blood. Ouch.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yep, you can take 1 Arcane Beat for letting the Paradox condition lapse, as it's been one day since you received the Condition. Then, gain another Arcane Beat for the first time you resolve a spell-related Condition this scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> A few people seem confused on the name change, but no one probes you on why you did so -- it's your shop, after all. Someone comments on the door being gone, and you share your practiced lie that you did some construction recently on that room, which they accept without hesitation.<br /> <br /> At one point, a middle-aged Asian woman, maybe Chinese or Japanese, is browsing through an aisle in front of you when she looks up and frowns, looking at the wall where the door is hidden. You suddenly feel a pulse of energy on your Periphery, and her eyes briefly narrow, and then she makes eye contact with you and smiles knowingly.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://marketingtochina.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/marilyn-tokuda.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> She doesn't say anything or approach you, instead continuing to peruse your selection of occult books. She picks out a slim, leather-bound book and comes up to the register to check out. The woman pays in cash. When she hands you the money, she also slips in a simple business card and says, <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Call me.&quot;</span> She winks and leaves the shop. When you look at the card, it has a picture of a cherry blossom tree, the name &quot;Falling Blossom&quot;, and a phone number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Ken is quickly engaged in your conversation about music. He goes from being this shy, quiet kid to excitedly discussing different types of music he really enjoys. He seems like he hasn't had many opportunities to be genuine about himself like this, and you hit it off well.<br /> <br /> When you start talking logistics and business, though, he shuts down again. He's awkward, and says he might need to think about it some more. However, he's willing to meet up tomorrow if you still haven't found anyone by then.<br /> <br /> When you meet up the next day and try your other angle, you see the eager, friendly side of Ken again. Convinced that you're a cool dude, he agrees to signing on as your roommate.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ok, now you can resolve that Aspiration about figuring out your bills, and replace it with a new one of your choice.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You call out to the mage, and he freezes in place. He slowly pivots and turns to look at you over his shoulder. His beady eyes look bloodshot, and he's fidgeting nervously while he glances all around. A few other people walk past him, assumedly on their way to other meetings or social gatherings. Still with your Sight fixed upon him, you see him begin to form an Imago using the Death Arcanum, and the spell starts to form around himself.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll rule that you still have your Active Sight on, since I said you used it to notice him in the first place. You can attempt to Counterspell if you like; make a roll if so.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You're not an expert on all things animal, but you can tell enough from this bird's behavior that it is unnaturally intelligent. Even though you know ravens are surprisingly smart birds for their species, this type of behavior is too controlled and calculated. Combined with your supernatural senses indicating a supernatural effect on your Periphery a moment ago, there appears to be something very unusual about this creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:52:09-07:00","id":993261,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Irritable, Informed (Rumors)<br /> Health: </b><b>L</b>OOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 1/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b><br /> </div><br /> He has just enough time to play the victim and shout some things he'll regret into the phone before Ace drops the call. He just hasn't had a good opportunity to really <i>detonate </i>on someone since Tuesday.<br /> <br /> Venomous and self-righteous: <b><i><span style=\"color:teal\">&quot;You,</span></i></b><i><span style=\"color:teal\"> can't</span></i><span style=\"color:teal\"> understand how I feel. How could you possibly? You didn't have what we had! And you aren't even Awakened- and you <i>never will be.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Click. Well. That's gonna come back to bite him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Good time to resolve Irritable. No other actions until Saturday! </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:08:31-07:00","id":993358,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal, Active (Death/Matter) | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>Informed | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>1 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 0</div> <br /> <br /> <b>FRIDAY</b><br /> <br /> Last day revelations about the abundance of ghosts still had Marvin a bit shocked, he would have to adapt his worldview acordingly. Thank god for Dante. His unexpectedly cheerful attitude and experience made everything easier to palate. He paused for a moment and shared his findings with him.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Her name is Margaret Parks and she worked as a secretary for the university. She was married to Henry Parks, teacher of statistics. Apparently she left him a widower in the late 1990s due to a medical condition, a stroke, for what I could deduce&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He takes a long sip of his take away moka and stares into the distance.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;She was looking for his husband... I think she is afraid and lost&quot;</span>-he pauses-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Please, help me allow her to move on&quot;</span> <br /> <br /> He says nothing to Dante, but this situation is hitting too close for him. What if Melissa is in the same situation? A pitiful shade of a previously vibrant woman, desperately looking for him? The thought terrifies him.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;If you are ready, so am I&quot;</span>-he gets up-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Let's go&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He guides the Libertine Moros to the classroom where Mrs. Parks is roaming aimlessly.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;There she is&quot;</span>-he says after opening his Sight again-<span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;What do you need me to do?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:00:49-07:00","id":993479,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 3/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> Okay, that's kinda creepy. Is he just freaked out, or is it something else?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attempting to read the mage's behavior, see if he can glean emotional state and/or motive.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/449771\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Empathy 2 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a><br /> <br /> On a side note, the new Aspiration with &quot;Join a cabal&quot;, taking a leaf from Caladriu.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Once he starts casting the Death spell, I immediately close my Sight and throw up my hands, saying <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Whoa, not here to hurt you. Just wondering if you can help me with something.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:03:50-07:00","id":993655,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Friday night, Ragnar is eating dinner when he suddenly recalls something that Patty said to him the day he moved in. She had made an offhand comment about her family being a bunch of kooks, having a history of getting committed committed (long-term or short-term) for seeing things that weren't there. At first he had written it off as Patty being comfortable with discussing an unfortunate family history of mental health to make him feel less awkward about coming out to her. Now that he knows that there are people who can see magic, but not do it- Sleepwalkers- he can't help but wonder if Patty is from a family of Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> He looks up and sees Patty watching TV. He briefly wonders how to ask her this question. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Hey, uh, Patty? You ever had any weird, unexplainable experiences? Seen anything... out of the ordinary?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is going to trying to get some information out of Patty as to her family's experiences. Let me know what roll you think might be appropriate.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-28-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:22:48-07:00","id":994217,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 3/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Scoured: -1 Str] [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 3 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <b>Friday</b><br /> <br /> Marlin spends his afternoon overthinking Falling Blossom's--if that's her name--request. Should he call up Valentine and get an idea of who she is first? No, maybe he should make a contact apart from the Shields of Dawn. He could scry on her... but that's an invasion of privacy and he probably couldn't accomplish it anyway. What'll he do if Daisy finds out he's calling strange women? Should he get a separate phone for wizarding stuff?<br /> <br /> It's only the approach of 4:00 that spurs him into action.<br /> <br /> <i>After I pick up Forest, my next chance is the middle of the night when they're asleep... and somehow I doubt she'd appreciate that.</i><br /> <br /> Before he can start &quot;planning&quot; this phone call any more, Binder picks up the phone and dials the number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:28:20-07:00","id":994657,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Part of you feels glad for venting at Ace. She certainly deserved the vitriol...right? You also wonder if she'll hold a grudge for this, and hope that it won't cause issues with getting more information from her down the road.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante nods understandingly as you describe her story. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Yes, let us go see her. I would be glad to assist in any way that I can, and I certainly enjoy the opportunity to guide our newer mages on their path to enlightenment.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As you walk to the class, he asks, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Have you put more thought into which of the Pentacle Orders you find most in line with your goals? Personally, although obviously biased, I <i>do</i> think the Free Council would be an excellent home for you. Our mages believe that Supernal understanding can be found from modern studies. We encourage innovation, and use democratic principles to guide our Order. We want <i>everyone</i> to feel part of a greater whole, to have a voice and a vote, in service of advancing our understanding of Truth.&quot;</span> Dante's voice is filled with passion and enthusiasm as he speaks.<br /> <br /> Dante again offers to cast the spell that reveals ghosts in Twilight and grants you the ability to see and interact with them. It doesn't take long for the two of you to find Mrs. Parks, who is again walking slowly around the classroom and adjacent hallways. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;What you do next and how we can assist her depends on your preferred methods,&quot;</span> he instructs. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;There are more passive and gentle approaches, and some that are more...direct...in exorcising a ghost. As I said before, she receives sustenance -- Essence, we call it -- from places, people, or objects that held meaning to her in life and Anchor her in the afterlife. Removing those, whether by destroying them or lessening her connection to them, will eventually lead her to lose all sustenance and move Beyond.<br /> <br /> &quot;The other approach involves draining her of her Essence, and damaging her bodily form. It is a brute-force method, usually preferred when direct action must be taken quickly against a hostile ghost or entity.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dante casts Speak with the Dead (Death 1) on the two of you, using the +1 reach option to allow you tell if Anchors are permanent or temporary. If you concentrate on Mrs. Parks, you learn that she only has 1 Anchor, which is linked to this academic building, where she previously worked as a secretary and where her husband taught statistics. It is permanent, meaning that she wasn't summoned here by any ritual.<br /> <br /> How you proceed depends on Ophis' style and preferences. You can either attempt an Intelligence + Investigation extended action to resolve the Anchor by finding and removing her personal ties to this building (5 successes required, 1 roll per hour); use the &quot;Buried Anchor&quot; spell I created on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=993546#post993546\">Creative Thaumaturgy thread</a>; or suggest some other course of action.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Hmm?&quot;</span> Patty asks, still watching the TV. She breaks her attention away and turns the volume down as she actually processes your request. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Oh, umm...&quot;</span> Patty looks hesitant, but shrugs nonchalantly. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I mean, I think a lot of people have seen things like that in their lifetime. Some people call it strange, but I think there are definitely things out there that science can't explain.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> You have the sense that she has more to say on this subject.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can roll Manipulation + Persuasion to try and get some more information right now. If you want to get her to open up more about her experiences as a Sleepwalker in general, or have other goals here you'd like to describe, you can attempt Social Maneuvering. She currently has a Good impression with you, so you can make 1 roll/day. She has 3 Doors for this type of goal, because she's trying to be more private about that part of her life.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> The phone rings three times, and then a woman answers; her voice matches the woman you met at your store. After you introduce yourself, she replies, <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Ah, I'm glad you called. I've been coming to your bookstore for some time now, and when I saw your spell, I knew that you would be someone who might appreciate the information I can offer.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The woman formally identifies herself as Falling Blossom. She says that she is a mage and member of the Mysterium, and that she has been recruiting mages who have interests in the pursuit of knowledge. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;The Mysterium is devoted to all knowledge, in all forms,&quot;</span> she explains. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;We are the curators, the historians, the discoverers and safe keepers of Supernal magic. We devote our cause to finding, teaching, and preserving ancient wisdom.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Falling Blossom tells you earnestly that she genuinely believes, based on what she has seen in your store and your interests in research, that you would find yourself readily accepted and at home with the Mysterium. She asks if you would like to meet after the Consilium meeting tomorrow, so she can tell you more about the Order and its goals.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Let me know if you would go by Binder when you introduce yourself, or Marlin. However, she may still know your sympathetic name, as she has been here before your Awakening.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:58:27-07:00","id":994683,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - FOREST</b><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Hey there,</span>&quot; Lynx calls, waving his greetings to the bird. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">How are you?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> As Lynx smiles up at the creature, he opens his senses to the Wild to give it a thorough look...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Action: Lynx activates Life and Spirit Senses to observe the bird. </b><br /> <br /> <i>Should I do a Revelation roll?</i></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:49:29-07:00","id":994762,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: Exceptional Luck (cast and ending this turn)<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired (added this turn)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ragnar brings his plate from the table and sits down next to her. He smiles at Patty. And silently, he reaches out to Fate to try and rig the dice in his favor once again.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to cast his Exceptional Luck Praxis on himself. He has one free Reach, which he spends on Instantaneous Casting. He will be casting to grant himself a boon of a number of dice equal to Potency (+2) for an upcoming Socialize roll that Ragnar will attempt for some Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> 1 Gnosis + 2 Fate = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450658\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> His smile becomes a little friendlier as he feels the spell take affect on himself. He settles in and chuckles. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Oh, come on. Haven't you ever had weird stuff happen to you?&quot; </span>Fate dredges up a memory of himself casting magic, and he decides to use it as an in. Not tell her everything, of course. But some sliver of the truth. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Ok, I'll go first. I'm, like, freakishly lucky. Like the dice are rigged in my favor. Things just seem to go my way, you know? Like, the least-likely scenario always happens for me.&quot; </span>He looks expectantly at her, silently urging her to share.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt Social Maneuvering on Patty to get her to reveal more about her family history. He'll attempt a Socialize roll.<br /> <br /> Manipulation 3 + Socialize 1 + Boon 2 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450664\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes</a>! That'll be an exceptional success, and two doors down. I'll also take the Inspired Condition.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-28-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:43:01-07:00","id":994795,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> You open yourself to the increasingly familiar senses of your Sight, letting the mundane world fade around you as you study the woods and this creature through the lens of the Primal Wild. To your surprise, there is a Life spell infused in and around this raven, suffusing it with an overwhelming sense of <i>power</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You're welcome to attempt a Revelation roll. However, you'll need to spend 1 WP to activate Focused Sight, and you only have time for 1 roll before the following occurs. Opacity is 4. I'll leave it up to you to decide whether it's worth attempting.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The raven flaps its wings and glides down to the ground. As it does, its form...changes. Within moments, it enlarges, growing into the form of a lithe woman who stands shorter than you but somehow appears to be staring down her nose at you. She has high cheekbones, and her eyes are fixed intently on you, keeping the same intense stare as she had moments ago in bird form. She appears to be clothed in black feathers. Her hair is black as midnight and falls in wavy patterns down past her waist.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig04.deviantart.net/f623/f/2012/072/b/1/woman_crow_by_articka_88-d4sok72.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The woman's aura flares around her, which you clearly perceive as her Nimbus. You immediately smell an odor that evokes an image of a wolf marking its territory. You hear a phantom wind blowing through the trees, but the trees are deathly still. It causes a powerful emotional reaction in you, a mixed rush of euphoria and fear.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Who are you?&quot;</span> she demands. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Why have you come here?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She flares her Nimbus, but didn't accrue enough successes to affect you. So, you don't mechanically experience anything; it's just for RP flavor. This means Lynx will feel the effect, but won't affect him on any rolls he attempts on his turn, should he attempt some for any reason.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You feel the dice roll in your mind and come up in your favor. You <i>know</i> that this thought that randomly pops into your mind isn't just convenient; it's auspicious. When you tell your example to Patty, a look of recognition and thought passes over her face. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Wow,&quot;</span> she replies simply. Her body language seems to ease. She's still holding back, but she seems thoughtful, and smiles at you knowingly. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I feel like I've spent a lot of time around people in my life who have experienced that kind of thing,&quot;</span> she admits. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I don't always talk about it because, you know, people can think it's weird. Or that I'm weird. But I've always believed in odd things. Supernatural things.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">What new Aspiration do you want to take in place of the one for investigating supernatural occurrences in your apartment?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Formatting 10-28-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:37:49-07:00","id":994850,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar nods. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I don't think it's weird. Sometimes things just work out differently for some </span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">people. Not everybody has the same experiences. But if you could share those experiences with you, would you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm not trying to make any sort of roll. Just some roleplaying stuff. The Silver Ladder definitely appeals to him, and part of him really likes the idea of helping people to Awaken, or at least turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers, so that even if they can't do magic, they can see it and appreciate it for what it is. I'll take &quot;Find out if Patty is a Sleepwalker&quot; as a short-term Aspiration.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:27:06-07:00","id":994893,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> If Patty has any indication that she knows you're a mage, she doesn't give anything away or make any other connections. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I mean, I think everyone wants to be something special or be able to do really cool things. I believe in ghosts and the supernatural, that sort of thing. I suppose it would be neat to have cool abilities or something, yeah. I certainly wish I was lucky like you, I know that,&quot;</span> she giggles.<br /> <br /> Patty shifts the conversation towards how she wishes she had superpowers, tells some creepy ghost stories she has heard about (<span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;but I never saw something like that&quot;</span>), and asks you about what kind of Jedi you would be if The Force existed. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She has 1 Door remaining. Aspiration sounds good!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:07:50-07:00","id":994923,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>Speak with the Dead<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>Informed | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>1 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;NO!&quot;</span></b>-even Marvin is startled at his own outburst at the suggestion of harming the ghost-<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;No&quot;</span></b>-he adds, regaining his composure-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;We will do it gently and without bringing more pain to this already tortured soul&quot;</b></span>-he walks around the class, thinking.-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;We will find exactly what it is that ties her to this place, and then we will decide our next step. Are you ok with that?&quot;</b></span> <br /> <br /> Once they agree to the plan, they split up, looking for any clues that can point to the actual Anchor.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Looking for the Anchor (1st hour) Intelligence + Investigation=<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450707\" target=\"_blank\">3 Successes!</a>I am resolving Informed to turn it into an Exceptional Success, choosing the option to reduce the number of Successes by my Skill dots (2), resolving the action.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After a frantic search through the building, about an hour since they got there, Marvin calls the other mage-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Dante! I think I have found it!&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:55:55-07:00","id":995053,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> This guy is definitely acting hurriedly out of self-preservation. He appears fidgety and not thinking clearly, like he's a little rushed, even before he sees you.<br /> <br /> You put your hands up defensively, trying to play yourself off as non-threatening. But that doesn't seem to change his mind; before your eyes, his body and clothing become translucent, and then he ultimately just...vanishes. You don't sense anything around you or see any other sign of him. It's like he just turned into a ghost.<br /> <br /> While you may not have been able to speak with him, you fix his image into your mind's eye. You are pretty sure you could pick him out of a lineup if needed. You wonder if he might be at the Consilium meeting this weekend.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You are welcome to keep searching this area for other signs or info about what he was doing here. You can roll Int + Investigation (extended action, 5 successes, 1 hour/roll), try checking out stuff with magic or Sight, or suggest something else.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You reach out to one of your contacts in the old Hunter cell. You're actually surprised you still have the right number; it means they haven't changed their phone numbers recently, and that a part of you decided they weren't completely useless to you.<br /> <br /> You get in touch with TJ, the leader of their little group, and arrange to meet up at a safe house. Only he and Tanya are there when you arrive; the other three you know of aren't here. TJ and Tanya are African American siblings in their late 20s. TJ is a computer analyst and hacker, while Tanya is a librarian in Chicago.<br /> <br /> TJ seems irritable the whole time you meet, but when you essentially plead for help, he gloats and laughs at you. &quot;I told you that he'd need us,&quot; he says pointedly in a statement directed to his sister. Tanya rolls her eyes and crosses her arms, but she smirks too. &quot;Why should we help you?&quot; TJ asks skeptically.<br /> <br /> While you're talking, Tanya listens quietly and looks at you. At one point she frowns and asks, &quot;Did something happen to your hands?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They're willing to help you search, but you'll need Social Maneuvering. Starting with 3 Doors (he has a Pride Vice that makes him not want to help you after the things you said before), and Average impression (1 week/roll). You can attempt to do something now to improve the impression level before starting.<br /> <br /> As for Tanya, you can attempt an appropriate Attribute + Skill roll of your choice to keep her from seeing your tattoos or lie about what happened to them (e.g., Manipulation + Subterfuge).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante nods with a serious expression and puts his hands up defensively at your strong reaction. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Understood, my friend. Let us search and see what we can find,&quot;</span> he says gently.<br /> <br /> Knowing that Mrs. Parks has a connection to this building, you begin to search for anything that might have meaning for her or reference her. Although the building itself might have a link, you find a plaque near the front entrance to the building indicating that this building was renovated and largely rebuilt from the ground up approximately 15 years ago, long after her death.<br /> <br /> The plaque gives you an idea. Perhaps there is some sort of sign or image that holds meaning for her. And that's what you find after an hour of scouring the building: a plaque with name tags and photos of previous staff who received commendation for their years of service. This picture of Mrs. Parks is her from when she was younger, and her face doesn't have the asymmetrical droop that she does as a ghost.<br /> <br /> Dante nods eagerly when you find the plaque. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Why, this must be it,&quot;</span> he agrees. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;People see the image and her name, even occasionally, and it allows her to linger here. You will need to remove the source, permanently, to make a lasting effect. Moving it will just transfer the Anchor to a new location. Without this Anchor, she will start to rapidly lose her Essence over the next few hours, and eventually she will go to the realm Beyond. May I?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Assuming he has your permission, Dante places his hand on the plaque. You smell a waft of decay and brimstone that you recognize as your Periphery Sight, and the picture warps and erodes at Dante's touch; her name on the plaque simply melts off. When you study the ghost again, you see that the Anchor weakens and then ultimately vanishes from her.<br /> <br /> Dante offers to stay with you watching Mrs. Parks until the end. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;It is much like falling asleep,&quot;</span> he says softly. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Ghosts that pass on to the Underworld can grow in strength, evolve their personality, and learn new things. When you hear tales of hauntings or demonic possessions, it is usually the work of a powerful specter or spirit.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Hours pass. While you wait, Dante talks to you about magic, his research, and above all, the Free Council. He explains that the success of the Order rests on the collective efforts of the group, but that all mages have a chance to innovate, and so Libertines are often recruiting new members the way union representatives would in a large company.<br /> <br /> Eventually, you see it happen: Mrs. Parks stops walking. She smiles and sighs, &quot;Henry, <i>there</i> you are.&quot; With Dante's spell, you see a dark, mysterious doorway appear and open, and Mrs. Parks steps through. The door vanishes a moment later.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gain a Beat for the Aspiration of helping this ghost, and choose another!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:48:57-07:00","id":995192,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>(Short and One-sided) Conversation with the Mage</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hey, wait-!&quot;</span> I plead, but too late, he's gone now. Dammit. It seemed like he ran because he saw me as a threat. I haven't seem him before, so that means he's either incredibly paranoid, or he knows I'm a Hunter. Seemed like he was in a rush, too. Is he looking for something? Maybe that little pebble of his is what he came for.<br /> <br /> I dunno, this kinda investigation isn't my area of expertise. I need some kinda investigator, and the only ones I can think of at the moment are...those guys. Problem is, even if they'd be willing to help me, I've got nothing for 'em. Not even a photo of the gu-Wait a minute, I've got magic! I have a decent mental image of him, maybe I can,,.<br /> <br /> I whip out my phone, take a picture for a background, then imprint my fresh mental image of the mage onto the photo.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">CT Forces + Mind Ruling spell Imprint Image.<br /> <br /> The spell imprints an image of something or someone from the caster's mind onto a computer picture. In this case, he's imprinting the mage onto the photo he's just taken. PSF Duration<br /> <br /> <b><u>Imprint Image (Forces 2 + Mind 2, CT)</u></b><br /> <b>Reach:</b> 1 free; 2 used for instant casting and advanced duration<br /> <b>Paradox:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450866\" target=\"_blank\">Overreach 1 - 2 DT = Chance die \u2192 Dramatic Failure</a><br /> <b>Containment:</b> None<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Dedicated Tool for Paradox penalty<br /> <b>Factors:</b> PSF Duration to 1 Week (-2)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450867\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Forces 2 + 3 WP - 2 Factors = 4 dice \u2192 2 successes</a><br /> <br /> By the way, the dramatic failure on the Paradox roll restores a point of WP, which I then used for the spell, so his WP stays the same.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there we go, I've got an image of him on my phone now. That might be enough to get me a lead for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Meeting the Hunters</b><br /> <br /> &quot;I told you that he'd need us.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Alright, I deserve that,&quot;</span> I agree, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I was an asshole saying we'd never need you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He's metaphorically getting on his knees. Apologizing in such a manner as to display profuse piety in order to improve the impression level.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450880\" target=\"_blank\">Manipulation 1 + Expression 2 = 3 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Why should we help you?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Wuh?&quot;</span> I gape in surprise, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I dunno, because he's a dangerous mage? He needs to be stopped? He already killed the rest of my cell?&quot;</span> I wave about my hands to gesture my confusion. Bad move on my part, it seems.<br /> <br /> &quot;Did something happen to your hands?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I, uh...&quot;</span> I stammer a little in response. I can't say what really happened, but I'm no good at lying. But they can't detect magic, can they?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Improvising a Mind spell.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Memory Hole (Mind 2, Corebook p, 160)</u></b><br /> <b>Reach:</b> 1 free; 1 used for instant casting<br /> <b>Paradox:</b> None<br /> <b>Containment:</b> None<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> None<br /> <b>Factors:</b> PSF Duration 2 turns<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/450873\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Mind 2 = 3 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I...actually have no idea,&quot;</span> I gaze at my palms. Guess the spell went off without a hitch, I have no idea where these-tattoos? came from. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Y'know what? Doesn't matter,&quot;</span> I eventually respond, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;If you care at all about keeping people safe from a magical madman, you'll help me. Or do you not care about the Vigil?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is an attempt at exploiting TJ's Vice in order to up the impression another step. Should I roll for this?</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:47:03-07:00","id":995259,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> You quickly focus the image of the other mage in your mind, and creatively improvise a way to transfer the image to your phone. You create your Imago, and are very pleased to see the picture successfully appear in your phone image gallery. <br /> <br /> You can see from the picture that this guy definitely looks nervous. But why?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Your admission that you made a mistake catches TJ somewhat off guard, and he chuckles in spite of himself. &quot;You better not be getting soft on me, Royce,&quot; he replies.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look, we've got a lot of leads on a lot of different things now. We might be able to help, but there might be something bigger going on. We've been trying to do more surveillance in the past week. We've seen some odd patterns, but it seems like those crazy storms we had last week had some kind of impact on some of the people we had been investigating. We thought we were really on to some of these sorcerers, but after the storm, the trails have gone cold on some. Not sure if they went into hiding, died, or what.&quot;<br /> <br /> You temporarily suppress your memories of the tattoos, and when your spell takes effect, your incredulous voice is genuine when you say that you have no idea where they came from. Tanya looks like she believes you, but still gives you an odd look. &quot;What have you been up to? We haven't heard from you in weeks. Not since the really bad storm last week at least.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your first roll improves your impression to Good, so you can make more attempts on a daily basis. You can't make multiple attempts to boost the impression right now, but you can make a Presence + Persuasion or Manipulation + Persuasion roll as your Social Maneuvering roll to try and open the first Door. Otherwise you can make any other roll you would like to try the first roll for Social Maneuvering.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-29-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:13:53-07:00","id":995269,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar nods at at Patty, getting into the conversation. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well, I guess I already have probability manipulation as a superpower!&quot; </span>It's true... from a certain point of view. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Hm... well, I guess teleportation would be cool.&quot; </span>Also true. He hasn't tried to work his well with Space yet, but he senses that he has some innate understanding of the Arcana that, in the Phenomenal world, is so closely linked to the Arcana of Time. Perhaps he can mend fences with Moonstone by asking him to helping him practice some Space spells. <br /> <br /> When the conversation turns to what kind of Jedi he would be, he gives it serious thought. &quot;Hm. I think I'd want to be a Jedi recruiter. You know, going around and looking for people who can use the Force. Or maybe being a teacher.&quot;<span style=\"color:#0000cd\"> Of course, it's all metaphor and code. What role does he want to play in the Consilium? Recruiter? Teacher? Maybe even a member of the leadership? He'll need to make contact with the th\u00e9archs tomorrow and see what they are like. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:11:53-07:00","id":995295,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> Lynx gazes at the scene that unfolds with awe. As the bird transforms, his Senses tremble: he breathes in the woman's aura, the thrill of fear, the marvellous euphoria... the <i>Wild</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Are you a Thyrsus?</span>&quot; Lynx blurts out excitedly before he digests her words. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm Lynx! Well, I call myself Lynx. I'm new. Uh. New here, I mean. And new to the whole... magic thing. How did you do that raven transformation? Is that a Life-y thing?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">...maybe I should try that breathing thing.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm looking for a spirit lynx,</span>&quot; Lynx continues quickly. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">A Great Lynx. Do you know anything about Great spirits? Are Great spirits a thing?</span>&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:07:12-07:00","id":995309,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> The woman blinks at you, taken off guard by your na\u00efvet\u00e9. She suddenly emits a peal of bubbling laughter. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Oh, my, but I like your courage. You really must be newly Awakened. Few would dare to come here so boldly. These woods are my domain.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The woman extends a hand in greeting. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I am Raven. I am indeed a Thyrsus, born of the Primal Wild, sworn to the Mysterium. I can do a great many things that you could only imagine.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven traces a fingertip along your cheek and chest. You smell her scent again on your Periphery and suddenly feel a torrent of euphoria pass through your body. You are paralyzed with pleasure stronger than anything you have ever felt, and it makes you gasp involuntarily as your breath catches in your throat.<br /> <br /> The mage removes her hand, and the feeling instantly fades. You can still feel your body pulsing with aftershocks of her spell, though. She smiles broadly, eyes taking you in from head to feet. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;You have a very handsome physique,&quot;</span> she compliments you.<br /> <br /> She purses her lips in thought at your question. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Some spirits are certainly greater than others. Generally speaking, spirits are reflections of something in this world: a tree, a mountain, a desert or valley. Some reflect a greater or more powerful concept, and as such, are greater themselves.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven smiles. Her eyes still have that intensity that they held earlier. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Perhaps you would like to learn more? I have other affairs to attend to now, but perhaps some night this weekend?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:38:57-07:00","id":995606,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats:</b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - FOREST</b><br /> <br /> Still gleeful, Lynx maintains his concentration and listens attentively - at least, until her touch and rush of euphoria, which has him gasping and then sighing in silent relief. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">You have a very handsome physique.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ah...thanks. I've heard that a lot recently</span>.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Perhaps you would like to learn more? I have other affairs to attend to now, but perhaps some night this weekend?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx perks up. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Learn more? Yes! Yes, of course I want to! I'ven't met any other Thyrsus...es? Thyrsi? Everybody else have been Acanthus... what are the plurals? Acanthus and Mastigos and Obrimos. I think there was a Moros, but she disappeared...</span>&quot; He sighs, more to himself, before he gazes at Raven, into her eyes. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">You feel...right.</span>&quot; He sniffs the air. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">You smell right too, like the <i>Wild</i>. I would love to learn more from you this weekend.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He grins and glances up at the sky for a moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh! If you're part of the Mysterium, does that mean you'll be at the Consilium meeting on Saturday?</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:18:50-07:00","id":995617,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> Raven smiles at your suggestion. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Perhaps,&quot;</span> she replies. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I try not to dabble in Consilium politics more than I need to, but when the Mysterium requires my input and the Hierarch calls us to a special meeting about the Deathstorm, I am inclined to attend.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her eyes linger on you, and she turns and begins to walk into the woods. She looks over her shoulder and adds, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I do not offer free knowledge to anyone. Perhaps I will mentor you, but I will require favors or knowledge in return. If you seek more knowledge, you really should consider the Mysterium. No other Order boasts the same depth and breadth of Supernal information, truly.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> With that, she transforms again into a raven, flying away into the darkness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't have anything else specific for you in this scene. I wanted to introduce someone for you to explore more in future scenes, but I think we should keep your Aspiration to get to know a Thyrsus (especially because you already got a Beat for that this scene).<br /> <br /> Let me know if you wanted to do anything else.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:42:07-07:00","id":995630,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> <br /> Binder will introduce himself as such, making an effort to get into his sorcerous persona on the phone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Ah, I'm glad you called. I've been coming to your bookstore for some time now, and when I saw your spell, I knew that you would be someone who might appreciate the information I can offer.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;It seems that I've had more Awakened business than I thought possible! To tell the truth, you're not the first mage I've spoken to, but I always appreciate further information.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Falling Blossom tells you earnestly that she genuinely believes, based on what she has seen in your store and your interests in research, that you would find yourself readily accepted and at home with the Mysterium. She asks if you would like to meet after the Consilium meeting tomorrow, so she can tell you more about the Order and its goals. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I'm flattered that you think so! What I've heard of the Mysterium definitely appeals to me. I'd love to be able to talk further about it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> After ending the call, Marlin does his best to not think about how he's just set up a clandestine meeting with another woman behind his wife's back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:35:50-07:00","id":995719,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>Speak with the Dead<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>3 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> Marvin watches Mrs. Parks finally moving on with a gentle smile on his face. When he faces Dante again he is quick to clean a single tear dropping down his cheek.-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Thanks. Thanks a lot. I want you to know that I consider myself in your debt. If you ever need my assitance or help with anything, you only have to ask&quot;</b></span>-he shakes his hand-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I will think about your proposal, that Free Council you have talked about seems interesting at the very least. I supose we could talk more about it this Saturday in that reunion (Council meeting?) you mentioned yesterday&quot;</b></span>.<br /> <br /> They both leave the college precints and go for a cup of coffee, or one of those exotic infusions in Dante's case.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;My treat&quot;</b></span>-he says, paying for both beberages-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;You have made obvious to me how much I need to learn... about everything. I have mixed feelings about it, to be honest. I am a doctor, so realizing that I do not really understand how the world works after devoting all my life to its study... it is kind of frustrating&quot;</b></span>.-he warms his hands with his cup of cofee and takes a short sip-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;On the other hand, a brand new world to learn about... it is exilarating&quot;</b></span>-He smiles and for a moment seems twenty years younger-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Again, you have my most sincere thanks. For everything&quot;</b></span>.<br /> <br /> The two mages, the experienced young one and the old novice kept talking for a while before their drinks. Important matters would be disccused tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-30-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:09:57-07:00","id":996044,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Excellent,&quot;</span> Falling Blossom replies happily. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I will look for you at the meeting. I'm sure it will be a fruitful conversation. Have a good day, Binder.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The rest of your day goes well. You arrive at Forest's school early and pick up him up as soon as school is out -- you've been very careful to watch the clock this week since the incident on Tuesday. He's pretty energetic today, and quickly tells you about all of the fun things he did in school and what he's learning about. For a while, the stress of juggling two lives becomes easy; all thoughts of Awakened society are pushed aside as you enjoy your time with your son. Daisy greets you when she gets home, and you enjoy a relaxing Friday evening with your family.<br /> <br /> Thoughts of the Consilium meeting do pop into your head later that evening, though. During the night, you have vivid dreams of the Gulmoths you faced, only this time you're alone. You try to stab them again and again with your knife, only to realize that your knife is made of plastic instead of steel. A masked man stands with his arms crossed, watching you from the shadows, saying nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante smiles and nods. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;It was my pleasure to help you. I will be transparent, of course, that I do not always have the means and the time to help freely. It is common for mages to exchange favors and services. If I have need of your aid in the future, I will let you know.&quot;</span> He shakes your hand and adds, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Yes, I will be at the Consilium meeting. I will look for you afterwards. Have a good evening, Ouroboros Ophis.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:18:27-07:00","id":996058,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (5/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 2 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY - FOREST (2/5 Willpower)</b><br /> <br /> Lynx listens to Raven's parting words as she transforms. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Nice meeting you! Hope I'll see you on Saturday!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">A mentor, huh... I want to know more about the Mysterium too. I like the idea of more Supernal knowledge. I'll ask on Saturday.</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx lingers for a little longer as he revels in the smell and sound and feel of the forest.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>WEDNESDAY EVENING - APARTMENT (2/5 Willpower)</b><br /> <br /> When he returns to the apartment, he kicks off his shoes and calls out, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Ewan?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> There is no reply. He glances around the apartment - all tidied up but for some pillows rather astray on the floor - and hums to himself. He slips out of his shirt on the way to the bathroom, and shortly after finds himself pensive in the warm shower stream...<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>THURSDAY - AFTER SCHOOL </b><b>(3/5 Willpower)</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar doesn't seem to pay much attention to Lynx that day, seemingly absorbed in his own magic. Lynx is still in mental euphoria after Wednesday's meeting with Raven, and as such they likely part ways at Uni without even saying a word to one another. Lynx studies a bit in the library, but frustrated with his curiosity unsated, he goes home early. At home, he surfs the internet like the &quot;good&quot; old days, keeping to himself for the rest of the day.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>FRIDAY (4/5 Willpower)</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">To keep up the pace of the plot, Lynx will spend Friday in normality. He'll finish schoolwork for next week. He will practise some Life and Spirit magic in his room, careful to keep his door closed and himself out of sight - Nothing that risks paradox or requires mana. In the evening, he will hang out with Ewan and join him at the gym to get a workout.</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-31-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:33:54-07:00","id":996061,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> &quot;You better not be getting soft on me, Royce,&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Nah, just knowing my place,&quot;</span> I reply, perking up a bit now that I'm done with the act. A successful act, it seems.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look, we've got a lot of leads on a lot of different things now. We might be able to help, but there might be something bigger going on. We've been trying to do more surveillance in the past week. We've seen some odd patterns, but it seems like those crazy storms we had last week had some kind of impact on some of the people we had been investigating. We thought we were really on to some of these sorcerers, but after the storm, the trails have gone cold on some. Not sure if they went into hiding, died, or what.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hmm...&quot;</span> I pipe down in acknowledgement of their situation, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Speaking of those storms, I don't know exactly what's causing them, but I do know they're magical in nature, which is why those sorcerers are drawn to them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Might be able to get some answers if we find Anubis, or maybe...&quot;</span> I pause to take my phone and show the photo of the mage I met yesterday, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;...this guy. Dunno who he is, but I do know he's a sorcerer and I found him on the scene where Anubis killed my cell. When I approached the guy, he disappeared.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;That, and he looks pretty damn nervous on here,&quot;</span> I point to his face in the photo, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I'd say he knows something.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Opening the first Door with Presence and Persuasion<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/451746\" target=\"_blank\">Presence 3 - 1 Untrained Persuasion + 3 WP = 5 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> By the way, could the little spat that Phoenix had in the last post be counted as fulfilling his Rigid Vice? He genuinely thought that they would help with the lead because they're Hunters and that's what they do. The concept of them having other priorities didn't enter his mind until he bumped right into it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;What have you been up to? We haven't heard from you in weeks. Not since the really bad storm last week at least.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Busy hunting, haven't been doing much else,&quot;</span> I answer as I get up to leave, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Well, see you guys tomorrow?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:05:28-07:00","id":996127,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> Most of the week passes quietly, which is fine with you. With few distractions, you're able to get far ahead in school work, which will allow you more time this weekend and early next week for your new &quot;extracurricular&quot; studies. Ewan is in and out of the apartment over the next few days. You know his general routine pretty well just by living with him, because of how consistent his schedule is: cardio or a long-distance run early in the morning, big breakfast with lots of protein, classes during the day, an afternoon weightlifting workout on 5 days out of the week, and homework or relax in the evening. He's pretty passionate about his exercise regimen and talks about it frequently, but he always tries to invite you along in case you're ever interested.<br /> <br /> In the privacy of your room, on Friday you practice simple Unveiling and Knowing spells the most. You gain increased comfort with investigating and exploring the arcane world around you. At one point while you're particularly focused in your studying, you feel a presence on your Periphery; your Spirit magic allows you to see a small, curious spirit in Twilight roaming your room. The creature is cautious towards you, but seems to be breathing in or feeding on the energy in your room. Speaking with it and studying it reveals that it is a tranquility spirit, and it is feeding on the calm Resonance your living environment has created. It leaves shortly after your conversation.<br /> <br /> Life magic seems to come even more naturally to you, and with less effort you can make even more noteworthy effects. You cast a Life spell on your muscles before going to your afternoon weightlifting session with Ewan, and easily have one of your best sessions: you're able to lift much more than you ever have, which even surprises Ewan. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;Holy shit, dude,&quot;</span> he comments, <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;you're a beast today!&quot;</span> Your muscles even <i>look</i> bigger. Another simple Life spell eases the tension in your muscles after your workout, causing the muscles to mend naturally without the usual post-workout fatigue.<br /> <br /> You awake on Saturday feeling energized, rested, and <i>alive</i> in a way you never possibly could have before you Awakened. It's intoxicating.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Taking some creative liberty here, but even with only casting a handful of Spirit and Life spells, Lynx would be able to see some pretty dramatic effects without Paradox using his Arcana. If he wouldn't have experimented with spells in the way I'm suggesting, tell me and I'll edit it out of my post. Just wanted to raise some ideas for things Lynx might be thinking about as he explores his new abilities.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> &quot;Man, you definitely have been busy,&quot; TJ comments. He seems very focused on your ideas about the storms, and he and Tanya continue to kick around ideas about how the storms might be related to these &quot;liches&quot; and &quot;sorcerers&quot; in Chicago. You make a pretty convincing case for why they should dedicate their efforts to finding <i>this</i> guy in particular. TJ looks at the photo, but shrugs. &quot;We'll see. It's all part of a bigger picture, you know? I'm not saying you're wrong. I'm just saying, I think we need to take a step back and figure out how it's all related. I wonder if these guys are somehow creating the storms, or using them to do something to the city?&quot;<br /> <br /> Tanya says, &quot;We can meet up again. You know how to reach us. We'll let you know if we find anything.&quot; Her tone doesn't sound promising, but at least it's cordial. She keeps looking at your hands.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You retain your Good impression with them, but fail to open the first Door. 3 Doors remaining, you can attempt on a daily basis currently.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of your Vice, and wasn't sure how to fit it in this scene. So yeah, go ahead and take a WP for that. In general, try to think of things Phoenix would do in consistent patterns or routines that he leans back on to avoid stressful situations, or when he doesn't know how to move forward on a problem. Especially if that behavior would put stress on another relationship or cause problems for him.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take a Beat for the end of the Chapter! I'll get to work on the next scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:50:32-07:00","id":996540,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Chapter 2: &quot;All in Order&quot;</b></span><br /> <i>Saturday, September 10, 2016. Mid-morning. One week after the Deathstorm.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You wake after a night with troubled dreams. You're dwelling on all of the things you've learned and faced in the past few days: Ace's distancing from you, Mathias' prophetic dreams of an apocalyptic storm wreaking havoc on Chicago, vague visions of The Destroyer. But today is another day. Today will be your first time attending a Consilium meeting as an <i>equal</i> of the mages you once served.<br /> <br /> Your phone has a text on it this morning saying that you'll need to leave the Arrow safe house today. You make sure to pack up everything you brought here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Sleeping in on the weekend with a young child is never easy, but you're used to the routine by now. You make breakfast for Daisy and Forest and enjoy time together with them. Although she usually assumes childcare and grocery shopping duties on Saturday while you tend to the bookstore, you explain to her that you have the store closed today because of a &quot;networking conference&quot; you need to attend. &quot;That sounds interesting,&quot; she comments. &quot;I hope it ends up being helpful and useful. I'm sure the extra business couldn't hurt, either.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You wake up early feeling fully rested. Ewan is already up getting ready for his morning run, and he invites you along if you're interested. He says that he already has a paper he needs to work on for his class, so he's going to take off for the morning afterwards so he can get that started. <span style=\"color:darkgoldenrod\">&quot;Don't want to let it get in the way of my workout later. Bros don't let bros skip leg day,&quot;</span> he jokes. You're not sure if he's using the word &quot;bro&quot; ironically or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> No messages or calls from TJ or Tanya this morning when you wake up. You're eager to see if they can help you track down the guy you saw, but you have a feeling he hasn't even started looking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You wake up to an email this morning from Dr. Jacob Langley, the UChi English professor who has befriended you, asking you if you're available sometime today or tomorrow to help out with some research. He's hoping to get your help writing down some notes while he examines some antique objects he has stumbled across recently. He asks that you call or email him later when you have time, noting that he is willing to work around your schedule if needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> You receive a text from Mathias, the th\u00e9arch whom you met recently and who urged you to attend this week's Consilium meeting to help introduce you to mage society. He asks you to arrive at the meeting around 11 am, where he would like to introduce you to a group of other newly Awakened mages. He thinks that you would be a good influence for them and would help balance out their personalities, so collectively you would have a well-rounded cabal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As a reminder, Valentine instructed you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=990236#post990236\">here</a> on where and when to arrive for the Consilium meeting, suggesting that you meet early so you can meet some other mages. He emphasized that you should not cast any spells on the church premises; you're of course welcome to ignore his advice if you choose. Please indicate in your posts whether you would cast any spells or rituals the morning before the meeting, or if there is anything else you would do before you go.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:35:38-07:00","id":996759,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 2/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> Moonstone wakes up and immediately knows it's going to be a bad day.<br /> <br /> He makes some tea and oatmeal in the sanctum kitchen and gets to work packing his things in a duffel bag. There's a cloud hanging over his head.<br /> <br /> When all the dancing shoes and ritual sacraments are put away, he stares at the stuffed bag on his neatly-made bed. Really not ready to go back home yet. He gestures like a magician and commands the bag: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;TELEPORT!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;AWAY WITH YOU!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;SHAZAM!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> No luck. It's like trying to flex a muscle you don't have. He's going to have to carry the bag himself, like a <i>Sleeper. </i>Ugh. He leaves a nice thank-you note on the kitchen table, but there's no smiley face. That's how upset he is.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Home still doesn't feel like home. He gets back to the apartment he shared with Hakim, sets down his bag, sits down for a second that becomes an hour curled up on the couch and crying. He thinks about skipping the Consilium meeting entirely, but eventually talks himself into at least taking a shower. That gets his forward momentum back. He puts on some more masculine formalwear, vest and tie and all, wraps the mirror in the cloak and tucks them both into his messenger bag. The stormcloud is still there.<br /> <br /> He takes the train (no storms or chance meetings this time) to the familiar Chicago station near St. John Cantius and arrives a little after 10. Listening to traffic and smelling greasy food takes his focus away from his thoughts. When he sees the familiar face of the guard outside the church, he nods and formally recites the passphrase: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I am here to open my eyes to the truth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Inside, he keeps an eye out for anyone he knows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:08:19-07:00","id":996792,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>4 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <b>06:00 AM.</b><br /> <br /> Marvin wokes up to the sound of his clock alarm. He gets up from the couch (their bed felt too big and empty without Melissa) and makes some stretches to ready himself. After his muscles are as awake as his mind, he changes into his sportswear and goes out for some light jogging.<br /> <br /> <b>07:00 AM.</b><br /> <br /> Back home he goes straight to the shower. Hot water followed by cold to help the circulation flow. He takes his time in front of the mirror, shaving his head and grooming his beard and moustache with the utmost care. Oils and creams to keep it lush and soft, covered a good portion of his side of the bathroom stall. He tried no to look to hers. He cries.<br /> <br /> <b>07:30 AM.</b><br /> <br /> He treats himself with a great breakfast: coffee, toasts, scrambled eggs and bacon. He smiles drinking his coffee and reading the news. His eyes still a little red.<br /> <br /> <b>07:45 AM.</b><br /> <br /> He practises his breathing and meditation exercises, followed by some Yoga. His pain recedes, his mind calms down.<br /> <br /> <b>08:10 AM.</b><br /> <br /> Time to work. He locks himself in his study, reading for the nth time the notes of his predecesor. He checks the class scheudles, the themes, the proposed work and bibliography. Takes another look at each of the files of each of his students, memorizing the names and the faces, noting down his own personal impressions and suggestion on how to motivate or focus each of them so they get the most out of the classes. Who knows? One of this young people could very well be in a position to save his life in the future. Better prepare them the best that he can.<br /> <br /> He likes this, working alone in his study everything seems normal. He can almost pretend Melissa is in the next room. Almost.<br /> <br /> <b>10:10 AM.</b><br /> <br /> He closes the books, orders his notes and leaves everything tidy and where it belongs. He gets out of his study and goes seeing his recent acquisition, a brand new terrarium reproducing the habitat of his pet, an Atheris Hispida, more commonly know as the spinny bush viper. He has not yet given it a name. He grabs a small mouse he took from the lab and feeds it to the snake. That reminds him that he should go shop for some groceries before attending the meeting. He consults his watch. Less than an hour left. Still, time enough.<br /> <br /> <b>10:35 AM.</b><br /> <br /> Groceries taken care of, he preapares for the Consilium. White shirt and dark grey pants with a matching vest. No tie. No jacket either, instead of that he takes a long grey coat he is quite fond of. An aniversary present. He caresses the soft yet sturdy fabric with a smile. He polishes his shoes until they shine.<br /> With calm he prepares his doctors bag, checking his list to make sure everything is there and in perfect condition. He makes sure to have his white doctor's coat at hand too. Mathias said no magic at the Consilium and he plans on observing the rules, but it is always better to be safe than sorry.<br /> <br /> He arrives to the meeting place and inmediately starts looking for the few known faces he expects, Dante, Mathias or Valentine.</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-02-2016, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:27:43-07:00","id":996876,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate, Time)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar debates with himself over whether to help Dr. Langley today or tomorrow. He decides to go tomorrow to campus, since he doesn't know how long the meeting is going to take, and he wants some time to get to know the th\u00e9archs besides Mathias, and possibly getting a lesson from Mathias. <br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Dr. Langley, I'll be happy to help you out for a few hours tomorrow. Would 10 to 3 be okay with you? - Simon</span></div> <br /> Ragnar eats breakfast, showers and dresses in a blue button-down shirt and gray slacks. Best foot forward and all that. He heads out around 10 to get there at 11. <hr />Ragnar stops at the entrance of St. John Cantius. He hasn't stepped inside of a church in months. Granted, it's been months since he Awakened, too. Will that make a difference? Can there possibly be some Truth that he was once blind to? Does some divinity or higher reality reside here, which he could not recognize as a Sleeper. When he notices the guard standing in front of the door, he recites the words that Valentine told him, with far more gravity and sincerity than he originally intended: <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I am here to open my eyes to the truth.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Inside, the Baroque architecture literally takes his breath away. He stares, turning slowly on the spot. He opens his Sight to Fate and Time. Surely there is some trace of the Supernal here, right? How can such beauty not have a touch of magic about it, even if it was built by Sleeper hands? <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar uses Active Mage Sight with the Fate and Time Arcana, just long enough to identify any Mysteries in the church and do Revelation and Scrutiny on them.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:00:29-07:00","id":996909,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> No immediate sign of anyone he knows well enough to talk to. He's hanging out in the narthex, like you do, when he sees Ragnar coming through the heavy wooden doors. His blood runs cold for a second- <i>greet, or hide?</i><br /> <br /> It's a moot point, as the young man appears to be having a religious experience. Moonstone is deflated. When you've seen one ornately decorated Catholic church in a large American urban center, you've pretty much seen them all, and the space doesn't have any particular significance to him beyond its role in the Consilium. He once heard Sleeper religious symbols described as merely <i>&quot;the wreckage of paradise,&quot;</i> and that's pretty much been his view since. Catchy phrase, too.<br /> <br /> So instead of interrupting Ragnar, he picks somebody else out of the crowd to soothe his nerves. There's an older man in a grey coat, bald with striking facial hair, who looks unfamiliar and curious. He gravitates toward the Moros called Ouroboros Ophis.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I haven't seen you at services here before. Are you newly joining us?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Just making sure the gentleman is on the level. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I've been coming for a while now, but I only recently converted. For my partner's sake. You know how it is.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:53:51-07:00","id":996934,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Thanks for the offer, but I've got a bus to catch in just a bit. Run fast!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#B8860B\">Heh, sure. Later.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx watches Ewan take off as he instinctively reaches for his silver pendant, his eyes on the clock. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">No magic on the premises...</span>&quot; he reminds himself. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'll catch breakfast in the city. Ought to be some sort of take-out nearby...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Lynx doesn't stop fiddling with his pendant, not on the bus, or at the shops, not even when consuming his breakfast - an early morning kebab (because it looked tasty) - though he makes sure to stop by a washroom to clean himself up before heading to the church. He looks around for familiar faces, but finds only the guard before the door.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Morning! I'm here to open my eyes to the truth. Or does it have to be '<i>I am here to open my eyes to the truth</i>'? Are contractions dangerous in our... world? Society?</span>&quot; Lynx rubs his beard as he ponders the irrelevant. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh, sorry,</span>&quot; he adds when he sees the guard's (likely incredulous) stare, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Nerves.</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-01-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:58:51-07:00","id":997098,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Changing some minor details about the scene from some of your posts, as I didn't make clear where the guards would be located. See below for details.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You've been to this church before for Consilium events, but you know from the ones you've attended and what Hakim has told you that many Consilium meetings are spread across various public locations around the city on a rotating schedule. Still, even with the rotating schedule, during your years of service you've been here enough to know the general procedure. Sleeper events are held here <a href=\"http://www.cantius.org/go/liturgy_devotions/category/liturgical_devotional_schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">on their usual schedule</a>, including mass, various special musical events, and prayer and devotional services. The Consilium events are held in private rooms away from the main sanctuary, down in the basement; inconspicuous guards, almost always th\u00e9archs, typically stand outside of a hallway near signs that read &quot;Private Event.&quot;<br /> <br /> When you arrive shortly after 10 am, there are no services currently in progress, but people are lingering from a mass that ended about half an hour ago. Several people are speaking with priests or deacons, reading scripture, or kneeling in silent prayer. You don't immediately recognize anyone or see any signs with guards nearby.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.cantius.org/uploads/images/cantius-church-chicago-wide.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> For a while, you wait in the narthex, mingling with the people coming and going for their individual religious practices. As it gets closer to 11 am, you start to see a few familiar faces: a few Sleepwalkers in service of cabals and other Orders you don't know that well, and a handful of mages you recognize but don't know by name. Ragnar arrives and seems engrossed in his study of the sanctuary, so you let him be for a while.<br /> <br /> It's then that you realize the guards have taken their position outside of a hallway from the narthex. You make your way over, smoothly say the passphrase, and they nod and wave you in with hardly a pause; they're trying not to draw too much attention, and they clearly recognize you. You walk along a tiled hallway into a large reception hall. There is a raised platform with simple chairs arranged in a semi-circle, where you know the Hierarch and Councilors (or their Provosts, depending on who attends) will be seated. Various mages and their associates are here, speaking with each other about private affairs. A few look towards you, but no one approaches you yet.<br /> <br /> That's when you see the surviving members of the Shield of Dawn speaking with a middle-aged Caucasian man with graying hair. You overhear Mathias refer to him as Ouroboros Ophis, and make your way over to greet him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Your home has a somber atmosphere this morning, as usual since Melissa's absence. Your morning routine helps you to calm your mind and mentally prepare you for the Consilium meeting. Although you don't fully know what to expect, you want to present yourself as calm, collected, and knowledgeable.<br /> <br /> You arrive at the church with a very polished and pristine outfit, dressed to impress. You don't immediately recognize anyone, however. You see various people and religious officials wandering the sanctuary, but no services are in progress. About 15 minutes after you arrive, Mathias and his cabalmates walk through the front door, and he greets you with a smile. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Good morning, Doctor,&quot;</span> he says as he shakes your hand. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I'm glad you could make it today.&quot;</span> He formally introduces you to Boomer and Valentine, his cabalmates, whom he has told you about but you haven't met. He escorts you to a hallway from the narthex where two people stand by a sign that reads &quot;Private Event.&quot; Mathias speaks the passphrase, and they nod and let you pass. You find yourself in a large reception hall, where sturdy chairs are neatly arranged in long rows facing a raised platform with more chairs in a semi-circle.<br /> <br /> As Mathias chats with you and begins referring to you by your Shadow Name, another mage approaches you and introduces himself as Moonstone. You recognize the name as one of the mages Mathias said may be interested in forming a cabal with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You receive an email reply from Dr. Langley shortly before leaving your apartment, saying that the time frame you suggested would be excellent. He offers to buy you lunch in exchange for your assistance.<br /> <br /> When you open yourself to the Supernal world as seen through the lens of Arcadia, you see that this building has a...weight to it. This building stands at the crossroads of fate, but in ways you don't immediately understand. You see large, thick cords of Fate wrapped around the building, filling the sanctuary; this surprises you, considering that you were told no one should be using magic here. But even though you don't yet understand the magic surrounding this place, you can guess based on its sheer size and scale that a strong mage, or perhaps a group of them, were involved in its casting.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may attempt Revelation and/or Scrutiny with Opacity 4.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After studying the room, you realize there aren't any guards here in the sanctuary as you thought there would be. You wander back through the narthex, and that's when you see the sign reading &quot;Private Event.&quot; You intone your passphrase, and thankfully they wave for you to pass through. You find Mathias and the rest of the Shields of Dawn standing a circle, next to Moonstone and, to your shock, <i>Dr. Bates</i>, the professor who has filled in for Dr. McCallister for your FYS class.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You are impressed at the size and scale of this building. As you approach, you feel the hairs on the back of your neck rise, a sign of something unseen on your Periphery. Glancing around with your Sight reveals quite a few spirits in Twilight circling the building, and within the building itself. They seem to be basking in the presence of this place. You notice some spirits that look like the one you saw at your apartment, tranquility spirits, as well as others you don't recognize.<br /> <br /> You speak the password to the guards you assume are here for the Consilium event. One's eyes widen a bit in surprise at your bumbling discussion, and the other rolls his eyes. &quot;Go on through,&quot; he says curtly, shaking his head with a sigh. As you walk by them, you hear him whisper to the other guard, &quot;<i>Newbies</i>, am I right?<i>&quot;</i> The other guard chuckles.<br /> <br /> You find the meeting room with little trouble after walking through the hallway. The Shields of Dawn are there conferring with Moonstone, Ragnar, and -- is that Dr. Bates? Your new FYS instructor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:39:29-07:00","id":997129,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 4 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> Marlin, unsure about the event's formality level, works through his closet. Eventually he decides to don a suit jacket, but leave off the tie. It's when he spends more than 15 seconds combing his hair that Daisy finally laughs at him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;I don't think I've seen you this nervous since you opened the bookstore! Is there someone you're hoping to impress?&quot; </span>She quirks a smile at him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Ah, well,&quot;</span> he looks a bit abashed.<br /> <br /> She steps close to him and brushes off his lapels. <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;Dear, relax. Just focus on being yourself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;You're right, of course. I'm just a little worried about feeling out of place. I'm barely more than a hobbyist and I'll be rubbing shoulders with <i>actual</i> professionals.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#CC99FF\">&quot;It'll be fine, hon. If you feel out of place, just try to find the other people who enjoy what they do. There's gotta be one or two at least, right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> They share a kiss, then Marlin heads out. He waves goodbye to Forest from the car as he backs out.<br /> <br /> On the way to the church, he focuses on donning his persona. At this point, it's still mostly internal. A switch in the name he calls himself. But he knows it's more than just a name. In the heat of battle, he drew on the persona's strength.<br /> <br /> When he arrives at the church, Binder banishes any awkwardness felt about entering such a place of worship. He strides to the guards and announces confidently: <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I am here to open my eyes to the truth.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:58:59-07:00","id":997138,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 5/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> Lynx does feel dumb as he passes by the guards, but his eyes widen at the majesty of the church's interiors. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">This place does feel powerful. Suits magic, but it's too... righteous. Artificial.</span></i><br /> <br /> His gaze lowers as he looks at the church's inhabitants, and he spots...<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ragnar and Dr. Bates? ... Moonstone and the Shields too? Hope there won't be a clash again.</span></i><br /> <br /> He approaches the group, and puts his hand on Ragnar's shoulder. He addresses them all happily - his voice a little too joyful, in fact. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Morning, Ragnar! Boomer!</span>&quot; He looks at the lady with a grin. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Wicked still, that's good. Mathias and Valentine, how're you doing?</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> He turns to Moonstone and studies him momentarily, opening his Life Senses to assess his physical health. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Moonstone! How've you been? Looks like you're in good form today. Are you healing properly? And ... Dr. Bates...</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> Lynx sniffs a bit and closes his eyes. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm assuming you're not here by accident?</span>&quot; His eyes open as his Senses close, and he looks around. He keeps his eyes off the group. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Has anyone seen Phoenix or Binder?</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:42:03-07:00","id":997409,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar dismisses his Sight. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Maybe after the meeting. </span></i>The moments he took observing the church were sufficient for now, but he'll let it lie for the time being. Perhaps he can examine it with Phoenix when he arrives: surely a place rooted in faith as much as this place carries some resonance with the Aether? <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">\u200bFate is strong here, but why? </span></i><br /> <br /> In the social hall, he walks up to the Shields, Moonstone, and... Dr. Bates. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Mathias. Boomer. Valentine.&quot; </span>He gives Mathias a slight bow, and nods politely to the others. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Moonstone. Good to see you again.&quot; </span>He puts out his hand. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Glad to meet again under better circumstances. I hope your week has been better since Tuesday.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He waits for Moonstone's reaction.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I haven't seen you at services here before. Are you newly joining us?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He turns his attention to Dr. Bates. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Yes, I'm a little surprised to see you here. Parishioner, or are you a catechumen?&quot; </span>\u200bThe lingo slides off the tongue, and he tries to put just enough innuendo that the true question shines through, disguised by church-talk for the benefit of any Sleepers who might still be milling around: <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Awakened or Sleepwalker?</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Morning, Ragnar! Boomer!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He spins around at the sound of Lynx's voice. His face lights up and he embraces his friend in a hearty bearhug. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Lynx! Good to see you here!&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He looks around at the gathering.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"> &quot;Binder and Phoenix here yet?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:28:26-07:00","id":997425,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Glad to meet again under better circumstances. I hope your week has been better since Tuesday.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone shakes his hand with a smile, but he's still cloudy. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Likewise. It's been...well, we can talk about it later. How are your classes? You two are students, aren't you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He shrinks back a bit when Ragnar and Lynx embrace, smiles knowingly at Ophis in a &quot;<i>kids these days</i>&quot; way.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Moonstone! How've you been? Looks like you're in good form today. Are you healing properly?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Physically? Um- well enough. I spent the week somewhere quiet.&quot;</span> His serious wounds have healed, but under Life Sight, his body looks somewhat withered and weakened all over, like a frayed cloth. His muscles haven't repaired themselves yet after a few days of flagellating his own Pattern for power. The best he can do for a pleasant greeting is: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I hope you've eaten.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He points to the door as Binder comes in, and beckons him over.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That's one of them. Maybe Phoenix tripped and fell down a very deep hole,&quot;</span> he speculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:46:14-07:00","id":997434,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>4 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> Ouroboros Ophis is as surprised as his students when he sees them there in those circumstances. He makes quick mental additions to his notes on these two: Ragnar. Linx.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Is that religious lingo really necessary? I thought we were meeting here because it was a safe place to treat these themes&quot;</b></span>- he casually asks to the Shields of Dawn after introductions are made.-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I am Ouroboros Ophis, Moros, and Nameless for the time being&quot;</b></span>-he offers his hand to each of them, giving a firm shake-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Who is this Phoenix that you are talking about? Perhaps another student of mine?&quot;</b></span>-smiles softly.-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I have been told that perhaps we all should associate, form what they call a <i>Cabal</i> for our mutual protection and support&quot;</b></span>-lets the idea sink in.-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I must admit I will find a little akward my double-sided relationship with you two, but I am sure we all are adult enough to figure something out, are we not?&quot;</b></span>-he adds to Ragnar and Linx.</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-03-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:01:35-07:00","id":997671,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> The guards standing beside the &quot;Private Event&quot; sign nod and wave you forward. You follow along a tiled hallway and take a small flight of stairs down to a large reception hall. Other people are starting to file in behind you, moving to claim open seats or conferring with associates around the room. You quickly spot several of the other Nameless mages whom you recently met, talking with Mathias, Boomer, Valentine, and a middle-aged man with graying hair you haven't been introduced to. Moonstone waves you over in time to hear this man introduce himself as Ouroboros Ophis, the Moros mage Mathias mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> Boomer grins in response to Ragnar's code words and Ophis' comments. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Hah! Yeah, everyone here is either a Sleepwalker or mage. No need for secrecy, at least about that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Shields of Dawn make small talk until Phoenix arrives. Once all of you are present, Mathias offers some brief advice about the meeting. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;The Chicago Consilium is a formal council, led by the Hierarch and five Councilors, one each as a representative for their respective Supernal Path. As this is your first meeting, you will be expected to introduce yourself. Because you are still learning about the rules and expectations of mage society, it is expected that you will pair with an experienced mage who will vouch for you. Until you officially join a cabal or Order, that mage assumes responsibility for educating you on the basic laws and principles of our Consilium.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It's not a free pass to screw around,&quot;</span> Boomer interjects. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;It's supposed to ensure that you get a fair chance to learn the rules, so you don't do anything stupid or get yourself in trouble. But if you break a big law, especially if your mentor clearly advised you not to, then it falls on you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As you talk, you realize that the room is filling quickly. You'd guess that there are probably 200 chairs arranged facing the center stage, and a quick glance tells you that many of them are rapidly filling. It's almost noon, and most of the mages who were standing and talking with each other are starting to move towards their chairs. Valentine is standing and looking around the room, studying various people, but he is quiet during this conversation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Do you have any questions?&quot;</span> Mathias asks.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Leaving room here for more conversation or RP between you all, so feel free to keep the conversation going as desired. It will also allow time for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> to post. If he doesn't, I'll assume that Phoenix arrived on time as Mathias was offering his advice, and that he didn't have anything to ask or share.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone </b><br /> As Mathias is talking, you notice the Knights of Alhambra walk past you. Rose of Sharon meets your eye and offers a polite smile, and she nods at you. She clearly hasn't forgotten about you, or (assumedly) her offer to introduce you to a Mind Adept who can help with your request.<br /> <br /> You also spot Ace walk in behind another group of Arrows whom you recognize but don't know personally. She glances in your direction and then quickly makes her way to the back of the room, where she stands with her arms crossed over her chest. She pointedly stares ahead, not looking in your direction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Shortly before you take your seat, you see Dante walk in with two other men and a woman. Dante is in his usual Gothic attire, and the others around him are wearing equally unusual outfits. The woman is wearing what essentially looks like a modern toga, a cloth dress wrapped around her body that has a short angular hemline, and her hair is neatly pulled back under a copper-toned headband. The two men similarly wear outfits that evoke a fusion of the old and the new, odd blends of outfits that have Greek references but modern haircuts. Dante smiles and waves to you before taking his seat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder and Lynx</b><br /> You each spot more familiar faces in the crowd. Falling Blossom and Raven walk in together; they're conversing as they approach the seats, but you can't hear what they're saying over the ambient noise in the room. Three other men walk in behind them and take seats next to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-04-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:47:56-07:00","id":997685,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> Get up. Before breakfast exercises. Breakfast. Check messages, no new messages. Of course there isn't. It's not like there's a killer on the loose or anything-!<br /> <br /> Alright, calm down. Just work it off with some more exercises. You really can't do much of anything in their department, and you'll be meeting up with them later today. Just work it off, channel that energy into something positive. Besides, you have a meeting to attend. Speaking of which, how formal is it? Is that something the Consilium concerns itself with? How 'bout I try on a leather jacket and see how they react to that.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I was dealing with soooo many possibilities with entering the scene. One of them being where he went early into town so he could shop for formal wear, to trying to meet up with one of the mages he's familiar with and ask for advice before hastily buying whatever was suggested. I ended going &quot;Fuck it, I'll just have him wear a leather jacket and see how that goes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the wait on that.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I arrive in the church, sort of wandering around the middle of the place. Not sure where I'm supposed to go exactly, so I just hang around until someone notices me. I look around, taking in the scenery. I chuckle at it all. How many would leave in horror if they knew what Heaven was truly like? Oh well, enough of that, time to look for someone familiar.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perceiving for any mage he knows.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/452985\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Composure 2 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:22:07-07:00","id":997715,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> You wander around St. John Cantius church, annoyed as you realize that Valentine's advice on where to find the meeting wasn't particularly clear. The sanctuary itself seems fairly quiet, as no services are being held by the time you arrive.<br /> <br /> You leave the sanctuary and wander around the narthex, where various people are gathered or walking around chatting. Finally, you notice Binder walk by in a nice suit with neatly combed hair, and see him just in time to walk by two men standing next to a hallway with a sign that reads &quot;Private Event.&quot; You speak the passphrase to the men, who wave you along down a tiled hallway and down a flight of stairs.<br /> <br /> You finally find yourself in a large reception hall, where various people -- assumedly mages -- have gathered. You quickly spot Boomer, who's wearing a similarly audacious outfit as when you met her on Tuesday, and then see that she's standing next to the other Nameless mages and Shields of Dawn whom you met earlier this week. You make your way over to them and join in on their conversation.<br /> <br /> Boomer smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Hey man, glad you could make it.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:22:22-07:00","id":997759,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#ff1493\">&quot;Hah! Yeah, everyone here is either a Sleepwalker or mage. No need for secrecy, at least about that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Sorry. I'm a little paranoid about that. Feels good to be able to talk openly about it, instead of whispering and talking in code.&quot;</span><i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">It shouldn't have to be that way. </span></i><br /> <br /> He nods to Dr. Bates- <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">no, Ouroboros Ophis. The snake eating his own tail. Cycles and renewal. </span></i>A curious name for a Moros. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I'm sure we'll be able to work something out, sir.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;Do you have any questions?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Yeah, about what happened Tuesday. I'm guessing the Consilium's going to want a full report on </span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">that? Or did you,&quot; </span>he gestures vaguely to the Shields of Dawn, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;fill anybody in on that? And how much do we need to tell them?&quot; </span>He looks at Moonstone with some concern. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I trust Moonstone when he said that he didn't mean to summon... you know... but is everybody else going to be as understanding? I mean,&quot; </span>he lowers his voice, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;a gulmoth's no laughing matter. And the Consilium has suffered enough losses as it is with the Death Storm. Is everybody going to accept Moonstone's explanation? I don't want his branded,&quot; </span>here he mouths the next word, the one Mathias briefly mentioned in his explanation of the Abyss, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;</span><i>Scelestus</i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">... for an accident.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">He perks up at Phoenix's arrival. &quot;Phoenix. Good to see you.&quot; He lowers his voice a little. &quot;Hey, would you mind hanging back for a minute or so after the meeting? There's... something I want your help with.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:48:01-07:00","id":997868,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 2/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div><br /> In response to Ophis' question:<span style=\"color:Teal\"> &quot;Phoenix is an Obrimos we've become entangled with. Young, headstrong, skilled warrior- no idea where he learned, though.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Apparently everyone is already acquainted. He leans over to Binder and stage-whispers: <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Do you know him too? Is it just me who doesn't?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He waves at Rose of Sharon, but talking to her and the others can wait for later. He can't bear to look at Ace, just seeing her makes his ears burn and brings his guilt to the surface. He's quiet and distracted until Ragnar mentions him in hushed tones. Ugly memories of standing guard while parents, teachers, employers, and mages whispered about his failures in the next room.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Don't talk about me like I'm not here,&quot;</span> he snaps. But he's more together this morning, and he flushes with embarrassment a second later. <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Sorry- I'm sorry, you're right. It's my fault. I'm the one to blame.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I really tried to center myself this week, but...I can't stop thinking about letting that <i>thing </i>into the world. How the light popped around it, how it almost killed Phoenix and Ragnar, how I reached into its mind and saw it <i>thinking about me...</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His fingers are curled in his hair. He blurts out: <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;I've been dreaming about it. It's like we're connected- I <i>miss</i> it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> What? That doesn't sound right. He looks as surprised as anyone that it tumbled out, staring at his fingers like they're bloody. <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Er- no, I don't! That's unwanted thoughts, that's not me. No. <i>God</i>, no! Ugh. Vile.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Deep breath. <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Listen. The Consilium will have a lot on their minds after the Deathstorm. They don't need the play-by-play of every Mystery their constituents encounter, including what happened Tuesday. But we <i>should </i>inform them that the thing is still in the Fallen World, for the safety of everyone. I performed a Divination along our...um, <i>connection,</i> and learned when <i>it </i>will manifest again: the evening of Saturday the 17th. When that gets closer, I can divine even more precise information about when and where to stop it before it hurts anyone else. I'm learning new things about the Arcana all the time: I can make this work, trust me!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He raises a finger: <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;<i>Caveat conjector- </i>'let the diviner beware.' Divinations can become less accurate when more people know about them and can change the future. It may be wiser to keep the specifics to ourselves until the matter is resolved. But I am willing to take responsibility before the Consilium when I introduce myself. You shouldn't be punished for my actions, even if we do form a cabal.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He turns to Ophis, fretting. <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;I&quot;m sorry. This must be making a terrible first impression. I'm sure we're all glad to work with you, but we do have a sword or two hanging over our heads.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Oh- Phoenix has been standing right there. He catches himself and switches back to polite-but-distant mode.<span style=\"color:Teal\"> &quot;Good morning.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-03-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:40:44-07:00","id":997889,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>4 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> Ouroboros nods and smiles back at Dante. He listens to the explanations of this... Moonstone, was him? and gets concerned as they devolve into an incoherent rant. Something happend to this young mages, something bad. He makes a mental note to go on about it later.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Phoenix. Good to see you.&quot;</span>-Ragnar's greeting to the newly arriving mage snaps him out of his thoughts, he turns around to introduce himself and gets taken by surprise when he sees his old aqcuaintance.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Ga..garrick?&quot;</b></span>-he blurts out before realizing what a <i>faux pass</i> that means in this context-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Phoenix&quot;</b></span>-he corrects himself-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Phoenix, nice name. I go by Ouroboros Ophis here. I am so glad to see you here son, it has been a while. You look good&quot;</b></span>-he is incredibly happy to see him and it shows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:31:16-07:00","id":997912,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Oh I'm sorry, let me scream it to the entire Consilium,&quot; </span>Ragnar hisses at Moonstone. Then he sighs.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"> &quot;Look. I'm just concerned about you, is all. When we explain what happened Tuesday, I won't mention any connection between you and the gulmoth. I'll legalese my way out of it. I have some plausible deniability. As far as I know, some mage on the other side of that Iris you and Phoenix came out of summoned it to attack you. If you want to confess, fine. But I'm not going to incriminate you. In all likelihood, we're going to be cabal-mates, and I don't want that any consequences against on you my head.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Moonstone's mention of Alux's return forms a knot of excitement in his stomach. This is his domain: an unavoidable confrontation, the pieces set on the board and the only thing to be done is to try and tip the scales to one side or another. This is wyrd, Fate. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Ragnar\u00f6k approaches.&quot; </span>He smiles. And planning may as well start now. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone, keep tabs on it. I was thinking about taking a peek at him, but I'll leave this to you. When the day gets closer, we'll be ready. Maybe you and Lynx can try something and try to work out its banes. Then when September 17 rolls around, we get a few Arrows to sit around where it's going to show up, and then they pop it. Problem solved.&quot; </span>He smiles at everyone.<span style=\"color:#0000cd\"> &quot;Great plan or what?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He notes Ouroboros Ophis' slip of Phoenix's Sympathetic name with some curiosity. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Garrick. Interesting.</span> </i>He regards the Theurge with interest. He's obviously had training, like Moonstone said. But where? And for what purpose? And perhaps more importantly, by <i>whom</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:50:19-07:00","id":997925,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> When Ragnar hugs him, he returns it affectionately. He listens in on the conversation - saying little, nodding at Moonstone as the man acknowledges his words - when he perks up and notices Raven entering the Cathedral. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">She came! But...</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx looks at her table for a minute, surveying them curiously, quietly,cautiously. The group's conversation grows dimmer to him, going in one ear and out the other. After his moment of mental absence, he rubs his beard and steps over to Boomer, giving her a soft nudge. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Boomer, the people on the table over there,</span>&quot; he points to Raven and her table. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">What do you know about them? Are they the good kind of magic, or...?</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:31:52-07:00","id":997974,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div><br /> He can't resist being catty to Ragnar about Divination. <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;I'm the only one of us who could do it, anyway. You said you're an Initiate of Space? You lack the puissance with the Arcanum to read someone else's future if they aren't present. Here's another riddle for you: what's the difference between asking <i>'when will <b>I</b> next encounter my enemy'</i> and <i>'when will <b>my enemy</b> be most vulnerable?'</i> Meditate on this and learn Wisdom, and something of the Art as well.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone preens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:05:33-07:00","id":997989,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Hey man, glad you could make it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Glad I could, too. In hindsight, I didn't get very clear directions,&quot;</span> I greet as I shoot off a slightly-annoyed glance at Valentine. I respond to all the other greetings with my own, except for one of them. Is that, Pops? He Awakened, too? And came to Chicago? I never took the phrase &quot;it's a small world&quot; all that seriously, but this inclines me to believe it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Ga..garrick?&quot;</b></span> Dr. Bates blurts out, guess he's just as surprised to see me, <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Phoenix. </b></span><span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>Phoenix, nice name. I go by Ouroboros Ophis here. I am so glad to see you here son, it has been a while. You look good&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> I didn't even notice I was gaping until I began to respond. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Uh, yeah. Nice to see you again, Pops. Ouroburos Ophis, snake eating it's own tail, eh? You an alchemist now or something?&quot;</span> I joke to break the ice, as well as get me out of my little stupor. After a bit of chit-chat, Ragnar comes up to me in a hushed tone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Hey, would you mind hanging back for a minute or so after the meeting? There's... something I want your help with.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;So long as it doesn't take very long. Got my own business and all,&quot;</span> I answer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sorry for not mentioning this earlier, but Phoenix is carrying his staff with him.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T05:45:27-07:00","id":998190,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm the only one of us who could do it, anyway. You said you're an Initiate of Space? You lack the puissance with the Arcanum to read someone else's future if they aren't present.</span><span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well then. Perhaps you could give me a lesson? Cast a Space spell on me and have me work through it, perhaps? You've already proven that your skill with Space is undeniable.&quot; </span>Ragnar hopes that the combination of flattery and the offer of a free swipe will be enough to ameliorate Moonstone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff0000\">&quot;So long as it doesn't take very long. Got my own business and all.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;No, it should only take a minute. We just need to walk over to the cathedral. I need an Obrimos' opinion on something.&quot; </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:15:39-07:00","id":998212,"title":"","content":"<b>Everyone</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Yeah, about what happened Tuesday. I'm guessing the Consilium's going to want a full report on </span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">that? Or did you,&quot; </span>he gestures vaguely to the Shields of Dawn, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;fill anybody in on that? And how much do we need to tell them?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Listen. The Consilium will have a lot on their minds after the Deathstorm. They don't need the play-by-play of every Mystery their constituents encounter, including what happened Tuesday. But we <i>should </i>inform them that the thing is still in the Fallen World, for the safety of everyone.&quot; ... &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#008080\">But I am willing to take responsibility before the Consilium when I introduce myself. You shouldn't be punished for my actions, even if we do form a cabal.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias crosses his arms over his chest, and his face darkens at the mention of the Gulmoth. However, Valentine is the first to comment on this topic. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The Council was already made aware of the incident,&quot;</span> he replies in clipped tones. His eyes are focused on Moonstone. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I am one of two Sentinels serving this Consilium, and a Guardian. Did you think no one else would know?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Shields of Dawn haven't explained much about the Council or Consilium structure, beyond the role of the Hierarch and Councilors. For the benefit of the other mages present who have not heard of his title, Valentine briefly explains that a Sentinel is a mage appointed by the Hierarch or the Council to patrol the Consilium's sancta and enforce its rulings and mandates. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I notified the Council on Tuesday. For now, only we here and the members of this Council are aware of the Gulmoth. As a result of his actions, Moonstone,&quot;</span> he looks again at the Nameless who summoned Alux, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;has been tasked with destroying the Gulmoth. Obviously, he should not do this alone. But as of yet, the Council is viewing this incident as a critical lesson on the dangers of Paradox, rather than a willful disobedience of Consilium law.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I don't want his branded </span><i>Scelestus</i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">... for an accident.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias quickly interjects with a serious tone. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Do not use that word lightly, Ragnar, under <i>any </i>circumstances.&quot;</span> He pauses, and his tone softens as he sighs. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Moonstone made a mistake. A serious one, but not unforgivable. This is why I cannot stress enough that it is important you all receive training and mentorship. The Pentacle Orders, and the Lex Magica, exist for this purpose -- to protect against serious threats to the integrity of our society.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone, keep tabs on it. I was thinking about taking a peek at him, but I'll leave this to you. When the day gets closer, we'll be ready. Maybe you and Lynx can try something and try to work out its banes. Then when September 17 rolls around, we get a few Arrows to sit around where it's going to show up, and then they pop it. Problem solved. Great plan or what?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer grins. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I like your enthusiasm, kid. But your group showed that you can beat it when you work together. I'm confident you can do it again. The hardest part is that you really could use someone with strength in Spirit. Gulmoths are kind of like tainted spirits, and respond to spells to control them that way. But without our shaman, Orca...&quot;</span> She trails off and frowns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm the only one of us who could do it, anyway. You said you're an Initiate of Space? You lack the puissance with the Arcanum to read someone else's future if they aren't present. Here's another riddle for you: what's the difference between asking <i>'when will <b>I</b> next encounter my enemy'</i> and <i>'when will <b>my enemy</b> be most vulnerable?'</i> Meditate on this and learn Wisdom, and something of the Art as well.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine smiles knowingly, but doesn't comment. Mathias jaw clenches and he replies chidingly, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I'm glad to see that you are <i>meditating</i> on gaining <i>Wisdom</i>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Boomer, the people on the table over there. </span><span style=\"color:#800000\">What do you know about them? Are they the good kind of magic, or...?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Boomer looks over to where you are pointing and chuckles. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Oh, them? Raven is a shaman...definitely an odd ball, if you ask me, but she's gifted with Life and Spirit magic. Falling Blossom is a Mastigos Mystagogue, but I don't know much about her. She seems cordial. Mathias could tell you more about Vincent and Shepherd, they're th\u00e9archs -- good upstanding people. And Pulse is an Arrow like me. Great fighter, wicked good with firearms.&quot;</span> She smiles. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;They're a cabal known as the Servants of Gaea. They formed their group around the Legacies of the Elemental Masteries. There are five standard Legacies, one for each Path.&quot;</span> She pauses and adds, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Uh...I guess we haven't talked to you about Legacies yet. It's a long story, one we don't have time for. Briefly, it's an advanced way of shaping how you experience and express your magic. It's a very personal decision.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:18:20-07:00","id":998261,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 2/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I am one of two Sentinels serving this Consilium, and a Guardian. Did you think no one else would know?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He flattens. Honestly, until this morning he'd been thinking of it as something that happened to <i>him</i> more than the other Nameless, much less the Consilium at large. Caught out by his own Naive nature. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;...kind of?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That gnawing Guilt will have to be resolved in a less dramatic and more authentic way, apparently. It sounds like the whole matter has already been negotiated in his absence. The Guardians really do have eyes everywhere, don't they?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Well then. Perhaps you could give me a lesson? Cast a Space spell on me and have me work through it, perhaps? You've already proven that your skill with Space is undeniable.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone's immense vanity is soothed. He clasps his hands, excited to be in the teaching role for once. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Perhaps I could! I've seen how Mastigos challenge their students before. It's a date. We'll discuss it after the Consilium.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I'm glad to see that you are <i>meditating</i> on gaining <i>Wisdom</i>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He smiles sweetly, playing flattered. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you, Mathias! Wouldn't that be a nice line for your book report today?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Triumphant</b>: Gain a Beat any time you throw your success in someone\u2019s face, even if it risks making him angry or resentful.<br /> <br /> Does this count?</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:31:33-07:00","id":998415,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'll get stronger with Spirit,</span>&quot; Lynx says absently as he studies Raven's entourage. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Definitely. Especially if it means protecting...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> His voice trails off in hesitation, his thoughts going elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>Raven, Falling Blossom, Vincent and Shepherd, the Servants of Gaea...</i></span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">You said there are five Elemental Masteries? What...</span>&quot; He starts, but his voice is drowned by:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I'm glad to see that you are <i>meditating</i> on gaining <i>Wisdom</i>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you, Mathias! Wouldn't that be a nice line for your book report today?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Lynx sighs, the exchange raising his hackles. He turns to both of them with an unamused look.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Could you two not do that <i>right now</i>?</span>&quot; Lynx says through gritted teeth. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>Faen da</i>, why are you two even talking to one another? Neither of you are coming off as remotely likeable.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx crosses his arms as he turns back to look at Raven's table, with a few steps away from the group and Mathias and Moonstone's feud - and he lowers his head in shame shortly after.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Yes, </span></i><span style=\"color:#800000\">that'll<i> improve the mood. Fucking genius I am.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-04-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T14:05:04-07:00","id":998426,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;Do not use that word lightly, Ragnar, under </span><i>any </i><span style=\"color:#008000\">circumstances.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar hangs his head a little.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Sorry, Mathias. I'll keep that in mind for the future. I was just concerned about how the Consilium would react to Moonstone's mistake. But since you already told the Hierarch and the Counselors, Valentine, that's not really an issue now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone and Mathias' sniping irritates Ragnar, but apparently not as much as it irritates Lynx. When he moves away from the rest of the group, Ragnar gives the others an apologetic look and walks over to Lynx. He puts a hand on his shoulder reassuringly. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Hey,&quot;</span> he whispers. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;It's okay. I know it's not exactly fun watching them bicker, but I think Tuesday is as bad as they're ever going to get. They're never going to really like each other, but sniping at each other's not so bad in comparison to a Duel Arcane every time they meet.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:03:32-07:00","id":998598,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone and Lynx</b><br /> Mathias' calm face rapidly turns into a scowl. Moonstone's statement clearly got under his skin. He opens his mouth to retort, but Valentine merely places a hand on his shoulder and Boomer shakes her head, and Mathias is able to restrain himself. Lynx's comment and clear agitation also helps Mathias to see that he is allowing himself to be manipulated by his emotions again.<br /> <br /> When he finally replies, Mathias says coldly, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Take your seats. The Council is coming.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Moonstone: You can take an extra Beat for speaking out in a way to intentionally goad your rival. As a consequence, your impression with Mathias dips further, which will add time and/or Doors to any future Social Maneuvering you might attempt with him.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> When you look around the room to find your seats, you realize just how many people there are gathered here. Most of the seats are filled by now, which means there are easily several hundred mages here, more than you could have possibly expected to see. To Moonstone, a quick head count will indicate that there are easily at least twice as many mages present here than at the next largest Consilium meeting he has attended. Clearly, few mages would want to miss the opportunity to hear the new Hierarch's comments on recent events.<br /> <br /> Over the din filling this room, you begin to hear footsteps approaching.<br /> <br /> There is a clatter as all mages present stand up and offer some sign of respect: some bow their heads, others kneel, and a select few even prostrate themselves on the ground, drawing smirks or nods of approval from various other mages nearby. Despite the number of mages present, a silence falls over the room. Boomer places a fist over her heart and mutters jokingly, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Look pretty.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The footsteps grow louder, and you all see a mixed group of three women and then three men appear. Your eyes are immediately drawn to the woman walking calmly to the center of the raised platform. Mathias has briefly explained who Cielo is, but hearing about her and seeing her in person are two very different things. The Hierarch is wearing a simple but elegant red dress that stops just below her knees, contrasted by red athletic shoes and dark hair that falls freely around her shoulders. She has high cheekbones and fierce eyes.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://roundbyroundboxing.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/MarlenEsparza1-977x1024.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> As Cielo moves to the center of the stage, the five Councilors take their place beside her. The other two Latina women, assumedly Estrella and Luna, stand on one side of Cielo and flash bright smiles at the room. They each wear a fashionable skirt or dress bearing their respective celestial symbols.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/83/b4/7a/83b47a8ed0f017640da2b117e803589a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/7c/f3/19/7cf3193b4b74c5a2f0027755e7a7e3cd.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The three men, whom most of you do not recognize, are each wearing a crisp, custom-tailored, three-piece suit. At seeing one of them, Mathias startles and Boomer whistles quietly in surprise. Murmurs spread around the room. Moonstone recognizes the face, but each of you hear a name whispered around the room: <i>Atlas</i>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/28/25/ab/2825ab46a3332606b089e878242dddab.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Cielo stands in a casual stance at the center of the stage and places one first on her hip. She raises her other hand in acknowledgement of the room's signs of respect, and everyone moves to sit as she lowers her hand. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Please, be seated.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may each make a roll to see what you can glean from the room, either Wits + Empathy or Intelligence + Politics.<br /> <br /> I wanted to get this post up but don't have time to write more at the moment. I'll add more when I have time, sorry.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:04:32-07:00","id":998599,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.moderngentlemanmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/04/mens-suit-patterns-pinstripes.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"http://image.dhgate.com/0x0/f2/albu/g1/M01/3A/13/rBVaGVTDpMyAb4K2AAEHHckr1T8534.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">These are Apollo and Poseidon, respectively, who will be introduced further shortly. Couldn't include more than 4 images in a single post.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:05:02-07:00","id":998600,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> </div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>Faen da</i>, why are you two even talking to one another? Neither of you are coming off as remotely likeable.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Moonstone crosses his arms and huffs, nose upturned. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'll be completely satisfied when he fulfills his oath today. I don't hold grudges.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He's just waiting for the meeting proper to start, before any more sugary venom is exchanged. He <i>knew </i>this was going to be a bad day. And what does <i>&quot;faen da&quot;</i> mean, anyway?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Finally they take their seats for the show itself. It's <i>weird </i>to be here as an Awakened one, not just a hanger-on to someone else's party. And from the size of the crowd, it's an auspicious day for a first impression.<br /> <br /> When the room clatters, Moonstone immediately kneels and lowers his head in obeisance. The others have the excuse of being new, but he'll show his reverence for the Hierarch, whomever holds the seat.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intelligence 1 + Politics 3 (Chicago Consilium): <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453521\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:46:43-07:00","id":998714,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar follows Mathias to a seat and sits next to him. As Cielo and the Councilors enter the room, he stands and bows his head, and then takes a seat when Cielo indicates. He gives her and her Councilors a look-over. Cielo, Estrella, and Luna are all beautiful, confident, and dangerous-looking. Estrella seems like the social one of the group. Luna has a calculating look, like a lioness watching a gazelle. <br /> <br /> He watches the devastatingly handsome Atlas with curiosity. Apparently, his presence is unexpected. Obviously, it's a major shift in the political landscape of the Consilium. Has he replaced a Councilor who died in the Death Storm? Or this some sort of unanticipated political alliance? <br /> <br /> [Ragnar attempts to parse out the significance of Atlas' presence, and the reaction to it. Intelligence 4 + Politics 1 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453576\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> Apollo doesn't give him any strong impression. Perhaps because he's overshadowed by Poseidon: the contrast of his immaculate blue suit with his wild beard and the tattoos creeping down his hands and up his neck is striking. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Thyrsus? </span></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:17:43-07:00","id":998772,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 3/5. Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">No, it isn't fun,</span>&quot; Lynx agrees quietly. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I should probably just leave any conversation where both of them are present. I can't keep from getting angry myself.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008000\">Take your seats. The Council is coming.</span>&quot; Lynx glances at the Mathias, frowning at the chill in his voice.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Definitely can't rely on him.</span></i><br /> <br /> His distaste disappears quickly however, as he catches the sound of footsteps. He finds a seat but remains standing, though he offers no real sign of respect but for stretching his shoulders. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">So that's Cielo... Powerful. Beautiful. Wow...<br /> <br /> All of them strong... And I'm so small...</span></i> <br /> <br /> When the room's asked to be seated, he does so. As the meeting is about to start, he looks around the room and immerses himself in his senses. He sniffs and tastes the air, his ears drawing in every murmur, the heavy breathing in search of heartbeats, the effort put into maintaining countenance and composure...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453608\" target=\"_blank\">Empathy roll to gauge room, Wits (3) + Empathy (3) + Willpower (+3), for 9 dice \u2192 2 successes. </a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">:&lt; 9 dice, 2 successes... Lynx isn't particularly lucky.</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T13:00:05-07:00","id":998876,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>4 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> Ouroboros is not particularly amused at the bickering between Moonstone and Matthias. He finds that petty and disrespetful tone regarding not just a fellow mage, but most probably a better and more experience one, disconcerting to say the least. He must take a long look at this young one when he has the opportunity.<br /> <br /> Linx and Ragnar's reaction, reinforce his first impression. Moonstone means problems, and yet... Some part of him feels a certain affinity with him, like if they shared something important in common. There's some great saddness buried below all that pettyness.<br /> <br /> As the Hierarch and Councilors enter the room, he gently bows his head in acknowledgement. The murmurs and surprise that filled the room at the appearance of Atlas intrigue him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Read te Room: Intelligence + Politics = 6 dice = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453668\" target=\"_blank\">0 Successes</a> let's make it a Dramatic Failure for a Beat</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:11:10-08:00","id":999171,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> So Moonstone's making a complete ass of himself, Mathias makes a slightly less ass of himself, Ragnar's arguing with Moonstone, and Lynx took the words right outta my mouth. Well, most of 'em, that is. Yeah, ain't nobody got time for that. Besides, I've got some catching up to do.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;So Pops, what's brings you to Chicago?&quot;</span> I start off.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008000\">Take your seats. The Council is coming.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> The meeting starts, and not a moment too soon! I bow in respect to the Council as everyone else does. When in Rome, after all. Speaking of which, considering the formal attire everyone's wearing (well, almost everyone's), looks like mages value fine clothes as much as Sleepers do. Now to see how they'll react to a complete lack of that when I come to make my introduction. Probably be very interesting. In the mean time, let's see what I can learn here.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using Wits + Empathy to glean information.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453879\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Empathy 2 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:10:30-08:00","id":999645,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>5 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;So Pops, what's brings you to Chicago?&quot;</span>-Phoenix seems as surprised as him of finding each other in this situation-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Well... after I awakened I felt the need for a change of scenery, so I and Mel decided to came here, to Chicago. It went well at first. We settled, I found people that helped me make sense of all the unbeliebeable things I had experienced... It was just what I was looking for. Then the Deathstorm came... and took my wife with it&quot;</b></span><b>-</b>He falls silent, not really expecting any reaction from the young man, just stating facts.</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:40:52-08:00","id":999924,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> You have seen these faces before and, as an Arrow Sleepwalker retainer, had to quickly learn how to navigate the political climate of the Consilium. You are surprised to see Atlas' face among the Councilors for two reasons.<br /> <br /> First, until last week, he had been serving as Hierarch of this Consilium, a role usually filled by the same individual until their death except in unusual circumstances. The news you've heard has all been focused on how Cielo assumed the role of Hierarch; you didn't actually know what had happened to Atlas. Clearly, few mages in attendance of this meeting knew about this switch, either.<br /> <br /> Secondly, as far as you knew, the Obrimos Councilor position was already filled before Cielo became Hierarch by a female mage known as Prism. So what become of her?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Although you have never seen these individuals gathered here before, let alone any mages in this large of a gathering, you guess that certain social aspects of government likely apply to this group as well. You try to mentally sift through the information presented before you like a puzzle.<br /> <br /> You can tell from the hushed whispers spreading rapidly around the room that Atlas' position on this Council is surprising. You remember from Mathias' instruction on Tuesday that Cielo used political leverage to convince Atlas to step down from his position as Hierarch; you deduce that the crowd is primarily surprised to see that he hasn't stepped down very far in power. It raises questions for you about who the Councilor was in that position before, and how Atlas' relationships might be with the others on the stage.<br /> <br /> Estrella and Luna certainly share an obvious physical appearance with Cielo, but more than that, they are sitting near each other and watching her with approval. Similarly, Atlas is wearing very similar attire as the other two men, and they are also sitting with their chairs somewhat closer to each other. You wonder if Atlas and the two men are part of a similar faction or maybe even cabal, just as Cielo and the other two women might be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You can see that the male and female Councilors on the stage seem to be ignoring each other as best they can. Their body language is superficially calm, but you see that the men and women's chairs are faced slightly away from those of the opposite sex, and their faces have hints of frowns. There might as well be an invisible wall standing right through the middle of the stage where Cielo is standing. Very likely, there is a power struggle or disagreement of some kind between these two groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> You quickly realize that you are not in your element. You are initially intrigued by the comments and whispers around you, but there is so little to base your judgment on that you're not sure how to use this information. Is Atlas liked, or disliked? Are they just surprised to see the previous Hierarch remaining in a position of power, or is there more to it? The hidden political undercurrents in the room make you feel uneasy, especially knowing that you're going to be speaking in front of them soon. You know that putting the wrong foot forward can set you up for headaches or even disaster down the road.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take the Beat for the dramatic failure. You gain the following custom Condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Misinformed (Consilium).</b> You struggle to understand the social undercurrents in a particular group, identified at the time you gain this Condition. You take -2 on Social rolls and Social Maneuvering attempts involving members of the social group related to this Condition. Whenever the Storyteller asks you to roll for a Social action or Social Maneuvering attempt pertaining to this Condition, instead of rolling you may voluntarily fail the roll and resolve this Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution:</u> Opt to fail a Social action or Social Maneuvering attempt with someone in the identified group, as described above.<br /> <br /> <u>Beat:</u> N/A.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> As the Councilors and Hierarch approach, you take a moment to observe the room, taking a mental step back and really studying how everyone around you is acting.<br /> <br /> First, you notice that most of the people in the room really are wearing formal attire, or at least nicer clothing. However, there are still a sizeable number of mages in the room with more casual clothes; Boomer is wearing a different outfit from the other day, rocking stilettos and a studded black leather jacket, but she's definitely not in any suit or formalwear. Still, it's a nice jacket, and Mathias and Valentine are certainly wearing formal attire. That signals to you that, at least at Consilium meetings, appearances are important to most people. A few people have given you glances, but that seems to be because they don't know who you are.<br /> <br /> Second, you can tell from the body language of the Councilors that there is a clear rift between the men and the women. You overhear someone whisper, &quot;Surprised Atlas is up there...I bet Medianoche isn't happy about that.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> Cielo stands with her hands resting in fists at her hips as she waits for the room to quiet down and everyone to find their seats. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Welcome, everyone. Thank you for coming on short notice.&quot;</span> Her speech is crisply articulated at a smooth pace. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;We have had changes in the representation on this Council. Here are your Councilors.&quot;</span> She briefly motions to each of them in turn: Estrella, an Acanthus; Luna, a Moros; Apollo, a Mastigos; Atlas, an Obrimos; and Poseidon, a Thyrsus. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Prism, our previous Councilor representing the Path to the Aether,&quot;</span> she explains simply, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;was killed during the Deathstorm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> At Cielo's announcement, the room is shocked to silence.<br /> <br /> After a long pause, Cielo continues, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;This is likely the largest gathering we have seen in our Consilium in recent years, and perhaps one of our most important meetings. All who have been part of this society for more than a few weeks know that the Highstorms have been a Mystery explored by many for over a century. Casualties have always been a risk of these storms, but our Mystagogues have informed me that never before in this Consilium's recorded history have we lost so many in a single storm. And these from the Storm itself, not the Uratha or Kindred poachers or their servants in this city.&quot;</span> Various mages around you grumble at the mention of these terms, but most of you do not recognize the names.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;I have served for some time as the Adamant Sage of the local Arrow caucus. It was the decision of this Council that a change in leadership would be wise, to provide a more direct response to this event and the anticipated reactions it may have among supernatural beings in the city. I do not take this decision lightly.&quot;</span> Her face hardens. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;I vow to act decisively, to take action as needed, to protect this Consilium from any person, organization, or being that threatens our civilization. I assure you that any practice of Abyssal magic, soul reaping, or service to the Exarchs or Seers of the Throne will be met with swift justice using lethal force.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-08-2016, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:47:10-08:00","id":1000270,"title":"","content":"<b>Everyone</b><br /> Many of the mages in attendance of this meeting nod along at Cielo's words. A few shift uncomfortably in their chairs at the heat in her words; Cielo is probably more direct than Atlas was in this position.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;In respect of the dead, I call for a moment of silence for the mages who passed away during the Deathstorm.&quot;</span> The room settles into silence. Cielo fixes her gaze on the floor and takes several slow breaths.<br /> <br /> After a long pause, the Hierarch clasps her hands and rests them at her waist. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;We have to remain strong, despite these losses. We can't let fear dominate us or control us. Know that this Council will continue to serve you and protect you and your interests. We also will continue to strictly enforce our Consilium laws and mandates. As before, Valentine of the Shields of Dawn,&quot;</span> she motions to him in the crowd, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;and Yari of the Shadow Spears,&quot;</span> she points to a middle-aged Asian man sitting not far from the stage, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;will continue in their roles as Sentinels. They act with full support of this Council.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Cielo pauses and surveys the room. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Alright, let's not waste any time. We have several individuals who have business to discuss here today. Let's get to it,&quot;</span> she says curtly. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Melody?&quot;</span> Cielo motions to someone in the crowd and then takes a seat, crossing her arms.<br /> <br /> An African American woman who looks to be in her 30s stands up and makes her way to the center of the stage. Boomer leans over and whispers to you, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;That's Melody, a th\u00e9arch who serves as the Herald -- kind of like a spokesperson and ambassador for the Consilium.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.blackwomenswellnessday.org/resources/bw1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;Hello everyone,&quot;</span> Melody says with a wide smile. <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;With many of the unfortunate losses suffered during the Deathstorm, we've had a number of changes in our local cabals, many of whom requested the opportunity to update the Consilium on their membership changes. When I call your name, please stand and send a representative to the front to share your announcement...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> For the next several minutes, various cabals are called upon. Mages come forward and briefly share their updates. In some cases, a cabal remained and added one or two new members to replace those who were lost in the Deathstorm. For cabals that were hit particularly hard, leaving only one or two members surviving, some mages announce that they have formed an entirely new group with a new name. Melody offers each of them a warm smile, although her face is tinged with sadness as they describe their losses; she seems to wear her emotions on her sleeve.<br /> <br /> After each of the cabals have shared their announcement, Melody looks down at a list in her hands and frowns curiously. She looks up at Mathias and calls out, <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;The Council recognizes Mathias, who says he has an announcement he would also like to share.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias clenches his jaw but smoothly stands and walks at a steady pace to the stage. He smiles briefly to Melody and bows in respect to Cielo and the Council, then turns to face the audience. He takes a deep breath and slowly exhales before speaking. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Ladies and gentlemen of this Consilium, I stand before you today to make an announcement per conditions agreed upon as part of a Duel Arcane. As some of you know, Moonstone, previously a Sleepwalker and retainer to Hakim, Thunderbolt Guardian of the Adamantine Arrow, has newly Awakened.&quot;</span> Mathias points out into the crowd directly at Moonstone, and his gaze remains fixed on him for as long as he stands on the stage. The announcement of Moonstone's Awakening draws some murmurs amongst the crowd, and the mages assembled here turn to look at him.<br /> <br /> Mathias continues in a very even, neutral tone, in a way that is clearly rehearsed. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I hereby announce that Moonstone defeated me, fairly and per our rules of engagement, in the Duel Arcane.&quot;</span> The whispers swell in volume, and many mages' eyes widen in surprise. A few chuckle or openly grin at Mathias' loss, but he simply keeps talking over the crowd. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I hereby announce that the late Hakim was my better as a mage, and a man. I apologize for dishonoring his memory by assaulting his favored student and dear companion.&quot;</span> His words are nearly identical to Moonstone's exact wording of his terms.<br /> <br /> Mathias bows his head at Moonstone and promptly walks down from the stage. His face is stoic, but his gait is stiff and his eyes are glaring. He returns back to his seat amidst a buzz in the crowd as the audience members gossip with each other and look at Moonstone and Mathias, as well as the rest of you sitting next to the Shields of Dawn. Mathias folds his arms and says nothing, staring pointedly ahead at the center stage.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can roll Wits + Empathy or Intelligence + Politics again if you would like to read the room more or get a sense of how the crowd is responding to Mathias' announcement.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Melody's frown deepens as she stares at Mathias, and then at Moonstone. Cielo coughs to clear her throat, and Melody quickly schools her face to a neutral expression. <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;Thank you for your announcement,&quot;</span> she murmurs. She coughs and summons her best smile again. <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;That is an excellent segue to our final order of business. We have learned that there are several new mages here among us, newly Awakened to the Supernal realms. As Herald, on behalf of the Hierarch, this Council, and your Chicago Consilium, I welcome you to our society. When I call your name, please stand and briefly introduce yourself.&quot;</span> To the room, she adds, <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;Until such time that these mages have joined a cabal, received a formal mentor, or been inducted into one of our Orders, I ask for volunteers to temporarily mentor each of these individuals and instruct them on our Consilium laws.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You are each given an opportunity to introduce yourself in however you see fit. When you do, please make an Expression roll using an appropriate Attribute that reflects how you would like to present yourself (e.g., Presence + Expression to appear bold or make a personal statement, Intelligence + Expression to speak eloquently).</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:16:55-08:00","id":1000401,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar watches as Mathias completes the terms of his Duel with Moonstone and humiliate himself for Moonstone's satisfaction. He had known this was coming, but he hadn't processed what this had meant for Mathias. He resists turning his head to glare at Moonstone, and keeps his face neutral. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>The </i>arrogance. <i>The </i>hubris. <i>I hope you're pleased with yourself. </i></span>He doesn't know when, he doesn't know how, but Moonstone will pay for this. Hakim couldn't have been without his flaws. And he will make Moonstone admit those. Maybe not to the entire Consilium. But certainly to Mathias. <br /> <br /> The gazes of the entire Consilium on them makes Ragnar uncomfortable, and he realizes that, if he asks Mathias to be his mentor, that will bring the attention of the Consilium on him, too. He allows his eyes to evaluate the eyes of the Consilium. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Who is taking pleasure in this? Who sympathizes with Mathias?</i> </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Intelligence 4 + Politics 1 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454601\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#da70d6\">&quot;That is an excellent segue to our final order of business. We have learned that there are several new mages here among us, newly Awakened to the Supernal realms. As Herald, on behalf of the Hierarch, this Council, and your Chicago Consilium, I welcome you to our society. When I call your name, please stand and briefly introduce yourself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar stands and looks around at the Consilium.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Good afternoon. Thank you, Hierarch Cielo,&quot;</span>he nods politely towards her, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Councilors,&quot;</span>he nods to Estrella, Luna, Atlas, Apollo, and Poseidon, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Herald Melody,&quot;</span>he nods to her as well,<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;for welcoming my companions and I into your midst. I am Ragnar, Acanthus of the Lunargent Thorn of Arcadia. I am not native to Chicago, but I wish to make Chicago and this Consilium my home. With your permission, Hierarch, I have someone in mind for an instructor in the Arcane arts.&quot; </span>He glances at Mathias, before returning his gaze to Cielo. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;If he will have me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intelligence 4 + Expression 3 = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454606\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:19:55-08:00","id":1000403,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454605\" target=\"_blank\">Empathy roll to gauge room, Wits (3) + Empathy (3), for 6 dice \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lynx ponders what to say when his name is called out. He fails to register it at first, and is momentarily perplexed with all eyes on him.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh. Right. I have legs.</span></i><br /> <br /> He rises from his seat.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Um. Hello. I'm Lynx. I'm not the best at words... with words?</span>&quot; He pauses and rubs his beard as he glances at the room. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I Woke up last Saturday, so I'm new at magic. I was excited to meet others like me, though I've only met one Thyrsus, and with what I've seen this week... having seen this room...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He looks up at the ceiling.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm not sure I like this. The society, I mean. Your society. Within half a day of being introduced to this... Pentacle, I got to see an ugly side of it. A mistake happened, and there was a heated moment between two mages, only instead of talking about it with apologies or considerations, it became this stupid declaration of a duel, with statements of titles, and... and political status, and power, with rules that makes it seem like you're in the right only because you're strong. And it was made with terms that forced the loser to declare...<br /> <br /> Well. You all heard. Some laughed too. <br /> <br /> I guess there's some irony that a Thyrsus isn't impressed with... what's the term again? Social Darwinism? Might makes right?</span>&quot; Lynx closes his eyes and ponders for a moment.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Don't get all philosophical now, you dork.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't know if that is the norm. Fighting duels rather than talk, I mean. Declaring humiliation as punishment, laughing at the loser. I hope what happened between Mathias and Moonstone is the exception, not the rule. I wanted to see something wonderful, something terrific and... and <i>real</i> from this first encounter with the Pentacle, not... Not that mess.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm not impressed. Not with Tuesday. Not today either. Not yet, at least.</span>&quot; He opens his eyes and glances over the room with determination. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">But I want to know more. There <i>is</i> more to this room, this society, to all of you. I smell it in the air, hear it as you move and breathe. I <i>feel</i> it.<br /> <br /> I don't have to like everything you do. I'm not convinced yet. Maybe you won't care to try convince me, and that's fine. I'm happy to be here either way. Happy to live in this moment. Happy and eager to <i>learn</i>.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx inhales slowly, and searches the room, when...<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Raven,</span>&quot; he calls out, his eyes landing on the dark-haired woman. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">You're the only Thyrsus I've met so far, and so...I want you to be my mentor. It ... it feels right that it's you.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> And without waiting for a response, he nods to the room as a whole and sits down.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454608\" target=\"_blank\">Expression roll to introduce himself, Presence (3) + Expression (-1), for 2 dice \u2192 1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-10-2016, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:42:26-08:00","id":1000413,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;I vow to act decisively, to take action as needed, to protect this Consilium from any person, organization, or being that threatens our civilization. I assure you that any practice of Abyssal magic, soul reaping, or service to the Exarchs or Seers of the Throne will be met with swift justice using lethal force.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone winces.<br /> <br /> He's only halfway paying attention to the others. Apparently Phoenix knows Ouroboros Ophis too? At least he'll be easy to integrate.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;In respect of the dead, I call for a moment of silence for the mages who passed away during the Deathstorm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He folds his hands, closes his eyes, and blanks his mind. A few seconds of semi-silence in a public space, except for breaths and creaking and quiet sniffs. It's nice.<br /> <br /> He listens closely when the cabal membership rolls are updated, taking some clean shorthand notes on an index card to review later. You have to know these things to stay as tapped into Politics as he is.<br /> <br /> And then comes the good part. When the crowd hushes and whispers, he stands up to be recognized, and probably draws the attention of the Consilium to his fellow Nameless as well. Considering the circumstances, he couldn't have asked for a better introduction. He raises his hand to acknowledge Mathias' brief bow, and sits again once he returns. No need to twist the knife further now that he has something to springboard off of.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Int+Politics (Consilium): <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454602\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Outside, he's calm. Inside, he's practically manic with excitement and anxiety, but he holds it together through Melody's segue and the words of the other Nameless.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This seems like the kind of highly stressful and public situation that might prompt a roll to resist Divergent, if you'd like me to roll it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>. Also, will I get any bonus to the Expression roll from that introduction? I'll just roll Manipulation 2+Expression 2+Willpower 3 for now. 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454603\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He's remarkably collected and controlled and small when he speaks. It's lucky that the acoustics are so good in the room, or he might be too quiet to hear.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you, Melody. And thank you, Mathias. Our terms are fulfilled. I hope to be as gracious in victory as you were in defeat. As to the ethics of the Duel Arcane and our freely chosen terms...I know we are a Consilium that respects power, and those who are bold enough to claim it. Like Hakim. Like Cielo. That is all I will say on that matter.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Okay, he'll twist the knife a <i>little </i>bit. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I have stood here before, but never as an Awakened one. I was with you when the fairy-lights haunted Lake Michigan that fateful autumn. I stood, burning blade in hand, side by side with the warriors of the Arrow when the Noctuku rose from the sewers. I looked over my shoulder for the Mad One called the Origami Killer, and wept for </span><b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willis_Tower#Height\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">the loss of the Dark Tower.</span></a></b><span style=\"color:#008080\"> I saw the sky-filling Whale Bone Woman in the winter of 2010, and the falling angels the following spring. I know the Whipping Boys of Boystown and the House of Ariadne. I have endured Highstorms before. And now I have endured the Deathstorm with you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Deep breath. Hands trembling. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;But now my eyes are open, and only now I do see how far I was from the Truth.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In light of my experience, and all that he has given and continues to give me, I request that Hakim be considered my mentor until I join an Order or cabal. To do otherwise would be an insult to his memory. Thank you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He steps down from the podium and returns to his seat to let someone else speak.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No, Moonstone, you can't have a dead person as your mentor. Can I count that public request as indulging Naive?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:47:40-08:00","id":1000520,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>5/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>Misinformed (Consilium) | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>5 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I am going to Resolve Misinformed to auto fail the second roll to understand the room's reaction to Mathias statements</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Things are getting progresively more confusing. Ouroboros, perhaps too acustomed to be the smartest man on the room, is completly caught off guard by Mathias declaration and the subsequent reaction of the rest of the mages present. Is this something usual? Is this what passes for justice in this society or is this a travesty of their rules? He cannot tell and feels like threading on thin ice, suddenly thrown into a maze of byzantine rules he cannot comprehend. And just then comes his turn to introduce himself. Perfect timming indeed<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Introduction: Intelligence + Expression + Willpower= 9 dice =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454651\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes</a></div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> He takes a deep breath, and gets up, slowly but steadily walking to the front of the room:<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Hierarch Cielo, Councilors, Herald&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> He makes a gentle bow as a sign of respect when he adress them, before facing the room.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;The name I have chosen and lived by almost since my recent awakening is that of Ouroboros Ophis, the snake eating his own tail, a symbol of birth, death and resurrection. This is a cycle we all go through, not only each of us as individuals, but also us all as community, a society. We have left our birth behind. We have just sufered terrible losses and death, and today I hope we are beholding the rebirth of this Consilium. New groups have been formed from the disapperance of others. New mages like my companions and myself have finally shed the scales from our eyes and have awakened. I walk the path to Stygia, and as Moros I am specially aware of how death is but a step in a longer journey&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> He makes a pause.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;We all have lost friends, colleages and loved ones in this Deathstorm and I appreciate the gesture of our Hierarch to remind us of those that are no longer with us, but not only the awakened suffered. There were sleepers lost in the fray too. Poor souls still trapped in the Lie that now should wait for another cycle to escape the prision of the Exarchs. Let's not forget about them. Please, join me, if you want, in a moment of silence to remember those souls that were not given the chance that we had&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> He closes his eyes and holds his hands with his head slightly inclined for a moment, thinking of Melissa.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Thanks. That is all&quot;</b></span> <br /> <br /> After another gentle bow to adress the Herald, Councilors and the Hierarch, he sits down again in his place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T08:11:41-08:00","id":1000793,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Well... after I awakened I felt the need for a change of scenery, so I and Mel decided to came here, to Chicago. It went well at first. We settled, I found people that helped me make sense of all the unbeliebeable things I had experienced... It was just what I was looking for. Then the Deathstorm came... and took my wife with it&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Aww, that sucks,&quot;</span> I reply. Is the wizard world just filled with loss or something? This Deathstorm seems to have taken something away from everyone, except for me, that is. But that's only because a mage took what was important to me before it got the chance.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Ladies and gentlemen of this Consilium, I stand before you today to make an announcement per conditions agreed upon as part of a Duel Arcane. As some of you know, Moonstone, previously a Sleepwalker and retainer to Hakim, Thunderbolt Guardian of the Adamantine Arrow, has newly Awakened. I hereby announce that Moonstone defeated me, fairly and per our rules of engagement, in the Duel Arcane. I hereby announce that the late Hakim was my better as a mage, and a man. I apologize for dishonoring his memory by assaulting his favored student and dear companion.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Bet you're mighty satisfied, ain't you Moonstone?<br /> <br /> I look around the room for people reacting to Mathias's speech, gauging who his allies and enemies in the Consilium are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Making a Wits + Empathy roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454785\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Empathy 2 = 5 dice \u2192 2 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#da70d6\">&quot;That is an excellent segue to our final order of business. We have learned that there are several new mages here among us, newly Awakened to the Supernal realms. As Herald, on behalf of the Hierarch, this Council, and your Chicago Consilium, I welcome you to our society. When I call your name, please stand and briefly introduce yourself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Now it's my turn, public speaking time now. Just introduce yourself, you don't have to read your essay or anything.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hierarch Cielo, Councilers, Herald Melody,&quot;</span> I bow to each one I address individually, then I face the rest of the Consilium, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;My name is Phoenix, I walk the Path of Might. Much like many of you here, I too, am recovering from loss. Mine weren't taken by the Deathstorm, but I have lost them all the same.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I have to pause for a long sigh.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Because of this, I wish to join the Adamantine Arrow. I want to prevent such loss from happening again and let people pass in peaceful, less sudden ways. I hope I can be of service.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454800\" target=\"_blank\">Presence 3 + Expression 2 = 5 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> I'll make this a dramatic failure for a Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I sit back down as fast as I can without going into a jog. I made an ass of myself, didn't I? Yup, I did. I so did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:10:55-08:00","id":1000829,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 4 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>I am Ouroboros Ophis, Moros, and Nameless for the time being&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>Oh thank god another adult.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Do you know him too? Is it just me who doesn't?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I do not. I wonder if it's just chance that there are so many subtle threads connecting what will likely become our cabal?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF1493\">&quot;Falling Blossom is a Mastigos Mystagogue, but I don't know much about her. ... They're a cabal known as the Servants of Gaea. They formed their group around the Legacies of the Elemental Masteries. There are five standard Legacies, one for each Path.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder's ears perk up at this tidbit, but he doesn't say anything. Lynx was asking about them... he'll have to make an attempt to get to know Lynx better if it ends up that their mentors share a cabal. More threads binding the cabal together can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;I don't know if that is the norm. Fighting duels rather than talk, I mean. Declaring humiliation as penalty. Laughing at the loser. I hope what happened between Mathias and Moonstone is the exception, not the rule. I wanted to see something wonderful, something terrific and... and </span><i>real</i><span style=\"color:#800000\">, not... Not that mess.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder attempts to control his expression. He doesn't disagree, but... using your introduction to make such a searing political statement? He's not sure if it's actually the worst idea he's ever heard of or if Lynx is just <i>significantly </i>ballsier than him.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> When it's his turn to address the room, Binder nervously stands up. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Ah, hello. It's possible that some of you recognize me from the book store that I run downtown. Please call me Binder.&quot;</span> A short pause. <i>N</i><i>o, dammit, </i><i>I </i>am<i> Binder</i>, he admonishes himself. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I am a Mastigos. While it's a pleasure to be here and meet you all, you all have my condolences for your recent losses.&quot;</span> <i>Well, it was somewhat shorter than the others, but I can't think of anything else to say. </i><span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Thank you,&quot;</span> he finishes, and sits back down.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Composure 4 (to project a calm demeanor) + Expression -1 = 3 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454812\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. As tempting as it is, I'd rather not take a dramatic failure for my first impression with the Consilium.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T06:52:40-08:00","id":1001738,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> You focus your attention on the Council and Hierarch, hypothesizing that their reactions will tell you the most about the general attitudes in this room. Melody and Estrella, also a th\u00e9arch, show the most disapproval of Moonstone's requirements that Mathias publicly humiliate himself. Melody shows more emotion; she's trying to hide her deep frown, but she keeps shooting glares at Moonstone during the speech. Estrella is more calm and collected, but her eyes widen and her lips twitch into a frown. In contrast, Poseidon appears to be smirking and enjoying this; whether that's due to a personal grudge or reflection of the Guardians' stance, you can't say. Apollo and Atlas seem more amused than anything, and Luna seems generally disinterested; she's staring at her fingernails and slowly shaking her head. Cielo herself has her arms crossed and a perfectly calm expression on her face, but her gaze is fixed on Moonstone for nearly the entire duration of Mathias' speech.<br /> <br /> When you stand and speak, you find many mages nodding approvingly towards you. You're clearly making a good impression. The Hierarch and Council members each bow their head in return to you. You get the sense that your presentation is what they would expect or prefer from all newly Awakened mages at their first Consilium meeting. Mathias smiles warmly towards you.<br /> <br /> At your suggestion for Mathias to mentor you, Melody beams and replies, <span style=\"color:orchid\">&quot;Well, usually we ask for volunteers rather than making you pick your own choice. Most mages who come here haven't had the opportunity to learn much about our Consilium or meet many of our kind.&quot;</span> She smiles warmly at Mathias, clearly intending this as a compliment on his ability to find so many mages so shortly after their Awakening.<br /> <br /> Cielo waves a hand dismissively. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;True, but it's perfectly fine if they want to pick their own, as long as the mage they choose accepts the selection. Otherwise, we'll call for volunteers or appoint one.&quot;</span> She turns to you and adds, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Welcome to this Consilium, Ragnar. I expect that you will quickly learn our customs and laws.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias claps you on the shoulder and says, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;And it will be my privilege to support him in his endeavors. I accept this role, Hierarch.&quot;</span> Cielo nodds in approval.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You use your keen eyes and ears to study the room, focusing primarily on those closest to you. Boomer huffs under her breath and glares ahead at no one in particular, although you can clearly tell who her anger is directed towards. Valentine smiles secretively, but that smile fades to a neutral expression over the course of Mathias' announcement. Many of the mages around you seem surprised, but for different reasons. Half of them seem surprised and shocked that Mathias would lose a Duel to such a newly Awakened mage, suggesting that he is generally respected in this society; the other half seem more impressed, perhaps even awed, at Moonstone for being such a mage to win the Duel against a superior opponent.<br /> <br /> When you speak and share your genuine but critical assessment of the Consilium, everyone turns to focus on you. Several of the Councilors and mages standing around you frown. However, your words are well-spoken and delivered with honesty and good intentions, and for that reason you're able to share your thoughts without angering the entire Consilium.<br /> <br /> Cielo replies, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Welcome, Lynx. You speak from the heart, and I appreciate your sincerity. But I think what you're missing right now is a sensible appreciation for the very serious threat that arises when mages in conflict use spells rather than the Duel to settle their arguments. Magic <i>is</i> powerful, and in the wrong hands or used impulsively, it has the ability to tear apart the very fabric of this Fallen World and lay waste to everyone within it. I would much rather have a Duel used to settle a petty argument, or even a challenge to the death, if it means that no collateral damage to bystanders occurs or it prevents an all-out magical war between cabals. We are not lawless. I hope that you will come to value this Consilum and what it has to offer.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> At your suggestion for Raven to be your mentor, a number of mages seem surprised; based on what you know of her and what she's told you, they are most likely surprised that you've even met her, given how she tends to avoid political gatherings when possible. Raven smiles eagerly and says, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;It would be my pleasure to teach you about the Wild.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You find yourself growing giddy with excitement and energy as Mathias speaks. You're trying to stay calm and collected, as you know you're about to give a very important introduction as your first time in this Consilium as a mage, but the powerful emotions inside of you are threatening to throw off your balance.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes, I'd like you to roll Resolve + Composure for Divergent. If you fail, take a Beat as it becomes active for the remainder of this scene, giving you -2 on all social and Resolve rolls per the condition. That includes the one you made in your post, but it looks like it won't make a difference for that one. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You quickly assess the room as Mathias speaks, using your pre-existing knowledge of this Consilium to read the political pulse in this room. The Knights of Alhambra seem to strongly disapprove of your Duel terms, and at the mention of Hakim, Rose of Sharon sits up straight and sniffs. Ghost Dog and Askia shake their heads and frown at you. The other Arrows you know seem more neutral or even sympathetic to the message; after all, Hakim was a respected Thunderbolt Guardian.<br /> <br /> The Guardians seem to take the most pleasure in Mathias' public shaming, with many of them smirking or even snickering. In constrast, the th\u00e9archs in general are very upset with you and seem very much offended at how Mathias has been forced to shame himself this way. The Mystagogues and Libertines seem generally neutral or apathetic.<br /> <br /> When you stand and speak about past events that are familiar to this Consilium, you find many people nodding in approval at your words. You clearly know more about politics here than the average mage who has newly Awakened. But at your suggestion for Hakim to be your &quot;mentor&quot;, Cielo flatly replies, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;No. I am sorry for your loss, and Hakim was very much a respected member of the Adamantine Arrow. But he is no longer with us,&quot;</span> she explains bluntly. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Even though you clearly have knowledge of this Consilium, you will abide by its customs and laws the same as any newly Awakened mage among us. I've seen too many Sleepers or Sleepwalkers in service of an Order lose themselves to hubris and temptation upon Awakening. Until you are ready, you will have a mentor like all the others.&quot;</span> She turns to the crowd and asks, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Who will volunteer to be Moonstone's mentor for the time being?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There are whispers amongst the crowd as they discuss their thoughts and respond to your speech. Rose of Sharon shakes her head, and Askia looks away from you. None of the Arrows raise their hand. Then, you hear a familiar voice call out, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I volunteer for this role, Hierarch.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Cielo nods in approval. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Thank you, Valentine.&quot;</span> He looks at you with a small, knowing smile on his face.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You don't get any bonus to the Expression roll because it's a wash -- some are impressed and see you favorably from your speech, and others are very much mad at you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take a Beat for resolving the Condition.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You clearly have no idea what is going on here under the surface. It's a very frustrating experience, to be so far outside of your comfort zone. Thankfully, you're not a stranger to giving important speeches in front of groups of people, so you introduce yourself to the best of your ability. The crowd quickly nods along at your words with approval, and many people offer warm smiles to you.<br /> <br /> At your comment about Sleepers and others not yet Awakened also being harmed by the Deathstorm, Apollo nods and murmurs in agreement. Dante and the group of mages he walked in with, assumedly his cabalmates, all nod enthusiastically and grin at you. Clearly, the Libertines share your perspective. In contrast, Luna shrugs and Atlas briefly rolls his eyes with a smirk, and Estrella seems perhaps annoyed that you use your introduction to call the Consilium to a moment of silence. No one talks during it, though.<br /> <br /> When you don't specifically request a mentor, Cielo calls out for volunteers to aid you at least temporarily until you join an Order or cabal. Dante quickly raises his hand and says, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;I would like to help, Hierarch.&quot;</span> He smiles at you as Cielo nods.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You watch Moonstone specifically and his reactions, and follow his eyes to see whom he is focusing his attention on. You see three people sitting together who look to be strongly dissatisfied with him, including a woman who briefly approached Moonstone before the Consilium meeting began. You can tell that many people are more generally impressed that he beat Mathias, who was apparently well respected here, but if you had to put money on it, the th\u00e9archs in the room are the most upset with Moonstone right now.<br /> <br /> Compared to the others who have spoken, your words are brief, blunt, and not very engaging. Most people don't even seem to be paying attention to you, focusing instead of Moonstone and Mathias still. Cielo replies curtly, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Welcome, Phoenix. The Arrow have their own initiation process you'll need to pass if you want to join, but you're welcome to try.&quot; </span>To the audience, she asks, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;This one needs a mentor, too.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Boomer raises her hand. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;I will vouch for this one, Hierarch.&quot;</span> She offers you an apologetic look and adds to you privately, <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Don't worry about them, it's just politics. You'll do great.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take the Misinformed (Consilium) condition as well, presented earlier this scene, and take a Beat for the dramatic failure.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> You stand and introduce yourself, and a few people smile at you whose faces seem vaguely familiar. How many people have visited your bookstore in La Grange, anyway? Is it coincidence, fate, or something else? When you try to talk, however, your words are brief and not particularly engaging. A few people nod at you, but ultimately they don't seem particularly interested overall. After the commotion at the meeting so far, and with so many other Nameless mages speaking before you, you get the impression that your words were forgettable.<br /> <br /> Because you also do not mention a request for a specific mentor, Cielo again calls out for volunteers. This time, there are several mages who quickly go to respond. Valentine opens his mouth, but Falling Blossom is the first to speak. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I will, Hiearch,&quot;</span> she speaks in crisp tones, carrying over the crowd. She smiles at you. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I will ensure that he learns the ins and outs of this Consilium quickly.&quot;</span> Cielo nods.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> Cielo stands and says, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;That is all on our agenda for today. I called for this meeting to ensure that we all move forward, united together as a society despite threats of fear or uncertainty. Any further announcements that we must pass between now and our next regularly scheduled meeting will passed along through our regular channels. In the meantime, you are welcome to contact members of this Council at any Consilum sanctum as usual. Does anyone have any other questions?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Giving everyone one more opportunity to get anything else out of this meeting that they wanted, or respond to this post, before we move on.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Added more for Phoenix's post. 11-11-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T16:58:01-08:00","id":1001984,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar rises from his seat. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Um... forgive me, Hierarch. But I have a... hypothesis about the Death Storm. Well, Moonstone and I. We wondered whether or not the Supernal symbol for storms itself in Chicago has been tainted by the Abyss. During Tuesday's High Storm, several of us noticed that the hail seemed to be... tainted. Perhaps even by the Abyss. Spirits were feeding on it. Has any mage who has Forces as a Ruling Arcana examined a High Storm with their Active Sight recently?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T18:04:49-08:00","id":1002021,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b><br /> </div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Resisting Divergent. Resolve+Composure-2 from Guilty: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455384\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He felt very small and unsteady as he took the podium, but once he started speaking, everything solidified again.<br /> <br /> The muted reactions to his victory, especially among the Knights, struck a discordant note in his mind. He won. He defended Hakim's honor! This isn't how it's supposed to be. Why isn't it like it's supposed to be?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;I've seen too many Sleepers or Sleepwalkers in service of an Order lose themselves to hubris and temptation upon Awakening. Until you are ready, you will have a mentor like all the others.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> But...what? No. No, no. That can't be right. This isn't hubris. He's doing what Hakim would have wanted. This is how mages are supposed to act. Why isn't everyone cheering?<br /> <br /> He's very obviously confused and unsteady when he walks back to his seat with the others. His ears are burning with embarrassment. He needs to talk to Valentine as soon as possible, not to mention the others.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Ragnar speaks up about their shared theory. He'd almost forgotten about this past week. The name flashes in his mind again: <i>the Destroyer. </i>But he doesn't know enough about that yet to say anything useful. He'll keep his Obsession close to his chest for now.<br /> <br /> He does stand up on wavering legs to support Ragnar. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Uh- yes. Seconded. I had Paradox in my Pattern during the storm, and the hailstones sapped my Mana. No one else with us experienced the same effect. How could the Consilium investigate this hypothesis further? Perhaps by questioning a Seraph?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T07:35:39-08:00","id":1002522,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I hope so too, Cielo.</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>I think you misunderstood what I meant...</i></span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx does smile when Raven accepts his request, and he sits down to observe the others, their introductions, the response and reactions. What stands out to him is Moonstone, whose reaction is pitiable; he watches the man carefully while rubbing his beard.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Um... forgive me, Hierarch. But I have a... hypothesis about the Death Storm. Well, Moonstone and I. We wondered whether or not the Supernal symbol for storms itself in Chicago has been tainted by the Abyss. During Tuesday's High Storm, several of us noticed that the hail seemed to be... tainted. Perhaps even by the Abyss. Spirits were feeding on it. Has any mage who has Forces as a Ruling Arcana examined a High Storm with their Active Sight recently?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Uh- yes. Seconded. I had Paradox in my Pattern during the storm, and the hailstones sapped my Mana. No one else with us experienced the same effect. How could the Consilium investigate this hypothesis further? Perhaps by questioning a Seraph?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Aaaand I'm lost. Dumb dog I am.</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx sighs to himself, glancing at Binder. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Our mentors are in the same cabal... He's probably smarter than me, so hopefully he can help me if... no, when I need help. He seems like a good guy, at least.</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:10:36-08:00","id":1002685,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> Your question, to your surprise, initially draws a reaction of unexpected laughter. Atlas smirks, and Poseidon and Apollo share a look and chuckle. Poseidon replies, <span style=\"color:Darkblue\">&quot;A hundred years of Highstorms, and you think we haven't thought to look upon them with Sight?&quot;</span> Another wave of laughter spreads through the audience.<br /> <br /> When you mention the tainted hail, and spirits feeding on it, the laughter dies off and the grin slips off Poseidon's face. A heavy silence fills the room.<br /> <br /> Cielo's voice fills the room. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;Thank you for this information. There are many mages who have studied the Mystery of these Highstorms, but there is always more we might be able to learn.&quot;</span> She sounds...uncertain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> As soon as you mention that you were in the Storm with Paradox infused in your Pattern, Cielo's eyes narrow. <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;The Council will take whatever appropriate steps are necessary to investigate the Highstorms. Even the Angels have limits to the knowledge they are able, or at least willing, to divulge about these Storms.&quot; </span>Cielo's eyes flicker between you and Ragnar as she studies you, but she says nothing more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Raven appears intently focused on Ragnar and Moonstone while they ask their question about the Storms, a curious expression fixed on her face. She catches your eye and smiles slyly, winking at you. You wonder what kind of mentor she might be, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-13-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:57:17-08:00","id":1002702,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;For the benefit of our newly Awakened mages, could an official briefly state the requirements for mages to form a new cabal with Consilium recognition?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:24:39-08:00","id":1002923,"title":"","content":"<b>Everyone</b><br /> Cielo nods and motions to Estrella, who smiles and stands before addressing you and the other Nameless in a clear, crisp voice. <span style=\"color:goldenrod\">&quot;The official requirements are quite simple: After you agree as a group on your list of members, you must agree upon a group name, and present yourselves as a group at a Consilium meeting or to the Herald or other Council member. Although not a formal requirement, you are also expected to mutually establish and swear oaths to a creed for your new cabal. This creed can and should include your cabal's mission, and serves to join your loyalties and create a shared vision for its members. You are not required to present your creed to the Consilium, but many cabals here have done so; the Silver Ladder keeps these on public record and can use them to settle disputes in certain cases.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Hierarch nods to Estrella and turns her gaze back to the audience. After allowing time for final questions, she claps her hands and announces, <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;This meeting is adjourned. We will return to our usual schedule on the first Saturday of each month at noon. That makes our next meeting on October 1, unless a special meeting is called. Remember that any spell casting on Consilium sanctum grounds is expressly forbidden. You are dismissed.&quot;</span> Cielo's gaze lingers on you all, as do several of the Councilors, before she and the Council members stand and walk off the stage. The Councilors quickly split into two separate groups based on their cabals and leave the room in separate directions.<br /> <br /> Mathias nods, and Boomer shakes her head with a smirk. <span style=\"color:deeppink\">&quot;Well, at least that wasn't a total waste of time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mathias smiles, but it fades again when he looks to Moonstone. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I have met your terms,&quot;</span> he says in an even tone. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Our business is finished.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Many of the mages leave the chamber over the next few minutes, heading upstairs and back to the church lobby. Some linger to talk to each other about the information shared at the meeting, or assumedly to discuss cabal issues. Several others approach you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar and Phoenix</b><br /> Mathias and Boomer meet with you respectively and arrange for meetings this week that fit your schedules. Boomer tells Phoenix to meet at dawn tomorrow, at an address she gives you on a slip of paper, while Mathias offers a few choices for when he might be available to see Ragnar in the next few days. However, they both suggest that you take some time to meet privately with the other Nameless mages you've been meeting with to discuss how you feel about joining a cabal.<br /> <br /> If you wander upstairs to investigate the sanctuary, there is currently no service in session, giving you freedom to explore the sanctuary further if desired.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx and Binder</b><br /> After the Consilium meeting, Falling Blossom and Raven approach both of you. Raven smiles and places a hand on Lynx's shoulder. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I am <i>very </i>much looking forward to mentoring you, little cub,&quot;</span> she smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Meet me again tonight in the woods, shortly after dusk.&quot;</span> She introduces herself to Binder with a broad smile.<br /> <br /> Falling Blossom smiles at her cabalmate and turns her attention to Binder. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I hope you do not mind my offer to mentor you,&quot;</span> she says. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I truly believe I and my colleagues with the Mysterium can be of great assistance to you. I cannot exaggerate the depth and breadth of knowledge we have stored.&quot;</span> She adds to both of you, <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;It seems that both of you are interested in learning about the Mysterium. What do you wish to know?&quot;</span> she asks. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Or would you prefer to meet privately and discuss these matters later? We do want to give you and your companions an opportunity to discuss your cabal. Cabals are a critical unit in our society.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> Several mages try to quickly approach you after the meeting. A few linger as they walk by just to observe you, without saying who they are or why they might be interested in you. A few people shake your hand and congratulate you on your victory against Mathias, and ask you details about the Duel Arcane and how you won (&quot;You have to tell us your technique!&quot;).<br /> <br /> Your would-be admirers look behind you and see Valentine, who is also walking up to you, and they suddenly move to leave. Apparently they feel nervous around a Sentinel, or perhaps Valentine has a different reputation you're not aware of.<br /> <br /> Before he can say anything, however, the Knights of Alhambra walk up to you. Rose of Sharon nods to you in greeting, but she jumps straight into business. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;Well met, Moonstone. So. You wish to discuss a favor among the Adamantine Arrow? There is a very well respected Arrow and old friend of mine, a Mastigos by the name of Spade, who is a Mind Adept. Although I cannot guarantee it, he may be willing to assist you. What do you require?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante's cabal leaves and heads up the stairs, but he says something to them and heads over to you instead of leaving. He smiles and claps you on the shoulder. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;I look forward to providing more support. I hope that I can be of aid to you, friend. Shall we discuss when and where to meet? I can check my schedule and see what we can do.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:51:49-08:00","id":1003018,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;I have met your terms,&quot;</span> says Mathias. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Our business is finished.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone opens his palms in a gesture of peace. Not even a Nicki track to back him up. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;As you say.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> When they have a few seconds with just the Nameless, he suggests to everyone: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Don't stray too far after this. Let's talk somewhere calm, while we're all here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The church isn't exactly in an arts district. The nearest thing to a cafe in this neighborhood is a certain donut-based fast food chain. But hey, that's where people do business in Chicago.<br /> <br /> He's swept away by his adoring fans before he can say more. It's another rush of nervous excitement, but he tries to ride the wave like he did on the podium. Shaking hands, bowing with a flourish, animatedly pointing and gesturing and showing off his fluid movements, blushing crimson. Rather Naively, he prattles on and on and tells the crowd a great deal about his dueling technique:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Of course I had seen the Duel Arcane many times before, which may have given me an edge, but I never imagined how it would <i>feel!</i> We think of it like physical combat, but that traps your creativity- I realized that it was a contest of mind and spirit- lowercase, not the Arcana, haha, although I <i>did </i>make use of Mind, among other Arcana- he relied exclusively on Fate, thinking his strongest Arcanum was all he needed. Another trap! Instead of <i>fighting</i> him, I <i>danced!</i> He insisted on a show of force, a boulder of sealed Fate rolling down a mountain, expecting me to raise a shield and be crushed- but the <i>canny</i> magician simply steals the boulder's momentum and redefines the conflict without ever donning armor! I knew that if I just kept him on the attack, my will could endure anything he threw at me while I gave <i>him</i> the so-called 'death of a thousand cuts,' and furthermore I knew- a little birdy told me- that he was too proud to take me seriously, and so I carefully worded my challenge and my terms to infuriate him into a blind offense. Can you believe that <i>he </i>wanted to teach <i>me </i>humility? <i>Ha!</i> Pride before the fall, as they say. It was a victory of the soft and cunning and poison-lipped over the bull-headed and proud- there you go, tire yourself out striking empty air, then <i>charge</i> right into the labyrinth of mirrors I've conjured for you! Aion knows I couldn't throw a fireball or sprout claws for the life of me, but there are so many ways to outwit and out-Will someone without laying a finger on them. Do you have any idea how many years I spent watching <i>every move</i> my master made, imagining <i>every possible thing</i> I could do with the Arcana if I had a chance? And then to see him laid low by the truth-force of my Awakened soul after he had the <i>temerity </i>to strike me, thinking me his lesser, after I saved his life no less- well, I'm not one to brag, but...&quot;</div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> They scatter. He looks over his shoulder, and the hair on the back of his neck stands up. Valentine casts a long shadow. Luckily(?) the Knights step in first, and immediately get to business. He clasps his hands for a nervous but warm-hearted greeting. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Rose- Askia- Ghost- it's, um, wonderful to see you again. I'll just get right to it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He briefly relates Tuesday's events, emphasizing that he doesn't know exactly what happened in the portal, only that he and Phoenix came back with a Gulmoth in tow. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;...and since then, I can't stop thinking about that <i>thing. </i>What it did to us- it showed me my worst moments in a mirror, it paralyzed us with fear, it would have killed people if Phoenix and I didn't stop it. I've, um...dreamed about it. Every night this week. It isn't magic or a curse, I don't think, but the trauma has a hold on my Mind. And when the others and I face this thing again and banish it for good, I can't let that trauma be a weakness. I want to make it a weapon instead.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I want to take the power my nightmare has over me and use it against the real thing. I'm done being imprisoned by my fear. I want to draw it out and make it serve me. And if Spade can help me with that, I want to at least make my case to him.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He forces himself to say a little more in a lower voice, thinking of his conversation with Ace. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Listen. This has been...so, so hard. It's too much, every day. I'm not going to ask you to- I mean- I made my choice when I left with him. We know. The Knights don't owe me anything.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His fingers are tied together tight. He's keenly aware of Valentine just over his shoulder. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm proud of my victory over Mathias. But I feel like I'm not acting right lately. I won't worry you with the details. The Awakening didn't, um, get rid of my personality stuff, in case you were wondering. But I see it more clearly. And I- you know- obviously, I can't um, rely on him anymore. It's just me now. And maybe the Nameless, but they can't become a new thing to depend on. I <i>need</i> help, so I can get better. For him. And I don't think Sleeping medicine will help- I would have to lie about so, so much. But maybe Oneiros magic will work. Ace told me there are Mind mages who specialize in mental health...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...I'm trying to ask you whether Spade is safe. Is he someone I can talk to, or will I have to keep it to magic?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:50:46-08:00","id":1003084,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Just give me and Phoenix a minute.&quot; </span>Ragnar leads Phoenix into the sanctuary upstairs. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Okay. Before the Consilium meeting, I took a peek in here. I've been wanting to take a look at some Sleeper houses of worship for a while. I saw... chains of Fate. But nobody should have been casting spells in here if it's Consilium property, right? Take a look around with your Sight.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Ragnar steps further into the church and activates his Sight. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;What do you See?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:38:12-08:00","id":1003340,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Active Sight:</b> Prime, Forces | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Misinformed (Consilium) | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:orangered\">&quot;This meeting is adjourned. We will return to our usual schedule on the first Saturday of each month at noon. That makes our next meeting on October 1, unless a special meeting is called. Remember that any spell casting on Consilium sanctum grounds is expressly forbidden. You are dismissed.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Now with that outta the way, let's see if I can find the Death mage that ran the other day.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He'll try to see if he can find the mage he met earlier in the week in the crowd.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456319\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Composure 2 = 5 dice \u2192 3 successes</a><br /> <br /> He'll ask other Consilium members, including the other PCs and Shields of Dawn, about the mage, such as his name and what cabal he's in, using the photo from the phone to help. I'm not exactly sure if this needs a roll or not, and if it does, I'm not sure what to roll for it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Ragnar leads me upstairs to the main room. What's so special about this place? Guess he'll explain. One part watches the door we exited from, keeping watch for the Death mage exiting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Okay. Before the Consilium meeting, I took a peek in here. I've been wanting to take a look at some Sleeper houses of worship for a while. I saw... chains of Fate. But nobody should have been casting spells in here if it's Consilium property, right? Take a look around with your Sight.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Alright,&quot;</span> I follow, the gaudy walls shatter like glass as the real heaven reveals itself. Let's look for that spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 11-17-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:53:56-08:00","id":1003546,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> The small crowd drinks in the details, captivated by your story, until Valentine and the Knights of Alhambra arrive. Most of them are mages that you know have Awakened in the past few weeks to months, because you vaguely recognize them -- most have been recently introduced to the Consilium over the past few meetings. Your tale of besting an Adept at the Duel Arcane, especially a mage with apparently a lofty reputation, has them envious of your skill.<br /> <br /> As you describe your situation to the Knights of Alhambra, Rose of Sharon's jaw initially clenches with disapproval, and Askia shakes his head at you. However, as you continue to speak and candidly share your concerns and flaws, Rose of Sharon's face softens...a little bit. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;Your efforts to conquer your fear and this Gulmoth are admirable. Na\u00efve, perhaps, but admirable.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She sighs softly. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;Spade has the requisite skill with Mind to assist you with harnessing a goetic familiar. On behalf of his respect for Hakim and the Adamantine Arrow, I believe he will provide this service. And I know he has had interest in the past on using the Astral Realms to help others conquer their demons, quite literally. I do know his cabal, <b>52</b>, is a bit...strange at times,&quot;</span> she frowns. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;They're all a bit odd. I must withhold judgment on whether he is 'safe', because I do not know what that means to you. I believe he is trustworthy and has pure motives, if that helps.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> You've heard of 52 before. It's a cabal made up of four mages, each with a Shadow Name taken after a suit of cards: Spade, Heart, Diamond, and Club. You've mostly just heard gossip from other Arrows, but they might be a bit crazy and...unpredictable. You've heard Spade is a nice guy. A bit eccentric, but nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You were looking through the crowd for that weird mage during the Consilium meeting, and you continue to search for him now. You have keen eyes, and you quickly search through the audience -- this was your M.O. as a Hunter, after all. But despite the scanning and searching, you never see anyone that fits your memory of the mage who vanished after you approached him.<br /> <br /> You pull out your phone and show it around to the other people you know here at the meeting, including Boomer and the other Shields of Dawn. None of the Nameless mages or your other associates here recognize him. Mathias in particular seems unsettled by his difficulty to recognize the man. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You remember how quickly you came across other Pentacle mages after your Awakening, correct? <i>All</i> of us search to find those who have Awakened, and introduce them to our society,&quot;</span> he explains. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;But I have no idea who this man is. I don't recognize him, and I haven't heard of anyone else who has seen a new mage recently Awakened who might fit his description. Either he is very newly Awakened, or he has deliberately avoided contact with the Orders. Odd.&quot;</span> He frowns.<br /> <br /> When you go into the sanctuary of the church and open your Sight, you see electricity coursing through wires within the walls, powering the building's lights and air conditioning. But what draws your attention the most is the presence of a spell surrounding the entire sanctuary. Whereas Ragnar apparently saw this phenomenon as chains of Fate, you see Supernal energy pulsing all around this space. With effort, you might be able to glean more from the magical effect, but this Mystery appears complex at its surface.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may attempt Revelation and/or Scrutiny with Opacity 4.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Added updated info for Phoenix's actions. Nothing added for Ragnar because no specific action seemed needed from ST. 11-17-2016, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:07:03-08:00","id":1003588,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It helps. Thank you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's better than nothing. Even if this 52 cabal isn't exactly...playing with a full deck? Oh, Moonstone, you <i>card. </i>What will you think of next?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;<i>snrk-</i> I'm not laughing at you, sorry, I was just, um, thinking about something funny.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Warlock is giggling. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Because of their name. The whole- the cards thing they do.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Dead air.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;That's fun. So! How can I reach Spade? Is his cabal here?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Things on the immediate agenda: make a time with Spade to do this thing, preferably before Alux returns on the 17th. And probably talk to Valentine first, since he's waiting so patiently.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:22:48-08:00","id":1003981,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 4 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After the Consilium meeting, Falling Blossom and Raven approach both of you. Raven smiles and places a hand on Lynx's shoulder. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I am <i>very </i>much looking forward to mentoring you, little cub,&quot;</span> she smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Meet me again tonight in the woods, shortly after dusk.&quot;</span> She introduces herself to Binder with a broad smile. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;It's a pleasure to meet you, Raven.&quot;</span> Turning to Lynx, <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;it looks like our paths are aligned, despite the discrepancy in our <i>Paths</i>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Falling Blossom smiles at her cabalmate and turns her attention to Binder. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I hope you do not mind my offer to mentor you,&quot;</span>she says. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I truly believe I and my colleagues with the Mysterium can be of great assistance to you. I cannot exaggerate the depth and breadth of knowledge we have stored.&quot;</span> She adds to both of you, <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;It seems that both of you are interested in learning about the Mysterium. What do you wish to know?&quot;</span> she asks. <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\">&quot;Or would you prefer to meet privately and discuss these matters later? We do want to give you and your companions an opportunity to discuss your cabal. Cabals are a critical unit in our society.&quot;</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I don't mind at all! The only reason I didn't speak up like the others did was because I didn't want to presume. Regarding the Mysterium, how exactly are your repository of knowledge stored and accessed? I'm also curious about the process of joining, though I understand if it's a little early to talk about that.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:35:40-08:00","id":1004636,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Focused Sight:</b> Prime [going to Peripheral at end of post] | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Misinformed [Consilium] | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;There's definitely a spell here,&quot;</span> I whisper, careful for any Sleepers not to overhear, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;But it's heavily occluded. I don't know if I can get anything out of it, but I'll try.&quot;</span> Let's just get this over with, I don't have time for any stupid little spells.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Starting with a Revelation roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/457019\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosis 1 + Prime 2 - Opacity 4 = Chance die \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Opting to make this a dramatic failure for a Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why am I looking at this? I shouldn't be here. I need to meet up with the other Hunters. Those thoughts bubbled up into my Sight itself, muddling the spell into an indecipherable mess. Dammit, I can't look at this even if I did have the time. I give a hasty <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Sorry.&quot;</span> before leaving in frustration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:59:16-08:00","id":1004726,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 (4/5 at the end of Downtime). Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I am <i>very </i>much looking forward to mentoring you, little cub,&quot;</span> she smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Meet me again tonight in the woods, shortly after dusk.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;It looks like our paths are aligned, despite the discrepancy in our <i>Paths</i>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Yes, looks like it,</span>&quot; Lynx grins. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm looking forward to getting to know you more. It's good to know I'll not be alone in being new.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;It seems that both of you are interested in learning about the Mysterium. What do you wish to know?&quot;</span> she asks. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Or would you prefer to meet privately and discuss these matters later? We do want to give you and your companions an opportunity to discuss your cabal. Cabals are a critical unit in our society.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Actually... I was wondering if you knew any Thyrsus...es? Thyrsi? What is the bloody plural here anyway?</span>&quot; He grumbles and sighs. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I want to learn, I really do, only I don't understand this Pentacle yet. I want to know the points of view from a Thyrsus from each Order. I want a greater understanding of the picture here, politically, philosophically, from others that know the Wild.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx rubs his beard and looks at the two Mystagogues. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I do feel like I'm a cub. I don't understand half of what was mentioned here today... Seraph and Hierarchs and...</span>&quot; He sighs again. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Rambling, sorry. I'll meet you in the woods tonight, but I'd be really happy if I could talk to some other Thyrsus...es from the other Orders too.</span>&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T06:36:18-08:00","id":1005329,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Active (Fate)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> A certain part of Ragnar seethes at Phoenix's clumsiness, but he quickly quells it. He himself increased the Opacity of the Mystery in his own apartment building. He has no room to chide or look down on Phoenix. He returns to the others. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well that could have gone better.&quot; </span>He smiles sheepishly at his own failure and suggests tomorrow evening as a possible meeting time to Mathias for their first lesson. He agrees with Moonstone's suggested meeting place. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;That should do nicely.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:41:04-08:00","id":1005813,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div><br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>6 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;I look forward to providing more support. I hope that I can be of aid to you, friend. Shall we discuss when and where to meet? I can check my schedule and see what we can do.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>-&quot;Except for my classes at the University I am free to meet with you whenever you consider oportune, Dante. You have been really suportive in these last few days. I hoped I could respond to you and yours in kind, if you give me the opportunity&quot;</b></span>-they shake hands and Dante leaves to catch his cabalmates.<br /> <br /> The older Moros then turns to look for the other recent awakenings. He cannot shake the feeling that all this event should have been more significant for him, but is still getting acustomed to all these new protocols and it shows. Hopefully forming a cabal with other mages as inexperienced as him (including, surprisingly enough, Garrick, or should it be Phoenix?) will help him get up to date at a manageable pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-20-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:00:14-08:00","id":1006173,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Rose of Sharon's face hardens again, and she clearly resists the urge to roll her eyes at your sense of humor. Askia makes no such effort to hide his irritation, and Ghost Dog just continues to stare at you blankly.<br /> <br /> Rose of Sharon looks around the room and shakes her head. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;I thought I saw him earlier, but he appears to have left already. I will contact him directly and appeal to him at your request, out of respect for Hakim.&quot;</span> She looks behind you at Valentine and then adds, <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;It seems your mentor would like a word with you. But I wanted to ask...Do you still have interest in serving the Adamantine Arrow? You would need to go through the proper initiation testing, as is only proper. You know of our mission and principles. With your new perspective of the Supernal Realms, and your previous knowledge of the Order, you certainly could be a boon.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Feel free to continue this conversation if desired, Valentine would wait until the Knights are done with you before approaching you. Just wanted to add the next part to keep the scene moving.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After you finish your conversation, the Knights of Alhambra say their goodbyes, and Valentine approaches you as they leave. He looks after them and comments, <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;They are very well respected in this community for their wisdom and contributions to the Adamantine Arrow.&quot;</span> Valentine turns to face you. He has a slight frown, and his eyes sharply focus on you. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Until you no longer require supervision, I will be overseeing your introduction to this Consilium. I know that you have a great deal of knowledge about Awakened society and magic. Honestly, you might know even more about certain aspects of magic than I do in some domains because of your tenure with the Arrows,&quot;</span> he admits in a self-deprecating way. He smiles warmly. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;But I do want to make sure you learn everything you need to survive in this world. And perhaps, if you're open to it, I might even be able to show you a few things along the way. I might have a little more...finesse in some ways than the Knights. It's part of the reason Cielo placed me in this position.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine gently claps you on each of your shoulders. He exhales slowly. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The truth of the matter, Moonstone, is that magic is incredibly powerful -- but also can be incredibly dangerous, at least in the wrong hands or when used inappropriately. The Guardians exist to safeguard the world and each other from such dangerous uses of magic. Even the Arrows respect us for that,&quot;</span> he smiles. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I think you know that. I think you can appreciate how important that mission is. And I even think it might appeal to you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Valentine looks around, then leans forward and gives you a small slip of paper. His voice becomes a whisper. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;This is my personal cell phone. I would like you to keep this private between us. I don't usually give out number except in special circumstances. Don't share it with anyone. But if you need to reach me, you may use it.&quot;</span> He leans back and speaks at his normal volume again. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Now, I would like to meet you tomorrow, perhaps over lunch? Call me and we can arrange a meeting location. Until then, I encourage you to speak with your new associates and discuss your thoughts about forming a cabal.&quot;</span> He inclines his head and gives you an opportunity to ask any further questions before leaving.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Falling Blossom smiles in reply. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Well, I am glad you are receptive to the pairing. It need not be permanent, as Cielo noted, just long enough for you to learn the ins and outs of our society. But as a member of the Mysterium, I can also guide you through the initiation process and answer your questions as I am able, to help further your Supernal advancement into the ways of knowledge and truth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> In response to your question, Falling Blossom nods and begins to take on a practiced instructive tone as she speaks. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;Excellent question. We Mystagogues have various centers and repositories of tomes, grimoires, and Artifacts all around the globe. These places are called Athenaea, essentially Supernal libraries and storehouses. We can take you both to one this week and introduce you to some of our other members, should you be interested.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> When you mention initiation, Falling Blossom's smile deepens and her tone sounds eager. She seems to enjoy recruiting new mages to her Order. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;I am so glad to hear that you are interested. The Mysterium is dedicated to the important task, a critical one, of collecting and safeguarding knowledge. As long as that interests you, I would be glad to serve as your formal mentor.&quot;</span> Her voice takes on a serious tone. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;The Mysterium utilizes a very traditional mentor-apprentice bond. By our customs, I am required to teach you a basic understanding about Awakened society, but also magical theory, High Speech, and how to cast rote spells. I am also held responsible for your criminal actions, if you take any,&quot;</span> she notes with a very serious frown. Her tone clearly indicates that she expects there not to be any problems.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;In exchange, you are expected to freely share any special or esoteric Supernal knowledge with me that you encounter or obtain, and assist me with my own studies and interests. I will have various tasks I need you to do for me periodically. As for actual initiation, we can discuss that more at an Athenaeum. I'm confident the process will not be too taxing on you, Binder,&quot;</span> Falling Blossom waves a hand dismissively. <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;There are some whom we worry about because they are too eager, too impatient to use our knowledge unwisely. Such misuse would risk a great deal of danger for many. But I don't think you're like that, are you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> The Fallen World fades to a whisper around you even as the Supernal magic in this room grows to a vibrant crescendo to your eyes and ears. Through the lens of the Prime Arcanum, the spell before you hums with powerful energy. The holy fire of the Aether shines in your eyes as you gaze into the spell. But you're distracted, and without your focus, you find yourself staring so intently that the supernatural light of the spell burns your Sight. The Truth of this Mystery not only eludes you, but it blinds you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take an Arcane Beat for the optional dramatic failure. You also gain the following custom Condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Blindness.</b> Like a blind spot from staring too close to the sun, your intense gaze upon a Mystery has temporarily harmed your Sight. You must spend a Willpower point to enter your active Mage Sight, even for the first time you use it per scene; you may then maintain it for the remainder of the scene or until leaving active Mage Sight. You also suffer -2 penalties to all Revelation and Scrutiny rolls.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution:</u> This Condition is resolved when you successfully Reveal the surface or deep information of a Mystery. Resolving this Condition grants an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <u>Beat:</u> N/A.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> By the time you and Ragnar leave the sanctuary, the other Nameless mages you've met are congregating in the narthex.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;The correct plural is actually 'Thyrsus',&quot;</span> Falling Blossom comments.<br /> <br /> Raven laughs. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;We are <i>Shamans</i>, Lynx. Call us by our formal name if you prefer, but our calling is that of <i>real</i> magic, of life and energy and <i>power</i> all fused together. It's what gives the spirits their life breath, and courses through your veins, your very <i>cells</i>.&quot;</span> She shakes her head at the mention of the Pentacle. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Politics, phaw! Forget that for now. You're trying to understand why ants march in formation, why birds fly in a flock. That will come later. First, I'm going to teach you why they <i>exist.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven rubs her chin pensively and adds, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;It might help you to meet more Shamans, I suppose. Perhaps the Shadow Spears?&quot;</span> she asks, turning to Falling Blossom. The other mage nods, and Raven explains, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;The Shadow Spears are an all-Thyrsus cabal. You saw Yari earlier, one of this Consilium's Sentinels. He is an Arrow, alongside our colleague and fellow Mystagogue Ascalon, and Trident of the Free Council. They are a focused lot, but may take time to meet with us this week. But your basic education must come first,&quot;</span> she states firmly. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Talk to your companions about your possible pack, your cabal, and I will further educate you on more important matters. You won't regret it,&quot;</span> she grins again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Mathias nods at you and reminds you to contact him with any questions or concerns, and he says goodbye before leaving. In the sanctuary, you find yourself longing to know more about this place. It's a thirst for knowledge that you've rarely felt before, at least of this magnitude. You got only a small taste of it here, but you are hungry for more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Although you weren't able to learn more about the magic here, take an Arcane Beat for pursuing your Aspiration this scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dante nods. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Let us get started sooner rather than later, then. Perhaps late this evening, after the sun sets. I will be attending to some business in the suburbs. Meet me in La Grange at the Vial House.&quot;</span> You've heard of this building; it's a museum and research center, used by the La Grange Area Historical Center. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;I will need to start teaching you some of the basics of other aspects of magic, so you can start to truly understand your gifts. There is so much to show you, to teach you,&quot;</span> he smiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typos, formatting 11-21-2016, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:29:19-08:00","id":1006398,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;Do you still have interest in serving the Adamantine Arrow?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;After all that I've done, I at least have to try, don't I? I owe it to Hakim to follow in his footsteps. But I've become entangled with Sentinel Valentine over the last week, without quite meaning to. I'll hear what he has to say out of respect, but after that, you'll be the first to know what my next steps are with the Arrow.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> A few words for Ghost Dog in particular: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Whatever happens, I want to sharpen my swordsmanship. I'm used to fighting with you and Hakim, but I want to broaden my style to be an independent combatant and incorporate magic into combat. What if we had a training session this week, see what our chemistry is as two mages, and decide where to go from there?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This doesn't need to be a big onscreen thing, but I want to use Allies (Arrow) this chapter to &quot;buy&quot; a training session with Ghost Dog.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They spend a little while longer just catching up. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;...Ragnar was absolutely starstruck when he came in. I think he's one of those mages who look for echoes of the Supernal in Sleeper religion- with all due respect, Rose. You might like him, actually, or like the person he might become. He's off with Phoenix studying the sanctuary right now. Keep an eye out for that boy, he's being pointed toward the Arrow. He knows more than most about the world of magic. I don't know whether he was a Sleepwalker, but he's seen behind the Veil somehow, and he lost someone in the Deathstorm. I think his grief may be affecting his judgment.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He says this with no apparent irony.<br /> <br /> After saying his goodbyes and hoping to hear about Spade soon, he talks with Valentine. He listens, nods, and is polite. He doesn't mind Valentine touching him, he doesn't flinch or anything. It's different here. He takes the paper with solemnity and tucks it away- he can be trusted about this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Let me be frank. I recognize that you're sticking your neck out for me. I see you, and I appreciate it. If only for the sentiment, thank you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;This is where I am: I don't know the Guardians. I know only broad statements and rumors, and I believe that is how your Order likes it. I do know that the mage whom I swore to serve unto death was an Adamantine Arrow. I also know that more than a decade of following the Adamant Way did not lead me to Awaken. My master's death did. I don't know what that means yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I want to learn to control my magic. I've seen what happens when magic endangers Awakened and Sleepers, when it could have been stopped earlier. I feel like I've been running in a wheel with pictures of magic painted on the inside, and now it's broken and I've stepped outside the wheel into the real thing. But that wheel has been my <i>world</i> until now. I can't honestly say more than that right now. I will meditate sincerely and speak to you about it tomorrow. Not lunch. Somewhere outdoors.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He lowers his voice. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;One more thing. I tried to read the shared Sympathy of the Deathstorm victims, like we discussed. Consider trying it yourself. I want to talk about what I saw tomorrow, too.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> That's all for now. He says his goodbyes and leaves, soon finding the other Nameless.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I know we're all busy witches with cauldrons to attend to, but we should talk. There's a cafe called Awake <i>(yes, i know, it's very funny)</i> next to a park a few blocks west of here. We always used to go there after Consilium. It's 10 minutes away, we can walk and talk. I'll Veil us so we can speak freely- even buy you coffee, Aion knows it's the least I can do. What do you say?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:53:00-08:00","id":1006520,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> Lynx grins at Falling Blossom and Raven, his eyes alive with joy. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Wicked! I'm looking forward to it! All of it! I'll see you at dusk!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> He returns to the other Nameless as soon as their gathering starts. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I know we're all busy witches with cauldrons to attend to, but we should talk. There's a cafe called Awake </span><i>(yes, i know, it's very funny)</i><span style=\"color:#008080\"> next to a park a few blocks west of here. We always used to go there after Consilium. It's 10 minutes away, we can walk and talk. I'll Veil us so we can speak freely- even buy you coffee, Aion knows it's the least I can do. What do you say?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm game,</span>&quot; Lynx nods eagerly, bouncing impatiently. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Getting to know you lot's going to be good.</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T01:07:18-08:00","id":1006628,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>6 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b></div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I know we're all busy witches with cauldrons to attend to, but we should talk. There's a cafe called Awake </span><i>(yes, i know, it's very funny)</i><span style=\"color:#008080\"> next to a park a few blocks west of here. We always used to go there after Consilium. It's 10 minutes away, we can walk and talk. I'll Veil us so we can speak freely- even buy you coffee, Aion knows it's the least I can do. What do you say?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm game,</span>&quot; Lynx nods eagerly, bouncing impatiently. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Getting to know you lot's going to be good.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I could certainly use a good cup of coffee, I am afraid all this Consilium meeting has confused me further rather than solve any of my doubts. Hopefully we can share our impressions together and disipate some of them, as it seems some of you are no new to all this bizarre protocols and politics&quot;</b></span>-he smiles, warmly-<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;It really reminds me when I first started getting involved in academia...&quot;</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T19:45:33-08:00","id":1007528,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> As if it wasn't overwhelming enough, the Aether starts flooding my Sight. It's too hard to look at, so I revert back to my mundane senses. As I leave to go look for Anubis, I see the other Nameless gathering. Oh right, they exist.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I know we're all busy witches with cauldrons to attend to, but we should talk. There's a cafe called Awake <i>(yes, i know, it's very funny)</i> next to a park a few blocks west of here. We always used to go there after Consilium. It's 10 minutes away, we can walk and talk. I'll Veil us so we can speak freely- even buy you coffee, Aion knows it's the least I can do. What do you say?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Yeah, we do have a few things to discuss before I head off. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Coffee sounds nice,&quot;</span> I accept simply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T23:43:11-08:00","id":1007595,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Wonderful.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Once everyone has finished their business, he heads outside the church grounds, nodding at the guard again on his way out. After they've gotten a block away and there are less parishioners and magicians filing out, he takes off his glove and holds out his bandaged left hand to the group. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm going to hide our words. Touch my hand, please.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Improvising a Mind 2 Veiling effect in the spirit of Incognito Presence. Touch range, 1 Reach for instant, +1 Reach for advanced duration, +1 Reach for advanced scale. Containing any Paradox, 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458973\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1+Mind 2, 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458974\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's a feeling like their ears are adjusting to a change in pressure. His Periphery centers him as his own Imago takes effect. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You can let go. Here's how this should work: we can understand one another, but as long as we keep our voices down and don't draw attention, other people will only hear us talking about the weather or the Cubs or...I don't know, whatever Sleepers talk about in a cafe. It's social camouflage.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> They make their way into Awake. The smells and the atmosphere are familiar, even if the context is different. Lots of laptops and wooden tables and shelves full of board games. Moonstone smiles brightly at the cashier, points to the menu, orders drinks for the group and pays in cash without saying a word aloud. He can't really afford this. Little known fact: Sleepwalkers are responsible for mundane chores as well as magical ones. They're like interns who can hold your spells for you.<br /> <br /> Once it's all sorted, he guides everyone to a corner booth, assigns mugs from a tray like a professional butler, and lays out a Scrabble board. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;To maintain cover. Also, I like Scrabble.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Only when he's confirmed that everyone is comfortable does he sit down, rest his face in his hands and let his muscles relax with a prolonged sigh. He reaffirms: <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm here.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Alright. For the last week, we've been treated as a single unit- only a few hours for you, Ophis. The Shields of Dawn expect us to form a cabal. But the future is unwritten, none of this is set in stone. Who are we? What are we thinking? Do we want to formally establish ties? Did I get all of your orders right?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T05:10:13-08:00","id":1007665,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar is still furious with Moonstone, but he can't help but give him a grin when he casts his spell. &quot;Impressive.&quot; <br /> <br /> Once they are at Awake, Ragnar takes a seat next to Lynx. He briefly takes a look around the six of them: Lynx, who is unimpressed with the Consilium as a whole; Binder, the bookstore owner, who seems poised to join the Mysterium with Lynx; Phoenix, the young man asking about a mage named Anubis, and a seasoned combatant even though he's barely in his 20s; Moonstone, his new frenemy; and Ouroboros, who is still something of an unknown quantity. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>I've heard of motley crews, but this is insane. </i></span><br /> <br /> He looks down at the coffee. He's never been keen on coffee; it's not particularly kind to his body, and he has to load it up with creamer and sugar to make it even somewhat palatable. He takes a sip. He grabs some Scrabble pieces and shares them between himself and Lynx. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Alright. For the last week, we've been treated as a single unit- only a few hours for you, Ophis. The Shields of Dawn expect us to form a cabal. But the future is unwritten, none of this is set in stone. Who are we? What are we thinking? Do we want to formally establish ties? Did I get all of your orders right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar shrugs. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;We all Awakened or arrived in Chicago at around the same time. Six newly-Awakened mages in the same place at the same time? That's Fate right there. Besides, the Hierarch expects us to work together to bring down the Gulmoth. So we're stuck working together until then, at the very least. I say, 'Why not?'.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T11:09:55-08:00","id":1007774,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> Rose of Sharon nods at your answer and does not seem surprised. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;If you need guidance, you can contact me. And if you decide to pursue the Arrow, you know the protocol.&quot;</span> <br /> <br /> You've been witness to that part enough in Hakim's company: You know you need to petition a ranking member, such as a Thunderbolt Guardian or the Adamant Sage, who then provides instruction on the necessary traits to gain initiation. Of course, as a Sleepwalker, you weren't as often privy to what exactly that initiation process later entailed. <br /> <br /> Rose smiles briefly. <span style=\"color:palevioletred\">&quot;As for the young man, I believe Boomer will be an excellent mentor for him. The Arrow is already eyeing him. But I think your assessment is fair.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ghost Dog agrees to your suggestion with a nod. He isn't usually one for many words when a gesture can suffice. You have each other's contact information, so you know that you can probably reach him without too much effort.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Perhaps it means the Adamant Way does not speak to your soul the way you need to experience the Supernal,&quot;</span> Valentine suggests softly. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;The Guardians can do more than just teach you to control your own magic; we can teach you how to protect the world from others who cannot or will not control their own magic. Our calling, and our burden, is to ensure the safety of all mages, not just ourselves.&quot;</span> Valentine's usually neutral tone takes on a tone of passion and eagerness as he speaks. <br /> <br /> At your suggestion, Valentine frowns but nods slowly. <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;I will,&quot;</span> he replies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> It's only a short walk west down Chicago Ave to the Awake Caf\u00e9. It's a casual, comfortable and modern cafe that contrasts the austere church you have just left. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3-media4.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/fXsrP0kjj1hYHgvlY7NX8A/o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> With the spell wrapped around you, no one seems to be paying you any more attention than usual. Well, Phoenix's staff draws a little more attention at a coffee shop, but the people of Chicago have seen stranger things.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ok, looks like no one else needed specific feedback from the ST in recent posts. Go ahead and feel free to take the scene and run with it. If anyone needs a specific response from me or if I have anything to add, I'll post.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:05:11-08:00","id":1007994,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Scrabble, huh. Been a while.</span>&quot; Lynx breathes in the normality of Awake as he sips his own coffee. He fiddles with his letters as Ragnar sends them his way (RIEGAPUO). <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ague?</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">Alright. For the last week, we've been treated as a single unit- only a few hours for you, Ophis. The Shields of Dawn expect us to form a cabal. But the future is unwritten, none of this is set in stone. Who are we? What are we thinking? Do we want to formally establish ties? Did I get all of your orders right?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Ragnar shrugs next to him. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">We all Awakened or arrived in Chicago at around the same time. Six newly-Awakened mages in the same place at the same time? That's Fate right there. Besides, the Hierarch expects us to work together to bring down the Gulmoth. So we're stuck working together until then, at the very least. I say, 'Why not?'.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Hmm.</span>&quot; Lynx rubs his beard. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">That doesn't sit right with me. Me and Ragnar arrived after... whatever happened,</span>&quot; he glances at the others, sans Ragnar and Ouroboros Ophis, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">And Ophis didn't know about the six... the five of us,</span>&quot; he corrects himself, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Until today. I don't mind helping with the Gulmoth,</span>&quot; he adds as he idly rearranges his Scrabble tiles - <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Pager is a word, right?</span></i> - &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">But to expect it from me and Ragnar? What was she told, exactly, about the incident? I don't like it.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">As for... formally?</span>&quot; He scoffs, not at the suggestion but the word. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Magic society really is pretentious, isn't it? Forming a Cabal, I'm for that. I like all of you. None of you feel... off. Or wrong. Weird, yes, but that's good. You're the first mages I met, so...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">I guess you're my pack.</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't really know who <i>we</i> are. I guess I'm the pet dog or bear or cat or... or something...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Agrope?</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I want knowledge. I want understanding. I want to learn. I also want to see you all safe and healthy. So unless us grouping up is going to deprive me of that, I don't see a problem.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He looks down at his tiles again, smiling. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't suppose Norwegian words are allowed at Scrabble?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>Gauper.</i> Lynxes.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-25-2016, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:21:15-08:00","id":1008050,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> Walking down the street, I hold the staff like a walking stick so I don't draw too much unnecessary attention. Still get a few looks here and there, which is fine. Always liked standing out just that little bit. Other than that, the walk to the cafe is uneventful. I don't think I've been to Awake, this'll be new. I tell Moonstone to get me a simple black coffee, I'm not one for the fancy-schmanchinos.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;To maintain cover. Also, I like Scrabble.&quot;</span> Moonstone states as he brings the game over.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Oh yeah, a group o' guys playing Scrabble. Wonderful cover,&quot;</span> I chuckle with a smirk, then I wave my hand to show I'm just teasing and pick some letters. KSKOEMP, huh? I'm probably gonna lose. Kinda suck at Scrabble anyways.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Quite a ragtag crew we got here,&quot;</span> I chip in to the conversation as I take a sip, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;We've worked together pretty well when we knew nothing about each other, so that certainly counts for something. I think we could all end up as a unit.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The only real obstacle I see is Moonstone himself, really. Though I think he's trying not to be, so I don't bring it up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Although, about the formal ties thing, what does that entail exactly?&quot;</span> I ask, facing Moonstone, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do we like, sign a form for the Consilium, or is it a magical tie of something?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:07:32-08:00","id":1008070,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>6 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ouroboros sits next to Phoenix, a known face to act as a touchstone among all the weirdness of the latest days. He thanks Moonstone as he gets him a coffe and for a while is content with warming up his hands with the cup and take a sip or two, listening to the group work things out. But something catches his attention.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;We all Awakened or arrived in Chicago at around the same time. Six newly-Awakened mages in the same place at the same time? That's Fate right there. Besides, the Hierarch expects us to work together to bring down the Gulmoth. So we're stuck working together until then, at the very least. I say, 'Why not?'.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This Gulmoth thing again. What is that thing they fought but apparently did not quite managed to defeat? All things point to him soon be respnsible to hunt that... being down by association,he better inform himself.<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Ragnar, son, this is far from the first time I heard you all talking about your encounter with this... Gulmoth? Is that it? Could you please explain to this old man what exactly is this thing you faced, as it seems quite probable I would get involved with it in the future?&quot;</b></span>-he smiles, warmly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">...And Ophis didn't know about the six... the five of us...</span><br /> <br /> That makes him raise an eyebrow. They have already lost one of their numbers?<br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Excuse me, Lynx, sorry to interrupt, but have I understand correctly that you used to be six newly awakened at some point, prior to my appearance? What did happen to this sixth member if I may ask?&quot;</span></b>- he hopes that mage is not another casualty of the weird storms.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I want knowledge. I want understanding. I want to learn. I also want to see you all safe and healthy. So unless us grouping up is going to deprive me of that, I don't see a problem.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;I cannot speak for the rest -</b> <i>although I can hazard a good guess at Phoenix</i> <b>- but I think you will have no problem with us on that front. I am a doctor first, mage second. I have already sworn to keep people healthy and alive&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Although, about the formal ties thing, what does that entail exactly?</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Do we like, sign a form for the Consilium, or is it a magical tie of something?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#006400\">-&quot;That is a good question indeed, thanks to bring it up, Phoenix. I really do not mind about bindding agreements between gentlemen as I am sure we all are, but knowing the exact terms, rights and obligations would ease my mind a bit&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-25-2016, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:59:10-08:00","id":1008087,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Excuse me, Lynx, sorry to interrupt, but have I understand correctly that you used to be six newly awakened at some point, prior to my appearance? What did happen to this sixth member if I may ask?&quot;</span></b>- he hopes that mage is not another casualty of the weird storms.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't know,</span>&quot; Lynx sighs. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">When Mathias found me and Ragnar, the three of us had just popped out of one of those...alternate dimensions? I don't remember exactly. She ended up going back to uni with some other teacher or head of department or something like that while we ran off to help the others. Then she vanished. I've tried getting a hold of her, but... nothing. She taught the FYS class you took over.</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-25-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:19:21-08:00","id":1008377,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Small Talk (all PCs, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b><br /> </div> Moonstone digs in the box for some vowels, and spells out CONSILIUM.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You've met the Consilium. They aren't a government, exactly. More like a court of the Wise that settles disputes, provides sanctuary, and keeps magicians from killing each other by malice or ignorance. If you want to practice magic in the Chicago area, you most likely want to be bound by the laws and protections of the Consilium, the <i>Lex Magica</i>. There isn't some sort of larger Awakened nation that they answer to, despite the hopes of the Silver Ladder- although we <i>do </i>have Convocations every so often with the Consilia of other cities nearby, and that ghastly confederation of Shamans who live in the Shadow of Lake Michigan...I'm getting ahead of myself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Next to that, he spells ORDER.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;You've also heard about the Pentacle Orders. They provide purpose, instruction, and magical resources for their members. They don't answer to the Consilium, but their members are expected to follow the Lex Magica.You don't <i>need </i>to join an Order, but then, you don't <i>need </i>a job, a house, or friends. Some mages, just as some people, go without.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He just then notices Lynx's word. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I <i>thought</i> you were Scandinavian! Your accent is lovely. Are you an exchange student? In another life, I wanted to study abroad, but I never had the chance...anyway, cabals.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He spells CABAL underneath CONSILIUM and ORDER, on a triple word score. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Very important.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Your cabal is those whom you can always count on. Some are formal, some are informal, but a cabal is a group of individual mages recognized by others. You basically tell the Consilium that these people are in a cabal, and the cabal name is X. It's not a marriage, or a lease agreement, or a deathless oath- simply the people you have chosen to stand with. Mages join a cabal for mutual support and protection in their magical lives. There's a cabal in Boystown that just shares rent on a storage unit, compares notes once a month, and shows up in force if one of them is attacked. Others are more formal and mystically powerful. I used to serve a cabal called the Knights of Alhambra, all Adamantine Arrows who draw magical power from the symbol of al-Andalus as a kingdom of enlightened warriors. They have a number of Fate-bound oaths and obligations, but they entered them willingly, and they are stronger for it. Of course, all oaths can be broken, and no cabal is permanent. The Knights chose to condemn and expel my master, Hakim, for violating their oath- even though he was a founding member and certainly the strongest of them- and I chose to stand with him. And that was that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He disassembles CABAL and sips his coffee.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;At the most basic level, cabal members are expected to tell each other what they're working on in their magical lives, assume good faith and support each other in a crisis. If Phoenix told me that he was being threatened by a cult of necromancers, I would fight beside him first and ask <i>why</i> necromancers are attacking him later. If Ouroboros Ophis wanted to follow the Sympathy of some magical mystery he was studying, I would offer my help freely. And I would expect the same courtesy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;The more a cabal pulls together, the stronger its members become. Many cabals pool their resources and share a safe house or ritual space of some kind, or a place of power like a Hallow or Demesne- sites where the Supernal is closer to the Fallen, and working magic is easier. We can look into that later. Some cabals look for a shared theme or myth or magical symbol that fascinates their members, and draw power from that shared Mystery when they incorporate that symbol into their magic. A cabal might receive a boon by swearing a Fate-bound oath, or refine their Sympathy to act more alike, or enter an agreement with a powerful spirit or ghost to sponsor them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But none of this is strictly necessary. The fundamental thing is to, as Phoenix said, 'sign a form.' The cabal decides where it goes from there.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;To your question, Doctor. A Gulmoth is an...entity...summoned into our world from the Abyss when a mage causes a severe Paradox. It's a blasphemous idea given mostly-physical form.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone delicately draws out an X from the game box. He idly plays with the letters A - L - U - X, arranging the tiles in various combinations on the board, but can't bring himself to actually form the name.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;The entity in question represents the death of light. Not in the way that shadows are part of the Death Arcanum, but a vile perversion of that symbol. It manifests as a great thing of teeth and claws and sizzling darkness, and it can inflict terror on those who look at it. Phoenix stopped it on Tuesday...with some help from me...but it's only discorporated for now, still anchored to the world. It will reform on the 17th. To stop it for good and banish it from our world, we need to destroy its mystical being as well as its physical body. That might be difficult. Most magical entities, even twisted ones like the Gulmoth, have a Bane. It's like a price they pay for manifesting in our world. If we discovered its Bane, the material that especially harms it, we could destroy Alux for good.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Realizing he's said the name, he immediately shivers and tosses some artificial sweetener over his shoulder. Warding gesture. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;We could also try draining the Essence that sustains it. It will be easier to annihilate when its starving.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T07:58:16-08:00","id":1008537,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <b>&quot;Ragnar, son, this is far from the first time I heard you all talking about your encounter with this... Gulmoth? Is that it? Could you please explain to this old man what exactly is this thing you faced, as it seems quite probable I would get involved with it in the future?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ragnar is about to answer when Moonstone speaks up. </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;To your question, Doctor. A Gulmoth is an...entity...summoned into our world from the Abyss when a mage causes a severe Paradox. It's a blasphemous idea given mostly-physical form. The entity in question represents the death of light. Not in the way that shadows are part of the Death Arcanum, but a vile perversion of that symbol.<br /> <br /> Ragnar nods. </span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Moonstone... well, I'm not quite clear on the particulars, but he cast a spell that incurred a ridiculous amount of Paradox. It was a complete accident, of course. I don't want to think about how crazy somebody would have to be to summon a Gulmoth intentionally. But since it was one of our number who summoned it, Hierarch Cielo and the Counselors decided that we would handle it ourselves. As an... object lesson on the dangers of Paradox.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It's like a price they pay for manifesting in our world. If we discovered its Bane, the material that especially harms it, we could destroy Alux for good.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar squirms a little at the memory of the Gulmoth's shadowy tendrils slicing and stabbing his flesh. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Don't. In all the old stories, if you say something's name, it knows about it. Say it too many times, and it might just show up. 'Speak of the devil, and in he will walk,' you know. If we want to say its name, let's just wait until we're looking the bastard in the face again.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He looks over at Lynx and smiles. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well, figuring out its Bane should be the Spirit Arcanum, right? And draining its Essence might also be Spirit. Or Prime, I'm not sure.&quot; <br /> <br /> The discussion of a cabal gets him nodding. &quot;I know we don't have to be a formal thing... but do some cabals have, like, united goals? What if we got tasked with destroying the Gulmoth because that's what we're here in Chicago to do? Go around, investigate Abyssal intrusions.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:47:44-08:00","id":1009189,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Small Talk (all PCs, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Well, figuring out its Bane should be the Spirit Arcanum, right? And draining its Essence might also be Spirit. Or Prime, I'm not sure.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Very astute, Ragnar. Gulmoth are something like twisted reflections of spirits. If any Arcanum can help us here, it is Spirit.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I know we don't have to be a formal thing... but do some cabals have, like, united goals? What if we got tasked with destroying the Gulmoth because that's what we're here in Chicago to do? Go around, investigate Abyssal intrusions.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone groans. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Think loftier thoughts, I beg of you! One of the Knights, Rose of Sharon, is a member of the Choir of Hashmallim- mages dedicated to scouring the Abyss. It is a heavy burden, even for those well-equipped to bear it, which we are not. One Gulmoth is enough for my lifetime, and I saw more than that as a Sleepwalker. There is so much more mystery and beauty in the world of magic than slaying Intruders in some corrupt Verge. Even our own suburbia of La Grange has mysticism and hidden things. Seek out the Supernal, not the Abyss, even to oppose it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He snaps his fingers and brightens. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I've got it! We must all be fascinated by something. Magic has a way of obsessing you. Let's discuss what we're working on, and decide what we could pursue together and compare notes on. Exploring a Mystery, any Mystery with magic behind it, can make all of us better magicians. I'll start: I will be clearing out some demons from my psyche this week, which I mean quite literally. A mage I don't know will be guiding me through it. Frankly, I could use an escort, especially if any of you are comfortable with demons of the mind. Or trip sitting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">AKA: say what your Obsession and/or &quot;thing you want to do this chapter&quot; is, and let's do it...<i>together </i>(or at least in small groups)</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-28-2016, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T02:45:47-08:00","id":1009250,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I've got it! We must all be fascinated by something. Magic has a way of obsessing you. Let's discuss what we're working on, and decide what we could pursue together and compare notes on. Exploring a Mystery, any Mystery with magic behind it, can make all of us better magicians. I'll start: I will be clearing out some demons from my psyche this week, which I mean quite literally. A mage I don't know will be guiding me through it. Frankly, I could use an escort, especially if any of you are comfortable with demons of the mind. Or trip sitting.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Mystery?</span>&quot; Lynx murmurs as he looks for more letter tiles to spell out other Norwegian words. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm not sure you could help me. It's a Thyrsus thing. A Primal Wild thing. I'm looking for the one who Awakened me. A Great Lynx. He guided me during my second visit to the Wild. I want to find him again. Pretty sure it's a him, at least. Not really sure if spirits have gender yet...</span>&quot; He hums a little as he looks at the group. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I doubt you can relate to this. If any of you know Spirit magic, I guess that could help. I'll appreciate any help you're willing to give, though.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">If you want a more realistic Mystery to pursue together from my end, it'll be insight into one another. What's it like being an Acanthus? What's it feel like to wield Space or Forces? What's it like being attuned to... Stygia, was it? There's so much to learn. I think we can teach each other a lot. Reach an understanding. Become friends and allies.</span>&quot; He looks to Moonstone, then to Phoenix and Ragnar, with a look of amusement. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Enjoy some friction.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Wait, what?</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:12:25-08:00","id":1009295,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> I just sit there and stare at Moonstone as I drink both the information and the coffee. I don't think I even blink, it's a lot to take in all in one sitting. I wince slightly when he talks of our encounter with the Gulmoth. My memories of that place were vague, but the image of those bleeding holes in me are still crisp and clean, as much as I'd love them not to be. When he gets to the part about dealing with it, I do appreciate how he acknowledges at least someone else other than himself, but...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;As well as the others,&quot;</span> I chime in, gesturing towards Ragnar, Lynx, and Binder with my paper mug. It's a start for him, I suppose. Looks like he's on the heroic path, he just tripped up a bit is all. After that, he mentions that the Gulmoth would appear on...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;The 17th? Doesn't give us a whole lot of time...&quot;</span> I sigh with a concerned breath.<br /> <br /> The subject of a common goal for our cabal pops up, with Moonstone suggesting we all pitch in on our projects. That...is gonna complicate matters. If they pitch in on me searching for Anubis, they might find out I'm a Hunter. Can't let them know that I once dedicated my life to killing mages. Maybe I can change the subject.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do we really need a common goal? At least, to start with, I mean. We're all new to the world of magic, if only as active participants for some of us,&quot;</span> I state, glancing at Moonstone with that last part, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;What's the rush? Let's just work together and leave it at that for the time being. A common goal will probably crop up naturally that way, anyways.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I hope that gets them off the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T07:44:32-08:00","id":1009326,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 4 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;These places are called Athenaea, essentially Supernal libraries and storehouses. We can take you both to one this week and introduce you to some of our other members, should you be interested.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"> &quot;I certainly would be! We'll need to work out a time; I have unavoidable obligations during the late afternoon and evening.&quot;</span> Binder is careful to use his tone to convey that these obligations are not unpleasant; they're unavoidable because he chooses to not avoid them. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Free all morning and night, though.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:brown\">&quot;There are some whom we worry about because they are too eager, too impatient to use our knowledge unwisely. Such misuse would risk a great deal of danger for many. But I don't think you're like that, are you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I certainly feel eager. But I like to think that I'm not terribly impatient.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I don't really know who <i>we</i> are. I guess I'm the pet dog or bear or cat or... or something...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Binder makes a concerned face at Lynx's self-deprecation. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Please, Lynx, you're not a <i>pet</i>; we're all equals here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I'll start: I will be clearing out some demons from my psyche this week, which I mean quite literally. A mage I don't know will be guiding me through it. Frankly, I could use an escort, especially if any of you are comfortable with demons of the mind. Or trip sitting.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I'd be interested in that, if you're willing to have me. It would be good to learn more about the practical applications of mind magic.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'm not sure you could help me. It's a Thyrsus thing. A Primal Wild thing. I'm looking for the one who Awakened me. A Great Lynx. He guided me during my second visit to the Wild. I want to find him again. Pretty sure it's a him, at least. Not really sure if spirits have gender yet...</span>&quot; He hums a little as he looks at the group. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I doubt you can relate to this. If any of you know Spirit magic, I guess that could help. I'll appreciate any help you're willing to give, though.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I might be able to relate more than you think. My awakening was triggered by an otherworldly entity as well. Though,&quot;</span> he admits, <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;mine was a demon. I know a little of Spirit, and I'd be interested to learn more about the ephemeral.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">If you want a more realistic Mystery to pursue together from my end, it'll be insight into one another. What's it like being an Acanthus? What's it feel like to wield Space or Forces? What's it like being attuned to... Stygia, was it? There's so much to learn. I think we can teach each other a lot. Reach an understanding. Become friends and allies.</span>&quot; He looks to Moonstone, then to Phoenix and Ragnar, with a look of amusement. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Enjoy some friction.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Binder breezes past the sexual implications of that last remark. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;If you'd ever like to stop by the bookstore sometime, I'd be very happy to discuss our paths in relation to each other! That, of course, goes for everyone. In fact, that reminds me; Moonstone, you mentioned that cabal's often share a ritual space? I don't know anything about Hallows or Demesnes, but I've been outfitting the upper floor of the bookstore as a ritual space these past few days, and I'd be happy to share it with the rest of you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I've got something in mind that I'm thinking of looking into, though I don't know if it's a mystery <i>per se</i>. I really do want to do a little more research before bringing it before the group though.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:14:47-08:00","id":1009672,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Small Talk (all PCs, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 3/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I doubt you can relate to this. If any of you know Spirit magic, I guess that could help. I'll appreciate any help you're willing to give, though.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Spirits and vision quests are a little messy for me. Askia was always more of an Ecstatic than a Shaman. But this Great Lynx sounds like a thing of the Primal Wild more than the Shadow, and there are ways of calling out the Beasts of the Wild for an audience. I suggest you ask an elder Shaman about summoning.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;I'd be interested in that, if you're willing to have me. It would be good to learn more about the practical applications of mind magic.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Wonderful! We'll make a day of it.&quot;</span> He really has wanted to know Marlin/Binder better, given their shared Path and general friendliness. If there's anyone at the table he'd trust to be a second, it's him.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;I think we can teach each other a lot. Reach an understanding. Become friends and allies.</span>&quot; Moonstone notices Lynx looking from him to Ragnar and Phoenix, and smiling. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Enjoy some friction.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He clears his throat, self-conscious. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I would rather avoid any more <i>friction</i>between these dashing young men and myself.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;If you'd ever like to stop by the bookstore sometime, I'd be very happy to discuss our paths in relation to each other! That, of course, goes for everyone. In fact, that reminds me; Moonstone, you mentioned that cabal's often share a ritual space? I don't know anything about Hallows or Demesnes, but I've been outfitting the upper floor of the bookstore as a ritual space these past few days, and I'd be happy to share it with the rest of you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank you, Binder, how generous! You all should see his bookstore, it has potential. Oh, I'm so excited, this is all fitting together so well!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do we really need a common goal? At least, to start with, I mean. We're all new to the world of magic, if only as active participants for some of us,&quot;</span> Phoenix glances at him. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;What's the rush? Let's just work together and leave it at that for the time being. A common goal will probably crop up naturally that way, anyways.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Moonstone deflates. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I suppose that's true. We don't <i>need </i>a statement of purpose just yet. We're only just getting started.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He wrings his hands, drains the rest of his coffee, and speaks up in a quiet voice. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;But...listen. I <i>want</i> to form a cabal with you all. Whatever brought us together- Fate, Sympathy, circumstance- I want to make the most of it. I don't want this to dissolve after we deal with the Gulmoth. Magic is an anchor for me. It's been so long since I was on my own in the world of Sleepers- my 'normal' is the world of magic. This is where I find stability: working with mages, being of service, giving myself to others. I know how to help a cabal- how to help all of you!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But I also realize that I've caused you all a great deal of grief and trouble since we've met. And if we're going to work together, I need to take ownership of that. I want to make what I know available to you, to be your bridge into the Consilium. And if I can make up for what I've done through sacrifice and service, I want to. I'd swear an Oath if I could, but for now, all I can offer is my solemn word and my magic.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Basically offering to use Moonstone's Social merits [like Allies 3 (Arrow) and Contacts (Sleepwalkers, Occultists)] for the benefit of the cabal/whoever wants to use their mechanical effects this chapter, and/or doing favors or casting spells for the group. Seriously, the band is taking requests.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T05:34:03-08:00","id":1009734,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">If you want a more realistic Mystery to pursue together from my end, it'll be insight into one another. What's it like being an Acanthus? What's it feel like to wield Space or Forces? What's it like being attuned to... Stygia, was it? There's so much to learn. I think we can teach each other a lot. Reach an understanding. Become friends and allies.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar nods. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;That sounds like a good idea. I'm going to have Moonstone to give me a lesson on Space magic, and I've been meaning to ask you to give me a lesson on Life magic, Lynx. Maybe we could all get together and give each other lessons?&quot; </span> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Enjoy some friction.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Ragnar is taking a sip of coffee as he hears this. An image of himself and Lynx making inventive use of friction pops into his head, and he immediately gags on the coffee. He spends a couple seconds coughing. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Um.. define 'tension,'&quot; </span>he says weakly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:15:54-08:00","id":1010155,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">Please, Lynx, you're not a <i>pet</i>;</span><span style=\"color:#800080\"> we're all equals here.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx chuckles weakly. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Old habits die hard.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:purple\">I might be able to relate more than you think. My awakening was triggered by an otherworldly entity as well. Though,&quot;</span> he admits, <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;mine was a demon. I know a little of Spirit, and I'd be interested to learn more about the ephemeral.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">That's great! We're already set up to learning together, so this is an added bonus.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Um.. define 'tension,</span>'&quot; Ragnar says weakly. Lynx snorts.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">The tension between you three is amusing. Touchable.</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">I would rather avoid any more </span><i>friction</i><span style=\"color:#008080\">between these dashing young men and myself.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Well, conflict's a good way to get to know one another. I'm sure you three know more about each other than I do.</span>&quot; Lynx rubs his beard. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Why do they all look so awkward?</span></i><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">If you'd ever like to stop by the bookstore sometime, I'd be very happy to discuss our paths in relation to each other! That, of course, goes for everyone. In fact, that reminds me; Moonstone, you mentioned that cabal's often share a ritual space? I don't know anything about Hallows or Demesnes, but I've been outfitting the upper floor of the bookstore as a ritual space these past few days, and I'd be happy to share it with the rest of you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Oh, I'll definitely come visit. I think I know where your shop is.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Do we really need a common goal? At least, to start with, I mean. We're all new to the world of magic, if only as active participants for some of us,&quot;</span> Phoenix says, glancing at Moonstone with that last part, &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">What's the rush? Let's just work together and leave it at that for the time being. A common goal will probably crop up naturally that way, anyways.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">It's a great way to get to know one another, though,</span>&quot; Lynx murmurs. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'd like to be useful to you lot, but in order to do that, knowing the gist of what you want is kinda necessary.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">That sounds like a good idea. I'm going to have Moonstone to give me a lesson on Space magic, and I've been meaning to ask you to give me a lesson on Life magic, Lynx. Maybe we could all get together and give each other lessons?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Yes! Great idea! I'd love to see your magic in practise. Hell, maybe all of us should meet and try teach each other new stuff.</span>&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T18:01:59-08:00","id":1010884,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0</div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">The tension between you three is amusing. Touchable.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Ragnar's face begins to flush. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Oh. Okay, because, I, uh, thought. You. Meant...&quot; </span>Ragnar stops and stares fixedly at the table.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i> Open mouth, insert foot. Brilliant, Ragnar.</i></span><br /> <br /> He looks around. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;So, uh. Yeah. Lessons would be neat. How do we want to do it? Cast some spells on each other? Something simple, just to show each other what it feels like to have each Arcanum affect you, so you know for future reference?&quot; </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T01:22:32-08:00","id":1010974,"title":"","content":"<b><div align=\"center\">Moonstone</div></b><br /> <br /> Ragnar blushes, Moonstone is terse: <span style=\"color:Teal\">&quot;Yes, we know. The sheer sexual tension is nearly unbearable. Moving on.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My masters would sometimes challenge each other with magic, or test their own bodies and minds to their limit. Create their own gauntlets and come out stronger for the experience. I believe we learn more from struggle and crisis than passive instruction, with due respect to the teachers among us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;At any rate, a crowded coffeehouse isn't the Wisest place to experiment with magic, if you ask me. Binder's bookstore would be better- but our session will be downtown, Ragnar, if you're free for the afternoon. If we are agreed on forming a cabal beyond the immediate threat, then I consider our business happily finished. &quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:45:16-08:00","id":1011014,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>6 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;If I may add my vote on this... I think we could use the appointed mission to deal with that Gulmoth as an starting point for our cabal. Then we will see how well we work together and if some overall interest binds us further together&quot;</span></b>- pauses to take a long sip of cofee- <span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;<b>Speaking of interests, there is something you all can do for me, but I understand if you are wary. The soul is a matter of profound fascination to a doctor like me, I have made an habit out of looking at them and I will be forever grateful if I could get your permission to gaze at yours&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> He makes his best to ignore the mention of sexual tension among members of the group.<br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;I am, of course, ready to provide any insight or help any of you may need, as well as medical attention of both the mundane and mystical sort. I might not walk the same Path as Lynx, here, but my constant practice has made me a Disciple of the Mysteries of Life. There is a lot that can be acomplished by mixing medical knowledge with mystical healing, I have found&quot;.</span></b><br /> <br /> Another sip of cofee.<br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;And, there is also the issue of the name. How are we going to call our Cabal? Names are quite important. They can define you... consume you...&quot;</span></b>- you think you can hear the faint sound of slithering scales.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 12-02-2016, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:35:58-08:00","id":1011336,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;The soul is a matter of profound fascination to a doctor like me, I have made an habit out of looking at them and I will be forever grateful if I could get your permission to gaze at yours&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;My soul is rather personal to me, but it wouldn't be the first time a mage studied it. I'm amenable if you don't touch it, and I can gaze back at you in return.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;And, there is also the issue of the name. How are we going to call our Cabal? Names are quite important. They can define you... consume you...&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> Was that a serpentine sound? He furrows his brow and plays with the tiles.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Tell me about it. I haven't used my dead name since the Clinton years. Storm...knights. Storm lords. Storm chasers. Seven instead of six members would be preferable for numerology, but we have options. Hexagrams? I have more affinity with I Ching hexagrams than the Abrahamic six-pointed star, but both have powerful occult resonance...the Children of Aion? Honoring the Oracles is a good use of a name.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T18:51:19-08:00","id":1011778,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> <br /> </div> Ragnar looks down at his tiles and blinks. He lays the tiles down on the board: T-A-R-O-T. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Could tarot work? I've never tried to do a reading, but I know the symbolism behind them. I could do a ritual and try to divine a path forward for us.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T05:46:21-08:00","id":1011960,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">It's a great way to get to know one another, though,</span>&quot; Lynx murmurs. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I'd like to be useful to you lot, but in order to do that, knowing the gist of what you want is kinda necessary.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I guess,&quot;</span> I reply simply. Lynx's intentions are honest, so I can't fault him for that. I'll have to come up with something new to pursue to keep 'em off the scent (no pun intended), but I'm not sure what.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">The tension between you three is amusing. Touchable.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Well, if you're interested, we could make it a foursome,&quot;</span> I retort with a chuckle, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Would that be beastiality, though?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;The soul is a matter of profound fascination to a doctor like me, I have made an habit out of looking at them and I will be forever grateful if I could get your permission to gaze at yours&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> Huh, Pops always struck me as a purely scientific type, though he did manage to Awaken, so obviously there's more to him. Still, he's interested in souls of all things. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;What about the soul stands out to you?&quot;</span> my curiosity asks.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;And, there is also the issue of the name. How are we going to call our Cabal? Names are quite important. They can define you... consume you...&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> That sounded like...slithering? I would be more intrigued, but my gut speaks for me, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Yeah, no kidding.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Where did that come from? It's like-I somehow knew that all my life. Actually, it feels like I knew longer than that, but how is that possible? Oh hey! I could use that to throw them off the scent. That, and it's something I'd actually like to know, so I can kill two birds with one stone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Speaking of names, I chose a particularly...prominent one. Is reincarnation a thing?&quot;</span> I ask the group.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Tell me about it. I haven't used my dead name since the Clinton years. Storm...knights. Storm lords. Storm chasers. Seven instead of six members would be preferable for numerology, but we have options. Hexagrams? I have more affinity with I Ching hexagrams than the Abrahamic six-pointed star, but both have powerful occult resonance...the Children of Aion? Honoring the Oracles is a good use of a name.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;We should probably keep it simple and focus on what we've all got in common rather than numbers or Oracles or whatever, so the storm thing looks like a good place to start,&quot;</span> I suggest.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Could tarot work? I've never tried to do a reading, but I know the symbolism behind them. I could do a ritual and try to divine a path forward for us.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;How would the tarot get us a name?&quot;</span> I wonder, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Do we like, draw two cards and splice their names together or something?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T03:58:29-08:00","id":1012480,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Oh. Okay, because, I, uh, thought. You. Meant...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#008080\">Yes, we know. The sheer sexual tension is nearly unbearable. Moving on.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Well, if you're interested, we could make it a foursome. </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Would that be beastiality, though?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx goes still.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">I didn't mean...<br /> <br /> ...</span></i><br /> <br /> He remains quiet as the others carry on.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">We should probably keep it simple and focus on what we've all got in common rather than numbers or Oracles or whatever, so the storm thing looks like a good place to start.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I Awakened after the storm,</span>&quot; Lynx mumbles more to himself, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">But since we're all part of this ... well. Storm of events going on, maybe something like... Born of the Storm? Stormborn?</span>&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T12:52:22-08:00","id":1012732,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0<br /> </div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I Awakened after the storm. </span><span style=\"color:#800000\">But since we're all part of this ... well. Storm of events going on, maybe something like... Born of the Storm? Stormborn?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Ragnar perks up at that. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;How about 'The Stormborne'? With a silent 'e' on the end? That way, it refers to both the fact that some of us Awakened during and after the Deathstorm, and that we came together as a result of a Highstorm?&quot; </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 12-05-2016, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:39:09-08:00","id":1012787,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hear, hear. Stormborne with an 'e'. Short but sweet. I assent.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:30:34-08:00","id":1014277,"title":"","content":"<b>Everyone</b><br /> Just as Ragnar speaks the suggestion for the cabal name, one of the baristas walks past your table and suddenly slips on a napkin lying on the floor. She reflexively puts a hand on the table to catch herself, but it slips when it falls on a pile of Scrabble tiles. &quot;Whoa!&quot; she cries out, before unceremoniously dropping an empty coffee mug, some game tiles, and several packets of sugar. The mug bounces several times, but to her surprise, it ends up resting upright on the ground without a single chip or mark. &quot;Wow, that was lucky,&quot; she mutters to herself as she picks it up. &quot;Sorry for the mess, guys,&quot; she apologizes to your table with a blush before quickly moving back to the kitchen.<br /> <br /> As she leaves, Ragnar sees five tiles lying face up on the floor by his chair. The tiles read S-T-O-R-M. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Binder, Moonstone, and Phoenix each take a Beat for completing their &quot;join a cabal&quot; Aspiration. Replace it with a new one for those who haven't already indicated it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <b>* NEW SCENE *</b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> At the tail end of your conversation with your new cabal, you receive a phone call from an unknown number. <span style=\"color:darkslategray\">&quot;Why hello there,&quot;</span> a gravelly but energetic male voice says. <span style=\"color:darkslategray\">&quot;Just got a friendly call from a certain Rose, said you wanted to meet up and go digging through your brain. Sounds like just the kind of action I could use on a boring weekend. You free late tonight?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Shortly after the meeting ends, you finally get a text from Tanya. She asks if you could meet up with the group at the public library where she works in West Town. It's actually just a little west of you, not even a mile away, so you could walk there pretty easily.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm assuming that Phoenix is going to go meet up with the Hunter cell. For everyone else, let me know how you would like to spend the next few hours.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 12-08-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:16:17-08:00","id":1014356,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b><br /> </div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Small Talk&quot; spell ends. Everyone can be heard normally now. Also, resolved &quot;Join a Cabal&quot; for 1 Beat, and replaced it with &quot;Teach a cabalmate something about magic.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Before everyone leaves, Moonstone explains that those Stormborne with an affinity for Space (like himself) will be able to cast sympathetic magic on the cabal more easily if they have a recent photo, and asks permission to take one. After letting anyone decline who doesn't want a record, he snaps a group picture on his phone, and shares the yantra with Binder and anyone else who asks. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;It won't make it to social media- I don't even <i>have </i>Twitter.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As they're exiting, he suggests to Ragnar that this is a good time to work on Space. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;We'll take the train downtown first. I'll make the city into a labyrinth, just for you. You'll need to expand your understanding of Space to escape. But I'll be watching, so don't worry- oh, someone's calling me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Unknown number. Wait, how did he...oh, right, magic. Goosebumps as he realizes just how easily other mages can reach him, without Hakim's protection. Time to practice his wards. He answers: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Ah. I know who this is. Yes, I need what only you can give me, uh, baby. My evening is open. Where should we meet?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> After the call, he lays his hand on Ragnar's shoulder and opens the cabal photo on his phone. Once he's studied it intently and worked it into his Imago, he rifles through his bag and gazes into his mirror. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Just checking today's weather.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting my Praxis, Divination, on Ragnar at touch range. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for detailed answers.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Time 2, material sympathy +2, path tool +1, willpower +3. 9 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464025\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>. That's exceptional with a Praxis, I'll regain that willpower and take Inspired for this teaching session.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Imago takes shape. Moonstone reorients his awareness relative to Time, peeks around the corner, and asks: <i>Will stranding Ragnar in the city place him in serious danger? </i>And, <i>Will magically confusing his senses and making him overcome the hex be a useful learning experience for him?</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:01:58-08:00","id":1014721,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You guessed right, rwknoll. As for the Aspiration, I'm replacing it with &quot;Aid Moonstone in defeating Alux&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Stormborne, eh? I like that. It's short and sweet, and accurate. Now that we're a cabal, it looks like time for me to depart for more pressing matters. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;be there few min&quot;</span> I text to Tanya right after saying my goodbyes to the group. That was a pretty quick response, considering the backlog they supposedly had, and convenient. In fact, it was precisely timed and within walking distance. That's a little fishy, best be on guard when I get there.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On arrival at the library, Phoenix will make a perception check on anything suspicious.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464302\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Composure 2 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Finding Tanya at the library, I approach cautiously, making sure I've got a clean exit should the need arise. I pick through the book shelves for something on mythology, sit near Tanya, and open the book on a random page as a bit of cover. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;So, what's up?&quot;</span> I ask, my eyes on the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:52:25-08:00","id":1014899,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkslategray\">&quot;HA!&quot;</span> Spade laughs loudly. <span style=\"color:darkslategray\">&quot;I like you. You're great. Don't ever change,&quot;</span> he replies. <span style=\"color:darkslategray\">&quot;Look, this is really something you need to do in a place you trust. Someplace safe. Your sanctum. And while we're at it, might be best for someone else to come, just in case things get hairy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In your mind's eye, the mirror cracks, with each new sliver revealing a possible future. Countless possible outcomes simultaneously play out, but several clear trends provide the answers you seek. <i>He will be in danger from a mage, but not mortal danger.</i><br /> <br /> The scenes are all different, but all share the image of a shifty-looking man with a smirk that you clearly recognize. You don't actually know him by name, but you saw him once at Hakim's apartment less than two weeks ago. You were on your way to meet your master, and saw him and this man having a heated argument in hushed tones just as you arrived. The man hastily left and disappeared when you arrived. Hakim refused to talk about it.<br /> <br /> <i>The lesson will be useful for showing him another perspective about magic and other dangers.</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s5.favim.com/orig/51/guy-boy-punk-rock-style-skater-Favim.com-470960.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Pssst...I went back and edited <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991693#post991693\">this post</a> because I realize I never put a picture there, but this is the same mage that Phoenix saw and is currently looking for.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Nothing seems particularly fishy or suspicious when you arrive at the library. On a Saturday in the middle of the day, there is a steady flow of pedestrian traffic in and out of the building.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://interactivedesignarchitects.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/DSC_7984-Pano-1024x444.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You find Tanya after a few minutes of walking around the library. She's busy shelving books, and tries to play it cool when you walk up by not paying you too much attention and just focusing on the books in her hands. &quot;The rest of the group is in a study room in the back,&quot; she says quietly. &quot;I can't step away for too long or I'll get in trouble, but I'll try to swing by in a bit.&quot; She glances at you and smiles briefly, then gets back to her work.<br /> <br /> Looking through the glass door into the study room, you see a table, a few chairs, a desktop computer in the corner, and the last possible group of people you'd expect to find in the same place. TJ's there, tapping away rapidly at his laptop, so absorbed in his task that he doesn't even look up. The other three you remember well, but haven't seen them in weeks. Brandon is a pyro, and even here in the library he's flicking a Zippo lighter on and off. He smirks as you approach and nods to you. Gretchen is a petite young woman with long brown hair, round-framed glasses, and a stack of books piled a foot high next to the one she's tearing through. And Thomas is an older heavyset man with thin, graying hair and a nervous smile. &quot;Oh, greetings, Garrick!&quot; he says to you as you enter the room.<br /> <br /> Gretchen is still too busy reading to even look at you. Actually, you're not even sure she has realized yet that you're here.<br /> <br /> TJ eventually pauses and looks up to you. &quot;Hey,&quot; he offers casually in way of greeting. He closes his laptop and shoots an annoyed glare at Brandon. &quot;Knock it off, dude.&quot; Brandon rolls his eyes but pockets his lighter. TJ continues, &quot;We finally had a chance to get together and thought we'd see if you were free to talk. I feel like we're on the verge of figuring something out about these storms, it's just not clear.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can attempt your Social Maneuvering again to help convince the Hunter cell to assist you with finding the mage you're seeking. Pick a roll that makes sense and describe how you'd like to convince them to help.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:11:58-08:00","id":1014911,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 4/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> Lynx remains wordless as they round off their meeting. He agrees to Moonstone's photoshoot and puts up a smile, and he gives them all farewells before hitting the bus on the way home. <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Sex, huh...</span></i><br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Lynx finds himself in the woods as dusk falls. The rest of his day had gone by quietly as he had spent today alone in the flat - Ewan popped in to change some clothes for some occasion which he seemed excited to attend - and he looks around for Raven. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T22:55:02-08:00","id":1015168,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 6/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Thank...you.&quot;</span> What a flattering complete stranger Spade is! <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I was thinking the same thing. It's in La Grange. Call again for the address when you're close.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He waves down Binder before he leaves. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Can I take you up on that offer of your ritual space? The summoning is tonight, and I have to host. I'd be glad if you were present.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>That face.</i><br /> <br /> He had forgotten it until now. Seeing it again, now, in Ragnar's future, is a punch to the gut. His eyes are wide as he gazes into the future, one hand on Ragnar's shoulder still.<br /> <br /> <i>Not mortal danger, but not safe. </i>He should warn his new cabalmate- but. This is a potential lead. Someone who saw Hakim is potentially entering his future. And don't they say that warning people about their future is how you change it? If Ragnar backs out or changes his approach, the man might slip out of the stream of possibility. And after all, the point is to challenge him and force learning.<br /> <br /> He pockets his things, obviously lost in thought. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Listen: keep your wits about you. There might be, um...well, I'll keep an eye on you. You won't be alone if you run into trouble.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Moonstone leads Ragnar to a CVS down the block. As they wander the aisles under artificial lighting, he quietly explains: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Challenge is how we learn. I was thinking all through coffee about it, trying to think like a mage. When you're put in a new situation, you can't do what you always do. You have to find a new path. New tools. If you <i>must </i>use Space, you <i>will. </i>Oh, here it is.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He buys a 99-cent bright red Superball off the rack in the toys aisle. They proceed to the nearest metro stop, climb the stairs, and sit on a bench. Moonstone draws out a length of black silk from his bag. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm going to blindfold you. Don't worry, I'm very good at it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And he is. He hums a tune in the cool station as they wait for a train. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hold out your hand.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He places the Superball in Ragnar's palm. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Don't look at. Feel where it is in Space. Find it. Got it? Give it back. It's in my pocket now. Do you still feel it?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He opens his Space Sight for just a few seconds to watch and make sure he casts an appropriate Knowing spell. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;All you need to do for this exercise is draw a line between two points. Point A is the ball. Point B is the lobby of Willis Tower. And we're going to take the train there right now. Easy. Hold my hand, please. I don't want you to get separated.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> For the next half hour, they're boarding trains, riding them for a few stops, then abruptly getting off and crossing the platform to another line. It doesn't seem to serve any purpose beyond getting hopelessly lost. But Moonstone makes intermittent quiet conversation when they're sitting together. Not about magic, just...stuff. It's easier to be open when he has the other person at his mercy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;When I first came to Chicago, I thought the L was the coolest thing. I was an absolute tourist- I'm from LA originally. It's all cars there.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So, you have classes with Lynx and Ophis? How do you find them?...In another life, I did a dance program at UCLA, but I dropped out to come here. I've always been an awful student. I couldn't listen.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not like this because of a curse, just so you know. Or some kind of divine madness. I used to think that was it. I have what's called <i>emotionally unstable personality disorder. </i>It means I react badly to stress and, um, being surprised by other people. Just so you know.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He's been forming an Imago during their trip. If you drew their train-switching route on a map, it would be a line that eternally circled Willis Tower without ever getting any closer to it. Ouroborous would be proud. As the blue line slows down, he looks at the picture of Ragnar on his phone and instructs him: <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Drop your defenses.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Improvising a Space spell in the vein of Lying Maps, with Mind 2 mixed in for some special effects. Ragnar will perceive downtown Chicago as an Inception/Dr. Strange-esque urban labyrinth: buildings growing upside down, blocks extending infinitely in all directions, corners that go nowhere, and Willis Tower looming over everything like the Dark Tower it is, but seemingly impossible to reach.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, he inflicts the Lost Condition on Ragnar, and gives him a [Potency] penalty to the Wits+Streetwise roll. I assume an Acanthus has various ways to get around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD 289</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">LOST<br /> Your character has no idea where she is, or how to reach<br /> her target. She cannot make any headway toward her goal<br /> without first navigating and finding out where she is. This<br /> requires a successful Wits + Streetwise action (in the city) or<br /> Wits + Survival action (in the wilderness).<br /> Resolution: Abandoning the goal, successfully navigating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space 2 &quot;Urban Jungle&quot;, Veiling, primary factor Duration. Touch range. 1 Reach for instant, 1 Reach to change primary to Potency, 1 Reach for advanced duration. 2 paradox dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464529\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Space 2, Environment +1, Material sympathy +2. Resolving Inspired for this roll. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464530\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Potency 2, scene duration.<br /> <br /> +1 willpower and +1 arcane beat from Inspired.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The hex takes hold as the train comes to a stop somewhere in the Loop. As soon as the door opens and people get up, he hurls the Superball out onto the elevated platform. Mercifully, it's facing the street, not another train. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Willis Tower. Follow the bouncing ball!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He gets off a few stops later, once he's alone. Less of a walk that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T11:26:36-08:00","id":1015315,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>7 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Stormborne it is, then. Very appropiate, fitting&quot;</span></b>- The meeting ends and everyone goes their separate ways. Ouroboros just wanders to the nearest graveyard, he wants to test something that has been in his mind since Dante revealed to him how ghosts where apparently everywhere.<br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Ok, then&quot;</span></b>-he takes a long breath-<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;Let's do this&quot;</b></span>-he exhales and in doing so opens his Sight looking for Death resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 12-10-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:41:16-08:00","id":1015487,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 5/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0</div> <br /> <br /> Ragnar crowds in with the others for the picture, throwing a friendly arm around Lynx's shoulder before separating and leaving with Moonstone.<br /> <br /> Moonstone removes his hand from Ragnar's shoulder and his expression is troubled. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Listen: keep your wits about you. There might be, um...well, I'll keep an eye on you. You won't be alone if you run into trouble.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">He used Time to look ahead. He must have seen something that concerns him. But what? </span></i>Ragnar's lips begin to move, but he stops and begins to gather magic to himself so that he might look forward in time... but stops himself. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><i>No. Trust him. Even if you're angry with him, he's not an enemy. There's no reason for you to think he's trying to set you up. </i></span>Whatever happens, Ragnar is just going to trust that Moonstone will be able to bail him out. And the Warlock has proven himself skilled in combat.<br /> <br /> He arcs an eyebrow as Moonstone purchases the ball, but remains obediently silent. He remains silent as he is blindfolded.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Hold out your hand.&quot; </span>Ragnar obeys, and feels the sudden wait of the Superball. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Don't look at. Feel where it is in Space. Find it. Got it?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Aha! Moonstone is probably going to move the ball around and make him sense it at varying distances, probably. He opens himself to magic and attempts to sense Space. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Where there is Time, there must also be Space. Threads running in different directions to form the fabric of reality itself. How can you claim to understand Time if you don't understand Space?</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to cast Locate Object (Space 1) as an Improvised Spell. He has one free Reach, which he will use for Instant casting. He will spend two further Reach, one for Advanced Scale, and the other for Advanced Duration. 2 Reach = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464739\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> With no Paradox risked, Ragnar moves on to the Casting Roll. He pays 1 Mana for a Common Arcana spell. Gnosis 1 + Space 1 + Willpower 3 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464743\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. He has expended a Mana and a Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It takes a good deal of focus to grasp Space, to feel the ball in his hand. Oh, he <i>definitely </i>needs to practice Space.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Give it back. It's in my pocket now. Do you still feel it?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar reaches out, and sure enough, the ball is in Moonstone's pocket, almost like he reached his hand in to find it. He allows himself a small, pleased smile. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;Oh, yeah.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;All you need to do for this exercise is draw a line between two points. Point A is the ball. Point B is the lobby of Willis Tower. And we're going to take the train there right now. Easy. Hold my hand, please. I don't want you to get separated.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Okay. Slightly more complicated than he thought. But it shouldn't been too difficult. But he can't help but get just a tad snarky. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Why worry? I'm going to be able to sense that thing for the next hour from a building away.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;When I first came to Chicago, I thought the L was the coolest thing. I was an absolute tourist- I'm from LA originally. It's all cars there.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;I'm from a small town in Amish country in Pennsylvania. It's the same thing. Expect, you know, less congested.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;So, you have classes with Lynx and Ophis? How do you find them?...In another life, I did a dance program at UCLA, but I dropped out to come here. I've always been an awful student. I couldn't listen.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Lynx is... sweet. He's straightforward and honest. He doesn't seem to like politics and conflict. I hope he finds an Order that's a good fit. The Mysterium is pretty apolitical, right? Ophis is still a bit of an unknown to me. But I'm surprised he knows Phoenix. Speaking of which...&quot; he lowers his voice. &quot;He's had training somewhere. Could he have been a Sleepwalker? Or is he something else entirely?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I'm not like this because of a curse, just so you know. Or some kind of divine madness. I used to think that was it. I have what's called <i>emotionally unstable personality disorder. </i>It means I react badly to stress and, um, being surprised by other people. Just so you know.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">So he does have a disorder. Good to know. </span></i><br /> <br /> Then the door opens, and then the city turns into a kaleidoscope. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Okay. Do not meddle in the affairs of Warlocks, because they will give you such a freaking headache. </span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Willis Tower. Follow the bouncing ball!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Okay, he's going to need as much help as he can get. He begins tugging at the strings of Fate, trying to tether himself to the ball that he senses is bouncing away even as he casts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will cast his Exceptional Luck (Fate 2) Praxis. 1 free Reach, spent for Instant Casting. One extra Reach for casting beyond his limit. 1 Reach = 1 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464748\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a>.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Fate 2 = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464749\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Oh, come on. </i></span><br /> <br /> He rushes after the ball, trying to keep in range of it. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Follow the bouncing red ball, follow the bouncing red ball. Follow, follow, follow, follow, follow the bouncing red ball.</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is going to attempt to navigate his way to the Willis Tower. Wits 2 - Streetwise 1 - Lost 2 = chance dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/464750\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To summarize: Ragnar has spent a Mana, a Willpower, has Locate Object as an active spell, is currently suffering from the Lost condition, and whatever consequence comes out of the Dramatic Failure.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 12-11-2016, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:17:45-08:00","id":1015803,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 9/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> Moonstone gets off at the next stop. He's going to have a learning experience of his own by seeing how well he can shadow Ragnar at a distance during his ordeal.<br /> <br /> As he's leaving the station, he falls in behind a crowd of people pushing toward the exit. Drawing on their mutual anonymity as city-dwellers, he forms an Imago to make himself just another generic face in the crowd, and eventually no one at all.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Incognito Presence on himself. 1 reach for instant, 1 reach for advanced duration, 1 reach for exceeding spell control. 2 paradox dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/465119\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Wisdom to contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/465120\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>, 1 bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Mind 2, Environment 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/465122\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. 1 Mana spent. Moonstone is unseen for the scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Lie bites back, but the magic takes hold. Once he gets out to the street, he takes out his mirror and phone and traces circles with his finger until the glass grows cloudy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Scrying on Ragnar! 1 reach for instant, 1 for sensory range, 1 for advanced duration, 1 to make primary factor potency, 2 for exceeding spell control. Spending 2 Mana to reduce paradox. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/465126\" target=\"_blank\">fail.</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Space 2, sympathy yantra 0, path tool 1, Potency -4, Willpower 3. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/465127\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Potency 4 should overcome Withstand 3 for Weak sympathy. Scrying is active for the scene.<br /> <br /> edit: wait, it would be Withstand 4 because he doesn't know sympathetic name. Potency 5 would be another -2. I'll just dramatic fail it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 12-11-2016, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:18:37-08:00","id":1017022,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Hey guys,&quot;</span> I greet as I enter the study room. I skim through the pages of my book, waiting when the others are ready.<br /> <br /> &quot;We finally had a chance to get together and thought we'd see if you were free to talk. I feel like we're on the verge of figuring something out about these storms, it's just not clear.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Are the storms anything but clear?&quot;</span> I joke, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;But seriously, what have you guys found?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:45:56-08:00","id":1017733,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 4/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [Shaken]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Beats: 0 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Can I take you up on that offer of your ritual space? The summoning is tonight, and I have to host. I'd be glad if you were present.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder nods. <span style=\"color:purple\">&quot;Absolutely. Say around midnight? That'll let me make sure my absence from home isn't noticed.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:06:52-08:00","id":1018676,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> Dusk settles peacefully on La Grange. It's a pleasant evening as you enter Bemis Woods, the forest preserves on the north side of La Grange where you met Raven before. The forest is quiet, but you're not alone as you enter the trails leading into the woods; you occasionally pass by the occasional jogger or couple taking an evening stroll. You notice that most of the people you pass are leaving the forest rather than traveling in your direction. Not many people seem to want to be here in the evening.<br /> <br /> Your ears pick up a faint howl in the distance. You pass a few signs warning of coyotes, but see nothing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.saltcreekgreenwayassociation.org/images/Cricket%20Creek/image%208%20CC%20DDolecki.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> After about half an hour of walking into the woods without any sign of Raven, you come across Salt Creek, located at the heart of Bemis Woods. The hairs on the back of your neck rise as a chill passes down your spine, just as a distinct odor begins to fills your nose on your Periphery. The sensation grows, indicating something -- or some things -- supernatural in your presence. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;You feel them, don't you?&quot;</span> Raven speaks softly to you, making only a quiet rustle as she glides up to you from the woods. Your new mentor is cloaked in a simple brown robe, held around her body with a forest green rope belt. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Spirits are not native to the Fallen World, but they often come here. To an Apprentice of Spirit, you can instinctively sense their very presence.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven smiles and turns to you. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Tonight, I will teach you some of the essential tools at a Shaman's disposal. Politics must wait. It is critical that you learn about spirits, as it will aid you and your allies immensely.&quot;</span> She purses her lips thoughtfully. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;You are not yet an initiate of the Mysterium, but since you are interested in joining, I will offer you a glimpse of the knowledge you can gain from us.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven takes a breath and begins to speak to you, but the sounds coming from her mouth are like nothing you've ever heard in English or Norwegian. The words sound like gibberish, but as you hear them, your Periphery explodes with colors, senses, and emotions. It's like communicating in imagery rather than words, but somehow your Awakened mind instinctively translates the symbolic intent of her speech. <span style=\"color:indigo\"><i>&quot;You must command the world with the Supernal tongue.&quot;</i></span><br /> <br /> Raven asks you to sit on a bench in a secluded part of the woods overlooking the creek. For the next hour, she carefully instructs you on the uses of High Speech. It feels awkward and foreign, but with her guidance, you gradually find yourself growing accustomed to this new form of speech. Somehow, it feels natural to you, just waiting for an opportunity to be unleashed.<br /> <br /> Your mentor nods and smiles. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;I think you are ready to try it. Form a spell in your mind's eye, and chant in High Speech to imbue the magic with Supernal symbolism.&quot;</span> She watches you closely with a critical eye to study the results of your spellcasting attempt.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may now use your <b>High Speech</b> merit, which comes from your Order. A narrative description of High Speech is on p. 66, and details about the mechanics of using High Speech as a Yantra is found on p. 120. Essentially, it grants a +2 bonus to spellcasting, but can't be used reflexively; if you use it in combat or while in initiative, it takes an action/turn to chant, and then you can cast on your next turn using the bonus. Outside of time-limited situations, however, you can use it for any spells you wish.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> Your spell snaps into place, and although you can't see the world through the hex that you've created for Ragnar, your Imago is firmly held in your mind. You watch your new cabalmate leave the train, and easily find yourself lost in thought about the man from your glimpse into Ragnar's very near future.<br /> <br /> You wince in pain at the Paradox from your spellcasting, but the spell thankfully takes hold. Within moments, everyone nearby looks away from you, subconsciously moving out of your way but immediately forgetting you were ever there. You're just another face in the crowd.<br /> <br /> As you exit the train and begin to cast your own Space magic, you press your will against the symbolic connections tying you to Ragnar the way a guitarist might pluck a string. But your efforts slip, and interference from your own Space hex on Ragnar creates dissonance. The magic reverberates, and suddenly you find yourself in the very urban labyrinth you have placed Ragnar in. The buildings shrink and then grow and loom over you, and car horns sound from everywhere at once as you hopelessly spin in a circle. You're utterly lost.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You take an Arcane Beat for resolving Inspired. For the dramatic failure on the spellcasting, you take another Arcane Beat; mechanically, for the condition resulting from that dramatic failure, I'm just going to give you the same <b>Lost </b>condition -- the above is just a narrative description. Before you can attempt to Scry on Ragnar or navigate in the city, you'll need to resolve the Lost condition by making a successful Wits + Streetwise roll.<br /> <br /> Also, unless I'm mistaken, for the Scrying roll you actually have an extra die in that Paradox pool because of multiple Paradox rolls in the same scene. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/467228\" target=\"_blank\">Extra Paradox</a>: 1 success.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You step off the train as Moonstone throws the ball, and find yourself in a world that warps all sense of physics and logic. The streets seem to shrink and expand, turning without moving, and buildings collapse and sprout new skyscrapers. The sensation is dizzying.<br /> <br /> And in the midst of the illusion gripping you, through the chaos and the confusion before you eyes, you sense the ball with perfect clarity. You know which way it's moving, so you try to move in that direction -- and suddenly find yourself moving in multiple directions at once. The ball moves farther and farther away as it bounces down the street, but you struggle to make your way through the city towards it. Knowing precisely where you need to go, but finding yourself lost in a maze of where exactly &quot;there&quot; is, threatens to send your mind into apoplexy.<br /> <br /> You attempt to wrap good luck like a Fate-woven blanket around you, but in your confusion, the spell collapses and the Lie cuts into you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Like Caladriu, I believe you forgot to add 1d10 to your Paradox roll for multiple consecutive Paradox rolls in a scene. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/467638\" target=\"_blank\">Extra Paradox</a>: <b>1 success</b>. You didn't state in your post, but I'll assume that you would attempt to contain it. Feel free to roll Wisdom to do so, or indicate if you would release it.<br /> <br /> Also, you actually rolled a 5 on that chance die; the 0 that came up is the number of successes. So it's only a normal failure, unless you want to opt to make it a dramatic one for a beat. I'll treat it as a normal failure for now unless you tell me otherwise.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> When you leave the cafe, you find yourself drawn by a strong desire to travel to a cemetery. Everything Dante has taught you so far has left you with a thirst you haven't been able to quench. You hop on a train at the Chicago Metra station again by the church and head north before you really know where you're headed. As you travel north to Uptown, you find yourself heading to the Graceland Cemetery, a historic 19th century graveyard with many notable people interred there, including old several mayors of Chicago.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://archaeology-travel.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/04/graceland-cemetery-schoenhofen-detail.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Even before you walk through the main entrance, your skin is tingling and the hairs on your neck are rising. With your budding knowledge of Death and recent exposure to ghosts, you instinctively associate this sensation with the presence of ghosts around you. That sensation intensifies as you enter the graveyard, and even though it's sunny on this late summer afternoon, you feel a chill pass down your spine.<br /> <br /> When you open your Sight through the lens of your Path to Stygia, the Fallen World fades and the ghosts appear around you. As earlier with Dante, these ghosts seem unaware of, or unresponsive to, their immediate surroundings. There is a pure quality of death here, a kind of quiet serenity resting on the entire premises. You wander down the sidewalks through the cemetery, all but oblivious to the living beings wandering past you as you drink in the resonance of this cemetery.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://farm8.static.flickr.com/7091/7161599591_619e56c7a7_m.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You walk by a largue mausoleum in a secluded area of the cemetery, and your eyes are drawn to an intricate stone carving of a snake coiled around a door handle. You walk towards the mausoleum and notice a change in your Periphery, a different quality to the peaceful but stale smell of Death; to your Sight, here you see the air ripple in a shadowed crevice behind the tomb. It appears to form a door, which to your eyes appears to consume all light falling on it.<br /> <br /> As you study the door, you see a ghost of some middle-aged woman whom you don't recognize slowly walk up to the doorway. She reaches out her hands and steps forward, and the shadows engulf her.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You may roll Wits + Occult for a gut feeling about what the Avernian Gate might be or what it might do.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Thomas smiles and opens his mouth to reply, but Brandon snorts and cuts in. &quot;A fat load of horse shit, that's what we've found, if you ask me,&quot; He either ignores or doesn't notice TJ's eye roll or Thomas' hurt expression at being interrupted. &quot;We've been going over all of this for weeks. We already know the weather here is shitty. Anyone who's ever <i>visited </i>Chicago knows that. And yeah, bad things happen to people after a lot of the weirdest storms. But what was so special about this big one?&quot;<br /> <br /> Frowning, Thomas pauses thoughtfully and begins to reply when Gretchen suddenly and loudly sighs in exasperation, startling the older man. &quot;This doesn't make any sense,&quot; she complains. She moves a book over and you notice she has a notepad and pencil on the table, covered in complex formulas and mathematic equations that you couldn't even begin to recreate. Gretchen looks like she's barely 18. &quot;<i>All</i> weather patterns should be largely predictable, at least to a calculable degree for the immediate future. But the algorithms I'm using simply can't account for sufficient variance in these specific weather patterns.&quot; She furrows her eyebrows and adjusts her glasses while muttering under her breath, then begins to quickly erase some of her writing. &quot;Perhaps if I use the Fibonacci sequence...&quot;<br /> <br /> TJ and Brandon start to bicker about &quot;the mission&quot; they're on, and Gretchen seems like she's in her own world as she chews on her lower lip and rapidly does some calculations. Just as Tanya walks up to the door and quietly steps in, Thomas finally slams the table with a fist and announces angrily, &quot;I saw <i>him</i> again!&quot;<br /> <br /> The room suddenly goes quiet as TJ and Brandon stop their argument mid-sentence, and Gretchen even pauses in her work to look up at Thomas with a frown. From her place leaning against the wall, Tanya smiles and crosses her arms, looking at the older man. Thomas blinks and blushes, but he continues earnestly, &quot;I swear I saw the man again! This was one of those people I saw immediately after that terrible storm almost two weeks ago, the one who wears the fancy suits. He was looking at one of the bodies the police discovered. I know I've got the picture somewhere...&quot;<br /> <br /> As Thomas clumsily fishes his phone out of his pocket, he explains, &quot;I was at mass this morning at Saint John Cantius -- it's a lovely place, I've been going there for years, my sons were baptized there -- anyway, I was at mass and when I left, I saw there were some people going to some room blocked off for a private event. And I saw him! Look, this is his picture. Garrick, don't you think this could mean something?&quot;<br /> <br /> Thomas hands over his phone to you. It's an older flip phone, and the image screen is laughably small. But as best as you can tell, the picture looks remarkably like Valentine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Your afternoon passes without incident, thankfully. A quick search of the house when you return home reveals that Daisy and Forest are playing a board game in the living room. Forest is cheering enthusiastically and hopping around the room, causing Daisy to smirk and shake her head with amusement. She catches you looking in her direction and smiles warmly to you in greeting. &quot;Welcome home! How was the networking conference? Did it go as well as you hoped? Forest and I were just playing some games, but he's too smart for his own good. I guess he takes after his father,&quot; she winks.<br /> <br /> Later, after you and Daisy read bedtime stories to Forest and put him to bed, you and Daisy spend some time relaxing in the living room. During your conversation about your day, she asks, &quot;How have things been going at the bookstore, Marlin? I feel like we haven't talked about it very much lately. It seems like you've had a lot going on with the business lately. Is everything okay?&quot; She doesn't necessarily seem concerned, just curious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T03:21:17-08:00","id":1018752,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 3/5 (one spent during post, was at 4) Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> Lynx listens eagerly, wordlessly to Raven, nodding in acknowledgement of the presence of Spirits. He revels in the realisation that he finally has somebody who <i>gets</i> it! He practises the strange tongue to the best of his ability, noting that each word is only what it is, not open to interpretation - noting that each word is <i>truth</i>. <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">I think you are ready to try it. Form a spell in your mind's eye, and chant in High Speech to imbue the magic with Supernal symbolism.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He closes his eyes and takes a deep breath. <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">I already know what I want to sense.</span></i> He touches his pendant, his finger caressing the feline representation of his namesake. He expands his senses as far as he can, tapping into the pulse of life that only nature can represent, and he represents his intent through the Primal High Speech.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx attempts to cast Life 1 &quot;Web of Life&quot;, reaching for Instant, Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale. He innately specifies Humans, Animals (i.e., mammals and reptilians, not insects or bacteria) and Birds.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Lynx.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Advanced, 1 Week.<br /> <b>Scale:</b> Advanced, large warehouse or supermarket.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice), High Speech (+2 dice).<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Life 1 &quot;Web of Life&quot;: Life (3) + Gnosis (1) + High Speech (2) + Willpower (3) - Scale (4)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 3 Free Reaches: 1 on Instant Cast, 1 on Advanced Duration, 1 on Advanced Scale.<br /> <br /> <b>There is no risk of Paradox.</b><br /> <b>Total Dice Pool:</b> 5 dice. <br /> <br /> Roll for Life 1 &quot;Web of Life&quot; \u2192 2 successes.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:23:41-08:00","id":1018818,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> You take a deep breath and begin to speak using this new form of language. You firmly use High Speech to create vocal images of your will.<br /> <br /> As the spell settles, the forest explodes in life. Scents of all kinds of creatures fill your nose. You feel your heart beat in rhythm with the forest, and it echoes with the hearts of all the beasts in a large radius around you. Instinctively, you <i>feel</i> the bats and owls flying through the trees hunting prey, the deer lapping water from the creek, the squirrels and snakes and field mice roaming through the woods. There is so much <i>life</i> here that it's nearly overwhelming. <br /> <br /> Raven has been watching you closely, and at your reaction to the spell taking effect, she nods decisively and smiles again. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Oh, excellent, young cub. You must continue to practice this tool so it can serve you well. But remember, you must chant long enough to form the Speech in a meaningful way, so be careful when you are in distress.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven takes a seat beside you on the bench and says, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Some of the Mystagogue's best scholars believe that the High Speech is in ways related to the tongue of the spirits. It shares some qualities, but it is distantly related enough that we must use other magic or abilities to understand their native language.&quot;</span> She frowns as if annoyed by that inconvenience. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Now, tell me. What do you know about spirits? What have you learned already from your own studies and your first journey to the Primal Wild?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T09:20:54-08:00","id":1018829,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration), Incognito Presence (self, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors), Lost [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b>BOOOOO <b>| Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 6/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 2/5</b><br /> </div><br /> Invisible, and utterly lost. Breath catching in his chest. Suddenly realizing how much he doesn't know, how far he's out of his depth. Don't be a lifeguard if you can't pass the swim test!<br /> <br /> He stumbles away from a speeding car that seems to come from all directions. The drivers can't see him, of course. What do they say about labyrinths? If he can just get to a solid wall, he'll be able to push through. He tries to navigate to a sidewalk and run his hands along an edifice without colliding with anyone in the kaleidoscope.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">retroactively releasing the Scrying paradox.<br /> <br /> Wits+Streetwise should be 2 dice. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/467870\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> <br /> Unless my roll has a -2 penalty from my spell like Ragnar did? If so, I'll dramatic fail it and presumably get hit by a car that can't see Moonstone or something lol. Either way, my intent is to navigate to Willis Tower. Scrying is probably beyond Moonstone's abilities at present. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T08:30:36-08:00","id":1019251,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Locate Object<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 4/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0</div> <br /> <br /> The Lie beats at him. He knows what is going to come of it: he can either let the Paradox taint the world, or he can turn it in on himself. Memories of the fight with Alux flash through his mind, and he rejects the former option. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><i>Suffer the consequences of your own mistakes, Ragnar. Don't punish the world for your clumsiness.</i> </span><br /> <br /> Steeling himself for the pain he knows is coming, Ragnar attempts to force the Paradox inwards on his own body. He tells himself that it's better this way. But damn if he isn't having trouble believing it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to contain the Paradox. 7 Wisdom = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468212\" target=\"_blank\">oh dear</a>. And I think I'll keep the regular failure from the navigation roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But whether because he can't contain it or won't, the Paradox slips away from him, and into the world. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">No!</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 12-19-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:06:23-08:00","id":1019338,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> While casting your Scrying upon Ragnar, you reach beyond your abilities in attempt to contact your cabalmate, and don't notice the way the Lie tries to infect your spell. Just as you reach out to the sympathetic ties bonding you to him, dark energy hijacks your spell and flies through the ties.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So 1 reach option for the Paradox roll is to apply a Condition to the target of the spell. Because you're technically targeting Ragnar, he will take another condition as indicated below.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You frantically try to navigate your way through the city streets, caught in your own hex. But you have more experience with Space magic than Ragnar, and you also know exactly how this hex works. You assert your will against the Imago trapping you, and just as your fingers clutch onto a brick wall of a building that seems miles away, the spell shatters around you. Now, you're just standing on a sidewalk along an old building in downtown Chicago. The buildings are blissfully still.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No -2 penalty to the roll, because the penalty was from the spell itself, not the condition. You may now attempt to navigate as you like, or scry again.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> As you try to navigate the horrible circus maze that currently surrounds you, an image suddenly pops into your mind of Moonstone, who has a frantic look on his face as he stretches his arms out searching for something. Your vision blurs as a dark energy settles onto you, and suddenly your mind roils with emotions as you've never experienced before. Feelings of nervousness and concern balloon out of control into waves of terror and hopelessness. You try to quell the emotions, but they are <i>so</i> powerful.<br /> <br /> Just as your emotions grow uncontrollably, the Lie overpowers you, and more dark energy is pulled directly into you. You feel a cloud of Abyssal power warp your mind's eye.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First, from Moonstone's released Paradox, you gain the following condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Divergent. </b>Your character has a difficult time relating to other people and himself. If the self is a bowl of clear water, his bowl ripples and boils and freezes and spills more easily than most in response to stimuli. Apply a -2 to all Social rolls and rolls involving Resolve. The character also has 1 less Withstand against Mind spells targeting them.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution:</u> This Condition is resolved when you regain your full Willpower pool.<br /> <br /> <u>Beat:</u> N/A<br /> <br /> In addition, you gain the <b>Abyssal Imago</b> Paradox condition (p. 117). This means that you need to spend 1 extra Reach on each spell, or the spell automatically fails and you add 1 dice to the Paradox roll for a given spell. So for example, if you normally would get 2 free reach on a spell and want to spend reaches on instant casting and advanced duration, you would also need to spend a third reach on the spell (now making it risk Paradox) for Abyssal Imago or else the spell automatically fails and still risks Paradox.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:20:02-08:00","id":1019446,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 3/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> Lynx listens determinedly to her words, pondering her inconvenience.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Now, tell me. What do you know about spirits? What have you learned already from your own studies and your first journey to the Primal Wild?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Mathias and his cabal did mention spirits like textbook, but I couldn't relate to that,</span>&quot; Lynx hums as he rubs his beard. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Spirits... are?</span> Lynx suggests. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I mean, a spirit of tranquility is just... that. It's nothing more and nothing less. They embody ideals, I think, of what we think of them, or... do we think of them as what they are because that's what they are?</span>&quot; He frowns for a moment, trying to work it in his head. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">I did meet a lion spirit, and he was arrogant and proud. At least, the one I met. I also know there are Great spirits,</span>&quot; he put emphasis on Great, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">The lion I spoke to claimed he was one - he wasn't - but also that he might know of one. I know there's a world beyond ours, the Shadow, I think it's called? A reflection of our world, the home of Spirits...</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> He looks at Raven, and then beyond her. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">That's where I'll find the Great Lynx, isn't it?</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T05:44:13-08:00","id":1019728,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> &quot;We've been going over all of this for weeks. We already know the weather here is shitty. Anyone who's ever <i>visited </i>Chicago knows that. And yeah, bad things happen to people after a lot of the weirdest storms. But what was so special about this big one?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;It had magic up the wazoo, that's what,&quot;</span> I answered, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I mean, yeah all of the weird storms have some kind of magic about them, but the big one was on steroids. I could barely focus on it directly at the time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;I was at mass this morning at Saint John Cantius -- it's a lovely place, I've been going there for years, my sons were baptized there -- anyway, I was at mass and when I left, I saw there were some people going to some room blocked off for a private event. And I saw him! Look, this is his picture. Garrick, don't you think this could mean something?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Uh...maybe?&quot;</span> I say as I look at the blurry picture, why do the ones who sound like conspiracy nuts only have blurry photos? <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Can't really tell who this is, so I can't say.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Probably Valentine, though, by the looks of it. The suit, was at the Consilium meeting, makes the most sense, but hey, it could've been some other mage. That's not important, though. What is important is the fact that Thomas is clearly obsessed with this, and I need to know why.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Something going on with this guy and you?&quot;</span> I probe, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Like, has this guy done anything to do or your loved ones or something? Don't get me wrong, I understand that, it's just something I think we should know is all.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T02:59:18-08:00","id":1020248,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>7 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> Ouroboros feels like his breath is taken away as he sees the middle aged woman ghost dissappearing though that... door. He cannot but remeber the way the ghost residing in his classroom moved on once Dante and him resolved his ties to this world of flesh, and wonder if this is something similar or a completely different phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So, What Is That Door? (Wits+Occult) = 4 dice = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468789\" target=\"_blank\">2 Successes!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> -<span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;No, this is different. They do not even look alike. Could this be some sort of permanent door to the Otherlife?&quot;</b></span>- For a moment his desire to know almost pushes him to cross it himself, but his rational mind soon takes over.- <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>&quot;No, there is a lot of things I do not know about this. As far as I know it may very well be impossible for a living person with a physical body to enter, but even if it that is not true it would be folly to conduct such a potentially risky experiment on my own without back up. I need to share this with Dante, maybe he can shed light on this mystery&quot;</b></span>.<br /> <br /> He takes mental and physical note of the location and description of the mausoleum and the strange &quot;ghost door&quot; phenomena. The snake imagery surrounding it all did not pass unnoticed to him. He remembers someone warning him about these kind of things happening when one had especially strong ties to his Shadow Name. Maybe he should take a break and be just Marvin for a while.<br /> <br /> With that thought he closed his Sight and went for a walk through an actual park, full of living, breathing people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:39:43-08:00","id":1020318,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Locate Object<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost, Divergent, Abyssal Imago<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 4/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0</div> <br /> <br /> The Abyss lashes out at him, punishing him not just for his own spell, but Moonstone's as well. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">At once, his mind is whirling with emotion and self-loathing. <i>Idiot. Fool. You honestly thought you could do this? About the only thing you're good for is fortune telling, you can't even manage to follow a ball, you're not a mage, you're a cold-reading fraud. And now you're lost and will never find you're way home. You'll die out here, die out here, die out here...</i></span><br /> <br /> Trying to work through the paralyzing fear, Ragnar reaches a hand into his pocket and clutches the handle of his silver knife for all it's worth. Trying desperately to follow the ball, he tries to form another spell around himself to aid him. He feels the stricture of the Abyss surround him, but the feel of the silver steadies the Imago he attempts to cast, if not his mind.<span style=\"color:#0000cd\"> <i>Not enough, I need this to work.</i> </span>Then, his mouth starts forming words in a language he has never heard or spoken before, but he knows the words: the same ones he spoke during his Awakening. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;What was now is again; what is shall be once more; what shall be was before.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar is attempting to cast his Exceptional Luck Praxis again to grant himself a Boon of +2 to a Streetwise roll. He has one free Reach, which he spends for Instant Casting. He then spends another Reach for Abyssal Imago.<br /> <br /> This is the third casting that Ragnar has performed in this scene, so he gains an additional two Paradox dice. He will offset this with his Dedicated Tool Yantra and spend a Mana to bring it down to a chance die. Excess Reach 1 + Prior Risk 2 - Dedicated Tool 1 - Mana 1 = chance dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468802\" target=\"_blank\">no success</a>.<br /> <br /> Ragnar will now move on to his spell-casting roll. He will use Mantra as a Yantra for a +2 to the spell casting roll. Gnosis 1 + Fate 2 + Mantra 2 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468803\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This time, the spell takes effect, and Ragnar continues to follow the ball.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to navigate to undo the effects of Lost. Wits 2 + Streetwise 2 - Lost 2 = 2 dice -&gt;<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468805\" target=\"_blank\"> nope</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To summarize, Ragnar has spent a Mana this turn.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 12-21-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:57:15-08:00","id":1020532,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration), Incognito Presence (self, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b>OOOOO<b> | Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 6/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay. Breathe. The fractal has resolved. Turns out, being an inscrutable magical teacher is actually really hard! Is this what Hakim had to learn, too? When do you get so good that it becomes effortless? Or does it never get easier, and you just learn to hide it better?<br /> <br /> It's not hard to navigate to the Tower when you're not hexed: it's the tallest building in the city. His confidence builds while he walks, and his steps fall into a hidden rhythm with the sounds of cars and pedestrians. As he gets to a corner, a flicker of an idea makes him turn right instead of left. 10 minutes later, he's in Millennium Park.<br /> <br /> He's still unseen, and immediately forgotten as he pushes through the crowd of pedestrians in front of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_Gate\" target=\"_blank\">Cloud Gate.</a> <i>Always wanted to do this.</i><br /> <br /> He ritually mantles himself in the Cloak of Night, walks past a group of tourists, and kneels in a meditative pose underneath the mirrored sculpture.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Trying to cast Scrying again, this seems like a good place to monitor Ragnar from. Reach: Instant free, Sensory +1, Primary Factor to Potency +1, advanced Duration +1, exceeding spell control +2. So that's 5. And +2 for consecutive Paradox rolls. 7 dice. I'll spend 2 Mana to get that down to 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468874\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> Wisdom 7 to contain: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468877\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Moonstone should now have 3 bashing damage since his earlier backlash has healed after 15 minutes.<br /> <br /> Yantras: sympathy +0, environment +1. Gnosis 1, Space 2, and Willpower +3. -6 for Potency 2&gt;5. 1 die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468882\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a><br /> <br /> Currently at 4 Mana, 6 Willpower, and 3 resistant bashing damage. Turning on Mind+Space Active Sight.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He's got a throbbing migraine and nothing to show for it. The Warlock groans. <i>I'm such a shitty teacher.</i><br /> <br /> He breathes out his frustration, opens his third eye and gazes up into the omphalos of the sculpture. There has to be <i>something </i>Mysterious at or around the Cloud Gate, and either way, it resonates with Moonstone's budding magical aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 12-21-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T07:00:14-08:00","id":1021258,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 3/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [<b>Shaken</b>]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Spell Control (1): Hidden Door, Sleep of the Just<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <i>We already discussed it!</i> is Marlin's immediate thought, but his mouth says something different. That discussion hadn't stuck very well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Oh, everything's going fine. Changing up the business plan a little. I heard recently that the best way to compete with the bigger retailers is focus more on a niche market, so I'm trying that out with some re-branding, some cycling of stock.&quot;</span> It's easy to talk earnestly about because it's true. It's just not the whole truth. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I mean, I'm sure the store isn't ever going to do more than cover its own expenses, but it'll be an interesting experience.&quot;</span> He shrugs, unworried. Having the bookstore barely break even was more than he'd expected when he started it. Further success would be nice, but nothing to break a sweat over.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Lying in bed next to Daisy that night, Marlin can't help but remember what she'd forgotten. <i>Of course</i> he'd told her. She was the first person he went to. She was like him, a skeptic who wanted to believe. She was going to <i>flip</i>. Well, he hadn't been wrong, exactly.<br /> <br /> He doesn't remember the conversation leading up to it, not really. It amounted to: <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;Oh god my husband has had a psychotic break.&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;No really Daisy, here, let me show you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He opened a scrying window to the bookstore. She gasped and stumbled backward, horror and pain on her face. Something about her reaction was off. Sure, it was a surprise, but..? She glanced between the tear in space and her husband, eyes glassy and uncomprehending, looking nothing like the intelligent, inquisitive woman that he loved, but rather like an animal having a torch waved in its face. She made a strangled sound. He ended the spell.<br /> <br /> Her expression slowly changed from terrified bewilderment to irritated anger. <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;How <i>could</i> you,&quot;</span> she hissed, <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;I don't even know what to say. What a horrible... <i>prank</i>. What were you thinking?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Wha- prank? What do you-&quot;</span> But he's already putting it together.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;I can't believe it, Marlin. I can hardly-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Daisy. What do you remember? <i>What </i>did I show you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;I, I,&quot;</span> she looked scared again. <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;S-something awful. I don't-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;No,&quot;</span> he commanded, drawing his developing persona around him. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;<i>Remember</i>.&quot;</span> He cast again, placing his hand on her forehead, dispelling the fog that had already gathered around the memory.<br /> <br /> Daisy screamed, staggered backward, bumped against the wall, slid to the floor, buried her head in her hands. <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;No, no, no,&quot;</span> she babbled, <span style=\"color:#cc99ff\">&quot;it's wrong, wrong, it hurts!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Binder looked on in horror.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;Daddy?&quot;</span> Forest in the hallway, tired and confused. <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;What's going on? What's wrong with Mommy?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I'm not sure,&quot;</span> Binder said hopelessly. It was all going wrong.<span style=\"color:#800080\"> &quot;Come here, son.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Forest obeyed, scared but trusting, even when Binder pulled out the bronze knife. <i>If remembering is what hurts, then maybe forgetting will fix this.</i> He touched both of them with the knife, gently, following a ritual that came to him in bits and pieces. Daisy flinched, but didn't resist. Forest stared at his mother, starting to cry. <i>Forget</i>, Binder mouthed, as he cut away their memories of that night.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Marlin slowly comes out of his recollection, and drowsily checks his phone. Daisy's breathing has slowed, and he's still got plenty of time to get to the shop. He quietly gets up and prepares the spell that should ensure he isn't missed.<br /> <br /> First stop, the bathroom, where he plucks a pair of hairs from Daisy and Forest's brushes. Next the kitchen, where he grabs a packet of &quot;Sleepytime&quot; tea. He makes a mental note to buy a new box soon. The tea goes on to boil (which, Marlin recalls, provided a convenient excuse once previously when Daisy hadn't been sleeping as hard as he'd thought). When the tea is ready, Marlin pours a glass, then slowly and repeatadly dunks the hairs into it, visualizing them, and therefore their owners, becoming soaked in somnelesence. He lights a match, then burns the twined hairs. As a final step, he delivers the spell physically to its subjects; a goodnight kiss. Daisy mumbles and rolls over in her sleep. Forest, limbs askew and half-tangled in his covers already, sleeps like the dead.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Casting <i>Sleep of the Just</i> (Mind 3)<br /> 1 Reach free: Spending 3 on spell control, advanced duration, and to swap primary factor.<br /> Containing Paradox 2 vs Wisdom 7 = 2 vs 7 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469418\" target=\"_blank\">0</a> vs <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469419\" target=\"_blank\">3</a><br /> <br /> Yantras: Sympathetic Tool +2, Sacrament +1<br /> Factors: Potency 3, Duration day, range touch, subjects 2<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 + Yantras 3 + Willpower 3 - Factors 2 = 8 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469420\" target=\"_blank\">2</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Physical contact established, he releases the spell into the world, where it settles over his family like a shroud, delivering sound sleep and pleasant dreams.<br /> <br /> That done, Binder cleans up his spellcasting regeants and gets dressed, no longer worrying about being quiet. He double-checks the locks and potential fire hazards, then gets in the car and heads to the bookstore.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">-1 Willpower, +1 Beat for &quot;Keep magic a secret from his family&quot;?<br /> <br /> Hopefully everything looks fine here (not rolling out the flashback, assuming Daisy and Forest both have 2 or 1 Composure, touching multiple subjects for a spell). Let me know if I should alter anything!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:11:35-08:00","id":1021533,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> Raven nods as you speak. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;You have the thrust of it. Spirits are not quite ideals or pure concepts, necessarily. Those are more like Goetia.&quot;</span> She doesn't take the time to explain what those are, however. Instead, she picks up a stick from the ground and points to a patch of dirt by the bench. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Spirits are born as reflections of things -- places, objects, and yes, even emotions or ideas. These objects and emotions here, in the Fallen World,&quot;</span> she draws a circle with the stick, <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;create Resonance in the Shadow World.&quot;</span> Raven draws another circle alongside the first one.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;The Shadow is in some ways parallel to the Fallen World, as spirits that reflect the Fallen World reside there. But spirits are alive, and living things can change. They feed on Essence, a type of energy that blossoms into existence with a certain quality of Resonance matching its source. Spirits exist in constant struggle for existence. They consume each other to satisfy their hunger for Essence. The strongest survive; the weakest die.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven draws a line between the two circles. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;The Gauntlet is the barrier between the two metaphysical worlds. It tends to be at its strongest around areas with many people, and weakest in the wild. Some spirits seek refuge in the Fallen World, because the Essence is more accessible and there is less predation from other spirits. All spirits are native to the Shadow, not our world.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Your mentor sets down the stick in her hands. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;To understand the spirits, you must study them, speak with them, observe them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven takes a deep breath, and her eyes glaze over as she exhales. You smell again the distinct scent that you smelled when you first met Raven, a scent that makes your heart beat faster and fills you with joy and dread all at once. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;All spirits have names, strengths. Quirks. Weaknesses. Bans they must follow or must not follow. Banes that threaten them to their core. Study this spirit, and tell me what you see.&quot;</span> She points her finger ahead, and you feel the hairs rise on the back of your neck as something triggers your Periphery senses again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> &quot;Well...&quot; Thomas sputters defensively, &quot;No. Not necessarily. But this is my church. I worship here. It should be safe. And these...people, these sorcerers, could be desecrating it. With their Satan worship and their black voodoo magic. I swear, this man was investigating a body after that big storm. And I've seen him at this church at least once now. Now that I think about it, maybe more than once.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thomas's thick eyebrows furrow on his forehead, and he crosses his arms. &quot;Our goal is to hunt down and stop these people. To make our homes and our lives safer. He could lead us to many more of them, especially if they're meeting in our church. I'm sure of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> TJ and the others look at Thomas thoughtfully, nodding along at his words.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You're still able to make your daily attempt for Social Maneuvering to help convince him that he should be focusing his energy on the man you're tracking, rather than the other leads they're looking at.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> You suspect, based on your very limited knowledge of Death, that this is indeed some kind of portal that allows ghosts to travel to the other world Beyond, the afterlife. But unlike with Mrs. Parks, the ghostly woman whom you helped move to the Underworld, while the gate opened before her and closed immediately, this one stays open. You suspect that it might be a permanent, or at least semi-permanent, portal. But nothing seems to come out of the portal from the other direction, at least not while you study it.<br /> <br /> Your walk through a park with living people is simultaneously refreshing...and at least somewhat <i>disappointing</i>. It doesn't quite scratch the itch, not after studying Death the way you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> Fate duels against Space as you try to rely on your manipulation of luck to allow you to traverse through the kaleidoscope-like city that Moonstone has trapped you in. You close your eyes and choose your direction at random, trusting the spell to help guide you towards the bouncing ball instead of trusting in your mundane senses.<br /> <br /> You find yourself in an alley cutting between impossibly large buildings you don't recognize, while all the while the Willis Tower literally towers over you in the distance.<br /> <br /> You hear footsteps behind you.<br /> <br /> You turn around and see a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1014899#post1014899\">younger man</a> with pallid skin and frazzled, unruly dark brown hair. He has a thick beard that hasn't been trimmed or shaved recently. He's wearing ripped jeans and a tank top. The man takes a long drag off a cigarette, flicks it to the ground, and grinds it down with his heel. He leans over and picks up the red ball that Moonstone threw, and he studies it curiously. His eyes flicker to meet yours, and you notice that they're bloodshot and beady.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\">&quot;You in some kind of hurry?&quot;</span> he asks. His voice is unexpectedly raspy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">FYI, you don't have access to the High Speech merit yet. It's gained by joining an Order, and no one has taught it to you yet, so you can't use High Speech as a Yantra yet. I assumed that you would have used a different Path tool, such as your knife, for a +1 bonus and your spell would still succeed. It looks like you didn't adjust for duration, so unless I'm mistaken, the spell ends after the round on which you cast it -- so you don't get the bonus to subsequent rolls.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> For a moment, your frustration tries to grow and beat you down, the way it has when your emotional defenses have been worn out. But you've had more chances to rest recently, and your success with creating a cabal of your own uplifts you and reminds you that you're here to help Ragnar, your cabalmate. You take a breath through the frustration and turn to the Cloud Gate with determination. <br /> <br /> As you open your Sight, you immediately feel a hum of energy emanating from the sculpture. You can pick up the consciousness of every child, man and woman surrounding the Bean, laughing and taking pictures. But before your eyes, the Cloud Gate seems to flicker and twist in place, like it wants to <i>move</i>. And at the very center of the structure, where you can stand and look up into the reflective ceiling of the sculpture, you sense a spatial distortion that warps the air.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Opacity 4 for this Mystery. Yes, you may gain a WP for Naive. And I also need you to roll a Clash of Wills using Gnosis + Mind.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> Daisy nods thoughtfully. &quot;I know the business plan in the broader sense. Sometimes I just feel like you're off in another world. You've been a little distracted lately. I was worried that you were having trouble or something. But with all you've had going on between work and helping with Forest, I guess I underestimated how busy you must be.&quot; She smiles and caresses your cheek. &quot;If I haven't said it lately, thank you for all that you do for us and our son. For me.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Your spell settles onto Daisy and Forest, who slip deeper into their sleep. The house is peaceful and quiet when you leave. <br /> <br /> As you walk out into the front yard, you have an odd, inexplicable feeling of being watched, but there's no one outside that you can see. It quickly fades, and in a short amount of time, you arrive at the bookstore. No one else is in the area at this hour. <br /> <br /> When you go to open the bookstore, you realize that the door is unlocked. You swear you remember locking it when you left. You're always meticulous about it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sure, take a Beat for pursuing your long-term Aspiration and using magic to hide secrets from your family. I really liked the scene you wrote here! Awesome writing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Spell roll looks great. It's interesting to me that this is a Mind 3 spell actually.<br /> <br /> Roll Wits + Composure for a perception roll.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typos, formatting 12-24-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T11:35:05-08:00","id":1021626,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Focused Sight (Mind, Space) | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration), Incognito Presence (self, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b><b>BB</b>OOO<b> | Willpower: 7/8 | Mana: 4/10 | Beats: 4/5 | Arcane Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Calm, centered, focused on the Supernal World as filtered through the great mirror. The people around the sculpture become blurred shapes and vague icons, significant only as symbolizing that the mirror has the capacity to reflect them. The warping at the center of the Cloud Gate seems so much more elusive and subtle than his clumsy Veiling of Ragnar's spatial senses. Moonstone opens his palm, ready to accept knowledge as it comes to him rather than grasping desperately as he did with the Highstorm portal. He lets Mana rise from his hands and watches the reflections of the dancing patterns it forms. Like a secret message in reversed writing, the real truth is seen in the mirror.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 Willpower to activate Scrutiny, taking me to 6.<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills with Gnosis+Mind, 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469767\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a><br /> <br /> If the Clash is being caused by something I'm seeing with Focused Sight, I get the rote quality on the roll. If that's the case, here's a re-roll of my failures: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469768\" target=\"_blank\">still failed.</a><br /> <br /> First turn of Scrutiny. Spending 1 Mana. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469769\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> +1 from Mana.<br /> <br /> Second turn, spending 1 Mana. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469770\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> +1 from Mana. Should be at Opacity 3 now.<br /> <br /> Third turn, spending 1 Mana. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469771\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a> +1 from Mana. Should be at Opacity 2 now. Further Scrutiny rolls are unsafe.<br /> <br /> Fourth turn, spending 1 Willpower. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469774\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a> Should be at Opacity 1.<br /> <br /> Fifth turn. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469776\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Opacity 0. Made it through the gauntlet!<br /> <br /> Now let's attempt Revelation. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469779\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So: the rules say that if you fail Revelation, you can only try again once you've reduced the Opacity. But I've already reduced Opacity to 0. I'll go with however you want to resolve this, but my first thought is to roll again at -1 for a second attempt. Feel free to use or ignore!<br /> <br /> Second attempt, 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469781\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a><br /> <br /> Third attempt, 1 die, +3 from Willpower: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469782\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Currently at 1 Mana and 4 Willpower, or 5 Willpower if the additional Revelation attempts are invalid.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:11:01-08:00","id":1021946,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: Spirit (This post)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 2/5 </b><b>(one spent during post, was at 3) </b><b> Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 3 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">All spirits have names, strengths. Quirks. Weaknesses. Bans they must follow or must not follow. Banes that threaten them to their core. Study this spirit, and tell me what you see.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Lynx shivers as he allows his Senses to sink into the Wild, and he turns them straight to where Raven is pointing. Bipedal but hunched, pointed ears, markings like eyes but none on the face, jagged features, with wispy tendrils that wave and curl. He taps into his understanding of High Speech, tapping the pendant as he lets his magic ask his questions for him, his High Speech turning into questions, expressed through Raven's tongue, an ethereal song. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx opens his Senses to Spirit, and then attempts to cast Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot;, reaching for Instant casting time. He garners 2 successes. <br /> <br /> With Potency 4, subtracting the spirit's rank, he asks the following 4 questions in priority: Spirit's name, then Influence, then Rank, then Ban.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Unknown spirit. <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Path Tool (+1 dice), High Speech (+2 dice).<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot;: Spirit (2) + Gnosis (1) + High Speech (2) + Willpower (3) + Path Tool (1) - Potency (4)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 2 Free Reach: 1 on Instant Cast, 1 on spell maintenance (Web of Life). <br /> <br /> <b>There is no risk of Paradox.</b><br /> <b>Total Dice Pool:</b> 5 dice. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/469902\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot; \u2192 2 successes.</a></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T07:10:06-08:00","id":1022733,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 3/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> [<b>Shaken</b>]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Spell Control (1): Hidden Door, Sleep of the Just<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 2 + Composure 4 = 6 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/470247\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:44:02-08:00","id":1023208,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> &quot;Our goal is to hunt down and stop these people. To make our homes and our lives safer. He could lead us to many more of them, especially if they're meeting in our church. I'm sure of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems that he didn't see me along with them. Thank God for that. But he's too close to the Consilium for comfort. If I don't stop them, they'll find them for sure. I could warn Valentine that they're on to him, but then he'd wonder where I got the intel, and that'll draw unwanted attention on myself. Damned if you do, damned if you don't, and worse to pay if you try to get away from both. Such a bind. I need some time to think about this, fortunately I can buy some.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I don't think investigating a body makes them a witch necessarily. And even if they were, they haven't proven themselves a threat yet, unlike another witch I know,&quot;</span> I segue to a different mage, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Anubis has already killed people and still at large. I haven't seen him since the big storm, so maybe he's connected to it in some way. Maybe hiding in the storms somehow.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix is trying to use basic reasoning to convince the other Hunters to go after Anubis as his Social Maneuvering attempt, saying he's a clear threat to make him a priority and connecting him to the storms for that appeal.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/470423\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligence 2 + Wits 3 = 5 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:45:34-08:00","id":1023753,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Locate Object<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost, Divergent, Abyssal Imago<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 3/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 0</div> <br /> <br /> Ragnar looks at the stranger. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Someone's talking to me. No. Can't have that. No time. Need to get there. Need to fix myself. What if I cause a Paradox? He could be in danger. He could </span></i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">be<i> a danger. Is he? </i></span>Ragnar peers at the stranger, staying silent and still as he concentrates. He dips his finger into the stream of Time, trying to see ahead in time. Paradox has been beating at him a lot, recently, and it seems to be growing with each spell he casts. Eventually, it's going to spiral beyond his control, and the harm to himself or the world will be severe. He senses that his Mana is almost depleted, and he can't continue to rely on his body to take blow for him. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">You should've learned what Paradox costs, Ragnar. Let this be a lesson to you. Reel it in. If you can't Reach, you'll just have to get creative.</span> </i>He keeps his hand in his pocket, clutched around his silver dagger. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Is there a chance that this man might cast a spell on me? Does he pose any other threat to me?</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to cast Divination (Time 1). He has two free Reach, one of which he will spend to fulfill Abyssal Imago, the other one for Instant Casting. He has no excess Reach, so he risks no Paradox. He'll use the Concentration and Path Tool Yantras. <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 + Time 2 + Concentration 2 + Path Tool 1 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/470742\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T06:22:32-08:00","id":1024266,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> For a moment, as you scan the crowd around the Bean, for just a moment you think you brush your Sight across something, but the sensation fades as fast as it came on. As best you figure, it must be a consequence of studying the Cloud Gate so intently.<br /> <br /> You turn your attention to the Cloud Gate and the spatial distortion at its center. You focus your Sight more intensely on the ripple in the air, and the already dimmed sounds of people around you fade even further to faint murmurs on the edge of your consciousness. <br /> <br /> You watch the streams of mana flicker into the distortion with intense curiosity like an insatiable hunger. When the mana enters the shimmering air, you feel a pulse of energy and watch with awe as the mana refracts and scatters, vanishing in all different directions.<br /> <br /> Creatively inspired by the flow of mana, you intensely pour your willpower into studying this spatial distortion. The world fades around you. For a few minutes, all thoughts and worries about Ragnar, about your new cabal, about everything, fade to the background. The Cloud Gate is intoxicating. The Mystery eludes you for a moment, and you try harder, and <i>harder</i>, to understand it. Where was the mana going? How? <i>Why?</i> You feel a rising wave of frustration and nervousness as your emotions swell, but you study the Bean even more intently.<br /> <br /> And then, blissfully, the Mystery unlocks before you, and your eyes widen in surprise. Euphoria passes through you as you grasp the meaning of the warp. Although you have never directly used your own magic to teleport yourself, you sense that this distortion will allow you to instantly transport to anywhere in the city. It will need some mana to do so, and you'll need to guide yourself mentally. But you believe you could use this to travel anywhere in Chicago.<br /> <br /> As best as you can determine, this distortion was not created by an Awakened spell per se; instead, it developed in response to the sculpture. Over time, as other mages and Sleepers studied the Bean with magic and mundane senses, the mirrored surface created ripples in Space around the city. It's possible that the Highstorms enhanced this energy, and turned those ripples into a web of sympathy connecting the Bean to the entire city.<br /> <br /> You swell with pride at figuring it out on your own.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think your interpretation of the Revelation roll when failed at Opacity 0 makes sense, and I think it's fair. Arguably we could make it add to Opacity if you fail after too many tries, or make you come back after boosting Gnosis, but this seems more interesting.<br /> <br /> Totally made this up on the fly, I hope it's neat! You learn the following:<br /> <br /> Surface Information: The distortion is not made from an Awakened spell, but mimics the Teleportation spell (Space 4, p. 178). It resembles the Patterning practice. The distortion appears to be about a decade old.<br /> <br /> Deep Information: You learn how to utilize the distortion. You need to stand in the center of the Bean and spend 1 mana, and then make one of two possible skill rolls. First, you can attempt Wits + Composure for a perception roll; on a success, you can teleport to any location within line of sight of the Bean. This essentially amounts to a 1-mile radius of Millennium Park, and can even bring you inside a building, as long as it's within view of the Bean and not blocked by something else. Alternatively, you can roll Intelligence + Streetwise to target a specific location anywhere within the city limits of Chicago proper. If successful, you arrive on the nearest city street directly outside that location. Failed rolls still expend a mana point and will bring you to a different location.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You take a deep breath in and open your Senses, and as the Fallen World fades around you, the spirit lurking in front of you appears to your eyes. It's small, maybe the size of your head, and appears to be made of water. It has no discernible humanoid features, looking instead like a small puddle of water that ripples and undulates in the air.<br /> <br /> You speak in images and craft your spell, and your vision sharpens around the spirit. You feel a pulse of spiritual energy pass through you, and instantly, you simply <i>know</i> this creature. Its name comes to you in a complex image of a small puddle on a rainy day, echoed in the tongue of the spirits that you roughly translate as &quot;Aqua.&quot; Unsurprisingly, you sense that the spirit has the ability to modestly influence water, and the spirit itself feels relatively weak.<br /> <br /> Raven smiles proudly and holds out her hand, intoning in High Speech. With your Sight active, you clearly see her cast a simple Spirit spell that settles around the spirit. Aqua immediately turns towards Raven and moves towards her, swirling slowly around her. Raven points, and the spirit moves in the direction of her hand. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;The Spirit Arcanum is, obviously, your most important tool of all as you interact with these creatures. You can use it to study them, command them, protect yourself from their supernatural abilities. Even harm them and defeat them, if necessary.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Spirit spell on Aqua vanishes, and the spirit quickly moves away from Raven and into the nearby creek. It seems to be poking its &quot;head&quot; out of the water and studying Raven, then vanishes out of sight. Raven turns and walks up slowly to you. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Do you have any other questions before we continue?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> You look around and don't see anything else that seems to stand out to you. You hear a rustle in a bush next to the building, and your heart nearly leaps out of your chest, but then you see it's just a cat. It looks at you for a moment, mews, and then suddenly runs after something it must have spotted in a nearby alley. The street is otherwise quiet.<br /> <br /> When you look inside, you don't see anything out of place. Nothing else seems touched or missing. Your spell hiding the door to your sanctum is still there, and the door is closed.<br /> <br /> So why do you have an odd sense that someone or something was, or is, here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Thomas seems less confident about his concerns after your short speech. &quot;Well...I guess when you put it that way...&quot; TJ cocks his head and looks at you with a small nod and a frown, too. It seems like this time, your words have caught more of his attention.<br /> <br /> &quot;That is a good point,&quot; TJ admits. &quot;But we want to make sure we don't focus too much on any one lead. We've always done our best work when we come together as a team. Maybe we should check out all of the options.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would say that your roll needs to be an Attribute + Skill, not a dice pool using two Attributes. The only roll I can think of that uses that combination is a perception check. I'll say it succeeds this time, but for future rolls I would probably go with Intelligence + Persuasion for that kind of maneuvering attempt.<br /> <br /> You successfully open the first of TJ's three doors, so two Doors are left to convince him and the Hunter cell to stop pursuing their current leads and focus primarily on the man you're looking for. You currently have a Good impression, so you can make another attempt on the next day. I'll also point out that per the Social Maneuvering rules on p. 215, you can try other things to boost your impression with TJ. I'll say that you know from experience that his Vice is Pride. If you want, you can make an offer that feeds into his Vice or by using a gift/bribe to boost your impression to Excellent. If you do so, you can make additional Social Maneuvering rolls over the next few hours.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You feel a rush of adrenaline as Time wraps around you. Without pushing yourself to see a more detailed future, the answers to your questions come to you only as flashes of insight and instinctive feelings in your gut: <i>Yes. Yes.</i><br /> <br /> As soon as your Nimbus flares around you, the man smirks wickedly. You feel a pulse of energy on your own Periphery as the small red ball in his hand suddenly crumbles to dust before your eyes. Still trapped in Moonstone's hex, Willis Tower looms ominously over you from a distance.<br /> <br /> The man takes a step towards you. As he does, he pulls out a small metallic rod that appears to be made of lead. You're keenly aware of the fact that the alley is empty. <span style=\"color:darkred\">&quot;I just want to <i>talk</i>,&quot;</span> he says with a sneer.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take a divination spell to tell that he's lying.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Just as a reminder, you can only use the Concentration Yantra for spells with a Duration lasting more than 1 turn. Subtracting 2 dice from your pool still nets you a success, however, so your spell succeeds.<br /> <br /> Because you successfully cast a spell that did not risk Paradox, you resolve the Abyssal Imago condition. Take an Arcane Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I forgot to mention this earlier, but you resolve your Aspiration to find and study an Avernian Gate. Take a Beat and pick a new Aspiration! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, please let me know if there is anything else you would like to do during the afternoon. Otherwise, we can shift to the evening with your meeting with Dante.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 12-31-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T09:09:24-08:00","id":1024367,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 3/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>LB</b>OOOOO<br /> [<b>Shaken</b>]<br /> Mage Sight: Peripheral<br /> Spell Control (1): Hidden Door, Sleep of the Just, Sense Consciousness<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> Binder takes a few deep breaths to calm himself a little, then steps back from the door. He takes hold of the knife in his bag, centering himself around it, and casts a spell over the building and the area immediately surrounding it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting <i>Sense Consciousness</i> (Mind 1)<br /> 3 Reach free: Spending 2 for spell control, 1 for instant cast, 1 for advanced scale, 1 for advanced duration<br /> Containing Paradox 2 + 1 (prior risk) - 2 (dedicated tool) vs Wisdom 7 = 1 vs 7 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471032\" target=\"_blank\">1</a> vs <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471033\" target=\"_blank\">2</a> successes<br /> <br /> Yantras: Concentration +2, Dedicated Tool<br /> Factors: Potency 1, Duration week, Scale large building<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 + Yantras 2 = 6 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471034\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T18:44:13-08:00","id":1025665,"title":"","content":"<b>Binder</b><br /> Your spell settles over the entire building, and you suddenly develop an intuitive sense of the creatures present within it.<br /> <br /> You're comforted that there are no humans you can detect within the building. You do sense a stray cat that somehow found its way into the main store, and there are a few mice hiding in the walls -- you make a mental note to put out some traps -- but otherwise you do not sense anyone inside the book store.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:57:44-08:00","id":1025916,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: Locate Object<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost, Divergent<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 3/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 1</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even as he limits his spell, the clammy embrace of the Abyss disappears. He briefly marvels at the irony and truth of it. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">\u200bLike a Chinese finger trap. The way to escape is to accept your limitations. </span></i>But even as he shrugs off the Abyss, the answers to his questions turn his joy to fear. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">He's a mage. And he's not friendly. Shit. </span></i><br /> <br /> The man smirks, and Ragnar feels a pulse of magic as the red ball turns to dust. He feels another pang of fear, mixed with frustration. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Now how am I supposed to get there? </i></span><br /> <br /> The man then draws out a lead rod and takes a menacing step forward. <span style=\"color:#8B0000\">&quot;I just want to <i>talk.</i></span><span style=\"color:#8B0000\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar's every instinct tells him to run, but he stands his ground.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i> I'm a mage, too. I'm not going down without a fight. But maybe I can just scare him away. </i></span>Ragnar calmly pulls out his silver knife, as well as the smaller obsidian one he received from the Highstorm, and holds them in a stance that resembles one he's seen in action movies. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Ooo, you show me yours, I show you mine! I love this game! Yours is definitely longer, but I have two, and mine are pointier. Look, we could both really cut loose, but you and I both know it's not worth your time. Besides, I'm an Acanthus with a Death Arcana artifact picked up with from last week's Highstorm, and I've got a Mastigos friend who's on his way. And believe you me, he could jack your day up. Ever heard of Mathias of the Shields of Dawn? My buddy beat him in a Duel Arcane.&quot;</span> He feels a little disloyal, using Mathias' humiliation for his own benefit, but he reasons that it's for a good cause.<br /> <br /> He takes a moment to theatrically peer at the man. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;I don't remember seeing you at Consilium. Which probably means that you aren't on their good side. So here's how I see it: you fight me, I jack you up, and then my friend shows up, and we jack you up together. And even if you get away, I know what you look like, and suddenly there's a magical APB out for a shady mofo matching your description. And I'm sure the Guardians and Arrows would love to get to know you.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He gives the stranger a friendly look. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Or you could just walk away. You leave, I forget this ever happened. Choice is yours.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> As Ragnar speaks, he dismisses his Locate Object spell, which is useless now. In its place, he activates Fate and Time Active Sight. Part of him wants to try and call up a spell, but he knows the stranger will pick up on that immediately, and it would ruin his attempt to diffuse this situation peacefully. He's been talking a mile a minute, probably thanks to Moonstone's mess-up, but he hopes that his verbosity translates as &quot;crazy badass&quot; rather than &quot;scared novice.&quot; <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Come on, asshat. Take the out.</i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to convince the unknown mage to just leave without a fight. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 2 - Divergent 2 + Willpower 3 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471826\" target=\"_blank\">well I'll be damned, 2 successes.</a><br /> <br /> Ragnar also activates his Fate and Time Active Sight and spends another Willpower, bringing him down to 1.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 01-03-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:30:45-08:00","id":1027247,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: Spirit (This post)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 2/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 4 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Do you have any other questions before we continue?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">Hundreds of them,</span>&quot; Lynx replies with a grin, &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">But I can't seem to word any of them. Teach me what I should know, and I'll ask afterwards.</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:05:02-08:00","id":1028529,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Fair enough,&quot;</span> I sigh as I lean back on my seat, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;It's just...it's personal for me is all. I have to avenge them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He's presenting himself as sympathetic to raise the impression level.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/473352\" target=\"_blank\">Manipulation 1 + Empathy 2 = 3 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Newp!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Looks like they aren't biting, damn. Nothing more for me here, I guess.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;Well, I've leave you guys to it,&quot;</span> I say as I get up to leave, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I'll keep my eyes peeled for the freak storms and let you know anything I find out. See ya,&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Didn't get much out of that. I look at the Death mage's picture on my phone as I walk away from the library, maybe I'll find out more about him by the time I convince them. Now if only I can find that guy again. As much as I hate to admit it, this is definitely Moonstone's department. Didn't he take Ragnar to the central metropolitan area for Space training or something? It's a place to start at least.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using his Streetwise Skill to get a rough location (or at the very least a clue) on where Moonstone or Ragnar might be by asking the right people using their descriptions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/473354\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligence 2 + Streetwise 1 = 3 dice \u2192 0 successes</a><br /> <br /> Making this a dramatic failure, let's have some fun with the misinformation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T06:01:23-08:00","id":1032102,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> There's a dangerous gleam in the man's eyes as you threaten him. His eyes look bloodshot, and they are fixed on you with a hunger for violence that you've rarely seen before. But something about your words seems to put him off guard. He twitches when you mention the Shields of Dawn -- it's a subtle motion, but one you see because you're watching for a reaction -- and he wets his lips nervously at the mention of Mathias.<br /> <br /> After a pause, the man apparently decides that his agenda still outweighs the caution you've instilled in him. With your Sight, you see a dizzying halo of green energy flare around him as he rapidly lifts his metal rod and points it at your feet. Bruises suddenly appear along his arm, and he winces. A Matter spell forms at his hands and is channeled through the lead rod; a green bolt of energy flies through the air and strikes the ground beneath your feet. <br /> <br /> You suddenly find yourself with no firm ground to stand on as the cement beneath you liquefies. With a slurping sound, you collapse down to your thighs, barely able to move your legs. The man grins with delight. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mechanically, you take the Leg Wrack tilt applied to both legs (p. 323). You can move at speed 1, but then you can't take any other action this turn. You take -2 to Defense and physical rolls that require movement.<br /> <br /> As we discussed, for trying to calmly respond and buy time for Moonstone to find you rather than running or protecting yourself, you can use your Virtue to recover Willpower. Divergent ends for you (if only it was that easy for Moonstone!) and you take an Arcane Beat for resolving it. Unless you already got one for a condition this scene? I don't have my notes handy but I don't remember you having one for that this scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Raven nods and smiles. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Experience is a far more efficient teacher than I,&quot;</span> she replies. She walks up to you and turns so she is standing by your side.<br /> <br /> Raven lifts up her arms and begins to intone in High Speech. You see and feel her cast a Spirit spell, making the hairs on your neck and arms stand on end. The air in front of you shimmers and then tears apart, creating a doorway. Raven leads you through, and the door vanishes behind you. <br /> <br /> You find yourself, quite literally, in a completely different world. <br /> <br /> Where moments ago you had been standing in a park along a creek running through the woods, the landscape before you is a mighty forest. Tall, thick trees tower over you. The creek here is a wide winding river, and you see large fish swimming under its crystal clear surface. Except they aren't true fish; they are spirits shaped like fish, glowing with their own light as they propel themselves through the water, some leaping into the air and splashing back into the river. <br /> <br /> And then you realize that the entire forest is <i>teeming</i> with spirits. The trees are alive, beating branches against each other, almost like they're playing. Deer, squirrel, and rabbit spirits run between the trees. You hear a screech as a hawk spirit dives from a tree branch and tears its talons into a rabbit; the smaller spirit trembles, fades to mist, and then vanishes as the hawk feasts on its Essence. There are easily hundreds of spirits within your view at a single glance. <br /> <br /> Raven moves from your side, and the spirits move around her, giving her a wide berth, almost as if out of respect. You realize, however, that many of the spirits around you are watching you with a hostile look. The smallest spirits, of grass and squirrels and beetles, scamper away as you look at them. Some of the larger spirits seem to bristle at you, staring you down. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Mages are foreign to the Shadow World,&quot;</span> Raven explains. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;When you gain more mastery of the Spirit Arcanum, they will start to see you as one of their own and treat you accordingly per their natural hierarchy. Until then, it is up to you to assert your will and your dominance with them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven's familiar Nimbus flares and this time, she does something you've never seen before: She somehow seems to cast two spells at once, intertwining them together. As she chants in High Speech, a blanket of Spirit magic settles upon her and around her. The spirits that had been watching her suddenly seem to ignore her, as if she wasn't standing there at all. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;With these creatures, Spirit magic is your sword, shield, and cloak. Wield it wisely.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Raven steps back and a devilish grin crosses her face. She whistles, and her Nimbus flares again. Moments later, a spirit shaped like a large wolf comes springing from between the looming trees. Other spirits near it scatter at its approach, but the wolf spirit ignores them. It runs up near you and stops, sniffing the air. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Attack,&quot;</span> Raven commands. The wolf looks at you, bares its teeth, and growls.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No need to roll initiative, for convenience sake I will let you take the first action.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You begin asking for directions. Most of the people you talk to give you blank stares or shake their heads. In a city with millions of people, finding two specific individuals is not exactly an easy task. Ironically, you realize that if you had Ragnar or Moonstone's control of Fate or Time, this might be a little easier. <br /> <br /> One person claims to have seen your friends. He says he'll tell you for $5. You hand over the money and he gives you odd directions that bring you through some of the shadier areas on the south side of central Chicago. Before you know it, you're definitely lost. And some of the locals are eyeing you and that interesting staff in your hands like they're wondering what else you might have on you worth looking at.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take the Lost condition as previously described in this scene, minus all the wacky hex-fueled illusions, and take a Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> Dusk arrives, settling like a heavy blanket over La Grange. You make your way to the Vial House, the museum used as the home for the <a href=\"http://www.lagrangehistory.org/about-us/\" target=\"_blank\">La Grange Area Historical Society</a>. The house has a rustic look, dated but well maintained. You wonder when you arrive whether you might have come at the wrong time, because no one seems to be here. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.lagrangehistory.org/press/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/IMG_2087-300x225.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You just notice some signs of movement inside by looking through a window when you hear footsteps from behind you. You turn to see Dante, who is wearing his usual dark attire and carrying a briefcase in his left hand. He shakes your hand in greeting and says, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Well met, friend. Glad you could make it. Come, follow me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As you walk around the house, Dante explains softly, <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;You're about to meet some of my business associates. It's important that you be respectful. I know you will be, of course. Pay close attention here; this is a chance for you to open your mind and see something quite fascinating.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Dante motions for you to come through a private gate to the back of the house, and leads you through a small garden to the back door. He knocks three times, and after a moment the door opens to reveal a young woman who appears to be in her late 20s or early 30s.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fashionhoob.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/black-leather-jacket.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The woman offers a small smile and shakes Dante's hand. <span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;Punctual as always. I see you brought a friend.&quot;</span> The woman glances at you but says nothing else. <br /> <br /> Dante smiles and nods. <span style=\"color:red\">&quot;Hello, Desiree. This is my colleague, an esteemed physician known as Ouroboros Ophis. May he come in as well?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Desiree nods at you and says to Dante with a grin, <span style=\"color:Maroon\">&quot;You all have the weirdest names. Sure, come in. She's waiting.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> You follow Desiree and Dante into the house. Walking into the room feels like taking a step back in time. The house is well-maintained by the local historical society to keep its authentic feel as a 19th century home. The kitchen is antique, with a gas range and a water boiler located behind it. You notice a teapot on the stove heating. As you walk through the kitchen into the back room, you see quite a few couches and chairs arranged around the room. Oil lamps light the room, and there are dozens of portraits, knick knacks, and paintings adorning the wall. <br /> <br /> Lounging in a reclined position on a large chair on the far wall is an older looking woman in 19th century period attire, including a &quot;fashionable&quot; cap around her head. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://mimimatthews.files.wordpress.com/2015/08/portrait-of-elizaveta-olenina-by-alexander-varnek-1820.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> She looks to be in her late 60s. Something about her seems...off somehow, but it's hard to put your finger on it. She studies you with a sharp look and a critical gaze, but she quickly turns her attention to Dante and smiles politely. <span style=\"color:darkmagenta\">&quot;Well, good evening, Dante,&quot;</span> she says in a crisp, curt tone softened by her small smile. <span style=\"color:darkmagenta\">&quot;I trust that business has been well for you? It is good to see you again. And who is this?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:Red\">&quot;It is, Mrs. Vial, and thank you for asking.&quot;</span> Dante introduces you as he did with Desiree. <span style=\"color:Red\">&quot;He is newly joined to our society, madam. I truly hope you are not troubled by my inviting him.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mrs. Vial shakes her head and motions dismissively. <span style=\"color:darkmagenta\">&quot;Not at all. There's plenty of tea for the both of you, Desiree will see to it.&quot;</span> The matron snaps her finger and points to the kitchen with a firm look at Desiree, who quickly bows her head and briskly walks into the kitchen. She quickly returns with two steaming cups of tea on a serving tray, and she offers you and Dante a porcelain cup. Dante smiles and accepts it, setting the briefcase down and taking a seat in an open chair, and he nods to you to do the same. <br /> <br /> Mrs. Vial smiles, but her eyes repeatedly flicker to the briefcase. She seems distracted. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can make a perception roll if you like.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typos 01-15-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:28:57-08:00","id":1032401,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Fate, Time<br /> Active Spells: Exceptional Luck (as of this turn)<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Inspired, Lost (-2 to Streetwise), Leg Wrack (1 Speed, -2 to Defense and actions requiring movement)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO I WP: 3/4 I Mana: 3/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 1<br /> </div> <br /> Ragnar suddenly feels his mind clear. Whatever Moonstone did to him accidentally, it seems to have resolved itself. Was it his patience that undid it? Well, that doesn't matter. The mage points his rod at the ground and he suddenly starts to sink into it. <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">So much for diplomacy. </span></i>He stares at the mage in sudden hostility. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;<i>Fine,</i>&quot; </span>he spits at him, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;let's do this.&quot; </span>He immediately pulls the threads of Fate around himself, trying to cloak himself from the other man's actions. Then he raises his silver knife and slashes horizontally at the level of the other man's eyes. As he swings, red, translucent wisps, like a tangle of animated threads, fly from the knife at the height of the arc toward his attacker, the threads whipping menacingly towards his eyes. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>If I can't walk, you can't see. Reap what you sow.</i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to cast his Exceptional Luck Praxis to apply Hexes equal to potency, which will take the form of the Blind Tilt in both eyes. He has one Free Reach, which he will spend on Instant Casting. He'll spend additional Reaches for Sensory Range and Advanced Duration. He'll spend a point of Mana to reduce the Paradox dice to 1.<br /> <br /> 1 Reach = 1 die -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475651\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.<br /> <br /> He will roll to contain. 7 Wisdom = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475652\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Ragnar takes one point of Resistant Bashing Damage.<br /> <br /> Spell roll: 1 Gnosis + 2 Fate + 1 Path Tool + 3 Willpower = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475657\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> So to summarize: Ragnar has activated Fate Mage Armor, has spent a point each of Mana and Willpower, and has taken a Resistant Bashing wound.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":"@ is cool 01-15-2017, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:36:05-08:00","id":1032920,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: Spirit (This post)<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 2/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast (Resolving?)<br /> Beats: 4 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> Lynx draws in the world past the Gauntlet with awe, grinning broadly, wordlessly as Raven explains the Shadow. He barely registers her Nimbus, fighting off the urge to simply run off and talk to everything.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Attack.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Wait, what!?</span></i><br /> <br /> Lynx looks over to her, and then to the wolf. He feels a sense of danger crawl up his skin and he takes a step back, his lips tucked into a mirthless grin. <i>O<span style=\"color:#800000\">kay, High Speech is out. I don't have the time to study it either. It's a wolf, so I need to...</span></i><br /> <br /> With one hand instinctively reaching for his necklace, he thrusts his hand forward, fingers outstretched as though to grab the wolf by the neck. He asserts as strongly as he is able: &quot;<span style=\"color:#800000\">O' wolf, I <i>command</i> you! Stop!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Lynx attempts to cast Spirit 2 &quot;Command Spirit&quot;, reaching for Instant casting time, asking the spirit to stop in its tracks. Unfortunately, he gains no successes, and will instead resolve Steadfast to garner 1 success on the roll.</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Wolf spirit.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Path Tool (+1 dice).<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Spirit 2 &quot;Command Spirit&quot;: Spirit (2) + Gnosis (1) + Path Tool (1) - Potency (2)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 1 Free Reach: 1 on Instant Cast.<br /> <br /> <b>There is no risk of Paradox.</b><br /> <b>Total Dice Pool:</b> 2 dice. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475975\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Spirit 2 &quot;Command Spirit&quot; \u2192 0 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 02-09-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:11:44-08:00","id":1034546,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>BINDER</b><br /> Willpower: 3/7 Mana: 9/10 Health: <b>LB</b>OOOOO<br /> [<b>Shaken</b>]<br /> Mage Sight: <b>Active</b><br /> Spell Control (1): Hidden Door, Sleep of the Just, Sense Consciousness<br /> Beats: 1 Arcane Beats: 2</div> <br /> Feeling only slightly reassured by his spell, Binder turns on Mage Sight then quietly and carefully enters the shop.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dexterity 2 + Stealth 1 = 3 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476875\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:50:45-08:00","id":1037142,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness, Lost | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> Well, shit. I'm no closer to finding either Moonstone or Ragnar, and everybody around wants a piece of me, or at least a valuable of mine. Should've really thought about exchanging numbers when I had the chance. I'd gladly try to fight my way outta this, but I've got bigger fish to fry, so I'll just scare this one outta the pond.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">&quot;I don't think my buddies would wander in a place like this. Let's look somewhere else, shall we? I mean, it'd be such a shame if this staff of mine got some dents or stains on it,&quot;</span> I threaten the small fish.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He'll try to intimidate the guy he's following into leading him out of wherever he is right now. I think brandishing a weapon can grant a +1 on Intimidate rolls, as a knife or staff in this case tends to make someone much more intimidating.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/478438\" target=\"_blank\">Presence 3 + Intimidation 2 + 1 Weapon = 6 dice \u2192 1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:35:24-08:00","id":1037194,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>7 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <br /> Ouroboros Ophis greets and follows Dante to the house, letting him speak, just focused on paying attention to all details and hopefully learn more about the dealings of whom will now be his official &quot;teacher&quot; in all things pertaining to the Consilium and the Order. He finds himself curiously nervous and anxious, like he remembers being on his first year of college, both eaguer to learn and oh so conscious of his ignorance.<br /> <br /> He barely manages to make a quick nod and smile back at Desiree when they are introduced by Dante, but he gets completely off guard when he is finally presented to Mrs. Vial. He clears his throat and wets his dry lips with a long sip of tea before he gets to voice his thoughts.<br /> <br /> -<b><span style=\"color:#006400\">&quot;Excuse me, Mrs., but I cannot help but wonder... have I heard correctly? Mrs. Vial as in, <i>the actual</i> Mrs. Vial?&quot;</span></b>- he says making a gesture with his hand encompasing the whole room and house.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perception roll: Wits+Composure (6 dice) =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/478463\" target=\"_blank\">2 Successes</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:56:21-08:00","id":1037605,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight (Mind, Space) | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration), Incognito Presence (self, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b><b>BB</b>OOO<b> | Willpower: 4/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> A mirror that teleports people? Oracles preserve us! Moonstone is super jazzed about this revelation, and tucks it away in his growing mental folder of &quot;Cool Magical Doodads Where I'm The Only One Who Knows About It.&quot;<br /> <br /> For right now, he just sits invisibly in the lotus position under the Cloud Gate and contemplates his Gnosis. The divination that said Ragnar would be in danger today is still at the back of his mind, but he's at peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:07:37-08:00","id":1040542,"title":"","content":"<b>Ragnar</b><br /> The hostile mage recoils with a hiss of frustration as he suddenly loses his vision. He takes a deep breath to steady himself and glares in your general direction. <br /> <br /> The man snaps his fingers, and suddenly the liquid concrete you're sinking in is no longer liquid; you're trapped up to your knees in solid concrete. <br /> <br /> Although he can't see you, he still knows where you are and points his lead rod towards you. You suddenly feel an intense pain in your muscles and your very bones, as if your body is threatening to fall apart on you. It's a wave of exhaustion and pain that lasts for only a moment, but it takes your breath away. You notice ugly bruises already forming underneath your skin along your arms. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your spell appears to take effect. He has -5 on spell rolls requiring vision and loses his Defense. <br /> <br /> You lose Leg Wrack and gain a modified version of the Immobilized tilt as his State Change spell ends. You lose your Defense, have speed 0, but can still take combat actions that don't require your legs or movement (so you can still cast spells). You can attempt to break free using a Strength + Athletics roll with a -2 penalty for the Durability. <br /> <br /> You take 3 bashing damage from his spell effect, which he casts at sensory range.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You expertly craft your Imago and assert your will on the wolf spirit -- and find your magic slamming into the magical force Raven has placed on the spirit to force it to attack you. It's your will against hers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think the simplest way to resolve this is a Clash of Wills. Roll Gnosis + Spirit versus Raven's Gnosis + Spirit. If you win, the spirit listens to you for the duration of your spell (so this round only). If she wins, the wolf ignores you and gets its action to attack.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that you can also reflexively activate your Mage Armor, by the way, if you choose.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Binder</b><br /> You silently enter the store, keeping yourself low so you can move between the bookshelves without being seen. You survey the store, and your heart nearly leaps out of your chest as you sense movement -- only to see a small alley cat walking through the building. It looks at you with wide eyes and meows, then bolts past you through the open door. <br /> <br /> You have no idea how a cat got in here. But after spending several anxious minutes scanning the store with your mundane and magical senses, you are certain that you're alone in here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> Your tone and body language as you not-so-subtly threaten violence cause the would-be assailants to scramble. You find yourself alone, but still incredibly lost. You've never been to this part of town before. You might be able to find your way back if you take a minute and retrace your steps, though. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Still need a skill roll to end the Lost condition, but now you aren't at risk of being jumped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> The older woman sits up taller in her chair. <span style=\"color:darkmagenta\">&quot;I am indeed a Vial, and owner of this establishment, if that is what you mean. This home and its legacy has been in my family since it was built.&quot;</span> She gives a thin-lipped smile.<br /> <br /> As you sip your tea, Dante and Mrs. Vial make idle chatter about recent events in La Grange and Chicago. Desiree says nothing, standing quietly beside the older woman prepared to respond to any additional requests. She crosses her arms over her chest and studies you. <br /> <br /> As you listen to the conversation, you realize what bothers you about Mrs. Vial: it's her body language, and even her actual body. She has an unusually pale complexion. She makes odd facial expressions, at times smiling for no reason, and her lips move a fraction of a second delayed, as if her body isn't quite up to speed with expressing emotions. It seems superficial, like there is something else here going on under the surface. <br /> <br /> Mrs. Vial doesn't drink any tea. Neither does Desiree. The woman keeps looking at the briefcase sitting beside Dante. Your mentor glances at you and smiles knowingly.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Make a Wits + Subterfuge roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> You relax and meditate, contemplating Space and Gnosis, drinking in the atmosphere here by the sculpture in Millenium Park. <br /> <br /> And then, for just a moment, you feel a brief pulse of sympathetic energy connecting you to Ragnar, as some of the energy that you accidentally transferred to him while attempting to scry comes snapping back at you. For the briefest moment, you know exactly where your ally is within the city.<br /> <br /> The Cloud Gate shimmers with arcane energy, as if anticipating your next thought.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To help us get this scene on the move, I'm going to say that Ragnar successfully resolving his Divergent condition gives you a brief &quot;ping&quot; of his location. You can spend a mana and make an Int + Streetwise check to travel to his location as an instant action. Failure means you still travel but might not end up at exactly the right location.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:06:46-08:00","id":1040568,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness, Lost | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> Yeah, that's what I thought, you go look for some other prey. With those yo-yos outta the way, I still need to get my bearings. So I whip out my phone for a map to get myself to familiar streets.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'd say the smartphone could provide it's +1 bonus for navigation with Google Maps, but feel free to remove it if you want.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480493\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Streetwise 1 + 1 Smartphone = 5 dice \u2192 2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Well, even without the extra die, it's still a success. In the interest of speeding things along, perhaps Phoenix could find Ragnar?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:18:04-08:00","id":1040575,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 2/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: Steadfast<br /> Beats: 4 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480502\" target=\"_blank\">Clash of Wills, Spirit + Gnosis \u2192 2 successes.</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 01-31-2017, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:16:02-08:00","id":1040839,"title":"","content":"<b>Phoenix</b><br /> With a moment of peace to clear your mind, you realize that pulling out your phone and checking GPS will make it easier for you to navigate back to a familiar location. Within a few minutes, you're back in an area you know, and you start your search again for Ragnar or Moonstone.<br /> <br /> You still don't have any concrete evidence that you're in the right area, but you guess that it can't hurt to try a few random searches. And there had been that brief glimmer of recognition in the beggar's eyes, so maybe he had seen one of your cabalmates here recently.<br /> <br /> You instinctually pick a few random directions, and pay more attention to your GPS to make sure you don't get lost. And then after a few minutes, whether by complete luck or some divine intervention, you feel a pulse of energy on your Periphery and hear a familiar voice somewhere in the near vicinity of the alley you're standing in: <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;<i>Fine</i>, let's do this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> You resolve Lost. I think that's your first mundane Condition resolved in this scene, so take a Beat.<br /> <br /> I'll say that if you spend your instant action moving and make a successful Wits + Composure perception roll, you can join in the scene on the next round. Alternatively, you can spend an instant action to roll Dexterity + Stealth and try and sneak up on the others, which means you won't be able to act for 2 rounds. Or, you can try any other instant action, and then join in 2 rounds.<br /> <br /> Regardless, roll initiative.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> You assert your will as powerfully as you can, trying to fix your Imago into place with brute force to compel the wolf spirit to obey you. But Raven has far more experience with magic, and on this occasion, you falter.<br /> <br /> The wolf spirit bares its teeth, snarls, and leaps towards you. In the Fallen World, the spirits you've seen appear ephemeral, airy, lacking in substance. While this wolf is still obviously a spirit, there's definitely nothing ephemeral about it here. His claws rip into your skin.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.orokos.com/ross/480644\" target=\"_blank\">Attack</a>: 4d10 = <b>2 successes</b> after accounting for Defense 4. This roll will be modified if you choose to activate your Mage Armor (Life Armor is probably the most effective in this particular scenario, as it both boosts your Defense and offers Armor).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Clarified a few things 01-30-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:23:59-08:00","id":1040846,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight (Mind, Space) | Spells: Urban Jungle (on Ragnar, scene duration), Incognito Presence (self, scene duration)<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Passive), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b><b>BB</b>OOO<b> | Willpower: 4/8 | Mana: 1/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> Palms up, deep breathing. The wind blows. Moonstone becomes aware of Ragnar's exact location in Space. This is the correct time to act.<br /> <br /> He closes the lead clasp of the Cloak around his neck, letting it shield him from unwanted magic. Then he focuses. He doesn't have a vivid mental map of Chicago, unfortunately, but he translates the Space insight as best as he can, and lets his Mana go free.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Activating the Wards and Signs effect of my Artifact. 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480647\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. Moonstone has Withstand 4 against magic targeting him this scene, more if the spell would already be Withstood.<br /> <br /> And trying to operate the Cloud Gate warp. Spending 1 Mana and 1 Willpower, which makes Divergent active. Intelligence 1, Streetwise -1, Willpower 3. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480650\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a>. Off to wherever!<br /> <br /> Just in case, rolling initiative: 1d10+7: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480656\" target=\"_blank\">8</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Stupid, stupid. Instead of accepting the insight with an open palm, he grasps at it with a closed fist. As he reaches out, his awareness warps as his monkey mind whispers <i>&quot;oh shit, did I just experience <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kensh%C5%8D\" target=\"_blank\">kensho</a>?&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T06:21:08-08:00","id":1041222,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> You focus your will, take a breath to anchor your thoughts, and channel a thread of mana into the Cloud Gate. At the same time, you create a mental representation of Chicago, drawing lines between your current location and where you sensed Ragnar a moment ago.<br /> <br /> As soon as your thread of mana touches the sculpture, you feel a powerful force of raw energy surround you. To your Space Sight, the image of the Chicago skyline reflected in the sculpture suddenly zooms out and then zooms in, focusing on an alley deep in the city.<br /> <br /> You feel yourself yanked forward by an invisible force as the mana you channeled into the Cloud Gate connects you with the location. There's a dizzying, rushing sensation of movement. A cold wind whips around you.<br /> <br /> And suddenly, you're not in Millennium Park anymore.<br /> <br /> The good news: You can see Ragnar.<br /> <br /> The bad news: You can see Ragnar <i>way</i> down below you. You're standing on the railing to a fourth-story balcony of an old apartment complex. Your foot begins to slip.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You're 4 stories up from the ground, or 12 meters in game terms. You may make a reflexive Wits + Athletics roll to keep yourself from falling. Per the rules in the CoD core book, if you fall from this height you will take 12 bashing damage, which you can alleviate with successes on a Dexterity + Athletics roll on a 1:1 basis (or find a way to work around with magic).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You hear a faint ring of bells and see wisps of energy on your Periphery, coming from above you. When you look up, you see Moonstone there, teetering on the edge of a balcony railing four stories above you. The hostile mage in front of you whips his around, but with his mundane vision blinded, he can't see what's there. His expression darkens with anger.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't think I've had you roll Initiative yet, so go ahead and do it now.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:07:39-08:00","id":1041320,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight:<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Active Armour: Life (2 Defence, 2 general Armour)<br /> Willpower: 2/5 Mana: 5/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts:<br /> Beats: 4 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx reflexively activates Life Armour in response to the attack.</b></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>I don't even know what I expected... Why didn't it hurt?</i></span><br /> <br /> Lynx glances at his hands and skin, feeling it tighten and harden against his bones. He snaps out of it as the wolf prepares another attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><i>I need to get away from it! But...but...</i></span><br /> <br /> Through instinct he forms an imago: a feathery cloak of darkness that shrouds his presence from the wolf - and indeed, the Shadow as a whole. He clutches his silvery pendant as he wills the cloak into being.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx attempts to cast Spirit 2 &quot;Shadow Walk&quot;, reaching for Instant casting time and advanced duration. He garners 2 successes.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Self.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Day.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Dedicated Tool.<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Spirit 2 &quot;Shadow Walk&quot;: Spirit (2) + Gnosis (1) + Willpower (3)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 1 Free Reach: 1 on Instant Cast, 1 on Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Base Paradox dice:</b> 1 from Reach.<br /> <b>Paradox modifiers:</b> -2 from Dedicated Tool.<br /> <b>Final Paradox dice:</b> 0.<br /> If Paradox is obtained, Lynx will release it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480921\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Spirit 2 &quot;Shadow Walk&quot; \u2192 2 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 02-09-2017, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:55:27-08:00","id":1041346,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Active Sight (Mind, Space) | Spells: none<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b><b>BB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 3/8 | Mana: 0/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> Moonstone's foot slips and dangles four stories off the ground. His blood is ice. If only he had a highly trained body and years of practical athletic experience, oh wait:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Athletics is way more Moonstone's bag than Streetwise. Reflexively canceling Active Sight to avoid the -2 penalty. Wits+Athletics, 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480918\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> Also ending my Incognito Presence and Ragnar Space Hex spells. He already got an arcane beat from resolving a magical Condition this scene, he's good :P</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ragnar's perception returns to normal, which is good, because keeping him ensorcelled probably would have been the death of his would-be tutor. Without any magic to divide his focus, Moonstone instinctively twists his body backwards in a controlled fall back onto the balcony. Loud creak of aged iron. The warlock narrowly avoids bonking his noggin on a brick.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>(bless you, aion.</i></span>) <b>IT'S OKAY! EVERYONE WILL BE OKAY!</b>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Hopefully! Ragnar is...crouching, or something, he can't tell. But the wicked one from his Divination is here, too. He's still getting his balance, and he too-quickly fletches a little arrow of magic and flicks his wrist to pierce the familiar stranger's mind.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mind 1 Know Nature on this dude. Instant cast, +1 Reach to learn Aspirations and Obsessions. No paradox, yaaay.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1+Mind 2, 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480933\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a><br /> <br /> It was going to be an aimed spell, but there's no need to roll that now. This is a good setup for putting pressure on a mage btw, Moonstone has like no resources and no prep and no time to make up for it. Tense!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:56:18-08:00","id":1041462,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Phoenix</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Peripheral Sight</b> | <b>Armor:</b> None | <b>Active Spell(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>WP:</b> 4/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 2/10 | <b>Wisdom:</b> 7 (Understanding)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Grieving [Guilty], Supernal Blindness | <b>Tilts:</b> None</div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;Let's do this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That sounded a bit like Ragnar...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I tawt I taw a Raggycat.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480952\" target=\"_blank\">Wits 3 + Composure 2 = 5 dice \u2192 2 successes</a><br /> <br /> I did! I did taw a Raggycat!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480954\" target=\"_blank\">Initiative \u2192 4 + 5 Mod = 9</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is him, and that Death mage from the other day. Wait, what's happened to Ragnar? Oh, that coward's gonna bleed...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix has his staff ready.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:04:22-08:00","id":1041468,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">RAGNAR</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\">Mage Sight: Fate, Time<br /> Active Spells: Exceptional Luck (on the mage)<br /> Conditions/Tilts:Inspired, Immobilized (0 Speed, 0 Defense)<br /> Health: BBBBOOOO I WP: 2/4 I Mana: 2/10 I Wisdom: 7<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Arcane Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Arcane Experiences: 1</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480953\" target=\"_blank\"> 10</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ragnar grins as his spell takes effect and the mage is suddenly stricken with blindness. But his excitement turns to panic as the concrete around him freezes, and then he feels like the very life is being sucked out of him. <i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">Shit. He's better at Death than I am at Fate or Time. I need to do something fast. </span></i>But then he feels something on his Periphery, something... up. He looks and sees... Moonstone. On a balcony. Four stories up. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><i>Well, better late than never... wait... why did he end up there? </i></span>But then realization hits him.<span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><i> You moron, you flubbed the teleportation spell, didn't you? </i></span>But then the world goes back to blissful clarity, and suddenly, Moonstone is his favorite person in it. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Let's have some fun with this joker.</i> </span>He looks at the mage, whose head has whipped in the direction of Moonstone. <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;Should've run when you had the chance, asshole.&quot; </span>He then shouts up at Moonstone, <span style=\"color:#0000cd\">&quot;He's blind!&quot; </span>With that, he attempts to pull himself out of the concrete.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar will attempt to pull himself out of the concrete. Strength 1 + Athletic 2 - Durability 2 + Willpower 3 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/480962\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 01-31-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T19:14:19-08:00","id":1044323,"title":"","content":"<b>Lynx</b><br /> As you reflexively summon your armor in defense, the wolf spirit's bite fails to break your skin. It growls angrily, snarling at you. <br /> <br /> But your spell cloaks you from his senses, and he spins around searching for you. He sniffs the air, whining. As he does, his demeanor changes, and you can tell from subtle changes in how he walks that he's doing something to become more agile. <br /> <br /> Raven grins eagerly at you. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Well done, little cub! But don't underestimate him just yet.&quot;</span> She stands with her arms crossed, waiting to see what you will do next. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A few things about Paradox actually in your favor. First, any Spirit spell cast while in the Shadow World benefits from a -2 penalty on Paradox roll, without even using your Dedicated Tool. Also, you still roll Paradox even if it's a dice pool of 0 (chance roll). There is still a chance of successes on the roll, but if you get a dramatic failure, it actually gets you get things on your roll. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/482004\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox</a>: <b>0</b> successes, no dramatic failure, moot point. <br /> <br /> Your turn again.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone, Ragnar, and Phoenix</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative:<br /> Ragnar - 10<br /> Phoenix - 9<br /> Moonstone - 8<br /> Mysterious mage - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/482010\" target=\"_blank\">7</a><br /> <br /> Piecing in what you all put in your posts, Ragnar spends his turn breaking out of the ground, Phoenix spends his action arriving at the scene (let me know if you would do something different), and Moonstone spends his action trying to learn about the hostile mage, who is now up.<br /> <br /> For the next round, you can post in any order, but the actions will resolve in order of initiative.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The enemy mage looks up in Moonstone's general direction. Although his eyes are blinded, he cocks his head as if still looking at something. The man points the rod and smirks. A pulse of energy emanates from him, causing his Nimbus to flare with power for anyone studying him with their Sight.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the balcony Moonstone is hanging from simply...vanishes. Or, more precisely, the iron <i>sublimates</i>, defying natural physics as it turns directly from solid iron into gaseous form.<br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone</b><br /> Your spell fizzles as you form it. You're simply too distracted to press your Imago into place. <br /> <br /> You suddenly find yourself falling as the balcony you're resting on simply vanishes into thin air, literally. The ground rushes towards you. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You can make a reflexive Strength + Athletics roll at a -2 penalty to try and catch the balcony on the third story; if you succeed, you take no damage. If you fail, make a reflexive Dexterity + Athletics roll, which will allow you to reduce the falling damage you would take. <br /> <br /> You also can take an instant action, which you can do before or after your other rolls.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix</b><br /> You follow your ears and quickly race to the alley. You find Ragnar up to his knees in cement, and the mage fires a spell just before you arrive that causes Moonstone to start plummeting towards the ground.<br /> <br /> You hear Ragnar yell, <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;He's blind!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar</b><br /> You wriggle and push all of your strength into your legs and torso, straining to break free. And somehow, you do it. It hurts like hell, and you cut your legs in the process, but you're on your feet again. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Immobilized ends. You take 1 bashing damage.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T20:52:39-08:00","id":1044359,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone<br /> Peripheral Sight | Spells: none [Cloak: Wards and Signs, Potency 4]<br /> Conditions: Divergent (Active), Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors) [-1 Strength until evening]<br /> Health: </b><b>B</b><b>BB</b>OOO | <b>Willpower: 3/8 | Mana: 0/10 | Beats: 0/5 | Arcane Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The Mind spell doesn't hold together. Ugh. Well, at least the Cloak protects him from any magic this guy might throw his way in return.<br /> <br /> <i>oh no, where's the ground?</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Stay on the ledge, ledge disappears. We are going FULL LOONEY TUNES. Strength+Athletics-2, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/482514\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Should have rolled 1 less die due to scouring Strength, but there would still be 2 successes.<br /> <br /> Also, Cloak of Night activation roll for Shadow Flesh, 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/482520\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Moonstone is a flat shadow for up to 5 turns starting with this one, Cloak is now at 0 Mana. We're running on empty.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He plummets much too fast for his liking, but somehow thinks fast enough to catch the next-lowest balcony and not even lose a tooth. Stupid busted Cloak ward, doesn't even work...<span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;oh for god's sake- enough!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> With one free hand, he reaches back and pulls the hood of the Cloak over his head. Moonstone is wrapped up into cold darkness that creeps over the balcony's edge, sinks down the building, and spreads onto the ground like spilled ink. His shadow is cast against the wall, a silhouette finding its footing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T15:37:31-08:00","id":1046504,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Beats: 5 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Just yet? What's he going to do now? What should I do? Should I ask another spirit to help me?</span></i><br /> <br /> He glances at the wolf spirit and a sigh and smile escapes his lips.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">This is Pok\u00e9mon, isn't it?</span></i><br /> <br /> Internally facepalming, he slowly walks away from the wolf as he weaves the spell in his mind:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#800000\">Every spirit has a weakness. A Ban. A Bane. Let's find out what this wuff's weakness is.</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Lynx attempts to cast Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot; on the Wolf, reaching for Instant casting time, but garners no successes.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>1 target:</b> Wolf spirit.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant.<br /> <b>Yantra:</b> Path Tool (+1 dice).<br /> <b>Base Dice Pool:</b> Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot;: Spirit (2) + Gnosis (1) + Path Tool (1) + Willpower (3) - Potency (2)<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> 2 Free Reaches: 1 on Instant Cast, 1 on Spell maintenance.<br /> <br /> <b>There is no risk of Paradox.</b><br /> <b>Total Dice Pool:</b> 5 dice.</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://http://orokos.com/roll/483889\" target=\"_blank\">Roll for Spirit 1 &quot;Know Spirit&quot; \u2192 0 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T09:04:51-08:00","id":1046803,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#006400\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ouroboros Ophis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Mage Sight: </b>Periphereal | <b>Active Spells: </b>None<br /> <b>Health: </b>OOOOOO | <b>WP: </b>6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/10 | <b>Wisdom: </b>7 (Understanding)</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conditions: </b>None | <b>Tilts: </b>None | <b>Beats: </b>7 | <b>Arc. Beats:</b> 1</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\"><i><b>-&quot;</b></i><b><i>What have I gotten into?</i></b></span><b><i>&quot;</i></b>- Marvin thinks, forcing a polite smile to his frozen lips. He looks at Dante but finds only aknowledgement, not reasurance. The tea dissapears drink after drink while he ponders what to do. He has a terrible suspicion but doesn't want to embarrass Dante or himself by acting in any way that might be interpreted as rude or hostile. Could this Mrs. Vial or her assistant know if he used the Sight? Only one way to find out.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ouroboros Ophis activates Mage Sight (Death&amp;Matter).<br /> <br /> Wits + Subterfuge roll as requested = 1 die (Wits 2 -1 (Subterfuge 0) = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/484164\" target=\"_blank\">0 Successes</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T08:07:58-08:00","id":1047214,"title":"","content":"<b>Moonstone</b><br /> You reflexively grab the balcony beneath you and thank your fortune at being a talented athlete. You transform into a pool of shadows, and the hostile mage frowns as you do, his eyes sliding past you while he seems to look in your general direction. <br /> <br /> <b>Lynx</b><br /> Your spell fizzles despite the effort you pour into your Imago. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;A worthy effort, little cub,&quot;</span> Raven smiles. <span style=\"color:indigo\">&quot;Don't give up. The spirits can sense your hesitation. Assert your dominance. Prove your strength.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The wolf spirit lifts its nose and sniffs at the air. It utters a growl from deep in its throat. It seems to be focused on searching for you. <br /> <br /> You feel a weight of energy push against you, like the wolf is pressing against the cloak of Spirit magic you have wrapped around you. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Roll Clash of Wills using Gnosis + Spirit as the wolf spirit uses the Pathfinder Numen to search for you. Add the relevant bonus to your roll based on the duration of your spell (I think +1, can't remember). It takes an instant action, and if he succeeds, he will be able to find you for the scene. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros Ophis</b><br /> You simply can't tell if Mrs. Vial had anything to hide. Something seems off about her, but her words make sense, you suppose. <br /> <br /> If Mrs. Vial or Desiree are able to tell when you open your Sight, they give no indication. But any thought of what they might be thinking moves to the back of your mind as you See them for the first time.<br /> <br /> To your shock, you immediately sense that Mrs. Vial and Desiree are not alive. <br /> <br /> Neither woman has a heart beat. Sure, they have blood in their faces, making them appear flush and hale, Desiree more so than Mrs. Vial. They walk, and talk. Desiree goes through the motion of breathing, but her lungs are composed of dead tissue, and you realize that Mrs. Vial's chest isn't even rising or falling. As far as you can tell, they should be motionless corpses. So how are they having a conversation with you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:15:51-08:00","id":1047386,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>LYNX<br /> Active Sight: None<br /> Active Spells: None<br /> Willpower: 1/5 Mana: 6/10<br /> Conditions/Tilts: None<br /> Beats: 5 - Arcane Beats: 4</b></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler